reatinine ratio | Reference: 2010 - Association of estimated glomerular filtration rate and albuminuria with all-cause and cardio | AMA Style Guide References: Association of estimated glomerular filtration rate and albuminuria with all-cause and cardio. 2010. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001494 | Match Text: The ADA/KDIGO Consensus recommends that PCPs should treat all patients with CKD and refer appropriate patients to nephrology | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnot"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8144bebf-1702-4ec6-a4d3-dee7ecd88f9b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 76, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "source_hash": "0848f1de95dfa353dce3ba85df7352033c9d29afc95ce8d0ec6e3038763b6987", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "chunk_id": "8144bebf-1702-4ec6-a4d3-dee7ecd88f9b", "text": "Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: ADA=American Diabetes Association; CKD=chronic kidney disease; KDIGO=Kidney Disease: Improving Global Outcomes; PCP=primary care physician | Reference: 2022 - de Boer IH et al., Diabetes Care 2022; 45(12): 3075–90 | AMA Style Guide References: de Boer IH et al., Diabetes Care 2022. 45(12): 3075–90. 2022. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001496 | Match Text: Initiate JARDIANCE first line to reduce your patients’ risk of CV death and protect them right from the start | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: JARDIANCE helps protect by reducing CV and kidney risk.   CV=cardiovascular | Reference: Jardiance - EU/SmPC | AMA Style Guide References: - EU/SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001482 | Match Text: Initiate an SGLT2i early to slow kidney function decline | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARD"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:32757f0e-dffa-44df-a869-d88acc53b965", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 77, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "source_hash": "b29dac81ed161346db2a4da5e6a8124062c267f95c26782d4ee4a219589bd940", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "chunk_id": "32757f0e-dffa-44df-a869-d88acc53b965", "text": "rce: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001482 | Match Text: Initiate an SGLT2i early to slow kidney function decline | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic, Disease Awareness, Efficacy | Footnotes: SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor | Reference: 2024 KDIGO Guidelines | AMA Style Guide References: 2024 KDIGO Guidelines. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001490 | Match Text: Irreversible vascular damage may be present by the time T2D or CKD are diagnosed | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: CKD=chronic kidney disease; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: Palladino BMJ Open Diabetes Res Care 2020\n\n