ascular death | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therape"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f6d9e4b8-057c-449b-a0fa-1a3d72e9bd87", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 79, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "source_hash": "233aebd2fc987e16a6a5f5298d27a75ed03506ea0afa1d8efbcb61baf1dae0db", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "chunk_id": "f6d9e4b8-057c-449b-a0fa-1a3d72e9bd87", "text": "rEF, and HFpEF to reduce the risk of heart failure hospitalisation or cardiovascular death | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: HFmrEF=heart failure with mildly reduced ejection fraction; HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction; SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor | Reference: RD-169473 McDonagh TA et al. 2021 Eur Heart J. 2021;42(36):3599-3726\n\nMcDonagh TA, Metra M, Adamo M, et al. Eur Heart J 2023 | AMA Style Guide References: McDonagh TA et al. 2021 Eur Heart J. 2021;42(36):3599-3726.\n\nMcDonagh TA, Metra M, Adamo M, et al. Eur Heart J. 2023. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001483 | Match Text: Optimised treatment should go beyond HbA1c reduction and help protect your patients with T2D and CVD | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic, Efficacy, Guidelines | Footnotes: CVD=cardiovascul"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2921bdd4-0dec-4632-b737-c51f1bf740bd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 80, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "source_hash": "a2f814467834247f58ab3858c022ec21312a1f08311bcef0443779fc6a5f6d31", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "chunk_id": "2921bdd4-0dec-4632-b737-c51f1bf740bd", "text": "rea: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic, Efficacy, Guidelines | Footnotes: CVD=cardiovascular; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2022 - Management of Hyperglycemia in Type 2 Diabetes, 2022. A Consensus Report by the American Diab | AMA Style Guide References: Management of Hyperglycemia in Type 2 Diabetes, 2022. A Consensus Report by the American Diab. 2022. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001485 | Match Text: JARDIANCE is a guideline-recommended treatment for patients with HF across the LVEF spectrum, with or without T2D | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: HF=heart failure; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2022 - McDonagh TA httpsacademic.oup.comeurheartjarticle423635996358045\n\nMcDonagh TA, Metra M, Adamo M, et al. Eur Heart J 2023 | AMA Style Guide References: McDonagh TA httpsacademic.oup.comeurheartjarticle423635996358045. 2022.\n\nMcDonagh TA, Metra M, Adamo"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:98f9ea7b-5ccf-4996-a62d-b96c8b5aaa66", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 81, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "source_hash": "32a944f15ea17ed5535400be96fa1cf2b5e9a9e249e3d415e83b3d66e291cb42", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "chunk_id": "98f9ea7b-5ccf-4996-a62d-b96c8b5aaa66", "text": ". Eur Heart J 2023 | AMA Style Guide References: McDonagh TA httpsacademic.oup.comeurheartjarticle423635996358045. 2022.\n\nMcDonagh TA, Metra M, Adamo M, et al. Eur Heart J. 2023. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001489 | Match Text: The risk of CV death in patients increases with progression of T2D or CKD | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: CKD=chronic kidney disease; CV=cardiovascular; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: Raghavan J Am Heart Assoc 2019\n\nMatsushita Nat Rev Nephrol 2022 | AMA Style Guide References: Raghavan J Am Heart Assoc. 2019.\n\nMatsushita Nat Rev Nephrol. 2022. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001492 | Match Text: Primary care guidelines recommend including SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, as part of initial therapy for patients with T2D at high or very high cardiovascular risk | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guideline"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ad548e84-0780-493e-9d34-dd8c0d1d8b9b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 82, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "source_hash": "c2792fbab5092c33e67aa8af480683c51df17b5556a2f5a64be4bce7efa287a7", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "chunk_id": "ad548e84-0780-493e-9d34-dd8c0d1d8b9b", "text": "isk | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitor; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: Seidu S i wsp. Prim Care Diabetes 2022;16:223 | AMA Style Guide References: Seidu S i wsp. Prim Care Diabetes. 2022;16:223. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001484 | Match Text: In patients with T2D and eCVD, JARDIANCE reduced risk of CV death regardless of patients’ HbA1c or BMI. | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: In the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 7720 patients with T2D at high cardiovascular risk, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg (n=4867) were evaluated vs placebo (n=2333). Patients were adults with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke. The primary com"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1ed38f84-fedb-4d13-b767-7c9b4b6bc72c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 83, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "source_hash": "efeabe4282e438801625fb92e4ad167e7c83fd1d9cf536e588b5f5d0bb5bdb8b", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "chunk_id": "1ed38f84-fedb-4d13-b767-7c9b4b6bc72c", "text": "ere evaluated vs placebo (n=2333). Patients were adults with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke. The primary composite outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial was 3-point MACE, composed of death from CV causes, nonfatal MI, or nonfatal stroke, as analysed in the pooled JARDIANCE group vs the placebo group. The 14% RRR (1.6% ARR) in 3-point MACE (HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99; p<0.001 for noninferiority; p=0.04 for superiority) was driven by a reduction in the risk of CV death (HR=0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77); there was no change in risk of nonfatal MI (HR=0.87; 95% CI: 0.70, 1.09) or nonfatal stroke (HR=1.24; 95% CI: 0.92, 1.67).  A prespecified analysis included subgroups of patients with HbA1c <8.5% and ≥8.5%  Rate of CV death (%) across HbA1c subgroups: All values depict JARDIANCE vs placebo, respectively. <7.0%: 2.4 (n=297) vs 7.9 (n=127); 7.0%-<8.0%: 3.7 (n=2042) vs 6.1 (n=1029); 8.0%-<9.0%: 3.7 (n=1534) vs 5.4 (n=795); ≥9.0%: 4.2 (n=812) vs 5.5 (n=382).  Rate of CV death across BMI subgroups: In the BMI ≥30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate of CV death was 3.8% for JARDIANCE (n=2408) vs 4.8% for placebo (n=1213). In the BMI <30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate o"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c26e4989-25b7-418a-b05e-d01c99ab8a24", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 84, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "source_hash": "ff00a2203eda03e5b76cd22b2f0d3bed665024c94c3287438f1ba49f178504bb", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "chunk_id": "c26e4989-25b7-418a-b05e-d01c99ab8a24", "text": "e BMI ≥30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate of CV death was 3.8% for JARDIANCE (n=2408) vs 4.8% for placebo (n=1213). In the BMI <30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate of CV death was 3.5% for JARDIANCE (n=2279) vs 6.9% for placebo (n=1120).   RRR=relative risk reduction; ARR=absolute risk reduction; BMI=body mass index; CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; HR=hazard ratio; MACE=major adverse cardiovascular events; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes\n\nZinman N Engl J Med 2015 Supplement\n\nInzucchi Circulation 2018\n\n | AMA Style Guide References: Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes. 2015.\n\nZinman N Engl J Med. 2015 Supplement.\n\nInzucchi Circulation. 2018. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001486 | Match Text: SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, are Class I recommended for first-line use in patients with eCVD + T2D to reduce the risk of CV events | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3a9e1fde-b9ac-4d1d-8452-8240e99bc57b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 85, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "source_hash": "5fbfc50fbd06b0dfd1323d28d0701f3c7b3fec12ef5ed68a03fd5fda07641931", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "chunk_id": "3a9e1fde-b9ac-4d1d-8452-8240e99bc57b", "text": "ed for first-line use in patients with eCVD + T2D to reduce the risk of CV events | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; ESC=European Society of Cardiology; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: Marx Eur Heart J 2023 | AMA Style Guide References: Marx Eur Heart J. 2023. | Content M