hunk_index": 30, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "bea594c4-2c6e-483c-b23c-9c09bfaef9da", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE_Claims_Corrected_Final-1 (1) 2.xlsx", "source_hash": "4fed58a12b88c6d6afbef99721f71d6966d85ca01bf96ac14498268869464fdb", "source_document_id": "13ae0354-6211-4820-b97a-7634167e0ed0", "chunk_id": "545a5a0d-02e5-4586-8c40-1a452d1109da", "text": "rmed complete | Indication: Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Study/programme: EMPA-REG OUTCOME | Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.106 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 5 | Reference: EMPA-REG OUTCOME | 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.106\n#: 51 | Final Corrected Claim: EMPA-REG OUTCOME® trial: Early and sustained reductions in the risk of CV death5 Reducing the risk of CV death can help your patients get more time with their loved ones5 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Study/programme: EMPA-REG OUTCOME | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.26; 2026 PCP iVA p.31 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 5 | Reference: EMPA-RE"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3a8f1ef8-3844-4eca-942c-2f18ef33febc", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 31, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "bea594c4-2c6e-483c-b23c-9c09bfaef9da", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE_Claims_Corrected_Final-1 (1) 2.xlsx", "source_hash": "855fc339e5528447cb9479560607d47a23c676b048fa4015c1dd492d17a56c6e", "source_document_id": "13ae0354-6211-4820-b97a-7634167e0ed0", "chunk_id": "3a8f1ef8-3844-4eca-942c-2f18ef33febc", "text": "iVA p.31 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 5 | Reference: EMPA-REG OUTCOME | 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.26; 2026 PCP iVA p.31\n#: 52 | Final Corrected Claim: The 14% RRR in 3-point MACE (HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99; p<0.001 for noninferiority; p=0.04 for superiority) was driven by a reduction in the risk of CV death (HR=0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77); there was no change in risk of nonfatal MI (HR=0.87; 95% CI: 0.70, 1.09) or nonfatal stroke (HR=1.24; 95% CI: 0.92, 1.67).1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 14%; 95%; HR=0.86; HR=0.62; HR=0.87; HR=1.24; 95% CI: 0; p<0.001; p=0.04 | Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.104 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Card"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d3601272-20bd-4905-bd06-74000c17199f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 32, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "bea594c4-2c6e-483c-b23c-9c09bfaef9da", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE_Claims_Corrected_Final-1 (1) 2.xlsx", "source_hash": "c285909ebf7c5f3cdb1245a797f9cda5a9979579568468f2f6602e8633a04862", "source_document_id": "13ae0354-6211-4820-b97a-7634167e0ed0", "chunk_id": "d3601272-20bd-4905-bd06-74000c17199f", "text": "p.104 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.104\n#: 53 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE is a guideline-recommended option that can help your patients by reducing their risk of CV death | Status: Corrected | Indication: Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.41 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.41\n#: 54 | Final Corrected Claim: Contraindications and precautions \n• JARDIANCE should not be used for the treatment of patients with: \n– Type 1 diabetes \n– Severe hepatic impairment \n– Hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients \n• In patients 75 years and older, an increased risk of volume depletion"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a2f547ce-4082-4972-a8b3-78124af4d1a1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 33, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "bea594c4-2c6e-483c-b23c-9c09bfaef9da", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE_Claims_Corrected_Final-1 (1) 2.xlsx", "source_hash": "94aef54295da0fd3f9afefa1aa1a77165c28f765b4e653db1e8ca6f4d62dcd3b", "source_document_id": "13ae0354-6211-4820-b97a-7634167e0ed0", "chunk_id": "a2f547ce-4082-4972-a8b3-78124af4d1a1", "text": "ment \n– Hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients \n• In patients 75 years and older, an increased risk of volume depletion should be taken into account \n• Due to limited experience, it is not recommended to initiate treatment with empagliflozin in patients with an eGFR <20 mL/min/1.73 m2 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.37; 2026 PCP iVA p.47 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.37; 2026 PCP iVA p.47\n#: 55 | Final Corrected Claim: EMPA-KIDNEY: the largest SGLT2i kidney trial to date evaluated JARDIANCE across the broadest spectrum of patients with declining kidney function | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty cont"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4e6ba375-1e3c-494b-a75a-eb87253cfce9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 34, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "bea594c4-2c6e-483c-b23c-9c09bfaef9da", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE_Claims_Corrected_Final-1 (1) 2.xlsx", "source_hash": "4a18966947cb51b2352317240c1717d69d8de346cb831bc8d0bc4502a5b79c17", "source_document_id": "13ae0354-6211-4820-b97a-7634167e0ed0", "chunk_id": "4e6ba375-1e3c-494b-a75a-eb87253cfce9", "text": "rrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.74; 2026 Card iVA p.177; 2026 PCP iVA p.76 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local med