\n| JARDIANCE brand values . . . . . . . .                                         |   60 |\n| JARDIANCE brand purpose . . . . . .                                            |   61 |\n| JARDIANCE brand DNA . . . . . . . . .                                          |   62 |\n| JARDIANCE brand archetype . . . . .                                            |   63 |\n| JARDIANCE brand personality . . . .                                            |   64 |\n| JARDIANCE brand voice . . . . . . . . . .                                      |   65 |\n| 5. JARDIANCE family branding . . . . . .                                       |   66 |\n| Introduction to family branding . . . . . .                                    |   67 |\n| Promoting the family brands with JARDIANCE . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . |   68 |\n| SYNJARDY branding elements: symbol                                             |   69 |\n| Logo cluster . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2c926cf3-affc-41c0-874a-18c696329da2", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 8, "token_count": 98, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "be877221-3c90-42fb-b97f-a5011550fbdf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "1b5d57baaa8abe301a31af4c5cb8534e40114d6df48afb031a447af220973287", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "2c926cf3-affc-41c0-874a-18c696329da2", "text": "g elements: symbol                                             |   69 |\n| Logo cluster . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .                           |   70 |\n| GLYXAMBI branding elements: symbol                                             |   71 |\n| Logo cluster . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .                           |   72 |\n\nJARDIANCE digital guidance section coming soon."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f57409a9-5105-4729-919d-ab1a825dcac5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 9, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8d4aca3c-3187-4209-97a8-8fdea20f4f8f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f57409a9-5105-4729-919d-ab1a825dcac5", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:17d49bbc-32e1-4016-adcf-2e6b2aff47b7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 10, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "43213d3a-48b1-4e3f-bc4a-44508ace9173", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "17d49bbc-32e1-4016-adcf-2e6b2aff47b7", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:78fa5aa2-153f-43b0-bbf7-b7dafcdcd8fb", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 11, "token_count": 40, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ea38c908-f6fe-451c-97d6-43a54600c7c4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "67b23e4171b909da1c83c5ebc72f8d7af3e4bf3e50a9d41f0cce0ee2770dfe39", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "78fa5aa2-153f-43b0-bbf7-b7dafcdcd8fb", "text": "Early treatment significantly reduces serious CV complications in T2D, CKD, and/or CVD,* reinforcing the role of JARDIANCE as the first-line, proactive therapy"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9ecfc3dd-3992-4f56-aef2-fd83eb05af11", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 12, "token_count": 124, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "bf4f0bfc-226c-4422-abb3-b24a016dcd89", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "b7cac90fb20d4064fcbc999232cd73d4082a664917e47ad44a0f80ccdbbe5f4c", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "9ecfc3dd-3992-4f56-aef2-fd83eb05af11", "text": "to improve outcomes for all people living with T2D, CKD, and/or CVD* †\n\nThe proven cardiovascular benefits ‡  of JARDIANCE position it as a trusted and foundational choice across the CRM spectrum CV complications are the main cause of death in over 1 billion people who live with CRM conditions globally, highlighting the urgent need for early and foundational interventions like JARDIANCE\n\nJARDIANCE provides broad protection by reducing risk for people living with CKD, HF , or T2D with eCVD."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:eb0a9fc4-411d-4525-8da1-1323a588c713", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 13, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6dc55a9a-5599-4f75-8855-a902430ec2d7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "eb0a9fc4-411d-4525-8da1-1323a588c713", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:eed09794-633d-4274-8ec2-d4e34a79ec41", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 14, "token_count": 116, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0eda3ee1-af59-4b8a-8cbc-f8c2e1696ac5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "21abf5b2020849c10b4ad87f70f72ca97bab9f66a7789a861664c87c3b7e3826", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "eed09794-633d-4274-8ec2-d4e34a79ec41", "text": "*CVD as per label=T2D/eCVD, HF.\n\n† 1L in markets where 1L use is consistent with label. In JP this would have to be 'post SOC'.\n\nCSF 1\n\nCSF 2\n\nElevate the importance of addressing CV risk to drive urgency Increase urgency to address the cardiovascular and renal risks of T2D, CKD, or CVD*\n\nAccelerate early (1L) † and continued use of JARDIANCE in all approved indications\n\nStrengthen emotional connection to motivate behaviour change Enhance executional excellence"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:792c8154-90a4-4145-9b00-bdeb74baf6e8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 15, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ea0a44b1-9754-4bfd-baeb-06b0f9c8b2a3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "792c8154-90a4-4145-9b00-bdeb74baf6e8", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0e05e7d4-7537-44bd-bb87-34231e73a3a2", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 16, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "583236a0-6cf2-4e36-9a1d-dca33a9694f5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0e05e7d4-7537-44bd-bb87-34231e73a3a2", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:161b5d6f-f8dd-4c7f-afd0-7676f9fe0985", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 17, "token_count": 58, "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "194c9409-ba4d-4328-bf97-73a56aa8f517", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "f3b804e3a193e607bd72be030e1154979874dacf52005bd5471362df6f0a210b", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "161b5d6f-f8dd-4c7f-afd0-7676f9fe0985", "text": "CV complications are the number one cause of death for people living with T2D and/or CKD* and/or CVD 4-7\n\n- 40% of PCPs say JARDIANCE protects patients with elevated CV risk -better than other treatment options (including Forxiga)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e0fbc52d-23be-415f-ad52-d540014a346b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 18, "token_count": 82, "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c1a57f06-c8ff-4a70-8b7c-eb272accdf6b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "9514f4debaee6e89e06c28c76ce434d198216930837c6e42ae82f0c7feb97572", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e0fbc52d-23be-415f-ad52-d540014a346b", "text": "It can be difficult to treat beyond the primary disease I see in front of me, and knowing the best treatment options can be difficult. I'm also not convinced that there is a difference between SGLT2is.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nHCPs know that they need to protect patients-citing JARDIANCE as a resource that helps protect their patients †"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:89da094e-6240-45fb-b107-81d0ad20bc3e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 19, "token_count": 48, "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8c24ffc2-b197-49c6-8f6f-6793553ea30d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "6a68f054ca67a95483bb710cd4a406ab9728534a6e5a22293b17e549365b642e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "89da094e-6240-45fb-b107-81d0ad20bc3e", "text": "CV risk is significantly elevated by all CRM diseases, and SGLT2is are foundational to slowing disease progression. I'm responsible for treating my at-risk patients, and I rely on JARDIANCE."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d7281377-452f-4aed-a2b2-3d0a7673562d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 20, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a63f34a0-2441-4cff-a3c7-6d1802455dfa", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d7281377-452f-4aed-a2b2-3d0a7673562d", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6422c0ae-65af-41da-8e63-e662c3dd0fd5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 21, "token_count": 75, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a902db7e-214d-482a-a437-8b031f116e97", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "93ba84349a8edd87e2b0dbe6b5bcf53793d4597d4bb747e6492536cb7d745ead", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "6422c0ae-65af-41da-8e63-e662c3dd0fd5", "text": "HCPs do more than just treat disease-they protect their patients' futures. Reducing CV risk is about more than just protecting the heart. It is about owning the idea that JARDIANCE protects what the heart beats for by improving the lives of people with CRM diseases\n\nBuild long-term loyalty and trust"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:26537bde-49c9-488a-993b-be91a1716d53", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 22, "token_count": 18, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "edfb9462-a1a2-473f-a0f6-cc0022a3b9b9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "bbb0073348b480344947f5736c7648eb738c3783f0023af5859f8ec4917954f5", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "26537bde-49c9-488a-993b-be91a1716d53", "text": "JARDIANCE reduces CV risk across T2D, CKD, and CVD, and HCPs believe it"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:648b1f0c-9e3c-4a94-addc-9dc0c2d14e4e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 23, "token_count": 81, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3c6aec85-7961-4278-9f61-4fb239513690", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "90e2dd326b6524d41202c7935f4a2d4f8775c205bd711d04dde05a99dce28c9e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "648b1f0c-9e3c-4a94-addc-9dc0c2d14e4e", "text": "The impact of JARDIANCE on the lives of patients and HCPs must be felt in the moments that matter, beyond the clinical benefit\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nCreating this emotional connection will allow us to…\n\nIncrease engagement and advocacy Create a stronger brand connection Differentiate JARDIANCE in a crowded market"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f910826b-e02a-4744-a30d-69bfa6ff81fe", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 24, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ba9f3f32-536d-4d7f-9b22-4c042fbfdf4a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f910826b-e02a-4744-a30d-69bfa6ff81fe", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1c79eb61-aad8-42fc-8a15-b9d44e8e4f55", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 25, "token_count": 36, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "df6a28f3-0523-4825-8488-4d1547b0183d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "25ad0cd9a28accb3ee73e02ce9855eb73ad75593fc037bdd82ba7ad4db8638ec", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "1c79eb61-aad8-42fc-8a15-b9d44e8e4f55", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\nBe bold and disruptive to drive behaviour change\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nElevate the importance of reducing CV risk across indications"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:80fb8452-a6ff-4f10-a5be-ab04f0278875", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 26, "token_count": 66, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "536d1baf-d589-4bf0-a6ba-4a39eae8dce6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "0323325271644eb8e19359b91bd2b7d9dc42e87f4304e3e36a0e1457892a2ce4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "80fb8452-a6ff-4f10-a5be-ab04f0278875", "text": "by making early intervention with JARDIANCE urgent and tangible Showcase the strength of JARDIANCE in addressing CV risk Connect emotionally with customers to motivate behaviour change Simplify and focus our approach and narrative\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:20d55535-a739-48d3-a07d-98683ff8d419", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 27, "token_count": 20, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3a00027a-7ed1-4c93-8892-5e83473e071e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "a31ff65ae75ca75ebec0b7c219a3ed3bd57c4f59b041ac533cc209d52f4ea38e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "20d55535-a739-48d3-a07d-98683ff8d419", "text": "by creating brand distinction amid rising competition both in and out of class"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cc27bade-1375-4c15-a075-a24f76303343", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 28, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "b47a97a3-8051-48b9-a9d6-506d8aeda7cb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "cc27bade-1375-4c15-a075-a24f76303343", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2b7e835a-0d3c-4b7d-a169-e6019cdbc46b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 29, "token_count": 16, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "29e9009a-a8d2-4b7d-90cc-fbeac38d3c25", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "6808306235f948ef79ab16b2c83926534c0d860749f4219eaf3289199e44c4ff", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "2b7e835a-0d3c-4b7d-a169-e6019cdbc46b", "text": "With our new campaign, we seek to elevate JARDIANCE further as the"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0e6fdfae-94a0-4317-9fb8-932033e7d06e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 30, "token_count": 73, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6bfe8e86-82e2-4a74-b505-3eb52aaa5eae", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "3511b30e28ba2475904db569c5c10b96c31b74fe79fbbd0983191e83895e78f4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0e6fdfae-94a0-4317-9fb8-932033e7d06e", "text": "that unifies the CRM landscape through early CV risk interventioncementing its role as the first choice across indications and advancing its leadership in an increasingly competitive market.\n\n*This is internal, aspirational campaign language. Please do not use this copy in external materials."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:44d46d88-d2fb-4908-bdf3-c5e307e142ea", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 31, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "234433fa-f392-488d-92a3-f884b0f8402c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "44d46d88-d2fb-4908-bdf3-c5e307e142ea", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:17e819b0-a9cc-4d83-9937-b69457566f64", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 32, "token_count": 148, "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "114a1fc0-9233-45ea-9645-ccd2dc027ac7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "c7fcd4bf36143999341e8dabc7e286a9f08bc41938ae36f5b45cecdc6aad1c7a", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "17e819b0-a9cc-4d83-9937-b69457566f64", "text": "-   The CRM system is connected-and the heart is at the center of it all\n-   Reducing the risk of CV death should be a priority for all patients with CRM conditions\n-   Your patients are depending on you for protection\n\n*This is internal, aspirational campaign language. Please do not use this copy in external materials. † JARDIANCE provides broad protection by reducing risk for people living with CKD, HF, or T2D with eCVD.\n\nJARDIANCE is the heart of protection\n\n-   JARDIANCE has been protecting † patients for 10 years\n-   The benefits of JARDIANCE have been proven across multiple trials"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f5eadc87-d097-48d0-9fdf-0ad06118e2b0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 33, "token_count": 133, "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f03e7084-be42-46dc-8a0d-44e82f25d34c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "1ed1062b47a58eace99eb3e2dcf315a0c117077c3079fcd94fd3f31b0494b31f", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f5eadc87-d097-48d0-9fdf-0ad06118e2b0", "text": "-   JARDIANCE works quickly to protect † patients\n-   The sooner you start patients on JARDIANCE, the longer they can benefit\n-   JARDIANCE allows patients to live longer and do more\n\nJARDIANCE is an easy and foundational choice across indications\n\n-   JARDIANCE is recommended by multiple guidelines as a foundational treatment\n-   JARDIANCE fits easily into your treatment algorithm and can be used with other commonly prescribed medications\n\nDon't delay, start JARDIANCE today\n\n-   Choose JARDIANCE to protect †  patients' futures"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3d1a81ae-02f8-475d-8a92-47cb9d996a0f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 34, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "acd019a9-8a66-48b7-83d3-20e939c32ef1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "3d1a81ae-02f8-475d-8a92-47cb9d996a0f", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3d82206f-c2e6-4172-a368-63cd1b286b43", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 35, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c57e69e8-72dc-4ee8-95d5-838166a661a8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "3d82206f-c2e6-4172-a368-63cd1b286b43", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3995ab06-3204-480c-8681-8a1b203fba88", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 36, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0b000f90-4cda-4ee7-bf90-4a4a7f537c0a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "3995ab06-3204-480c-8681-8a1b203fba88", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:16663f83-bb2a-4b96-84fe-1643fcf9aa18", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 37, "token_count": 32, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "bc2873bd-d039-4373-abf6-d8bc816caa7f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e2f32f11ec69bbabd2c687606036072e6f8e421bff3b51eeb55e43e95f375083", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "16663f83-bb2a-4b96-84fe-1643fcf9aa18", "text": "The powerful tone and visual depict a 'critical moment,' which is considered motivating to addressing CV risk early with JARDIANCE"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:37a7aec3-de57-448d-86c4-e76e64b9dead", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 38, "token_count": 38, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "21b9fab1-bdfb-4411-a237-6f7c3c2b013f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7f24738627f1bacc574b9cc785bcd7b2e0877678f09e83943073977f10954599", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "37a7aec3-de57-448d-86c4-e76e64b9dead", "text": "The campaign generates an emotional reaction and stimulates curiosity, with respondents answering that the campaign made them feel inspired and motivated"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ae0b5067-f9d9-4ad2-89b7-0dc9129084b7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 39, "token_count": 52, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "9a455c12-0a2f-490c-976b-807141f7ac6c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "3f447e455dfd94eaf3b4308a617b91745e1ba87b3b80a2393cf82d8aca2ed29d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ae0b5067-f9d9-4ad2-89b7-0dc9129084b7", "text": "Anthem is the most impactful concept for motivating early action and change, which is crucial for JARDIANCE to shift entrenched prescribing behaviours, especially in specialties like nephrology and cardiology"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4e8031ad-7f8d-4d51-b662-e56cf0b45b0c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 40, "token_count": 44, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "5bf54b1d-24be-4d16-adec-1b776005023a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "c00287fe3e4b05f5712162a3776bdf47c0bf675713bc1347bd521831da234607", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "4e8031ad-7f8d-4d51-b662-e56cf0b45b0c", "text": "The unique, impactful visual of Anthem stands out and gives JARDIANCE a platform for driving change. Even as it polarises, it creates meaningful brand recall and stopping power"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0330d072-dab9-4f8f-9e4f-e7b3d3e0747c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 41, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d4748f85-a88a-4292-83bc-efeee89de3f8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0330d072-dab9-4f8f-9e4f-e7b3d3e0747c", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b8105b66-6afa-4951-817a-4bc970d82ab8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 42, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "730ec1f4-f0cf-4d5a-ab83-22787b52578e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b8105b66-6afa-4951-817a-4bc970d82ab8", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8a695095-8be4-45c0-99e1-ce1ea3f6dc8c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 43, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "32983bfd-632d-40bb-9b4d-1fe9f7da31a4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "8a695095-8be4-45c0-99e1-ce1ea3f6dc8c", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e15fa744-4502-48a4-ba86-f6c0e35588f8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 44, "token_count": 20, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f9e4eb93-1b99-4105-aad3-147fd9edda2d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "8dcba93605608f718eba74a59d46ff25da85445adf58192d9a40df2be5b07bf9", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e15fa744-4502-48a4-ba86-f6c0e35588f8", "text": "Our hero image is unique and impactful, as it stands out emotionally and visually."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:063b97a9-4694-4da4-a765-6dcff87fce0f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 45, "token_count": 40, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "4a4f7875-a827-426a-bfb8-bdd1b1832687", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "a42ec81cc1f6638a331a38a5d220181218c2673ff108e71812b3c4c1c3497b4d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "063b97a9-4694-4da4-a765-6dcff87fce0f", "text": "The chosen language generates an emotional reaction and stimulates curiosity, with respondents answering that this campaign made them feel inspired and motivated."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ff5e879c-f429-49c0-95e7-cb367314b129", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 46, "token_count": 48, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "33e4b4c7-08e4-4940-a040-12d9979fef8f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "f2498c78c697e1fa815ecaf073a7ceb426d4d77ee9232a0b6b17fbca307be363", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ff5e879c-f429-49c0-95e7-cb367314b129", "text": "The central focus of our hero image is the heart image on the hand, symbolising the connection between reducing the risk of CV death and everything that JARDIANCE can protect for these patients."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f38fce09-07e7-4b49-a60d-f6a669af4bf9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 47, "token_count": 32, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "836eda1c-68c3-4785-9a71-799b1ba51e1b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7f3e4c82894be387e290171aba9bfe9416bd697d29c23fa087910bea713163f4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f38fce09-07e7-4b49-a60d-f6a669af4bf9", "text": "The subhead provides the additional context to the headline and includes our indications to ensure a fair balance of information."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:82228253-acbd-49da-be6a-005e732bef5a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 48, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "75785c1b-7cdf-4897-9fd6-420293a985c1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "82228253-acbd-49da-be6a-005e732bef5a", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b6961da9-cc04-4179-aed8-5d1db1a47238", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 49, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "574d1e66-6091-4108-ab17-8a2c54bfad9d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b6961da9-cc04-4179-aed8-5d1db1a47238", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:15e4c583-9986-4b3b-b302-e2d039db090b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 50, "token_count": 42, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "49b44daa-9d6e-4ef6-a5b2-0d942d21776e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "23dc7bdcc7357c2ed7a86116fdbaf935f0e98ed5878bbfd1813565361f7df900", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "15e4c583-9986-4b3b-b302-e2d039db090b", "text": "-   Ensure the headline is the most prominent text on the page\n-   Maintain the placement of supporting copy with the headline and the visual shown here\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e3303fdd-6d52-45e9-98f3-25072eea2a75", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 51, "token_count": 69, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "4c8d0ac7-0a8a-4fb3-bc6e-81d4f86ad440", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "71c52cc7928203be5630c45a827beda99b0db07c2dcaaf039a08ab1749c63740", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e3303fdd-6d52-45e9-98f3-25072eea2a75", "text": "- DON'T alter the position or the size of the headline\n- DON'T use the headline and visual without supporting copy\n- DON'T alter the weight or the font size of the supporting copy in relation to the headline\n- DON'T adjust the ratio of colours or modify the graphic treatment"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:33330030-32cc-47bc-833f-baeb570297ab", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 52, "token_count": 201, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a958986f-e706-41f2-86e5-4dfccb6e594e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "2bee107dbee7af0535ce105631d6ea91916508b72dbaba25e267546e4a8361f4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "33330030-32cc-47bc-833f-baeb570297ab", "text": "Please ensure that the localized version of the campaign claim complies with all applicable local MLR requirements.\n\nTranslation : Keep translated copy, color, and placement as close as possible to the original. Changes should only be made if required by local MLR (Medical, Legal, Regulatory) standards.\n\nReview Process : The localized headline must be reviewed with your Country Point of Contact (CPC), and MLR teams to confirm that it accurately reflects the campaign enhancement and is suitable for local use.\n\nDocumentation : Ensure that all materials are uploaded to the appropriate system with correct disclaimers, prescribing information, and translation certifications where applicable.\n\nFinal usage of the claim may depend on local market conditions and country-specific laws and requirements ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e1e30b51-8602-44ac-a1d9-5c12e6ffb592", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 53, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0c8149e5-4d91-49cd-a4f1-8c5034210f04", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e1e30b51-8602-44ac-a1d9-5c12e6ffb592", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b686e729-d673-45c5-8000-baa31cc3ccf1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 54, "token_count": 32, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3678d2b8-3f2f-49ff-a233-42fe67b633f4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "603110fddcc11d99c5eb40aab7c51abbb5167d84e5561f091300d678ff49aa98", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b686e729-d673-45c5-8000-baa31cc3ccf1", "text": "Four different doctors are available for use. Choose the one who most closely aligns with your market's needs.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9fcef00b-1546-48ee-bc2b-127a83dfda89", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 55, "token_count": 30, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "14df1dc7-a285-4207-93ca-619b579d5891", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "50ca38f3b345bcaa094616b0513aed90cfce931659627b5eb7cf8ae4ce75679a", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "9fcef00b-1546-48ee-bc2b-127a83dfda89", "text": "-   Ensure the doctor is the focal point on the page\n-   Select ethnicity of doctor for your local market\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d937a1ff-0f68-40d7-846c-5b4d8ad1102c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 56, "token_count": 69, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a76a5570-66d5-4f5f-9380-a56f1d3ad637", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "3bbf30f874acdc39705b8c28a4a143b0c14856fd945555215be2bad1594043d7", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d937a1ff-0f68-40d7-846c-5b4d8ad1102c", "text": "- DON'T replace the doctor with any other imagery except what is supplied specifically for this campaign\n- DON'T alter the crop of the hero's face beyond what is currently shown. Facial cropping should remain consistent across all pieces, while body cropping may vary as needed"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0677b675-6c87-4ad6-9398-595fcfcc9fe5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 57, "token_count": 75, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "392c6584-1bc4-4a22-8a4f-ac3629e01b19", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "d22b21f5f43128ab2329af28ddedc260e3afa5b349dd436dcf9b6ca1231a5838", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0677b675-6c87-4ad6-9398-595fcfcc9fe5", "text": "Full likeness rights have not been secured for the four doctor images included in this campaign. All usage must ensure that any portion above the bridge of the nose is cropped or obscured to remain compliant with licensing restrictions.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c0557e23-fa84-4a40-85a9-bbd656121562", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 58, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 18, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "4b300f2a-04a1-4dbf-9bd9-b20f849a7842", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c0557e23-fa84-4a40-85a9-bbd656121562", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:85386c65-ad22-4ba3-9bc0-9658c8ef2210", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 59, "token_count": 52, "page_number": 18, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c9e34bbd-aa38-4d5f-b759-dd19be79d886", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "ebc8b58c366e1ecaeffd30893b0b8f513f62fc3bca3e32fe7a40c19f85c9270d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "85386c65-ad22-4ba3-9bc0-9658c8ef2210", "text": "The paint, textural, and colour swash elements provide visual impact, vibrancy, and a distinctive layer of brand expression that enhances recognition and engagement across campaign materials.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:89b8dfc7-20e7-47ff-8ed5-b7777c031408", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 60, "token_count": 78, "page_number": 18, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "b70a4da7-b789-436c-8282-9cc641eda358", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e4fdc6975dadc7225445e8d37ed20908a4aff696f56560529076f419dac34404", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "89b8dfc7-20e7-47ff-8ed5-b7777c031408", "text": "-   Use the supplied background images only\n-   Use textures and graphics from the hero visual in isolation for both print and digital applications where appropriate\n-   Ensure any usage outside the hero visual complements and does not interfere with established page layouts and brand architecture\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c340de02-1470-483f-ae31-47d629b507f6", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 61, "token_count": 59, "page_number": 18, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "4dea457f-4a27-4e53-8e03-1eec755da8d5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "c7ef780ae6fdd2e343ed21cefdfc14e4bed018283d94b45ca999c0aea2d2ed58", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c340de02-1470-483f-ae31-47d629b507f6", "text": "- DON'T use any other background images\n- DON'T alter the colours, colour ratios, or proportions of graphic treatment in the hero visual\n- DON'T apply graphic treatments to visuals that are unrelated to the campaign story\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:79152b0d-2815-49f3-854a-fe77b196e5bd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 62, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 19, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0e3b0805-066a-4b99-b489-ec29dfc117ea", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "79152b0d-2815-49f3-854a-fe77b196e5bd", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:edb6c066-ed09-4969-9323-9a702c9dc77c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 63, "token_count": 50, "page_number": 19, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8e9a9262-5416-446a-a490-1abaf0a16684", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "f91ce922e63dfd8d74db2cb983f36df8a5961c784fd5fa56a5f8550baf72a920", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "edb6c066-ed09-4969-9323-9a702c9dc77c", "text": "Short video sequences and cinemagraphs have been developed to expand the campaign's presence across platforms and mediums, adding versatility and visual interest beyond static visuals.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:00a5b796-69a7-4aae-9e25-08e8552f0c2f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 64, "token_count": 67, "page_number": 19, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "93d3695c-2e94-499f-8d64-14902811c6b1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "ab50b183888fc44fc9aba4b3480fcb4d7bec610b5bcbf152a232d763977dc087", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "00a5b796-69a7-4aae-9e25-08e8552f0c2f", "text": "-   Follow applicable guidance from static visuals (ie, use only provided assets, do not introduce new doctors with the campaign pose)\n-   Layer graphic elements (paint, textures, swashes) into animations where they add emphasis or enhance storytelling\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8c10c27d-cffa-4814-8b47-2e9045cd983d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 65, "token_count": 54, "page_number": 19, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ecb93aca-368b-4e2e-a151-cc15ed6f9924", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "4f6e1442bc5e61e372270d35c2277ebe67d4c2b50ce035af0be1025f17710d4d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "8c10c27d-cffa-4814-8b47-2e9045cd983d", "text": "- DON'T introduce animation styles, transitions, or effects that fall outside the established brand look and feel\n- DON'T apply graphic treatments to visuals or scenes unrelated to the campaign story\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:aaa0440d-21fb-44a2-ae5d-09134a8454b3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 66, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 20, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "210e261e-63ba-4ec3-9ea4-a62ad29d2efb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "aaa0440d-21fb-44a2-ae5d-09134a8454b3", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6bbc3af1-1e40-4fd5-a1a4-d56c71a0524d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 67, "token_count": 160, "page_number": 20, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0ed2ed37-a104-44f6-bd64-3c7927606a5d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "2545f6c337452e6d6289d69ac07d37546ef93b9c9c5e27b0583b84a293ed3c2e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "6bbc3af1-1e40-4fd5-a1a4-d56c71a0524d", "text": "At the outset of every sales call, the emotional hook helps to reinforce the JARDIANCE brand promise and enhance our campaign message.\n\nThe emotional hook effectively addresses the previously missing patient perspective in the Anthem campaign visual. Together with the campaign, the emotional hook sets up the conversation to explore data and real-world evidence in more detail and motivates HCPs to learn more about JARDIANCE.\n\nThe emotional hook helps to drive the desired mindset shift by putting the patient at the center, reframing future risk as a present threat, and anchoring on the HCP's instinct to protect patients.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bf67bab2-a7d9-4557-8a8e-504fcda38dc8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 68, "token_count": 70, "page_number": 20, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e4ee8634-2d11-4c03-8cae-35c54c5233d6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "9567e439be9806e7905deec33487f93b8b7380f59163e09151d4f1eca20190ba", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "bf67bab2-a7d9-4557-8a8e-504fcda38dc8", "text": "-   The emotional hook should be used only in the iVA and congress materials to ensure maximum emotional impact\n-   In the iVA, the emotional hook should directly follow the campaign home page\n-   The Anthem campaign should always be included with the emotional hook\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:19eae60d-54b6-4fed-be5d-6af3fb7ffba0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 69, "token_count": 18, "page_number": 20, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "629c9408-7aff-4bb9-b96e-8ed30150c47f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5e2ba4adcbb445fdc6968c35f76f3a1bdeea3611ea8c18a040727e4c821482c7", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "19eae60d-54b6-4fed-be5d-6af3fb7ffba0", "text": "- DON'T use the emotional hook without the Anthem campaign\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0a6fbd67-8019-4ce4-9809-ef7465249ddd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 70, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2d9e3887-a854-434d-a076-5e5d3383b989", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0a6fbd67-8019-4ce4-9809-ef7465249ddd", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:41334d6c-f5fd-47d6-b7b8-2c3dafc5a14d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 71, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3219ff19-2460-481d-8ea8-e65a68e9b436", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "41334d6c-f5fd-47d6-b7b8-2c3dafc5a14d", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cb2c2678-5a8d-4452-a504-ea740c6dee4a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 72, "token_count": 12, "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "15c3001a-b325-4cb7-83d0-5de0a7ad7cb9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e28e6aca837b6eb3183fecc428f5226a9151543dc39a05c24bf1f1035644aab4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "cb2c2678-5a8d-4452-a504-ea740c6dee4a", "text": "Reinforces our overall message for CV protection."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:39a5eb5a-1656-454f-bac2-e0be64acea01", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 73, "token_count": 26, "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "fbeec6a1-735a-49eb-be27-b5d249b77024", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "8de6f00f376eb0e28b50ed3240ac2340459ce4afeb9af8ae5689e2be59498ec2", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "39a5eb5a-1656-454f-bac2-e0be64acea01", "text": "The diversity of patients shown emphasises the relevance of JARDIANCE across age groups and conditions."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ce2935a9-014d-447c-9c21-936a95b7f3b6", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 74, "token_count": 52, "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "9bd45951-5220-4abd-95c5-99f3d296a277", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "2ffb2f7abb48310713c5758fa278dd074482a163bcb65ffd83c589985907fcbf", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ce2935a9-014d-447c-9c21-936a95b7f3b6", "text": "The headline encourages HCPs to think not only about the functional benefits that JARDIANCE offers (reducing CV risk), but to also consider the emotional benefits for patients (having more moments that matter)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:777319af-91f9-4c5e-b4f7-c2bc55186ea7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 75, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 22, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d3ac3ac2-f16d-414f-841a-50b8dc7634a5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "777319af-91f9-4c5e-b4f7-c2bc55186ea7", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b49751cd-bd5c-422f-b7d8-bfb6a4259fe4", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 76, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "5b985651-f63e-4928-bce3-64086c39aae0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b49751cd-bd5c-422f-b7d8-bfb6a4259fe4", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8f9a1a45-fee2-4567-b2c2-429539306324", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 77, "token_count": 248, "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d0465fbf-e1bf-468e-a0fb-627399ac4c3a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e844453e001bc00127652ffc97aa66623c47c9bc7ee567656ba5945995b74d0f", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "8f9a1a45-fee2-4567-b2c2-429539306324", "text": "The global branding system concept, 'Layers that run deep,' proudly promotes that the further you delve into the JARDIANCE proposition, the more depth and richness you will uncover.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nThat depth and richness includes benefits beyond the physical and traditional concerns of T2D and heart failure to include renal, as well as emotional, worries.\n\nIn addition to the logo, typography, symbol, colours, and colour environment, the JARDIANCE branding system utilises visual styling, a set of illustrative, visual layers and graphic treatments to represent the boundless depth of the JARDIANCE brand offering. The JARDIANCE branding elements involve layering with purpose and simplicity and utilise the brand colours to engage with various audiences.\n\nThrough its consistent, purposeful application on and beyond the printed page, the branding system helps to draw in the audience to engage with and foster a more enduring and meaningful emotional connection with the JARDIANCE brand."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bfbd7c65-e1f8-4889-aedf-627eb02b7a13", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 78, "token_count": 111, "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "58b5f5b0-a9b6-4cd5-9631-4c9b79484464", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "283240baefe718e519dca8bf7e70842dd52d34fdcb5db2bff44444cf9419ce98", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "bfbd7c65-e1f8-4889-aedf-627eb02b7a13", "text": "-   Conveys that there are more layers to JARDIANCE than originally thought\n-   Works on multiple levels , addresses multiple problems, and is concerned about more than just the one-sided physical dysfunction of T2D, HF, and/or CKD\n-   Focusing on this idea, and going through the effort of bringing it to life beyond the printed page (ie, creating actual experiences), builds deeper and more meaningful emotional connections with our audience"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ee1f263a-6487-44e9-9676-724bbe910c6b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 79, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "b92b3403-ac52-47ac-9f62-ac40a4791166", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ee1f263a-6487-44e9-9676-724bbe910c6b", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d914bd8e-31e0-4a28-bf6b-cc8b3c687e04", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 80, "token_count": 94, "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "1694bc6e-fd61-42fd-8419-2844929a9ee2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "1a2b29836ef2fe280112415b1a0c56cbab19367ebc090fedd808472c250db80a", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d914bd8e-31e0-4a28-bf6b-cc8b3c687e04", "text": "Logotype refers to the typographic treatment given to the brand name.\n\nUse teal for the JARDIANCE logotype and brown for the generic name (empagliflozin).\n\nNever use the brand name in a possessive form (eg, 'JARDIANCE's efficacy'), and do not use the logotype in a sentence.\n\nThe JARDIANCE logotype appears in teal (PMS 321C).\n\nThe generic logotype appears in brown (PMS 411C)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:93b0c1f2-b130-4ef4-85c5-910f22abe950", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 81, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 25, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "9aa076b6-8549-4dd1-804a-b50cbac077d1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "93b0c1f2-b130-4ef4-85c5-910f22abe950", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:855732f1-a447-4ae1-8a37-468bab39638f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 82, "token_count": 23, "page_number": 25, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f8ae80d6-b292-4584-9d44-3a1a97dab716", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "884ce80db7b679fcd0efa8976c84670071bd10dc9b91e31e2cb1ba3f834aa7a3", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "855732f1-a447-4ae1-8a37-468bab39638f", "text": "The symbol is a graphic element created to embody and project a relevant aspect of the brand."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b103e863-f428-43a8-ad17-6b9731512819", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 83, "token_count": 87, "page_number": 25, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3d65fc8f-e269-48f3-93d4-3d2c12c8c556", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "94258f0316ccfd7d27b071c62ce553d067464b6b49430d09ef040fa6c61bef29", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b103e863-f428-43a8-ad17-6b9731512819", "text": "- As part of the logo cluster\n-   As a separate element that can be used promotionally to strengthen the brand's presence (this must be permitted by local legal and regulatory authorities)\n- As a representation of the brand within unbranded materials, where possible (this must be permitted by local legal and regulatory authorities)\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:025eae22-90ab-4a45-be20-23827f5524aa", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 84, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3df00768-b711-487c-bdd3-82c6d588303a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e2c4d0ee9bb4ecf3d0c7c5e0a5dfa4167f10c07c53c0735607ff840ebecba223", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "025eae22-90ab-4a45-be20-23827f5524aa", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n3\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bd615138-3521-4e1d-badd-196cba59221a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 85, "token_count": 151, "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "9d261577-0b74-4259-93c3-d08274d76938", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "1872459a769431fe18e01f0f30c5425ee592882549f2fed76a55af57b79e292a", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "bd615138-3521-4e1d-badd-196cba59221a", "text": "The layered angles and curves of the JARDIANCE symbol come together as a reminder that JARDIANCE is a brand with boundless depth and richness.\n\nThese layers, which run deep in the symbol, were the inspiration for other elements of the JARDIANCE global branding system. Therefore, the symbol serves as a true foundation that strengthens the JARDIANCE branding as a whole.\n\nOn closer examination, you can see that the flowing, curved contours sweep the sides of the symbol, giving it a smooth and inviting, organic shape. Lines converge, carving sharp angles that give the symbol a crisp, energised feeling."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0545a8af-bed0-45de-a051-ee50bb34c8e1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 86, "token_count": 68, "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "b67b0ad2-e829-4a57-ad91-784e09fa6208", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "6e1080a7cd419688eb7af988f4351dbedcba524f9dfadd78ff5a24c23091e940", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0545a8af-bed0-45de-a051-ee50bb34c8e1", "text": "-   Form the symbol and the basis for the 'Layers that run deep' global branding system\n-   Highlight the depth and richness of JARDIANCE\n- Create a sense of directed boundlessness\n-   Offer a rich palette of different shapes that are consistent in their layering technique"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:fcf97bf6-9fe1-4f52-9a7e-cc18b4aef070", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 87, "token_count": 50, "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3e6c5cf6-7cc2-4c89-8790-c10880d7901f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "cda98b2c834f25392a3c0e9d3f2ffdf497cd3646d807cd13782be0cf4b299449", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "fcf97bf6-9fe1-4f52-9a7e-cc18b4aef070", "text": "- One in yellow\n- The other in teal\n\nThe brown tint gives the elements a layered effect, which speaks to the depth of the brand and the way it adds richness to the lives of patients.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f1c83e8e-dce6-471f-95b9-f54a93357560", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 88, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 27, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "334e3c72-25a4-410c-89b2-ff1256422baa", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f1c83e8e-dce6-471f-95b9-f54a93357560", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:741d478b-8449-4f3b-80a6-6378a48c7e35", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 89, "token_count": 92, "page_number": 27, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2a7a7c09-17ed-465b-ba9f-a6a1970a53d1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "06bba72563d5fc30216ce956197940daaeb5c9f84ce5d5520a4a21741116ec5d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "741d478b-8449-4f3b-80a6-6378a48c7e35", "text": "The logo cluster brings all of the logo elements together: the logotype, colours, registration mark, symbol, and generic name (where appropriate).\n\nThe JARDIANCE logotype and registration mark appear in teal (PMS 321C).\n\nThe generic name appears in brown (PMS 411C).\n\nTo ensure brand consistency across all markets, the logo cluster must not be altered.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6c3caef0-2ede-45ed-aab8-539fbb53b679", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 90, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "fd5af3dc-37c0-4155-a10b-cd03db303e66", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "6c3caef0-2ede-45ed-aab8-539fbb53b679", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3ddedeb2-6807-4c97-9147-db90828aeba8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 91, "token_count": 116, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e5e1003e-f1ba-47e7-9743-0582ab6b81b9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "4964e2122e1b932a4d7b39ddf9a9fdd68b6ef93af2047dcc322fa004f5ab75b4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "3ddedeb2-6807-4c97-9147-db90828aeba8", "text": "If the generic name (empagliflozin) is required by regulatory authorities to appear with the brand name, then the generic name must always appear with the largest display of the JARDIANCE logo on any surface or screen and should be at least one-third the size of the logotype.\n\nAlways use brown for the generic name unless local regulations or technical requirements state otherwise. Please follow individual country guidelines regarding use of the generic name."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0dafd8af-b710-4138-a3b8-0a88f9b81768", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 92, "token_count": 200, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f2c02b8c-bf99-49af-a05d-badfccf6119a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7f3d509ee22d08b0a73c51dab96b4a0258ef30b3b3a5dfe4328004fb75e9072e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0dafd8af-b710-4138-a3b8-0a88f9b81768", "text": "The JARDIANCE logo has a registration mark that appears at the end of the brand name, showing that the brand is a registered trademark. In some countries, the registration mark is required whenever the JARDIANCE brand name appears, while in other countries it may be required only on first appearance within a document or first appearance on each new page, spread, or screen.\n\nFor internal pieces, the registration mark and generic name are not required after the first mention. For your country-specific regulations, please contact the Corporate Department, Trademarks &amp; Unfair Competition for guidance prior to use.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nThis symbol forms an important part of the logo, must appear in the size and position shown, and must be scaled up or down in proportion to the size of the logo."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:294317fe-a843-42a2-b252-cb4ef99bd4bb", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 93, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 29, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "dc52b765-43ee-441e-9219-84b5f96f47f7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e2c4d0ee9bb4ecf3d0c7c5e0a5dfa4167f10c07c53c0735607ff840ebecba223", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "294317fe-a843-42a2-b252-cb4ef99bd4bb", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n3\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e2e649db-4f8e-4601-b097-d304bdd3e764", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 94, "token_count": 281, "page_number": 29, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "28f0f5a0-5174-4204-86d8-ec6b4e529e97", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "05efe3b61d5af95b561501e5323321668f67c2e7e1fc88da9b30a61dbd3999a4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e2e649db-4f8e-4601-b097-d304bdd3e764", "text": "Be consistent! Using the JARDIANCE logo cluster correctly and consistently across all markets and communications will help establish brand recognition worldwide.\n\nJardiance Conversely, improper use will compromise our brand's integrity. Always use the approved artwork to ensure accurate reproduction of the logo cluster.\n\n(empagliflozin)\n\nJardiance The following are examples of improper usage of the JARDIANCE logo cluster:\n\n(empagliflozin)\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nJardiance\n\n(empagliflozin) Do not change the typography used in the brand name.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDo not change the position or angle of the symbol as it relates to the logo cluster.\n\nY\n\nY\n\n.\n\nY\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDo not place the logo cluster over similar colours that make the logo cluster hard to read.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDo not stretch the logo cluster disproportionately.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDo not change proportions of logo cluster elements.\n\nDo not add drop shadows to the logo cluster that make it hard to read.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDo not change the colour of the logo cluster.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nNever alter, add to, or recreate the JARDIANCE logo cluster in any way."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1ff1da85-6891-49a0-a263-de23e1046e06", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 95, "token_count": 18, "page_number": 29, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "28f0f5a0-5174-4204-86d8-ec6b4e529e97", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "2511637437a56f1af33036ac88802ef159cdd57a1d2956311f7ab50a687ae8d4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "1ff1da85-6891-49a0-a263-de23e1046e06", "text": ">\n\nNever alter, add to, or recreate the JARDIANCE logo cluster in any way."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:208b7ba3-da9a-42b6-ad55-084c573d8530", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 96, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 30, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "83ab545c-7196-44c8-b52f-f5667ba786bc", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "208b7ba3-da9a-42b6-ad55-084c573d8530", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e7a38f99-7146-4d10-acc1-300efd9bd56a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 97, "token_count": 107, "page_number": 30, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2cd78d1a-d79d-4f44-9e10-f975bd6c21d4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "96b6f65e50b3b273f7d411422b50dfe073b70ab5356b1718b296765a49f99b3f", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e7a38f99-7146-4d10-acc1-300efd9bd56a", "text": "Make the clearance space above, below, and to the sides of the logo cluster equal to the size of the 'J' in the logotype. Keep this space free of all text, photographs, rules, illustrations, graphs, and any other graphic elements. Trimmed page edges should not encroach on the clearance space.\n\nThe only elements that can slightly run into the clearance space are the generic and, when necessary, the crystallised brand promise."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:dad7ce7f-98d1-40a1-9696-bc4ed6a1ab5f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 98, "token_count": 44, "page_number": 30, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3cfbfe7c-cca3-4880-89c1-cebd80967480", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "795cc738bba257cae72f1cb41abf11cf45f4cd32f6d2bf129d28f9dd0a9f711b", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "dad7ce7f-98d1-40a1-9696-bc4ed6a1ab5f", "text": "A minimum area of clearance space has been created around the JARDIANCE logo cluster to avoid crowding the brand name and to give it maximum impact on the page.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f0690e71-e349-408e-8a16-f8e763d878a1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 99, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 31, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e5ec7c55-85de-4928-9033-023ebb8ffbb5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f0690e71-e349-408e-8a16-f8e763d878a1", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1f8a142b-0651-4a18-bd1b-f00d771921ef", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 100, "token_count": 24, "page_number": 31, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8c928918-d099-4553-9210-1125577645c1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "ee8ef6aebe559bed8ff400cf0dcdd102ec9471c61414e52d32cc49dbf05921d4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "1f8a142b-0651-4a18-bd1b-f00d771921ef", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\nTo maintain legibility, keep the logo cluster at least 1 in (25.4 mm) in width"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d4555cc0-4f68-462f-b66f-1111c4b44c30", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 101, "token_count": 112, "page_number": 31, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "9079e23c-0f8c-4ccb-ae30-2cac320adf41", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "46363fcb93ca43c415173d3cf529fd3d904510485ebf95b0f372c688ad7e4f53", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d4555cc0-4f68-462f-b66f-1111c4b44c30", "text": "The following are approved variations of the JARDIANCE logo cluster. You may use these when the background or type of a piece (eg, fax page) does not allow for the usage of the 4-colour logo.\n\nNever alter, add to, or recreate the JARDIANCE logo cluster.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n4-colour logo cluster Greyscale logo cluster The minimum width is:\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n- 1 mm for print\n- 25.4 mm for digital\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nKnockout logo cluster"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:aa7feb2d-b6d5-4ddc-8080-a54193d64ec7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 102, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 32, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "487a3942-ff2c-49a0-8f17-0203b932f28f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "aa7feb2d-b6d5-4ddc-8080-a54193d64ec7", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cd6d5b3f-bf8a-4619-bccd-a5efeefec956", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 103, "token_count": 112, "page_number": 32, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e8f35e26-cca8-418c-ba00-d2b1847beab8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "ab648bf2ed13d835346d4797f20b7f9544a0cce9965aaf72aa0b4b2c47ca5883", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "cd6d5b3f-bf8a-4619-bccd-a5efeefec956", "text": "When the Boehringer Ingelheim logo and Lilly logo appear on the same surface, for non-product branded purposes, place the former in the bottom left corner and the latter in the bottom right corner. Try to preserve as much horizontal distance as possible between them.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPreserve a clear space around both logos, equal in space, with dimensions equal to the diameter of the Boehringer Ingelheim logogram.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:93df727f-7787-433f-bd75-7903b4865a03", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 104, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 33, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "b1c282cf-f210-4bf5-98b6-1f68453de92b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "93df727f-7787-433f-bd75-7903b4865a03", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d7794f76-8f57-4bcb-bb9c-5a2fc5a4c1ef", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 105, "token_count": 148, "page_number": 33, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f30bf5f1-2131-42c2-9432-b558ce625f3c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "9480367313434813c3ceda51fadebc89a79682a98aad7b79f59488b20a776f6f", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d7794f76-8f57-4bcb-bb9c-5a2fc5a4c1ef", "text": "Typography refers to more than just the choice of font-it includes how that font is used (eg, type compositions) in the headline and throughout copy.\n\nJARDIANCE uses the Lato font, which can be found on Google Fonts. This font can be used in both print and digital tactics and has differentiated letterforms that enhance legibility.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nLato ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n1234567890(.,;:?!£$&amp;@*)\n\nAa\n\nPlease note, for PowerPoint presentations, the Arial font should be used to avoid any issues across computer platforms."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:81359d41-3c51-4779-b853-afedd343db35", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 106, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 34, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "7d559235-097a-4aad-8564-756c4d125c82", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "81359d41-3c51-4779-b853-afedd343db35", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f84a1aaf-3bad-4a95-9f93-b445cd5c24e5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 107, "token_count": 80, "page_number": 34, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "45a5dd47-78cc-4545-8be4-f313bc343972", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "09177e148eab31cadf84072f502bfa585b9181682a301380d724a19e9bcdc871", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f84a1aaf-3bad-4a95-9f93-b445cd5c24e5", "text": "Callouts should be used to emphasise a key statistic, close out a section of content, or guide the viewer to read more on the next page.\n\nCallouts should be centered text housed between 2 thin yellow rules. As needed, an icon can be incorporated that connects with the content being discussed. See specific guidance below."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9a2104c0-2bfe-482b-91f7-382e71b5ada5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 108, "token_count": 49, "page_number": 34, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f9f8b7f0-04ad-4526-ba64-286c9c0b721b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "a63aff2e1b6c1071661524517025d3406aa301e172f041da530c8c8a99ed1a4e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "9a2104c0-2bfe-482b-91f7-382e71b5ada5", "text": "Teal copy on a white background\n\n1.5-point yellow rule Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit KO copy on a teal background\n\n1.5-point yellow rule"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:44fdb45c-db23-47a5-a4bd-7c494155c13d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 109, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 35, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "db7c78eb-11f7-46d5-bbe0-67d869b555a8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "44fdb45c-db23-47a5-a4bd-7c494155c13d", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5cce2706-f79e-48ed-bc01-36019fd7cc41", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 110, "token_count": 150, "page_number": 35, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "41600d86-5631-4399-a838-4fe9f23b539c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "c9136f0c98c8761f769fa8eea733c06dcc4c38cd0860332f775cee767fdf6ad4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "5cce2706-f79e-48ed-bc01-36019fd7cc41", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n-   Use teal text for headlines and callouts on light backgrounds\n-   Use brown text for body copy, references, and footnotes\n-   Use knockout text on dark backgrounds\n-   The JARDIANCE brand name should appear in ALL CAPS\n-   For digital: always balance readability\n-   For PowerPoint: always use Arial\n-   Be mindful of the contrast between the colour used for the copy vs that used for the surrounding background\n-   Always ensure the legibility of all text\n-   All copy should be tracked at +20\n- DON'T distort the font by stretching it vertically or horizontally\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:67ccb8f0-9991-4789-bd7c-31e800e52cce", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 111, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 36, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "78f1fb00-f82b-4271-8597-f7d46ae9ff92", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e2c4d0ee9bb4ecf3d0c7c5e0a5dfa4167f10c07c53c0735607ff840ebecba223", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "67ccb8f0-9991-4789-bd7c-31e800e52cce", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n3\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:66f573da-a75f-4eab-bb95-e2e07fbeda4b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 112, "token_count": 113, "page_number": 36, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e493fe94-1f99-469f-8493-2c4e22b1bc2c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "425967236df3ed86508bddaa1a680dcba6b579c0b1373a8702fbd624a2a1588e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "66f573da-a75f-4eab-bb95-e2e07fbeda4b", "text": "The power of colour is often underestimated in branding. Different colours and different combinations of colours cause different emotional and psychologic reactions.\n\nThe JARDIANCE brand colour palette is a strong reflection of the proactive, brave, and energising personality of the brand. It uses a combination of high-contrasting colours: teal, yellow, and brown.\n\nCodes for each colour and/or gradient range are provided within each colour swatch."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b6241d90-cf85-480b-bfc0-4e2df2cab523", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 113, "token_count": 52, "page_number": 36, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2ad751bb-5508-4883-a1e7-6ab0a3021009", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "1101cfd15bd87add0d4ece04e7bf6e96b17e15aee9d5be2f98bb680fe942fa2b", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b6241d90-cf85-480b-bfc0-4e2df2cab523", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nYellow\n\nCMYK     0 / 15 / 100 / 0\n\nRGB\n\n255 / 200 / 0\n\nHEX\n\n#FFC800\n\nPMS        116C\n\nCMYK     30 / 38 / 34 / 70\n\nRGB\n\n75 / 50 / 50\n\nHEX\n\n#4B3232\n\nPMS        411C"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0c012a26-0bf1-4832-af96-7b82a67d2339", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 114, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 36, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f727028a-ef95-427b-a740-c9caa4b7154c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0c012a26-0bf1-4832-af96-7b82a67d2339", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:256608fd-704d-4350-9210-cd7f7b3963c1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 115, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "4870051f-9511-46f8-b1a9-b64f704c969a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "256608fd-704d-4350-9210-cd7f7b3963c1", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ba2ca0af-0c48-4138-861e-df2ec2d6cf8c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 116, "token_count": 120, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6c99f884-6147-4d52-90a8-108ab60d6427", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "a7b9475660f06f3376a9ab888be8eaf8dd554b400d4c888fbf1e8d7b2cae60c7", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ba2ca0af-0c48-4138-861e-df2ec2d6cf8c", "text": "The colour environment includes not just the individual colours but also the relationship or ratio between the colours within the palette. For example, 2 brands may feature blue as a primary colour, but 1 brand may saturate the page in blue while the other may feature mostly white space punctuated by minimal blue accents. Same colour, very different colour environments. This is part of what makes the brand instantly recognisable and truly differentiated from its competitors."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cf108da3-35d0-43c6-a9ae-1a8b44e94b3e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 117, "token_count": 10, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "33b9ec23-4d69-48b1-a721-fbd9dfc1cdd7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7b165b60253d73aa740155b37a1110346dfd0bed5865e632e53072d6b77824b0", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "cf108da3-35d0-43c6-a9ae-1a8b44e94b3e", "text": "you can draw the viewer into the world of"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:567003f3-c169-4647-9a04-96b426094766", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 118, "token_count": 77, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "adc0cd5f-3623-4d8d-8dde-95430221d837", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "1e2d9297321c6556efaf8c2166c2014f66ce7060dc218c684e66f3ed63f60554", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "567003f3-c169-4647-9a04-96b426094766", "text": "The JARDIANCE colour environment is inspired by the colours and proportions of the JARDIANCE symbol and creates visual continuity across all executions. The multiple layers are designed to draw the viewer into the JARDIANCE world. Generous usage of the primary colour, teal, brings instant brand recognition."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3bb63a35-00a9-4763-bf4c-ff63cbc3e4ea", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 119, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "947c74fb-dbf7-474b-b855-1943d4432e19", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "3bb63a35-00a9-4763-bf4c-ff63cbc3e4ea", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0249b55e-3b3c-4d64-b99b-cceab8a36b5a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 120, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 38, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3533a271-52af-4ded-a953-65037003bd47", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0249b55e-3b3c-4d64-b99b-cceab8a36b5a", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c9a08e3b-7f5c-48ee-be89-0a9b1f332dac", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 121, "token_count": 69, "page_number": 38, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "acfb835d-97bf-45d9-8e82-330c79132d9e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "536ff27b7530b6ffc9c572fa2269e84244fe655a93db4610daf4e09fcbe529fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c9a08e3b-7f5c-48ee-be89-0a9b1f332dac", "text": "It is important to use the brand palette whenever possible. Best practice is to apply colours at 100% strength for maximum brand recognition; however, tints and shades may be used to enhance visual impact where necessary in both print and digital applications.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8730a6bd-a729-4a70-8570-1809c0b133b1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 122, "token_count": 70, "page_number": 38, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3b09ab45-eeba-4d46-bdee-4a574aabfbae", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "2cbf776ebc1749bb6bf2f7001858a0d92066eed76b9f9b6bacbb81bd7a11e484", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "8730a6bd-a729-4a70-8570-1809c0b133b1", "text": "-   Use full 100% brand colours wherever possible for maximum consistency and recognition\n-   Apply tints and shades only when they enhance clarity, hierarchy, or visual balance\n-   Verify colour contrast meets accessibility standards in all digital applications\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bb9df6ce-cf39-4871-b46f-4b032addea8b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 123, "token_count": 68, "page_number": 38, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "b968e3b9-cd56-4b60-9314-7ee065e01a5f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "785fbacbe91d6515e1e364a134ff1f145ff3ebcb833553a0ea0f494b680c0642", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "bb9df6ce-cf39-4871-b46f-4b032addea8b", "text": "- DON'T change R/G/B or C/M/Y/K tones manually; when changing shades, please make sure to use transparency settings (for R/G/B) or tint settings (for C/M/Y/K)\n- DON'T use tints or shades in a way that reduces legibility or weakens the brand's visual impact\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1c80dfc4-10b0-4544-bc33-45625f96c778", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 124, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 39, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c5703ac3-f3bf-4468-ba5c-188e44810870", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "1c80dfc4-10b0-4544-bc33-45625f96c778", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:61746e57-cd8c-4355-8545-66ed329435a4", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 125, "token_count": 78, "page_number": 39, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0ffa8c47-f86b-4721-88cb-2c47bf438bfb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "2ac93d0de9277a034869b3b3a906f5e0b01a910333fdbd5690dd005c4dda00ef", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "61746e57-cd8c-4355-8545-66ed329435a4", "text": "The Layers of Protection element features an evolved version of the page architecture to represent a holistic focus on the 3 key components of CRM protection: cardio, renal, and metabolic. It is used to emotionalise core JARDIANCE information and highlight the types of patients who the brand is able to protect."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e3cf4de1-10da-443f-b8f7-3e0d94c031cb", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 126, "token_count": 97, "page_number": 39, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c1e1e362-b99d-461d-8082-b89d2f65f27d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "d5df87c7b3d11124f2d221b68573cee35d633808aa56db2be96edfbe66b3f71f", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e3cf4de1-10da-443f-b8f7-3e0d94c031cb", "text": "You may apply the 3 layers as a frame to house a lifestyle image or as a block of the JARDIANCE teal to highlight key data points (see examples on previous page). The 3 layers are meant to be used in conjunction with the page architecture for print pieces; however, in the iVA these elements may compete. If space is limited, the page architecture should be used instead of the 3 layers."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:78f7cd53-50f7-4d90-b4ca-c53002195e3d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 127, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 39, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "be56b749-471b-4fe4-ae8c-c0e1a14b88b4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "78f7cd53-50f7-4d90-b4ca-c53002195e3d", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3210aff1-da51-4199-9ca4-534db5b51147", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 128, "token_count": 90, "page_number": 39, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "fe085a7b-a98a-4459-8eaa-b79d7c8a820b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "b51c4f190a1512cd3016dbb22960a02466b141a21d82c2241fc7c296d1363c7c", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "3210aff1-da51-4199-9ca4-534db5b51147", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n-   All 3 layers must be shown\n-   All 3 layers must be full saturation of yellow, teal, and grey\n-   JARDIANCE data/key messages need to be a primary focus\n-   Include lifestyle imagery inside the frame when space allows\n-   Images can be scaled back to 1/4 or 1/3 of the page depending on the print schematic\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1b645b99-a409-4cc4-9d06-4c15aca1386c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 129, "token_count": 41, "page_number": 39, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "359cdcd3-3c22-465b-927b-caa76c8a4067", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "ec3fd347d5b24b772ae1ed89c914cf9f73fbdc2534b8439cc0eb79d6ec9bd982", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "1b645b99-a409-4cc4-9d06-4c15aca1386c", "text": "- DON'T change the order of the colours\n- DON'T adjust the shadows on the colours\n- DON'T adjust the ratio of colours\n- DON'T add a drop shadow to the frames\n\n·\n\n·"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2f616f85-9036-4bf0-a2d7-ba4fab727dc5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 130, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 40, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "5251f4a0-249a-4f71-9a68-0505dec0e89c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "2f616f85-9036-4bf0-a2d7-ba4fab727dc5", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:56a9dca4-628b-4cee-a0f3-f2ddd3a7910a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 131, "token_count": 143, "page_number": 40, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a3b8e037-fa73-4533-bfad-01239990e7ef", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "ff33c6be04825844392093a532be99f78372a671b7b4d0ac8b32f2f9977c3900", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "56a9dca4-628b-4cee-a0f3-f2ddd3a7910a", "text": "Page architecture is an element of visual styling that allows the audience to readily identify a brand by sight.\n\nPage architecture should draw on other branding elements, such as the symbol, to create a distinct look and feel that supports the intention of the communication.\n\nIt is important for the page architecture to demonstrate versatility and be flexible enough to work across a variety of media, including digital, print, and experiential. It should also allow for use in landscape and portrait formats for pieces as small as a postcard or as large as a billboard."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:104c2c99-738f-422f-97b1-7226e0f879e0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 132, "token_count": 74, "page_number": 40, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f5950d36-1f86-4f9f-9f08-a182b82b99b7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "bfdb7bb3cc785c96b02d57fe44b5e8010cef6c3b99ad421cb8ec763f46e12fe7", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "104c2c99-738f-422f-97b1-7226e0f879e0", "text": "As if unfolded from the JARDIANCE symbol, both in form and colour, the page architecture embodies the deep layers of the brand. Its boundless nature is also seen in the layers stepping off of the page. Regardless of the medium or layout orientation, the page architecture should always be present."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:67b52d93-ac7c-46c0-9a9b-cde18a7db5f0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 133, "token_count": 84, "page_number": 40, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c2574437-58c0-4360-a8f9-99e493ad1651", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "c1b7ca82a5da74dc3e34d5138b8e9ac7f0e955fef9dd81a3ffee4be5ecbde378", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "67b52d93-ac7c-46c0-9a9b-cde18a7db5f0", "text": "This page architecture is approved for use across all print and digital materials.\n\nThe JARDIANCE page architecture uses a layered sequence. Use a full saturation of the 3 colours: yellow, teal, and grey. The 3 colours, when grouped together, become a layer. Without this graphic trio, the page architecture is incomplete.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ab735c38-81da-4093-ae1e-39f743bf383c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 134, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 41, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "78483c4c-987d-4144-8a9f-684094cc03fd", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ab735c38-81da-4093-ae1e-39f743bf383c", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:52a4351f-3db7-4eaf-ba07-4203face17f1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 135, "token_count": 48, "page_number": 41, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2d3eff54-7709-413a-898b-cc0ff7bcb0e0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "189231639150b6306d19b45077902a1459d914e9d81c1a900bc4df52444d9788", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "52a4351f-3db7-4eaf-ba07-4203face17f1", "text": "You may apply the page architecture to any corner of the page; however, the top right is preferred. Do not alter the proportions or sizing of the page architecture as per the examples given."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4c704295-c6d0-4c16-bee2-f9ed2f572436", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 136, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 41, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2f23ed4c-dfba-4fea-b3dc-71ab6491bb63", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "4c704295-c6d0-4c16-bee2-f9ed2f572436", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8c114e19-79ed-4725-8f51-02166b92a554", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 137, "token_count": 36, "page_number": 41, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3ff99a6a-1bb3-4881-af2d-46b27478bacb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "3a2400744f1eb857bbe42308714d2738a95cc05773eed681a1907207d92e5f43", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "8c114e19-79ed-4725-8f51-02166b92a554", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n-   All 3 layers must be shown\n-   All 3 layers must be full saturation of yellow, teal, and grey\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7be298ed-c553-49f0-b764-637693a81ead", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 138, "token_count": 29, "page_number": 41, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "9de0786c-b71f-40aa-9b3b-0bf4b2e48e9d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7b2ca47e20272eb5f7d618b77c51080120581027fbb35e02bba416c4b1cda2cb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "7be298ed-c553-49f0-b764-637693a81ead", "text": "- DON'T change the order of the colours\n- DON'T adjust the shadows on the colours\n- DON'T adjust the ratio of colours"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:81ed9cb9-03fb-4c68-a056-7014be508b03", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 139, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "50c7d4c0-41dc-4fc5-869c-b0e9c2696db5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "44c212c1eeca1704afe5da842990dcc18401a63577c3e5ed56110b6a46e935ed", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "81ed9cb9-03fb-4c68-a056-7014be508b03", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n3"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b57b20d1-ce33-43d6-88ef-8c10df7c346e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 140, "token_count": 121, "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "16e8cdd0-4601-48dc-846d-fe1921cdc8d4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "a5478d26494d55676677cafd467f994c9e2ee8b6c07222639edf2eb6d707a7d7", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b57b20d1-ce33-43d6-88ef-8c10df7c346e", "text": "Target patient images have been created for each indication. For some indications, the target patient is available in three age variations: earlystage patient, mid-stage patient, and late-stage patient. Additional ethnic variations of each target patient are available and should be selected based on the needs and preferences of the local market. The target patient is always linked to a specific HCP customer and used to illustrate patient profiles and case studies.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:89e7cad7-4591-4629-be0a-339f35634176", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 141, "token_count": 76, "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "053ef8fe-31d7-4704-bb3f-d2d4dd78ab33", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "13b183c2902e103d45c674224bc4f59756e04d12cbd07a7fc80c73dccd1326e2", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "89e7cad7-4591-4629-be0a-339f35634176", "text": "-   Use the appropriate target patient for the relevant indication and HCP audience\n-   Select the correct age variation (early, mid, late) based on the scenario or data being presented when applicable\n-   Use appropriate disclaimer language as directed by MLR for AI-generated image usage\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:74c6831d-3a1a-49f6-9b76-cba9b669726a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 142, "token_count": 100, "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d2e9978e-01e8-48a9-bac0-ca6e75ccb6b5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "2dd4ae60533b4e6759918e62b6ff64f68ff7b6b642bf0fb42d0c32c9ce262ea1", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "74c6831d-3a1a-49f6-9b76-cba9b669726a", "text": "- DON'T use target patient images for unrelated concepts or outside the intended indication context\n\nJoana (Early T2D) Audience: PCP, Endo\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nErik (CKD) Audience: Neph\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nJoana (T2D + eCVD) Audience: PCP, Endo, Card\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nRobert (HFrEF) Audience: Card\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nJames (Early CKD) Audience: PCP\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nLinda (HFpEF) Audience: Card\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:19b1344b-e261-4025-9631-d37d8fa2494f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 143, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "94f97689-815c-4f44-aff7-55f543b3458c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "19b1344b-e261-4025-9631-d37d8fa2494f", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:331a7ffa-01b4-45c3-b339-4be57f270c01", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 144, "token_count": 90, "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "bcd6bb80-24a2-4ce4-a137-30829a6e6519", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "a2dc796c421ce46741bd0cc8fdd489c10e0f45c1bc20d5c76301124b481ef0e7", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "331a7ffa-01b4-45c3-b339-4be57f270c01", "text": "Each target patient has imagery captured in various lifestyle scenarios to help emotionalise and contextualise the brand story. These images can be used across different brand pieces to create a relatable and human connection to the brand narrative. Samples are included below, though the library extends beyond these samples.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8eadce73-6d71-4164-87df-98aa755898a0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 145, "token_count": 275, "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6f1a8e4b-acfd-4b2f-ae70-7c217599212e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "289926d26dad7958f89b064d738c9ff0fbc76f67a4fc746fd14d13cecf024a1d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "8eadce73-6d71-4164-87df-98aa755898a0", "text": "Images are property of Boehringer Ingelheim is subject to the following restrictions:\n\nAny third party acting on Boehringer's behalf, including but not limited to any third-party vendors, agencies, freelancer, partners or collaborators, are expressly prohibited from modifying, altering, adapting, or further processing Outputs including but not limited by using any third-party software, generative AI tools, or machine learning technologies. This includes, but is not limited to, uploading Outputs into external AI platforms, training models on content, or applying visual transformations such as symptom changes, facial edits, or environment alterations. These restrictions exist to ensure medical accuracy, character consistency, and regulatory compliance. The Outputs are to be used as final assets only and may not serve as editable base material for any further AI-driven content generation.\n\nPatient imagery shown is available for download and use on the DAM:  T2D + eCVD (Joana), CKD (Erik, James), HFpEF (Linda), HFrEF (Robert)\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:fe96a485-1c4c-4d27-b445-76c012f8c5c4", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 146, "token_count": 13, "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6f1a8e4b-acfd-4b2f-ae70-7c217599212e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "4446ade595ed80f2b7d0598ff67a072993de6b9e00f7d36c2008e23ecfd46d4d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "fe96a485-1c4c-4d27-b445-76c012f8c5c4", "text": "-->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:04c49b4f-6dce-4345-8b5d-4ae69a8754a2", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 147, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 44, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "de59ca9e-622e-4aae-9592-210d77dcc7c9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "04c49b4f-6dce-4345-8b5d-4ae69a8754a2", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:58dc3b54-b8ff-46b6-b13d-d4d1a7a1a20c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 148, "token_count": 43, "page_number": 44, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f29f17c8-0cc5-4238-be6a-213beeaeadb7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7c39f890969c71bcc3db7feef4b40811aa4802d68185f61e687117f424c4d7f5", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "58dc3b54-b8ff-46b6-b13d-d4d1a7a1a20c", "text": "If you are unable to find a suitable image from the provided image library, use the guidelines below to select a new image from stock that suits your needs.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ab3e5b7b-bb51-4435-a64c-f7624928d302", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 149, "token_count": 130, "page_number": 44, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "69d9e86a-e190-4f40-a50d-7cf70d085767", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7387c28aa4ce0325a8b0c2c6ec31767f234cb6d012b8302efcc7233e49ada88f", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ab3e5b7b-bb51-4435-a64c-f7624928d302", "text": "-   Photos should feel natural, never a forced pose\n-   Patients should be active or actively engaged\n-   Patients should be reflective of target patient\n-   Patients should be between ages 40 to 65\n-   Patients need to be overweight and not slender but should not appear to have a body mass index (BMI) that classifies them as obese per local guidelines (ie, US BMI &gt;30)\n-   Images should be in more neutral or muted colours\n-   Select photos with clean, open backgrounds without distracting elements\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:31f74532-933d-45b2-ab6e-e8f83217b175", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 150, "token_count": 62, "page_number": 44, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ffed341c-5a52-4700-9531-588f0e9822fc", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "9643c4d9b18225708fe70955b7b769c12de86267d8ca2affd258203622f547a4", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "31f74532-933d-45b2-ab6e-e8f83217b175", "text": "- DON'T select images where patients are looking directly at the camera\n- DON'T select black and white images\n- DON'T select images where the patient looks too happy or joyful\n- DON'T select images where the patient looks depressed, sad, or sickly"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:dbd54f6e-29d7-4102-afd9-0c690cedd1d1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 151, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d3e8d3ad-ed3c-4b3e-8709-175ba4837255", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e2c4d0ee9bb4ecf3d0c7c5e0a5dfa4167f10c07c53c0735607ff840ebecba223", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "dbd54f6e-29d7-4102-afd9-0c690cedd1d1", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n3\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:61728c5b-3967-4c2e-82e2-0f1b1ddb9364", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 152, "token_count": 21, "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6e9cf068-eb6e-4a0a-9ccc-2eb908fcc0f4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "fef779ff8a55ac73c5b7ffba59fdf39d22ea808f1204a649f81145865ebfaf80", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "61728c5b-3967-4c2e-82e2-0f1b1ddb9364", "text": "PCP Line graphs show how key data change over time.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d432f5e6-5532-4a8c-a2d4-4e7e29047d94", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 153, "token_count": 74, "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "669f4412-d504-47f9-a293-fab549447481", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "c0e4f5b052775cc3b09eea7e4f47582024417fa8793848b947af7bd0ad1a9201", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d432f5e6-5532-4a8c-a2d4-4e7e29047d94", "text": "-   Use full saturation of teal in lines depicting JARDIANCE\n-   Use grey in lines depicting placebo\n-   Fill the space between the two lines with a teal gradient\n-   Use teal arrow to highlight key data points\n-   Use teal for X and Y axis numbers\n-   Use brown for axis labels\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:efe38992-ebe2-41e2-a3cc-d72296899046", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 154, "token_count": 10, "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "81574332-9dd3-4511-9b31-cfc5992ebb00", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "d4240d368ccb03381522808eac3503797705d961490a18990cd4880d5f295bb0", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "efe38992-ebe2-41e2-a3cc-d72296899046", "text": "- DON'T add frame or box around the graph"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c52d95be-89e6-40e6-9fcc-6e528922cd6d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 155, "token_count": 46, "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "626c56a7-10d5-4356-ac74-e1a7d7050e68", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5d7b6bb1d52f68fb6fe7d2580a69625f693086f34c2bbd78d9435c3f46675860", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c52d95be-89e6-40e6-9fcc-6e528922cd6d", "text": "The styling for JARDIANCE charts and graphs is characterised by clean, simple data and infographics. Refer to the examples provided when visualising data for promotional communications."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4178ed3c-f29b-4973-8814-5d585f8601c7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 156, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "48170bf8-78cd-4823-81aa-d1b1c2999e0f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "4178ed3c-f29b-4973-8814-5d585f8601c7", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:92c0a512-f32e-40f6-96ba-9a5de5bb5e12", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 157, "token_count": 50, "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6baa2c4e-3af6-480d-9f78-283b85569bcb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "3ba00a184973df50857a5d030c8834b91e81672ff7ac403e38306b82db53a862", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "92c0a512-f32e-40f6-96ba-9a5de5bb5e12", "text": "Bar charts offer a clear and concise presentation of data. The use of large numbers helps communicate a key data point. The arrows signify the change in each data point.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:46954e85-3604-48c6-a6d4-f0a2e73b385e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 158, "token_count": 60, "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "1453f2d8-d14c-41ba-9e4b-d2a5b281d7c7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "4b926d7a7ee92428344a587a047c2e5661707df0f11b909ce56861c79452ebe8", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "46954e85-3604-48c6-a6d4-f0a2e73b385e", "text": "-   Ensure JARDIANCE data are in knockout type within a teal arrow\n-   Ensure placebo information is a grey stroke\n-   Use arrows as shown for the bar designs\n-   Use teal for X and Y axis numbers\n-   Use brown for axis labels\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:34a0912a-12d6-46f0-a08e-22069d37d195", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 159, "token_count": 10, "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "44efde1f-d7db-4137-a92f-709d6148d52a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "2ed3462c4a2feb0668e31791e59e5b27dbb6f91b67728bbe45617a984b4185bb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "34a0912a-12d6-46f0-a08e-22069d37d195", "text": "- DON'T add drop shadows to the arrows"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:993c5983-f0a1-4eb4-af7c-d521103ecb3b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 160, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 47, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ecdc03de-9687-47a8-b907-f6c414c8a6b3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "993c5983-f0a1-4eb4-af7c-d521103ecb3b", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ba2d6db4-06fd-44fe-94c9-5d533ef01385", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 161, "token_count": 28, "page_number": 47, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8023779f-8c01-494d-86f7-4e699c6624ba", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "933398337d58fd1bb9a1d37afe27984e9717be1d05326101b36697ad76d14b96", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ba2d6db4-06fd-44fe-94c9-5d533ef01385", "text": "Use these examples for how to incorporate brand colours into charts and tables.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:09dfd55e-3d2a-4aef-b09d-544d32e6c093", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 162, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 48, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "391fa157-2b1f-48d7-91ab-c0c45010e94f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "09dfd55e-3d2a-4aef-b09d-544d32e6c093", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:86ba94a7-9124-43ad-a5c0-8e18acac2b9e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 163, "token_count": 258, "page_number": 48, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "54a88882-5bcc-4f06-808f-78cfebd0e570", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "3a6e6db9bc6a2872816a414501a5b4b93afe473025d7c17ea3e6cecb9d0a1357", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "86ba94a7-9124-43ad-a5c0-8e18acac2b9e", "text": "Tables provide a modular approach to breaking up information in a way that draws attention to the key data. The JARDIANCE table style uses 2 different colours. One corresponds to JARDIANCE and the other corresponds to placebo.\n\n| Selected very common and common AEs (EMPA-REG OUTCOME ® trial)   | JARDIANCE (n=4687)   | Placebo (n=2333)   |\n|------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------|--------------------|\n| Hypoglycaemia †                                                  | 27.8%                | 27.9%              |\n| Urinary tract infecti ons ‡                                      | 18.0%                | 18.1%              |\n| Genital infections ‡                                             | 6.4%                 | 1.8%               |\n| Acute renal failure                                              | 5.2%                 | 6.6%               |\n| Volume depletion                                                 | 5.1%                 | 4.9%               |\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0f41d7b3-e199-47d0-9f70-cd90ad5332f6", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 164, "token_count": 58, "page_number": 48, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "876f142b-92fc-47d0-ae92-932951821984", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "8e2713cc7db14de52245438424d625ea0458d7ad6c63fc35ea2262c972b3929d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "0f41d7b3-e199-47d0-9f70-cd90ad5332f6", "text": "-   Outline entire table in teal\n-   Ensure JARDIANCE information is in knockout type within a fully saturated teal column using a white rule between rows\n-   Ensure placebo information is filled with a 5% grey column\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d6ebccad-779a-46c0-b51f-942dd7d12412", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 165, "token_count": 14, "page_number": 48, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "4ddfa53e-30c6-4dfb-bb8b-d93a074d7849", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e45328066a8e68658a4a49644430ac17f05d6cfe2b954b00bb7501603c9d25a0", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d6ebccad-779a-46c0-b51f-942dd7d12412", "text": "- DON'T use too many colours to distract from the data"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bea4b441-d9db-441d-9fb3-0a5fda4bd9e5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 166, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c7fb5bac-36c5-4850-9253-5357947468b2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "bea4b441-d9db-441d-9fb3-0a5fda4bd9e5", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:41164adb-e882-42b2-b04c-0526b2a82451", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 167, "token_count": 28, "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "80dcf354-afdc-4624-aaf1-9188ce49a211", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "b293ce8e639b72f409683b0c0365820dd8528dc364773fadac2738d3b55ac5a0", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "41164adb-e882-42b2-b04c-0526b2a82451", "text": "Pie charts allow for a simplified way to divide data, highlighting information that is important to the brand."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:20ab261f-df44-4b25-a823-3e8e7b76c7ac", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 168, "token_count": 46, "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6a870dc4-2fd5-4ea2-b980-892600313ba9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e4cd76231c9e2bc987a3d2a3d9e8d713777c4a25b0e18de7789432122843968a", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "20ab261f-df44-4b25-a823-3e8e7b76c7ac", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n-   Use teal for the primary data\n-   Use yellow and/or brown for other data\n-   Use grey for placebo or other\n- DON'T add drop shadows\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:de1b4774-6f75-415a-ad9b-4c2295d49c23", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 169, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 50, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3d02c060-5557-416c-b328-cf8eaa7375e7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "de1b4774-6f75-415a-ad9b-4c2295d49c23", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:19a8556f-4cdb-409b-9a71-7255350a1120", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 170, "token_count": 83, "page_number": 50, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "3fcb7149-391a-4fa3-86c4-55be69d59756", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "875bdcf8cd623aa0480bebc6f2adf84b2d2e28c30473fefbf567b7f15687d471", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "19a8556f-4cdb-409b-9a71-7255350a1120", "text": "Icons provide a simplified approach that can call attention to key points of information. They can be used to make information more legible when a large amount of text is required. They can be used to showcase the key information or subject of the text.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5df593a2-f044-4f38-9d4b-ee9bd320bc87", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 171, "token_count": 67, "page_number": 50, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "28d9ff37-be73-4be8-aa07-7e5e0a8ca384", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "c2e6895d7ca104f315585bb9f9c578aadb2fb6fa1c45ab2310dc206d30232626", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "5df593a2-f044-4f38-9d4b-ee9bd320bc87", "text": "-   The icons should be 3 points, grey, and scaled accordingly\n-   Each icon should have a teal dashed line following a curve\n-   Icons should be easy to interpret with limited lines inside\n- Icons can be filled or lined based on the needs of the design\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c6bd7cb0-eb2a-411c-977d-d0b03746e4b2", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 172, "token_count": 9, "page_number": 50, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "dc9e7ae9-3c32-4a8d-b7f0-5e1e3d37f98e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7a478d21bf9f66bb121ce77a91d0af457905ab51015c74ee43993a947a75cca2", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c6bd7cb0-eb2a-411c-977d-d0b03746e4b2", "text": "- DON'T add drop shadows to any icons"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:73547675-9089-4014-a5fd-0968420b4b6d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 173, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 51, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a63147b2-eab4-4d3b-b472-b0b4b492221f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "44c212c1eeca1704afe5da842990dcc18401a63577c3e5ed56110b6a46e935ed", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "73547675-9089-4014-a5fd-0968420b4b6d", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n3"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e96d9af6-41a7-4ce7-b57f-c65d5ae9fd58", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 174, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 51, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "74d73c42-9acc-499c-8dba-0f5212ed3603", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "beb8c53c2c16d8c9cc7053295465f860d2c5d02558a6e4768753a171125abe98", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e96d9af6-41a7-4ce7-b57f-c65d5ae9fd58", "text": "Here is a library of approved icons in the JARDIANCE style. The icons shown are available for download and use on the DAM .\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nheart\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nfear\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nresources\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nkidney\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nemail\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nonce daily\n\n<!-- image -->\n\npancreas\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nguilt\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nadditional information\n\n<!-- image -->\n\neGFR\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nprotect/shield\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nreassure\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nhome\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncardiologist\n\n<!-- image -->\n\narrow\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nperson/ unmet need\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nany time of day\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nnephrologist\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncheckmark/ safety/proven\n\n<!-- image -->\n\npeople\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nmedical history\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nendocrinologist\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nstop/prevent\n\n<!-- image -->\n\neasy to store &amp; administer\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nhospital\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nalbuminuria\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nreferences\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nwrong way/no benefit shown\n\n<!-- image -->\n\npill\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPI\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nsummary\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ntalk bubble\n\n<!-- image -->\n\noverweight\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncontrol/ simplify\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nsite map\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e359abbb-ac60-4568-ae98-f6fdd01caaec", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 175, "token_count": 91, "page_number": 51, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "74d73c42-9acc-499c-8dba-0f5212ed3603", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "4f48253c75e28c7925c44670d88b5601964d0453dcc0249010f83cc9e065697e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e359abbb-ac60-4568-ae98-f6fdd01caaec", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\ntalk bubble\n\n<!-- image -->\n\noverweight\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\ncontrol/ simplify\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nsite map\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nwebsite\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\npill bottle/ dosing\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nno fasting required\n\nreduced inflammation\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nhypertension\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f8511afd-b1bc-4451-a87a-c4c00ac7f06f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 176, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 52, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6c287808-59f0-478f-ba0a-c52e240e4105", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e2c4d0ee9bb4ecf3d0c7c5e0a5dfa4167f10c07c53c0735607ff840ebecba223", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f8511afd-b1bc-4451-a87a-c4c00ac7f06f", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n3\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ea1b2dd9-e135-4807-94c4-be40ae86e9f1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 177, "token_count": 10, "page_number": 52, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e91018aa-ae1a-4f23-b014-1cfd0006a806", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "a322f0f571f1fce8153424a7b801be645b96b7dd88743ac7a2780024bda76561", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ea1b2dd9-e135-4807-94c4-be40ae86e9f1", "text": "technical instructions\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:144023f4-0610-4767-8421-f57a57c4d3cf", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 178, "token_count": 83, "page_number": 52, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "10d11004-9825-4c40-9ec3-755411d9a6fe", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "f9746b88cdee515a998138e6c87b855e81a69e8d1d6afa3d9809d3135bf8c4e2", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "144023f4-0610-4767-8421-f57a57c4d3cf", "text": "-   Alternative icons may be used to increase visibility and contrast\n-   This is especially important in designs with limited space, such as the use in predefined web boxes, or if digital assets are relatively small, such as banner ads\n-   Depending on the background of the design, inverted icon designs may be used\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:06ebea4d-3004-4b34-82c9-24b00c935caf", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 179, "token_count": 120, "page_number": 52, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0d129d4c-c4ed-416f-a22f-9a85979c5b69", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "bb4e74e55b384fbe8440a9d3b235ee8f1f1edb4eccb02b7bdcc32bd0446835b9", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "06ebea4d-3004-4b34-82c9-24b00c935caf", "text": "- DON'T use filled icons for scales large enough for the primary monoline icons to be readable\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:584c9272-e69e-4c4a-b883-ea421d98c5d5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 180, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 53, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c862e05b-c0a6-48ec-8c82-50f7c973e117", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "584c9272-e69e-4c4a-b883-ea421d98c5d5", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6165d9d4-f8cd-4cb1-a467-de69555b64a6", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 181, "token_count": 38, "page_number": 53, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "23e5eccf-cb06-4ddf-8121-23a39c30be3d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "b4bf044105d70fedd58b011f888cdf021fd7259fed23408d5579bde9bee26a64", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "6165d9d4-f8cd-4cb1-a467-de69555b64a6", "text": "This graphic can be used to help visualise the interconnected nature of cardiovascular, renal, and metabolic conditions.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:805e1bb0-65ac-4c5a-856f-332a04323213", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 182, "token_count": 32, "page_number": 53, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "396791ff-f8ae-48af-ba6e-906fc32cc6eb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "855399f9dd3c5ba4c4f7130a8f537780b27cc2f19b1b2de5141c9203d59139ac", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "805e1bb0-65ac-4c5a-856f-332a04323213", "text": "-   Maintain the proportional sizing of each organ\n-   The placement of the organs can be interchanged as needed\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2b45c0e1-576a-4426-93a8-fcba3b4efaad", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 183, "token_count": 40, "page_number": 53, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e6ed863c-6fbf-4594-be86-ee0292a3d5a6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "70f1034543eba580d4805736c6277913d808f9f095e28e502ecccd7723d44aa8", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "2b45c0e1-576a-4426-93a8-fcba3b4efaad", "text": "- DON'T remove any of the organs-all 3 must be present\n- DON'T make any organ larger or smaller than the others\n- DON'T remove the circles connecting the organs"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7f392a5a-97f2-464d-968a-f14f107481b0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 184, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 54, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "1b54b9a0-752e-4647-98b5-c1fee25c18fa", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "7f392a5a-97f2-464d-968a-f14f107481b0", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b7d87497-b62d-49ba-9bf8-fdb01eecf548", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 185, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 55, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6db1ccd4-ff0d-4450-920d-68fe62c0226a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b7d87497-b62d-49ba-9bf8-fdb01eecf548", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d4e3717f-c95e-4c9d-8e7a-ef2ab99c94b3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 186, "token_count": 122, "page_number": 55, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "55037364-6034-4112-8191-e20419b48e5c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "9b0e9c7fc761666e6383d460b1e293ca09042a1d51ed38294beb1eaf577c7f31", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d4e3717f-c95e-4c9d-8e7a-ef2ab99c94b3", "text": "In the case of JARDIANCE, with its robust scientific platform, positioning guides how the new data and new brand indications will be embraced by the community in the future. By establishing a strong and aspirational positioning, we can create a distinct need for JARDIANCE in the minds of customers that, regardless of new indications or clinical data, will remain true over the long term.\n\nThe JARDIANCE positioning statement must drive everything we do and say in representing our brand."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8dbfe7f8-27df-455f-8f35-947e6223caa9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 187, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 55, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d8670ad1-1317-4479-b9c9-a5fc7af80706", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "88416e88891c2a14db25f6afd450135d6e3c14f572adb4acda46d6ddb54f927d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "8dbfe7f8-27df-455f-8f35-947e6223caa9", "text": "| Audience              | For those whose pressures in life are amplified by the physical and emotional overload and the consequences of type 2 diabetes, heart failure, and/or kidney disease   |\n|-----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Frame of reference    | JARDIANCE is the multisystem de-stressor, which                                                                                                                        |\n| Competition           | Compared to the treatments that focus on a single physical disease                                                                                                     |\n| Promise               | Rapidly restores one's sense of well-being                                                                                                                             |\n| Reasons to believe    | Because JARDIANCE works on multiple factors to rebalance the interconnected cardiac, renal, and metabolic system and increase life expectancy                          |\n| Emotional end benefit | So t"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c7209991-81db-4b33-8d11-8cb6445bbdee", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 188, "token_count": 78, "page_number": 55, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d8670ad1-1317-4479-b9c9-a5fc7af80706", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "4ae4d80620361d8f4738c2be842b709fbc3012a96428e56f8d0e01368df0314d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c7209991-81db-4b33-8d11-8cb6445bbdee", "text": "balance the interconnected cardiac, renal, and metabolic system and increase life expectancy                          |\n| Emotional end benefit | So that the pressures of disease can be exchanged for a greater command over today and for longer, more optimistic tomorrows                                           |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:203eb7f6-6c13-44c9-b2cb-a531dee726a4", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 189, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 56, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "54fa65d8-171e-4a41-9c1d-5f3d753ca666", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "203eb7f6-6c13-44c9-b2cb-a531dee726a4", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c95da2ba-09f9-48b5-b7d0-e94bb76c6b13", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 190, "token_count": 205, "page_number": 56, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e6b8a4f1-90d9-43d2-abae-f79dc54e813e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "fab53785a49106e173b5f7b8df1c006fd9850f753dace1a2d00ed83f86427018", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c95da2ba-09f9-48b5-b7d0-e94bb76c6b13", "text": "The crystallised brand promise, as its name implies, is the distillation of the JARDIANCE positioning statement into a short, memorable phrase. Indications and data have been added over the last several years to the JARDIANCE brand story. With its broadening impact and potential, JARDIANCE is also gaining complexity, making it even more important that we express what the brand stands for with complete clarity. Recent market research across stakeholders and countries has identified one key territory.\n\nThis key territory is protection . * Protection unites individual indications to form a leadership position that ensures one global execution in the minds of our prescribers. It is a legacy of protection that helps to bring together our current indications while also allowing for new data and indications to come."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3c3381a0-243a-4420-bcb6-4d173863614a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 191, "token_count": 128, "page_number": 56, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d090d756-c67b-42ff-8c5b-b13a8ba56395", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "d88410928b27c7afc4953e98a8678b3ea063f7194ee3da386abfd32da4573230", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "3c3381a0-243a-4420-bcb6-4d173863614a", "text": "*Protection does not equate to prevention.\n\n†  Never to be used externally. Please see next page.\n\nBeing at the pinnacle or top means that others look to JARDIANCE for leadership and inspiration. It means that JARDIANCE can stand on its legacy and data to confidently speak to HCPs about the benefits that come with a JARDIANCE prescription. It means that any new data and indications will help JARDIANCE stand even taller.\n\nThe crystallised brand promise is a clear and simple summation of the brand positioning."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:91bfe24e-4f11-4eaf-b594-868892a8a4d0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 192, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 57, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "5daba59e-fd88-4f74-9364-1dd32ab89f9c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "91bfe24e-4f11-4eaf-b594-868892a8a4d0", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1840a433-69dc-4871-a312-95565bd55a23", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 193, "token_count": 198, "page_number": 57, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "245357da-52a3-477c-b1fd-35a0a881d22d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "d641a4b576a4469e6b252f13c17b4581a2532123a49ec884ed3d2bee4e97d60e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "1840a433-69dc-4871-a312-95565bd55a23", "text": "The 'Pinnacle of Protection' is internal language, not to be shared with external audiences. It is also not a tagline for any of our communication materials.\n\ntagline use in external communication The JARDIANCE brand values and personality remain steadfast; however, the brand promise instills a new spirit of confidence, capturing the essence of what JARDIANCE stands for and ensuring that our customers perceive it clearly.\n\nWhile we won't use the phrase 'Pinnacle of Protection' in any external communication, it should guide us in everything we do for JARDIANCE.\n\nYou can expect key communications that will bring the brand promise to life in our new creative campaign (debuting in 2023). The spirit of the brand promise, however, goes beyond creative to embody all aspects of the brand."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a59bf47b-64aa-4b47-a286-52c4d8cef9f3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 194, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 58, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f17d2e3e-bca7-4406-babd-8531b7e1fa37", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7a762c731e2d16832aa3ebf856aa30345f3640991dafe36c25b9967256114ed9", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "a59bf47b-64aa-4b47-a286-52c4d8cef9f3", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n4"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f0b04188-0076-4ec4-b4ed-5b567af7afe8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 195, "token_count": 94, "page_number": 58, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "89a7d627-f636-45c9-aced-13601362840a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "7787a530726e141b4e8613c8d423cb25b45447fc1b878836bf9d237290d4b64b", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f0b04188-0076-4ec4-b4ed-5b567af7afe8", "text": "While branded communications about a product promote ideas and information, they also project an emotional impression or 'character' that can influence how the information is received.\n\nWhen establishing brand character, we must define what drives the brand on the inside and how it is expressed as personality on the outside-that is, how the elements relate to one another."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b7ff68ed-a9e7-4834-b928-4127772aa734", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 196, "token_count": 104, "page_number": 58, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "25366a17-2ca3-4936-8b3c-dc4491f9a254", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "afa315c94c15aaa824dd9d48860f95bf74df63527ec141cc300af0f468117190", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b7ff68ed-a9e7-4834-b928-4127772aa734", "text": "The underlying values and motivation that define a brand's reason for being .\n\nFor a brand to become truly distinctive, meaningful, and valued, it must infuse its brand character into every aspect of brand promotion and customer engagement. When the brand lives its values and purpose through authentic brand experiences, it creates strong and enduring emotional connections with the target audience.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cf7d771f-414a-47d4-93b6-30561ca3cdcf", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 197, "token_count": 143, "page_number": 58, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "dcec9675-b3b2-4832-aecd-057f15512181", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "ba56880d809f45eeeac8d9e532f1d0f06a0a018db448f616840a8e8b706f6ced", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "cf7d771f-414a-47d4-93b6-30561ca3cdcf", "text": "The permanent behaviour that never changes. Identifying DNA allows us to craft an eventual brand character that is authentic .\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nThe authentic brand character is not to be shared verbatim with external audiences, but is intended to shape all interactions related to the brand .\n\nThe brand character is defined as the set of human attributes and characteristics associated with the brand, giving it a unique persona in the market and in the mind of the customer. It comprises the following elements: brand values and purpose, DNA, archetype, and personality."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e1dd1d4e-99c8-4661-8e36-257917e7861c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 198, "token_count": 56, "page_number": 58, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ce8146bd-0a17-4f51-b752-e32f7fbf64b5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "22a9eb3f825cfe509f8b11697a1ea46c6622408dbfa59df580471af6798e032e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e1dd1d4e-99c8-4661-8e36-257917e7861c", "text": "Classic psychologic disposition that categorises how individuals will always relate to the world . Identifying the archetype helps establish the territory within which our final brand character will reside.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:013e2387-945e-4977-889b-5e6dba47186b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 199, "token_count": 38, "page_number": 58, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "4cc2af14-7f90-4d2e-8395-cfa0f9176c17", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "18f87076b4cd53991bf589d26e15c0015861132604ab2307e972de07dab22dbd", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "013e2387-945e-4977-889b-5e6dba47186b", "text": "The type of energy we bring to any situation. Identifying the personality refines and brings important nuances to the brand archetype.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b501060e-f8ba-4514-aca3-82bed00ddaad", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 200, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 59, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f48b2f73-c5c3-4d16-b6ef-5432e201bd6a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b501060e-f8ba-4514-aca3-82bed00ddaad", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e8e1315c-747e-4605-b3ac-025bd0caded3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 201, "token_count": 20, "page_number": 59, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "73fb9d42-5d8e-4b54-aa3e-b7f6a6169d0f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "dba04f0302294604cf308b1d8ac3ff92f9d6ef7778a68e07110e51ebd13a0df7", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e8e1315c-747e-4605-b3ac-025bd0caded3", "text": "Purposeful exploration led to the JARDIANCE brand character, which is shown below."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ec6e9c3e-eede-4877-9214-a014a3057bfc", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 202, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 59, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ebea268d-c241-44b3-9fe9-fb1f175b4cc2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "4d64e77c67cea5a761274b16b8e1e6919401577b287e4aa79d9fed144797a17b", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ec6e9c3e-eede-4877-9214-a014a3057bfc", "text": "Empathy Vision Courage Liberation"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6e8c6fb6-cfbe-4b88-a540-7bdc46f3e4b7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 203, "token_count": 28, "page_number": 59, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "35d5a333-628e-4bc4-ae0a-137722f37dc2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "31d2889753b0d55b3e622eb94dce9fba5d8e57b6c971fa2afcc1e519f087ef05", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "6e8c6fb6-cfbe-4b88-a540-7bdc46f3e4b7", "text": "The catalyst that revitalises and extends life\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f1260c42-754c-4b55-887b-fbe6d351c60e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 204, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 60, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a361c143-7fa9-4b00-bb16-5f20ac5d4da1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f1260c42-754c-4b55-887b-fbe6d351c60e", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3e174feb-a390-4e51-bde6-ee5c79e33eb3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 205, "token_count": 29, "page_number": 60, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a42351e8-b504-42f1-a20d-8399182654e2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "330f834d1149f713681d9efd218d488b6b0d528c54755a0c0fa00c7488f6ffb6", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "3e174feb-a390-4e51-bde6-ee5c79e33eb3", "text": "The platform, or the foundation that the brand stands on, represents the underlying values and purpose of the brand."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e3f24c3d-e475-4215-8363-dd9275bb69a7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 206, "token_count": 23, "page_number": 60, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c279b45a-19ee-4e95-ba22-383da36261e9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "30d57c27eda46d4997761333bfa303c68ba93ae3e82f951e0ffb0453a3a96011", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "e3f24c3d-e475-4215-8363-dd9275bb69a7", "text": "JARDIANCE believes that it is essential to understand another's perspective or circumstance."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a74c950e-86e7-4d4b-a17c-819f83436ecb", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 207, "token_count": 26, "page_number": 60, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "29798ae5-fd79-4f37-ab01-a47031f374bd", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "b1bcc45b6c143f54611499d3bab5667ce64f492ed1b20abe14abd1ad8121ef4e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "a74c950e-86e7-4d4b-a17c-819f83436ecb", "text": "JARDIANCE believes that it is essential to have the passion and focus to envision and affect the future."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:58a33b15-436c-4fce-b4fb-94fc8b02e7cb", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 208, "token_count": 24, "page_number": 60, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "92c44ab0-0d95-4ff7-90e2-8ce444734e42", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "a8ec3de51a30b0cdb7c5b9327ef38e99c5bde31806558a902c01921756047f7e", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "58a33b15-436c-4fce-b4fb-94fc8b02e7cb", "text": "JARDIANCE believes that it is essential to take a stand and advocate for what's best for patients."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:076e1d02-d878-41eb-ba9a-6b32e4c89eec", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 209, "token_count": 24, "page_number": 60, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "256955a2-b548-4377-9664-636ae404a753", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "8bc1c79476c093e50f2821b5f379d2c5fdf8df6906aba30f05bf3b8e3a08e5e1", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "076e1d02-d878-41eb-ba9a-6b32e4c89eec", "text": "JARDIANCE believes that when people are uplifted, free of burdens, they can live their best life."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b4212d19-6fd1-4663-87d2-2d314fed0c11", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 210, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 61, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "14f40c48-2b78-4330-add1-a82abbb37d3f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b4212d19-6fd1-4663-87d2-2d314fed0c11", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6415e55b-7016-4553-aba7-700d7c763b8e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 211, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 62, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8429f60f-65dc-48cf-9bfd-a975174b0657", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "6415e55b-7016-4553-aba7-700d7c763b8e", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b908c9dc-9c27-4427-9003-720cbdbd5edd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 212, "token_count": 77, "page_number": 62, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "99b49aba-690e-43e0-a524-e6c2be44526b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "16bf67d1f922ce5695fdbd3e003def13a01c98bb9e856b0ddac51341a276a79b", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "b908c9dc-9c27-4427-9003-720cbdbd5edd", "text": "The boundless nature of JARDIANCE comes through in multiple areas. For example, JARDIANCE is boundless in its vision, its performance, its potential, and in the possibilities it provides to its patients.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nAt its core, JARDIANCE is BOUNDLESS-defined as vast, limitless, and without boundaries."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:fcf1ee92-a1a8-41a9-8aa6-d4de813e8e66", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 213, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 63, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "15b73440-2998-4b98-99e6-3f692c00f72a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "fcf1ee92-a1a8-41a9-8aa6-d4de813e8e66", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:649143e8-e86f-4df3-a5be-6ca8ada67fc8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 214, "token_count": 92, "page_number": 63, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e6f53908-a57e-4c29-9795-d193bce41745", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "b742299f314b0419bf0701ca540f830da939f8c9e0001e34b9c21db9a941adce", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "649143e8-e86f-4df3-a5be-6ca8ada67fc8", "text": "Committed to progressing beyond what was thought possible, JARDIANCE frees others from their burdens and liberates the greatness within so they can live their best lives.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nThe JARDIANCE archetype personified 'For to be free is not merely to cast off one's chains, but to live in a way that respects and enhances the freedom of others.' -Nelson Mandela"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:48618125-e9fc-4338-a08a-d291b4ae4fcb", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 215, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 64, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a6c70ad8-d4fa-4717-8bd3-1888de017a0e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "48618125-e9fc-4338-a08a-d291b4ae4fcb", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8045c298-33da-41ff-95be-bb76506c8a13", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 216, "token_count": 35, "page_number": 64, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d1167e88-1a95-45b7-a3a8-e1cdddc99012", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "b1996d0735b11e9a3ca0288add584c0a2ee588ffdeafedf933a5d63586736449", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "8045c298-33da-41ff-95be-bb76506c8a13", "text": "JARDIANCE is focused on achieving the best possible future .\n\nIt is not: Aggressive, short-sighted, focused on instant wins, inconsiderate."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2ca77ce8-ffcb-4ab7-b029-41a47e9e74ed", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 217, "token_count": 35, "page_number": 64, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "102aa704-d839-4b37-80b8-ab59cc73e9b6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "2259987937aef37bcf594b95e80f07bfac37f83f423e2683da65b22786d45d0f", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "2ca77ce8-ffcb-4ab7-b029-41a47e9e74ed", "text": "JARDIANCE takes a stand for a noble cause .\n\nIt is not: Impulsive, daring, a risk-taker that does not consider the consequences, audacious."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:69bf6055-bea5-4777-a112-5ab9111393d5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 218, "token_count": 29, "page_number": 64, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "840284b0-f18b-44f8-9ad2-24fe8f6392b5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "4973c1d633a20cfdbfc5d4cef4652dbffb80da2ec99b5c94caa5b3ec8d1df310", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "69bf6055-bea5-4777-a112-5ab9111393d5", "text": "JARDIANCE is the catalyst that empowers people to live in the moment.\n\nIt is not:\n\nFrenetic, excessive, exhausting."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ab90948a-916b-4db0-8c0e-f4944e9ad240", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 219, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 65, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "86b457aa-4f10-4b2f-93b6-22fbf37dc7d7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ab90948a-916b-4db0-8c0e-f4944e9ad240", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:06aa42bd-639c-42cd-8439-babaf800b011", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 220, "token_count": 89, "page_number": 65, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8e575eb3-68c5-4fe2-9786-5cb2480351e3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "9706153455a3c10fb9fdb6efe68591389cdbd532acb8da7d66d5ea147bf2060b", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "06aa42bd-639c-42cd-8439-babaf800b011", "text": "JARDIANCE speaks to its readers/listeners much like a motivational coach who cares about his or her outcomes. JARDIANCE is not overly aggressive-it\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nis brave and energising and confident. The overall tone is optimistic and proactive, as JARDIANCE can deliver liberation to both patients and physicians-now and in the future.\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bcb3b421-23d6-41d1-9101-20b3db01d55e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 221, "token_count": 183, "page_number": 65, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c0ef518e-9d29-4fc5-bc8a-dc151bdb3e8a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "11773d844220ddad1aa0d5b958a35ec5c987781daa6c97f810fede20869e729f", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "bcb3b421-23d6-41d1-9101-20b3db01d55e", "text": "Consider the following when developing content:\n\n-   Convey a sense of empathy with the challenges that HCPs and patients face when treating/managing the disease\n-   Infuse headlines, callouts, and lead-ins with energy; use upbeat and positive language\n- Speak with confidence and assuredness\n-   When possible, use present and future tenses. (Note, in the EU, use past tense for all CV claims ['JARDIANCE demonstrated' vs 'JARDIANCE demonstrates']. Similarly, for safety statements in either the EU or Mexico, only past tense is acceptable.)\n-   Speak directly to the reader (when appropriate), as in 'you' and 'your'\n-   Start sentences or paragraphs with verbs (eg, 'Give,' 'Choose,' 'Ask') to encourage the reader to take action"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:47663600-aa5d-429c-83ff-bcc03a257c6d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 222, "token_count": 8, "page_number": 66, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "08533a7d-141d-47d5-b1ba-9f75633263d3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "5a7784a711e89a32919aefc7993fb951126abe87dd147da00664bdd965c27d72", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "47663600-aa5d-429c-83ff-bcc03a257c6d", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:98c74cff-d91e-4bcc-96d5-9419e606b290", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 223, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 67, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d38e756b-a4f6-4937-9bc4-c5da3e08c8b3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "98c74cff-d91e-4bcc-96d5-9419e606b290", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ad8a6e97-fe65-4803-88da-8af832ce383d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 224, "token_count": 284, "page_number": 67, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "66ad13f4-f620-4999-8bdd-31026196938b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "f31741489c33a4389884ca54fd418f7ee6416c9fda04878782192f316e26fd41", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ad8a6e97-fe65-4803-88da-8af832ce383d", "text": "The global branding system applies to the 'JARDIANCE family' in a way that visually depicts the relationship between the Boehringer Ingelheim/Lilly Alliance and among its related product brands in the Diabetes Portfolio.\n\nThere are 3 products that comprise the JARDIANCE family, with JARDIANCE being the lead brand and SYNJARDY and GLYXAMBI as line extensions:\n\n- JARDIANCE ®  (empagliflozin)\n- SYNJARDY ®  (empagliflozin/metformin HCl)\n- GLYXAMBI ®  (empagliflozin/linagliptin)\n\nThis section highlights the specific JARDIANCE family branding elements, explains the rationale behind them, and provides detailed instructions for approved use to ensure consistency throughout all communications.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nKeep in mind that when any of the family brands are used in combination with JARDIANCE, the JARDIANCE branding elements (eg, colour, environment, page architecture) must be adhered to.\n\nImportant: please note that the Boehringer Ingelheim/Lilly Alliance is not currently pursuing future heart failure or chronic kidney disease indications for SYNJARDY or GLYXAMBI. There are no updates to design or branding on family brands."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c4a9d2dc-34e9-431d-aa4d-cf3a1be2ad3b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 225, "token_count": 22, "page_number": 67, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "66ad13f4-f620-4999-8bdd-31026196938b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "669d8d61b196a40fcd37a5dd0696d3ac2c27193aa641933a131469197b47095a", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c4a9d2dc-34e9-431d-aa4d-cf3a1be2ad3b", "text": "for SYNJARDY or GLYXAMBI. There are no updates to design or branding on family brands."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d25c5541-12b9-4248-a8da-0abf4592a4c5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 226, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 68, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "7106f6b6-40cc-4792-900f-82075459ac19", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d25c5541-12b9-4248-a8da-0abf4592a4c5", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f601c141-1cf8-499d-a2ed-2ead2db5365f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 227, "token_count": 98, "page_number": 68, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ec4f8dab-dac2-4b4e-a97d-40f48d95209d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "8ed211cb8b5fe0e59b3561682933b62a673247016d6694363093ef884fb22a58", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "f601c141-1cf8-499d-a2ed-2ead2db5365f", "text": "There are times when JARDIANCE will appear with SYNJARDY and/or GLYXAMBI in promotion. The rules for these combinations can be found on the following pages. Be sure to follow the rules to ensure consistent branding, whenever and wherever any combination of family brands is used.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ade75541-6091-4d69-9b4f-724a9dacec0b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 228, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 69, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "42fa75c7-69a3-4b2f-954e-4ef6c9bd15ec", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ade75541-6091-4d69-9b4f-724a9dacec0b", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8132c47c-6c48-48b4-a8af-8216bbf09efb", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 229, "token_count": 46, "page_number": 69, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "1c3ee0fb-f8de-48ef-ae21-f81979bdf77c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "3a92ede85892229e39c9880f4b046707df45966db4b46457ebb80e1d04cbffb5", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "8132c47c-6c48-48b4-a8af-8216bbf09efb", "text": "The symbol is a graphic element created to embody and project a relevant aspect of the brand.\n\nThe SYNJARDY symbol mirrors that of JARDIANCE in its curves, angles, and boundless depth."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:070f8e3d-02c3-44b6-a480-d3e5b3da082a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 230, "token_count": 92, "page_number": 69, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ff695f3f-efef-4840-931d-063e50b8758a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "af68d681767a3a6595c92a357c393d57b0f7e30773801b0cf436466b6a98a5e7", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "070f8e3d-02c3-44b6-a480-d3e5b3da082a", "text": "- One in orange\n- The other in teal\n\nThe brown tint gives the elements a layered effect.\n\nFor more information about the 'Layers that run deep' global branding system, please see page 20.\n\nThe SYNJARDY symbol\n\nOrange PMS 716C C0/M65/Y100/K0 R244/G121/B32 #EC7700\n\nBrown PMS 411C C30/M38/Y34/K70 R75/G50/B50 #4B3232\n\nTeal PMS 321C C100/M0/Y45/K10 R0/G140/B125 #008C7D"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c0a091e4-b619-4947-a5dd-95f0f5ee8570", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 231, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 70, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a44d8401-57ec-458e-b025-ce3fcd945818", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c0a091e4-b619-4947-a5dd-95f0f5ee8570", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:017c0d5a-32f1-48e6-ab8b-585ebc842097", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 232, "token_count": 112, "page_number": 70, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2398bee7-e1c2-4077-9d41-be35bd678f41", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "cf577036e5d3be2727bc8b59be5cf348f67648e6a59e4c52a6bcf7b4957f2875", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "017c0d5a-32f1-48e6-ab8b-585ebc842097", "text": "The logo cluster brings all of the logo elements together: the logotype, colours, registration mark, symbol, and generic name (where appropriate).\n\nThe SYNJARDY logotype and registration mark appear in teal (PMS 321C).\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nThe generic name appears in brown (PMS 411C).\n\nTo ensure brand consistency across all markets, the logo cluster must not be altered.\n\nThe symbol appears in brown (PMS 411C), teal (PMS 321C), and orange (PMS 716C)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d56fcfaa-d106-42ff-b5dc-f85f31dc2fed", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 233, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 71, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "47834069-cbaf-4f79-a179-9115a2302621", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "d56fcfaa-d106-42ff-b5dc-f85f31dc2fed", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ef886443-6059-40b9-b38d-c68c68acb7fc", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 234, "token_count": 46, "page_number": 71, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d0a2a239-eb28-4f04-a9b4-c4e3973aa168", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "cfd035483a1479e9fbf5bff5a502742844a6ef445ff9d870e9c2e3b0d853de40", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ef886443-6059-40b9-b38d-c68c68acb7fc", "text": "The symbol is a graphic element created to embody and project a relevant aspect of the brand.\n\nThe GLYXAMBI symbol mirrors that of JARDIANCE in its curves, angles, and boundless depth."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ef50e7bf-6449-4001-8a99-3816f648c265", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 235, "token_count": 92, "page_number": 71, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c45f07c7-991a-4870-ab79-e52563919c13", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "83cd8bc21437da6a961776ce26c3b391543cfaa10c9f37afa504d980c677ef28", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "ef50e7bf-6449-4001-8a99-3816f648c265", "text": "- One in magenta\n- The other in teal\n\nThe brown tint gives the elements a layered effect.\n\nFor more information about the 'Layers that run deep' global branding system, please see page 20.\n\nThe GLYXAMBI symbol\n\nMagenta PMS 219C C6/M98/Y9/K0 R218/G24/B132 #DF1683\n\nBrown PMS 411C C30/M38/Y34/K70 R75/G50/B50 #4B3232\n\nTeal PMS 321C C100/M0/Y45/K10 R0/G140/B125 #008C7D"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c1261247-fbf0-415c-bad4-1189fa6b955a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 236, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 72, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8f61659e-1123-4c02-b178-86888827daea", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e5dc819883d3c4b39a4a3f3054652d05bbceb23ae07f1d5f396b3cb309cce5fb", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "c1261247-fbf0-415c-bad4-1189fa6b955a", "text": "<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9d4caa77-4700-4944-9985-74edb32c9363", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 237, "token_count": 36, "page_number": 72, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0374e466-7e86-4b2c-8961-83cf257fbf37", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e3a5a9deb69086e7c832f2620f47445f361452ff82427916538d62ac2fa1796d", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "9d4caa77-4700-4944-9985-74edb32c9363", "text": "The logo cluster brings all of the logo elements together: the logotype, colours, registration mark, symbol, and generic name (where appropriate)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7d699827-c59f-4722-b27d-33f11dc93a4c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 238, "token_count": 130, "page_number": 72, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "6d3bb492-5b07-4826-b05f-8c84ee9c8716", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "e4f1724d88846ced107372db57cdcacbd111a2c0e9212ab75b198789a2924fd3", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "7d699827-c59f-4722-b27d-33f11dc93a4c", "text": "The crystallised brand promise is a fixed branding element. Even if the wording of the crystallised brand promise changes (eg, due to a change in positioning), where it is placed in the logo cluster does not change.\n\nThe GLYXAMBI logotype and registration mark appear in teal (PMS 321C).\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nThe symbol appears in brown (PMS 411C), teal (PMS 321C), and magenta (PMS 219C).\n\nThe generic name appears in brown (PMS 411C).\n\nTo ensure brand consistency across all markets, the logo cluster must not be altered."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:404b9d05-4eb0-4dab-a5a1-06944e8a586c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 239, "token_count": 16, "page_number": 73, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "9a93e808-dea2-4d9f-b8f9-af69d954f492", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_hash": "817608aeb4472447eb5365837c82d0060bda320da2f217eeb9db8824a4da7d19", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "chunk_id": "404b9d05-4eb0-4dab-a5a1-06944e8a586c", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:89fb7807-c3a9-49a3-9f6e-b84612ef12a1", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 0, "token_count": 57, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "02c3962f-9738-4add-a977-b0e43fdc0272", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "484e9cf8b671eab158a8638ad566dcff6531ec46a52f82039f0aa81735bd8c8c", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "89fb7807-c3a9-49a3-9f6e-b84612ef12a1", "text": "These highlights do not include all the information needed to use JARDIANCE safely and effectively. See full prescribing information for JARDIANCE.\n\nJARDIANCE ®  (empagliflozin tablets), for oral use\n\nInitial U.S. Approval: 2014"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e7a90319-7bf3-4681-a4a9-240d933939e7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 1, "token_count": 10, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7ef8c3e1-ee2d-467d-84af-eeda2efb8f1a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "9b659b51af0e97ef99193d02b2f49780812ceb4f83831ea7b33c7ec62e99d43b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "e7a90319-7bf3-4681-a4a9-240d933939e7", "text": "Warnings and Precautions (5.3)\n\n10/2025"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:43d75440-26d7-48ab-a764-a63f48d7f763", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 2, "token_count": 168, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "a0d22c6f-3704-402a-8bef-b0039f4472c1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "9db5d7e24b4c9a6702a4a231a536aab6dba52558c0e4867ec08a1b47f5081dbb", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "43d75440-26d7-48ab-a764-a63f48d7f763", "text": "JARDIANCE is a sodium-glucose co-transporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitor indicated:\n\n- x To reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization for heart failure in adults with heart failure. (1)\n- x To reduce the risk of sustained decline in eGFR, end-stage kidney disease, cardiovascular death, and hospitalization in adults with chronic kidney disease at risk of progression. (1)\n- x To reduce the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus and established cardiovascular disease. (1)\n- x As an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults and pediatric patients aged 10 years and older with type 2 diabetes mellitus. (1)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3d4d4ba7-5408-46a5-b8d0-7288c4678397", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 3, "token_count": 162, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ad7eaca9-7cd2-4fa9-b9c1-052b1adb8aad", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "65021344e398032c251fe213a03a2fad5dbe6e21150d9df089500db98cf516aa", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "3d4d4ba7-5408-46a5-b8d0-7288c4678397", "text": "- x Not recommended for use to improve glycemic control in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus. It may increase the risk of diabetic ketoacidosis in these patients. (1)\n- x Not recommended for use to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus with an eGFR less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . (1)\n- x Not recommended for the treatment of chronic kidney disease in patients with polycystic kidney disease or patients requiring or with a recent history of intravenous immunosuppressive therapy or greater than 45 mg of prednisone or equivalent for kidney disease. JARDIANCE is not expected to be effective in these populations. (1)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:56fffa3c-98e0-400c-bdbc-5c561bf0827d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 4, "token_count": 146, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "862c2857-c3db-4b79-917f-521b8ba93688", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5a564b5441ad745e27ad8fe51ddd969d3d5177a934df6c6635d706ffb118c546", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "56fffa3c-98e0-400c-bdbc-5c561bf0827d", "text": "- x Assess renal function before initiating and as clinically indicated. Assess volume status and correct volume depletion before initiating. (2.1)\n- x Recommended dosage is 10 mg orally once daily in the morning, taken with or without food. (2.2)\n- x For additional glycemic control, dosage may be increased to 25 mg orally once daily in patients tolerating JARDIANCE. (2.2)\n- x Withhold JARDIANCE for at least 3 days, if possible, prior to surgery or procedures associated with prolonged fasting. (2.3)\n- x Hypersensitivity to empagliflozin or any of the excipients in JARDIANCE. (4)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ed6ed1f7-a4d2-4e42-be55-d476232e38df", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 5, "token_count": 6, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "f2361244-a5ac-459c-a1aa-f6622f08fb34", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "d46bf74f1c08fb07cb6bffd055125069829c39e0e5b7b756b7d97361298c2892", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "ed6ed1f7-a4d2-4e42-be55-d476232e38df", "text": "Tablets: 10 mg, 25 mg (3)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:496aac05-7d08-4479-8c2c-01d2b073358e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 6, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "034c5600-3a9e-4f0e-86d6-8db16ed2a246", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4c3a64c3dce7916c29757efe7fc2d8c86862a7a2dce419bb9069783638a1d52c", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "496aac05-7d08-4479-8c2c-01d2b073358e", "text": "- x Diabetic Ketoacidosis in Patients with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus and Other Ketoacidosis: Consider ketone monitoring in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus and consider ketone monitoring in others at risk for ketoacidosis, as indicated. Assess for ketoacidosis regardless of presenting blood glucose levels and discontinue JARDIANCE if ketoacidosis is suspected. Monitor patients for resolution of ketoacidosis before restarting. (5.1)\n- x Volume Depletion: Before initiating JARDIANCE, assess volume status and renal function in patients with impaired renal function, elderly patients, or patients on loop diuretics. Monitor for signs and symptoms during therapy. (5.2)\n- x Genitourinary Infections, including Urosepsis, Pyelonephritis, Necrotizing Fasciitis of the Perineum (Fournier's Gangrene), and Genital Mycotic Infections: Monitor patients for signs and symptoms of genitourinary infections and treat promptly, if indicated. Immediately evaluate patients presenting with pain or tenderness, erythema, or swelling in the genital or perineal area, along with fever or malaise, for necrotizing fasciitis and if suspected, discontinue JARDIANCE, and promptly institute appropriate medical an"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:fcac7e84-1c72-4ca1-8547-dda6b0d78b8e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 7, "token_count": 229, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "034c5600-3a9e-4f0e-86d6-8db16ed2a246", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "e5f7b72e5e9220cdcd707ba1235323545f7ddf536c0c897ef131a77a56907acf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "fcac7e84-1c72-4ca1-8547-dda6b0d78b8e", "text": "al area, along with fever or malaise, for necrotizing fasciitis and if suspected, discontinue JARDIANCE, and promptly institute appropriate medical and/or surgical intervention. (5.3)\n- x Hypoglycemia: Adult patients taking an insulin secretagogue or insulin may have an increased risk of hypoglycemia. In pediatric patients 10 years of age and older, the risk of hypoglycemia was higher regardless of insulin use. Consider lowering the dosage of insulin secretagogue or insulin to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia when initiating JARDIANCE. (5.4)\n- x Lower Limb Amputation: Monitor patients for infections or ulcers of lower limbs, and institute appropriate treatment (5.5)\n- x Hypersensitivity Reactions: Serious hypersensitivity reactions (e.g., angioedema) have occurred with JARDIANCE. If hypersensitivity reactions occur, discontinue JARDIANCE, treat promptly, and monitor until signs and symptoms resolve. (5.6)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:18ec6c4a-2f9c-44a4-8fc2-75b6079c6d89", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 8, "token_count": 72, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "8464457d-e8da-4e8c-8d69-4e56ccc126e7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "d515a354290c132229195234747d85ae07aa55fe10c32ef67bdffa8e831ede3e", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "18ec6c4a-2f9c-44a4-8fc2-75b6079c6d89", "text": "Most common adverse reactions (5% or greater incidence) were urinary tract infections and female genital mycotic infections (6.1)\n\nTo report SUSPECTED ADVERSE REACTIONS, contact Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc. at 1-800-542-6257 or FDA at 1-800-FDA1088 or www.fda.gov/medwatch ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9c282d22-5027-4295-b9a5-93eb4a82d330", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 9, "token_count": 32, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "1dc1786d-68b0-486f-a2a6-f4a38d5d6614", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "bd46b1f917e3f4f3d00b6a53a9a4623100969325ee70f8b63a6d3d5aec6c444d", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9c282d22-5027-4295-b9a5-93eb4a82d330", "text": "See full prescribing information for information on drug interactions and interference of JARDIANCE with laboratory tests. (7)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4daea3ae-f32d-4d2e-bdc7-94b75471673f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 10, "token_count": 189, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "19829346-10c0-4e65-a3e2-d5e9a3651c59", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4780278d1e3444829727100456b31070393ab0df9159933bd28e0c868f5d2fda", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "4daea3ae-f32d-4d2e-bdc7-94b75471673f", "text": "- x Pregnancy: Advise females of the potential risk to a fetus especially during the second and third trimesters. (8.1)\n- x Lactation: Not recommended when breastfeeding. (8.2)\n- x Geriatric Patients: Higher incidence of adverse reactions related to volume depletion and reduced renal function. (8.5)\n- x Renal Impairment: Higher incidence of adverse reactions related to reduced renal function. (8.6)\n\nSee 17 for PATIENT COUNSELING INFORMATION and Medication Guide.\n\nRevised: 10/2025\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c4e281f1-0d69-426b-b686-7394ac7a4187", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 11, "token_count": 256, "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "8c5d072c-f908-46a8-93f3-c6c1ba26784c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "2661775476db17a40091dec51f2c17cbf4d1f05f2448ce6cf8ee398de6f9b58d", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c4e281f1-0d69-426b-b686-7394ac7a4187", "text": "- 1 INDICATIONS AND USAGE 2 DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION\n- 2.1 Testing Prior to Initiation of JARDIANCE\n- 2.2 Recommended Dosage\n- 2.3 Temporary Interruption for Surgery\n- 2.4 Recommendations Regarding Missed Dose\n- 3 DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS\n- 4 CONTRAINDICATIONS\n- 5 WARNINGS AND PRECAUTIONS\n- 5.1 Diabetic Ketoacidosis in Patients with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus and Other Ketoacidosis\n- 5.2 Volume Depletion\n- 5.3 Genitourinary Infections, including Urosepsis, Pyelonephritis, Necrotizing Fasciitis of the Perineum (Fournier's Gangrene), and Genital Mycotic Infections\n- 5.4 Hypoglycemia\n- 5.5 Lower Limb Amputation\n- 5.6 Hypersensitivity Reactions\n- 6 ADVERSE REACTIONS\n- 6.1 Clinical Trials Experience\n- 6.2 Postmarketing Experience\n- 7 DRUG INTERACTIONS\n- 8 USE IN SPECIFIC POPULATIONS\n- 8.1 Pregnancy\n- 8.2 Lactation\n- 8.4 Pediatric Use\n- 8.5 Geriatric Use\n- 8.6 Renal Impairment\n- 8.7 Hepatic Impairment\n- 10  OVERDOSAGE\n- 11  DESCRIPTION\n- 12  CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY\n- 12.1  Mechanism of Action\n- 12.2  Pharmacodynamics"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:08c35ba8-5473-43ad-93fe-a0cc584ecc5e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 12, "token_count": 6, "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "e94afe23-beb0-419c-8575-4d771a622513", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "9e2e82a5c7c3f91d7a0e9cad1a5e0de8ac200ebd62d6cdb29e0b3ab08ba34750", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "08c35ba8-5473-43ad-93fe-a0cc584ecc5e", "text": "- 12.3  Pharmacokinetics"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3f1bc58f-a500-48bf-9c6b-100dbf832c79", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 13, "token_count": 14, "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "315b14f9-ba31-4d13-a3db-66d444ce9941", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "6ab60df0b87382b54f31286acf021bdd35d18923f31fdd601b80e5f51e07de11", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "3f1bc58f-a500-48bf-9c6b-100dbf832c79", "text": "13.1  Carcinogenesis, Mutagenesis, Impairment of Fertility"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:76e0637d-ce88-4e66-a495-d2679265006b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 14, "token_count": 93, "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "4d733750-7e16-4e6b-98e8-7d1bf61c04c5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4ac79d5ccd665a1a500672be31575b5fe8813b955fc090c286bd96d762e0b5d8", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "76e0637d-ce88-4e66-a495-d2679265006b", "text": "- 14.1  Glycemic Control Trials in Adults with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus\n- 14.2  Glycemic Control Trial in Pediatric Patients Aged 10 to 17 Years with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus\n- 14.3  Cardiovascular Outcomes in Adults with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus and Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease\n\n14.4  Heart Failure Trials in Adults 14.5  Chronic Kidney Disease Trial in Adults"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:61fc90cc-b9c9-4060-ac61-8c7c0ea061b5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 15, "token_count": 22, "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0ec1ad5d-a957-4023-af8b-3cc921b80879", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "44d87ba7136940aa1956aeabde14a6fc0cf965005c7480dcde566cc9d1171d76", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "61fc90cc-b9c9-4060-ac61-8c7c0ea061b5", "text": "*Sections or subsections omitted from the full prescribing information are not listed."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2e4dca44-c5e0-4293-bcc1-8a5001b28f16", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 16, "token_count": 151, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "693bc5c6-125b-45bc-9c4e-b4e86296cb08", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ccdb11a0608151442c647cd887f243b819abf1b42afcd95aad8606a8435cab34", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "2e4dca44-c5e0-4293-bcc1-8a5001b28f16", "text": "JARDIANCE is indicated:\n\n- x to reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization for heart failure in adults with heart failure.\n- x to reduce the risk of sustained decline in eGFR, end-stage kidney disease, cardiovascular death, and hospitalization in adults with chronic kidney disease at risk of progression.\n- x to reduce the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus and established cardiovascular disease.\n- x as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults and pediatric patients aged 10 years and older with type 2 diabetes mellitus."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:82c4ec56-1c87-4610-a589-2558d866e1a0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 17, "token_count": 206, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "96018e41-ad7d-4129-90a4-0c35970ce596", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "0f9c04c7edf70471aab0e90e72f39de085b261ebebb45403e878888c5c7243e1", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "82c4ec56-1c87-4610-a589-2558d866e1a0", "text": "JARDIANCE is not recommended for use to improve glycemic control in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus. It may increase the risk of diabetic ketoacidosis in these patients [see Warnings and Precautions (5.1)] .\n\nJARDIANCE is not recommended for use to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus with an eGFR less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . JARDIANCE is likely to be ineffective in this setting based upon its mechanism of action.\n\nJARDIANCE is not recommended for the treatment of chronic kidney disease in patients with polycystic kidney disease or patients requiring or with a recent history of intravenous immunosuppressive therapy or greater than 45 mg of prednisone or equivalent for kidney disease [see Clinical Studies (14.5)] . JARDIANCE is not expected to be effective in these populations."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:65163356-fd66-4b21-847a-4307a1d85063", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 18, "token_count": 114, "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "51566a18-af1a-44d5-b28a-49d8a48ee4ce", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "2d565e62e24227688d3b23ccfff474b43b7f481d178d1225f9d81a540275688d", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "65163356-fd66-4b21-847a-4307a1d85063", "text": "- x Assess renal function before initiating JARDIANCE and as clinically indicated [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2)] .\n- o Use for glycemic control is not recommended in patients with an eGFR less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 [see Use in Specific Populations (8.6)].\n- x Assess volume status. In patients with volume depletion, correct this condition before initiating JARDIANCE [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2) and Use in Specific Populations (8.5, 8.6)]."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c258064d-2a38-4165-a155-7ddc1bccff31", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 19, "token_count": 279, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "745496c7-b701-428d-9f4f-0f37977b02e0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "8375002c8498dcb3e33a79a45b947de61b63cfb6f0f88fc375c2da2770e138ab", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c258064d-2a38-4165-a155-7ddc1bccff31", "text": "Table 1 presents the recommended dosage of JARDIANCE in adult and pediatric patients aged 10 years and older.\n\nTable 1 Recommended Dosage of JARDIANCE\n\n| Population                                 | Indication                                                                                                                                                                      | Recommended Dosage                                                                                                                                                                        |\n|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Adults                                     | Reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization in patients with heart failure"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:61999922-0fc7-45af-9338-fcc0efafcaf3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 20, "token_count": 294, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "745496c7-b701-428d-9f4f-0f37977b02e0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "28d8a328ce15004f6a3d434d4dce54b7b65ce27ad7bbbb2bc1b7c327cf777790", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "61999922-0fc7-45af-9338-fcc0efafcaf3", "text": "vascular death and hospitalization in patients with heart failure                                                                                      | x 10 mg orally once daily in the morning, taken with or without food.                                                                                                                     |\n| Adults                                     | Reduce the risk of sustained decline in eGFR, end-stage kidney disease, cardiovascular death, and hospitalization in adults with chronic kidney disease at risk of progression. | x 10 mg orally once daily in the morning, taken with or without food.                                                                                                                     |\n| Adults                                     | Reduce the risk of cardiovascular death in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus with established cardiovascular disease                                                       | x 10 mg orally once daily in the morning, taken with or without food.                                                                                                                     |\n| Adults"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:58ecb058-28ca-4c15-b734-3e221a045268", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 21, "token_count": 207, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "745496c7-b701-428d-9f4f-0f37977b02e0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a5143ea53c2cb40146a98a8d9cbe3a53207fc05b7ade418af04939647417c030", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "58ecb058-28ca-4c15-b734-3e221a045268", "text": "|\n| Adults                                     | Glycemic control in type 2 diabetes mellitus                                                                                                                                    | x 10 mg orally once daily in the morning, taken with or without food. x For additional glycemic control, may increase to 25 mg orally once daily in patients tolerating 10 mg once daily. |\n| Pediatric patients aged 10 years and older | Glycemic control in type 2 diabetes mellitus                                                                                                                                    | x 10 mg orally once daily in the morning, taken with or without food. x For additional glycemic control, may increase to 25 mg orally once daily in patients tolerating 10 mg once daily. |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7bdd7608-06dd-413d-adc6-5ac27af57857", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 22, "token_count": 68, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7c84e31b-6757-4523-aaf1-dffa3dce95f2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4dac55cfc3f723bd32b0190fdf1dc5b0f1bd5a55b08b2c99b507f13af1695d6f", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "7bdd7608-06dd-413d-adc6-5ac27af57857", "text": "Withhold JARDIANCE for at least 3 days, if possible, prior to surgery or procedures associated with prolonged fasting. Resume JARDIANCE when the patient is clinically stable and has resumed oral intake [see Warnings and Precautions (5.1) and Clinical Pharmacology (12.2)]."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ca8fc8a4-2e0a-456f-9e18-390521ca250b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 23, "token_count": 33, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "646166ce-5057-48b0-a078-5a371ab2c82e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "58bbf701979b65af2b642aeba63347d5d14822820551e1322203d651f579b5cc", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "ca8fc8a4-2e0a-456f-9e18-390521ca250b", "text": "- x If a dose is missed, instruct patients to take the dose as soon as possible.\n- x Advise patients not to double up the next dose."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:429c334a-7b29-4093-962b-ccf50ae23e5d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 24, "token_count": 90, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "be3206bc-d5e2-4dfe-ad3d-e45c20e9c589", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ece550fe7a8ffffeb1b46e8aeeb28946ec00c9c7302c8c2ea5bec85e64a20323", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "429c334a-7b29-4093-962b-ccf50ae23e5d", "text": "JARDIANCE tablets available as:\n\n- x 10 mg pale yellow, round, biconvex and bevel-edged, film-coated tablets debossed with 'S 10' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol on the other side.\n- x 25 mg pale yellow, oval, biconvex, film-coated tablets debossed with 'S 25' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol on the other side."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3f927168-29cc-4cfd-b327-a34daa04c077", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 25, "token_count": 52, "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0f73b948-5692-40ed-8cff-89a1278a9105", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a23ac6dae8b0881b08b4cc50df5eb707ad66934af37237f12577b4f32d7192cf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "3f927168-29cc-4cfd-b327-a34daa04c077", "text": "JARDIANCE is contraindicated in patients:\n\n- x with a hypersensitivity to empagliflozin or any of the excipients in JARDIANCE, reactions such as angioedema have occurred [see Warnings and Precautions (5.6)] ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:55196673-c2c6-4185-8501-f984b42b80b9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 26, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "90e80cf2-3fa3-4f66-9dc2-1a4532ebd11c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "06ec1082d0f09bed84ab2a60fde5e23f4af45511949b69901d29c3f9c735a1ba", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "55196673-c2c6-4185-8501-f984b42b80b9", "text": "In patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus, JARDIANCE significantly increases the risk of diabetic ketoacidosis, a life-threatening event, beyond the background rate. In placebo-controlled trials of patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus, the risk of ketoacidosis was markedly increased in patients who received sodium glucose co-transporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors compared to patients who received placebo and fatal ketoacidosis has occurred with JARDIANCE. JARDIANCE is not indicated for glycemic control in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus.\n\nType 2 diabetes mellitus and pancreatic disorders (e.g., history of pancreatitis or pancreatic surgery) are also risk factors for ketoacidosis. There have been postmarketing reports of fatal events of ketoacidosis in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus using SGLT2 inhibitors, including JARDIANCE.\n\nPrecipitating conditions for diabetic ketoacidosis or other ketoacidosis include under-insulinization due to insulin dose reduction or missed insulin doses, acute febrile illness, reduced caloric intake, ketogenic diet, surgery, volume depletion, and alcohol abuse.\n\nSigns and symptoms are consistent with dehydration and severe metabolic acidosis an"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6b42daf0-489d-4cd0-b911-6ab301c52682", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 27, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "90e80cf2-3fa3-4f66-9dc2-1a4532ebd11c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "edf22d5e0cdd8ebd3b808cc57a39b7e3e2c56281132215496faf7798a2476b34", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "6b42daf0-489d-4cd0-b911-6ab301c52682", "text": "ke, ketogenic diet, surgery, volume depletion, and alcohol abuse.\n\nSigns and symptoms are consistent with dehydration and severe metabolic acidosis and include nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, generalized malaise, and shortness of breath. Blood glucose levels at presentation may be below those typically expected for diabetic ketoacidosis (e.g., less than 250 mg/dL). Ketoacidosis and glucosuria may persist longer than typically expected. Urinary glucose excretion persists for 3 days after discontinuing JARDIANCE [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.2)] ; however, there have been postmarketing reports of ketoacidosis and/or glucosuria lasting greater than 6 days and some up to 2 weeks after discontinuation of SGLT2 inhibitors.\n\nConsider ketone monitoring in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus and consider ketone monitoring in others at risk for ketoacidosis if indicated by the clinical situation. Assess for ketoacidosis regardless of presenting blood glucose levels in patients who present with signs and symptoms consistent with severe metabolic acidosis. If ketoacidosis is suspected, discontinue JARDIANCE, promptly evaluate, and treat ketoacidosis, if confirmed. Monitor patients for re"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b28e51a7-1a93-4659-8e27-d9d143fb0e1f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 28, "token_count": 155, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "90e80cf2-3fa3-4f66-9dc2-1a4532ebd11c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "9c283d632ab025866d6e1468e2c7ade922502adfc6ed0a1c2a1d7aedb5f2a341", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b28e51a7-1a93-4659-8e27-d9d143fb0e1f", "text": "abolic acidosis. If ketoacidosis is suspected, discontinue JARDIANCE, promptly evaluate, and treat ketoacidosis, if confirmed. Monitor patients for resolution of ketoacidosis before restarting JARDIANCE.\n\nWithhold JARDIANCE, if possible, in temporary clinical situations that could predispose patients to ketoacidosis. Resume JARDIANCE when the patient is clinically stable and has resumed oral intake [see Dosage and Administration (2.3)] .\n\nEducate all patients on the signs and symptoms of ketoacidosis and instruct patients to discontinue JARDIANCE and seek medical attention immediately if signs and symptoms occur."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f1a17838-39cc-4301-a0ec-5e0a44fc0fe3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 29, "token_count": 218, "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "85d76290-0f19-41ac-bfe5-6cabbd83b70a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "453946ff5f7db9ade3315b259105afc39bce8c07db407662ec6ba8debcbafd0b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "f1a17838-39cc-4301-a0ec-5e0a44fc0fe3", "text": "JARDIANCE can cause intravascular volume depletion which may sometimes manifest as symptomatic hypotension or acute transient changes in creatinine [see Adverse Reactions (6.1)] . There have been postmarketing reports of acute kidney injury, some requiring hospitalization and dialysis, in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus receiving SGLT2 inhibitors, including JARDIANCE. Patients with impaired renal function (eGFR less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ), elderly patients, or patients on loop diuretics may be at increased risk for volume depletion or hypotension. Before initiating JARDIANCE in patients with one or more of these characteristics, assess volume status and renal function. In patients with volume depletion, correct this condition before initiating JARDIANCE. Monitor for signs and symptoms of volume depletion, and renal function after initiating therapy."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6432f3a1-9e32-4e91-a6a3-92e24d74b276", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 30, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "338a75cd-a262-4b06-a0fc-a06d5eb1c109", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4bd8f5e670f9fd1e46fe7c9d92f4a041a5ae995aa5a4298a05dd8935a20419e7", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "6432f3a1-9e32-4e91-a6a3-92e24d74b276", "text": "JARDIANCE increases urinary glucose excretion [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.2)] and increases the risk of genitourinary infections including urinary tract infections and genital mycotic infections in both male and female patients [see Adverse Reactions (6.1)] .\n\nSerious genitourinary infections, including urosepsis, pyelonephritis, and necrotizing fasciitis of the perineum (Fournier's gangrene, a rare life-threatening infection requiring urgent surgical intervention), have occurred in patients with and without diabetes mellitus receiving SGLT2 inhibitors, including JARDIANCE [see Adverse Reactions (6.2)]. Cases have required hospitalization. In patients with Fournier's gangrene, serious outcomes have included multiple surgeries and death.\n\nPatients with a history of chronic or recurrent genitourinary infections are more likely to develop genitourinary infections when using JARDIANCE. Monitor patients for signs and symptoms of genitourinary infections and treat promptly, if indicated.\n\nImmediately evaluate patients presenting with pain or tenderness, erythema, or swelling in the genital or perineal area, along with fever or malaise, for necrotizing fasciitis. If suspected, disconti"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:37cb1f37-67ed-4f01-a2db-8668e49bd172", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 31, "token_count": 59, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "338a75cd-a262-4b06-a0fc-a06d5eb1c109", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "e3e7796f75e1c2fceb3587b0926147706690e7aa74cae7bdcde4c67b7189a8fd", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "37cb1f37-67ed-4f01-a2db-8668e49bd172", "text": "n or tenderness, erythema, or swelling in the genital or perineal area, along with fever or malaise, for necrotizing fasciitis. If suspected, discontinue JARDIANCE and promptly institute appropriate medical and/or surgical intervention."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b3b71422-fcd4-4196-94c8-a9e0a5a8103f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 32, "token_count": 175, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "bf8adfcf-7bba-422a-bd4a-3649193d74b1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "aebe3fe8f96fce94f5cc6262d9af20f299cd43cf8d797684b65896bd82366ff3", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b3b71422-fcd4-4196-94c8-a9e0a5a8103f", "text": "Insulin and insulin secretagogues are known to cause hypoglycemia.  In adult patients, the risk of hypoglycemia may be increased when JARDIANCE is used in combination with insulin secretagogues (e.g., sulfonylurea) or insulin. In pediatric patients aged 10 years and older, the risk of hypoglycemia was higher with JARDIANCE regardless of insulin use [see Adverse Reactions (6.1)] .\n\nThe risk of hypoglycemia may be lowered by a reduction in the dose of sulfonylurea (or other concomitantly administered insulin secretagogues) or insulin. Inform patients using these concomitant medications and pediatric patients of the risk of hypoglycemia and educate them on the signs and symptoms of hypoglycemia."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:74618fe8-865c-4b3d-9727-eb5d069e6dc9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 33, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "fdbf050a-faf0-4094-9471-da23b0a85491", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "887c2c58d0fe1b9c4c025d66ff3b3a48b9d0f7b162706f1e1a3d8668e49fe947", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "74618fe8-865c-4b3d-9727-eb5d069e6dc9", "text": "In some clinical studies with SGLT2 inhibitors an imbalance in the incidence of lower limb amputation has been observed. Across four JARDIANCE outcome trials, lower limb amputation event rates were 4.3 and 5.0 events per 1,000 patient-years in the placebo group and the JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg dose group, respectively, with a HR of 1.05 (95 % CI) (0.81, 1.36).\n\nIn a long-term cardio-renal outcome trial [see Clinical Studies 14.5] , in patients with chronic kidney disease, the occurrence of lower limb amputations was reported with event rates of 2.9, and 4.3 events per 1,000 patientyears in the placebo, and JARDIANCE 10 mg treatment arms, respectively. Amputation of the toe and mid-foot were most frequent (21 out of 28 JARDIANCE 10 mg treated patients with lower limb amputations), and some involving above and below the knee. Some patients had multiple amputations.\n\nPeripheral artery disease, and diabetic foot infection (including osteomyelitis), were the most common precipitating medical events leading to the need for an amputation. The risk of amputation was highest in patients with a baseline history of diabetic foot, peripheral artery disease (including previous amputation) or di"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3fe89c76-121f-4099-8f4e-a7500f649e5e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 34, "token_count": 112, "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "fdbf050a-faf0-4094-9471-da23b0a85491", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "0922ecc4747d6e2161f9ec1e5a9d5cbfdd30b683656ee4fb6e5fa73a4d4909a9", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "3fe89c76-121f-4099-8f4e-a7500f649e5e", "text": "e risk of amputation was highest in patients with a baseline history of diabetic foot, peripheral artery disease (including previous amputation) or diabetes.\n\nCounsel patients about the importance of routine preventative foot care. Monitor patients receiving JARDIANCE for signs and symptoms of diabetic foot infection (including osteomyelitis), new pain or tenderness, sores or ulcers involving the lower limbs, and institute appropriate treatment."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:69d622e1-bf0d-4acc-9fcc-9ba395b27441", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 35, "token_count": 106, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "fde9277c-a247-4706-9d41-3c0dd5eb082d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "3b894c0a4459320aa4a14aad7d56da0183df5f649f486925d0266fdb3af3d5ad", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "69d622e1-bf0d-4acc-9fcc-9ba395b27441", "text": "There have been postmarketing reports of serious hypersensitivity reactions (e.g., angioedema) in patients treated with JARDIANCE.  If a hypersensitivity reaction occurs, discontinue JARDIANCE; treat promptly per standard of care, and monitor until signs and symptoms resolve.  JARDIANCE is contraindicated in patients with hypersensitivity to empagliflozin or any of the excipients in JARDIANCE [see Contraindications (4)] ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bfb4eb0f-4428-418e-8a06-b6d68066c962", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 36, "token_count": 149, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "b8f88a87-25cb-428a-846e-a9bed8221b0c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "d0e2b59f88370e04cdd40f796d20eb14638c8870b657d15f7f35058a8601b8f4", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "bfb4eb0f-4428-418e-8a06-b6d68066c962", "text": "The following important adverse reactions are described below and elsewhere in the labeling:\n\n- x Diabetic Ketoacidosis in Patients with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus and Other Ketoacidosis [see Warnings and Precautions (5.1)]\n- x Volume Depletion [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2)]\n- x Genitourinary Infections, including Urosepsis, Pyelonephritis, Necrotizing Fasciitis of the Perineum (Fournier's Gangrene), and Genital Mycotic Infections [see Warnings and Precautions (5.3)]\n- x Hypoglycemia [see Warnings and Precautions (5.4)]\n- x Hypersensitivity Reactions [see Warnings and Precautions (5.6)]"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7a5f6253-caf4-4666-afec-e8f42d7d8745", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 37, "token_count": 141, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "c38a08f3-236b-484a-8e6f-895335e62a8a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "42433123adbaea065304b3a6e82edeaeefb25e5021606da1cdc89f87318222c7", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "7a5f6253-caf4-4666-afec-e8f42d7d8745", "text": "Because clinical trials are conducted under widely varying conditions, adverse reaction rates observed in the clinical trials of a drug cannot be directly compared to rates in the clinical trials of another drug and may not reflect the rates observed in practice.\n\nJARDIANCE has been evaluated in clinical trials in adult and pediatric patients aged 10 to 17 years with type 2 diabetes mellitus, in adults with heart failure, and in adults with chronic kidney disease. The overall safety profile of JARDIANCE was generally consistent across the studied indications."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bc5b0b2c-07ce-4695-9e1c-00f4b3bf1875", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 38, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "085984f1-1542-41ef-8125-9f2f9f3d871f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "351be4da475f9b83ed6458647cef215ca29028fd1ada638c58caec3107a61401", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "bc5b0b2c-07ce-4695-9e1c-00f4b3bf1875", "text": "The data in Table 2 are derived from a pool of four 24-week placebo-controlled trials and 18-week data from a placebo-controlled trial with insulin in adult patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus.  JARDIANCE was used as monotherapy in one trial and as add-on therapy in four trials [see Clinical Studies (14.1)] .\n\nThese data reflect exposure of 1,976 adult patients to JARDIANCE with a mean exposure duration of approximately 23 weeks.  Patients received placebo (N=995), JARDIANCE 10 mg (N=999), or JARDIANCE 25 mg (N=977) once daily.  The mean age of the population was 56 years and 3% were older than 75 years of age.  More than half (55%) of the population was male; 46% were White, 50% were Asian, and 3% were Black or African American.  At baseline, 57% of the population had diabetes mellitus more than 5 years and had a mean hemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) of 8%.  Established microvascular complications of diabetes mellitus at baseline included diabetic nephropathy (7%), retinopathy (8%), or neuropathy (16%).  Baseline renal function was normal or mildly impaired in 91% of patients and moderately impaired in 9% of patients (mean eGFR 86.8 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ).\n\nTable 2 shows adverse reactions (ex"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6a70a55b-759f-486d-ab49-883d76955377", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 39, "token_count": 87, "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "085984f1-1542-41ef-8125-9f2f9f3d871f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "1f8625a83a3fd32fa7ef01cc75568a9d1bdf77980e77fa2b94d81001f4736e66", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "6a70a55b-759f-486d-ab49-883d76955377", "text": "r mildly impaired in 91% of patients and moderately impaired in 9% of patients (mean eGFR 86.8 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ).\n\nTable 2 shows adverse reactions (excluding hypoglycemia) that were not present at baseline, occurred more commonly in JARDIANCE-treated patients than on placebo and occurred in greater than or equal to 2% JARDIANCE-treated patients."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5f7542c1-eb50-4150-8465-35d2a873087e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 40, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "3e80dc96-eaf6-4a28-8ee4-812fbd6398c0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "e1739c755fb4497b1c46fd6c2af8c752e927d72d3d9a08f19cd3de5baa5fc88f", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "5f7542c1-eb50-4150-8465-35d2a873087e", "text": "Table 2 Adverse Reactions Reported in t 2% of Adults with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Treated with JARDIANCE and Greater than Placebo in Pooled Placebo-Controlled Clinical Trials of JARDIANCE Monotherapy or Combination Therapy\n\n| Adverse Reactions                   |   Placebo (%) N=995 |   JARDIANCE 10 mg (%) N=999 |   JARDIANCE 25 mg (%) N=977 |\n|-------------------------------------|---------------------|-----------------------------|-----------------------------|\n| Urinary tract infection a           |                 7.6 |                         9.3 |                         7.6 |\n| Female genital mycotic infections b |                 1.5 |                         5.4 |                         6.4 |\n| Upper respiratory tract infection   |                 3.8 |                         3.1 |                         4.0 |\n| Increased urination c               |                 1.0 |                         3.4 |                         3.2 |\n| Dyslipidemia                        |                 3.4 |                         3.9 |                         2.9 |\n| Arthralgia                          |                 2.2 |                         2.4 |                         2.3 |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b368e4b1-d3c4-4bca-bcb5-0f83bb86383c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 41, "token_count": 126, "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "3e80dc96-eaf6-4a28-8ee4-812fbd6398c0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "8688fac88f178ed20b86d1ae01eea0c1f38388b5decba8459f5c2874e1df12fd", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b368e4b1-d3c4-4bca-bcb5-0f83bb86383c", "text": "2.9 |\n| Arthralgia                          |                 2.2 |                         2.4 |                         2.3 |\n| Male genital mycotic infections d   |                 0.4 |                         3.1 |                         1.6 |\n| Nausea                              |                 1.4 |                         2.3 |                         1.1 |\n\nThirst (including polydipsia) was reported in 0%, 1.7%, and 1.5% for placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0f322641-ae3b-4635-a361-7a47cd8a1470", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 42, "token_count": 168, "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "cff8808f-16b2-4245-93f4-d95ea4cc6f83", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "63bff9dac44bd239b1a194ee2a32417546d014c7ebc0d9607de18933a5f864e3", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "0f322641-ae3b-4635-a361-7a47cd8a1470", "text": "JARDIANCE causes an osmotic diuresis, which may lead to intravascular volume contraction and adverse reactions related to volume depletion.  In the pool of five placebo-controlled clinical trials in adults, adverse reactions related to volume depletion (e.g., blood pressure (ambulatory) decreased, blood pressure systolic decreased, dehydration, hypotension, hypovolemia, orthostatic hypotension, and syncope) were reported by 0.3%, 0.5%, and 0.3% of patients treated with placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively.  JARDIANCE may increase the risk of hypotension in patients at risk for volume contraction [see Use in Specific Populations (8.5, 8.6)]."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5e883a24-34c3-4506-a6e6-83ec539fdf22", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 43, "token_count": 158, "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "fe8e2916-27cf-4ad4-934a-00d6030bf6ca", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "1de4e297958f9ccae70d10339ee9d51f481e1cbe8034ac302b2ebe355dba0132", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "5e883a24-34c3-4506-a6e6-83ec539fdf22", "text": "In the pool of five placebo-controlled clinical trials in adults, adverse reactions of increased urination (e.g., polyuria, pollakiuria, and nocturia) occurred more frequently on JARDIANCE than on placebo (see Table 2). Specifically, nocturia was reported by 0.4%, 0.3%, and 0.8% of patients treated with placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively.\n\nHypoglycemia in Clinical Trials for Glycemic Control in Adults with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus The incidence of hypoglycemia in adults by trial is shown in Table 3.  The incidence of hypoglycemia increased when JARDIANCE was administered with insulin or sulfonylurea."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9d90f88f-a321-4b8d-8bc6-9f92c3359f8e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 44, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "03af77b0-bccd-4226-bf08-6efc4f74856c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "06818c8030c2208e112bb6337d1daab2c73a5742e9ceffe86c64d288d02cce2b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9d90f88f-a321-4b8d-8bc6-9f92c3359f8e", "text": "Table 3 Incidence of Overall a  and Severe b  Hypoglycemic Events in Placebo-Controlled Clinical Trials for Glycemic Control in Adults with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus c\n\n| Monotherapy (24 weeks)                                        | Placebo (n=229)             | JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=224)                              | JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=223)                              |\n|---------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|\n| Overall (%)                                                   | 0.4                         | 0.4                                                  | 0.4                                                  |\n| Severe (%)                                                    | 0                           | 0                                                    | 0                                                    |\n| In Combination with Metformin (24 weeks)                      | Placebo + Metformin (n=206) | JARDIANCE 10 mg + Metformin (n=217)                  | JARDIANCE 25 mg + Metformin (n=214)                  |\n|"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:494ffba3-e9f6-42c0-9939-39d6f0f3cc41", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 45, "token_count": 298, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "03af77b0-bccd-4226-bf08-6efc4f74856c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "43aa1010347a3bb99f352a79cfa2d7cd8d7f9595ed9947e0986259b4812e55f2", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "494ffba3-e9f6-42c0-9939-39d6f0f3cc41", "text": "| Placebo + Metformin (n=206) | JARDIANCE 10 mg + Metformin (n=217)                  | JARDIANCE 25 mg + Metformin (n=214)                  |\n| Overall (%)                                                   | 0.5                         | 1.8                                                  | 1.4                                                  |\n| Severe (%)                                                    | 0                           | 0                                                    | 0                                                    |\n| In Combination with Metformin + Sulfonylurea (24 weeks)       | Placebo (n=225)             | JARDIANCE 10 mg + Metformin + Sulfonylurea (n=224)   | JARDIANCE 25 mg + Metformin + Sulfonylurea (n=217)   |\n| Overall (%)                                                   | 8.4                         | 16.1                                                 | 11.5                                                 |\n| Severe (%)                                                    | 0                           | 0                                                    | 0                                                    |\n| In Combination with"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1ff17953-b411-47f3-89a8-43db25e10e57", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 46, "token_count": 288, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "03af77b0-bccd-4226-bf08-6efc4f74856c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "8c01a8c20b0d0ab50ede9f5ff7cb7270f653c5056fd1964db7196cdb456d7500", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "1ff17953-b411-47f3-89a8-43db25e10e57", "text": "| 0                                                    | 0                                                    |\n| In Combination with Pioglitazone +/- Metformin (24 weeks)     | Placebo (n=165)             | JARDIANCE 10 mg + Pioglitazone +/- Metformin (n=165) | JARDIANCE 25 mg + Pioglitazone +/- Metformin (n=168) |\n| Overall (%)                                                   | 1.8                         | 1.2                                                  | 2.4                                                  |\n| Severe (%)                                                    | 0                           | 0                                                    | 0                                                    |\n| In Combination with Basal Insulin +/- Metformin (18 weeks d ) | Placebo (n=170)             | JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=169)                              | JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=155)                              |\n| Overall (%)                                                   | 20.6                        | 19.5                                                 | 28.4                                                 |\n| Severe (%)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:462010ed-97e6-4559-aaaf-b7f9e76363ce", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 47, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "03af77b0-bccd-4226-bf08-6efc4f74856c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5b65661c2a7d383a14c01fba5aaf126c3d7cdd23ca89cc2b191623543ddb2f23", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "462010ed-97e6-4559-aaaf-b7f9e76363ce", "text": ".5                                                 | 28.4                                                 |\n| Severe (%)                                                    | 0                           | 0                                                    | 1.3                                                  |\n| In Combination with MDI Insulin +/-Metformin (18 weeks d )    | Placebo (n=188)             | JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=186)                              | JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=189)                              |\n| Overall (%)                                                   | 37.2                        | 39.8                                                 | 41.3                                                 |\n| Severe (%)                                                    | 0.5                         | 0.5                                                  | 0.5                                                  |\n\nOther Adverse Reactions in Clinical Trials for Glycemic Control in Adults with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus\n\n- x Genital Mycotic Infections: In the pool of five placebo-controlled clinical trials in adults, the incidence of genital mycotic infections (e.g., vaginal mycot"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bcf04b45-9439-4c9e-bcf8-8b856cbacddc", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 48, "token_count": 289, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "03af77b0-bccd-4226-bf08-6efc4f74856c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "57b3321857f6f37cddbf3b82817673c008730cd0ea7c3e634d753b2c37de7015", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "bcf04b45-9439-4c9e-bcf8-8b856cbacddc", "text": "Mycotic Infections: In the pool of five placebo-controlled clinical trials in adults, the incidence of genital mycotic infections (e.g., vaginal mycotic infection, vaginal infection, genital infection fungal, vulvovaginal candidiasis, and vulvitis) was increased in patients treated with JARDIANCE compared to placebo, occurring in 0.9%, 4.1%, and 3.7% of patients randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively.  Discontinuation from trial due to genital infection occurred in 0% of placebo-treated patients and 0.2% of patients treated with either JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg.\n\nGenital mycotic infections occurred more frequently in female than male patients (see Table 2).\n\nPhimosis occurred more frequently in male patients treated with JARDIANCE 10 mg (less than 0.1%) and JARDIANCE 25 mg (0.1%) than placebo (0%).\n\n- Urinary Tract Infections: In the pool of five placebo-controlled clinical trials in adults, the incidence of urinary tract infections (e.g., urinary tract infection, asymptomatic bacteriuria, and cystitis) was increased in patients treated with JARDIANCE compared to placebo (see Table 2).  Patients with a x"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4e96bbd5-35f7-4fe6-8bab-f476c2b9f8b5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 49, "token_count": 26, "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "03af77b0-bccd-4226-bf08-6efc4f74856c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "7a531ddc7aeb67f69c887d2b9f4aeb801c3ce6b9c03b397456a7904fc7b545f0", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "4e96bbd5-35f7-4fe6-8bab-f476c2b9f8b5", "text": "s) was increased in patients treated with JARDIANCE compared to placebo (see Table 2).  Patients with a x"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5d2dd211-4f5a-4030-bde4-1c43dd293e46", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 50, "token_count": 178, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0e91383f-891f-429a-ab40-686f5e3ffd27", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a5f19ef4f8a1ff5a6c920bbed777ce47d4c28b92c830f9049a8767e7a1c0dfa9", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "5d2dd211-4f5a-4030-bde4-1c43dd293e46", "text": "history of chronic or recurrent urinary tract infections were more likely to experience a urinary tract infection.  The rate of treatment discontinuation due to urinary tract infections was 0.1%, 0.2%, and 0.1% for placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively.\n\nUrinary tract infections occurred more frequently in female patients.  The incidence of urinary tract infections in female patients randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg was 16.6%, 18.4%, and 17.0%, respectively.  The incidence of urinary tract infections in male patients randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg was 3.2%, 3.6%, and 4.1%, respectively [see Use in Specific Populations (8.5)] ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:240f37ea-f962-480c-8440-7b0ab1212ae3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 51, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "dbcb51ea-941f-409c-9207-62af48568249", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "2a7d7166150133524c76228cc3e86ab814daea3cb12a4a4a1b2780d9d6ca7bfb", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "240f37ea-f962-480c-8440-7b0ab1212ae3", "text": "JARDIANCE was administered to 52 patients in a trial of 157 pediatric patients aged 10 to 17 years with type 2 diabetes mellitus with a mean exposure to JARDIANCE of 23.8 weeks [see Clinical Studies (14.2)] . Background therapies as adjunct to diet and exercise included metformin (51%), a combination of metformin and insulin (40.1%), insulin (3.2%), or none (5.7%). The mean HbA1c at baseline was 8.0% and the mean duration of type 2 diabetes mellitus was 2.1 years. The mean age was 14.5 years (range: 10-17 years) and 51.6% were aged 15 years and older. Approximately, 50% were White, 6% were Asian, 31% were Black or African American, and 38% were of Hispanic or Latino ethnicity. The mean BMI was 36.0 kg/m 2  and mean BMI Zscore was 3.0. Approximately 25% of the trial population had microalbuminuria or macroalbuminuria.\n\nThe risk of hypoglycemia was higher in pediatric patients treated with JARDIANCE regardless of concomitant insulin use. Hypoglycemia, defined as a blood glucose &lt;54 mg/dL, occurred in 10 (19.2%) patients and in 4 (7.5%) patients treated with JARDIANCE and placebo, respectively. No severe hypoglycemic events occurred (severe hypoglycemia was defined as an event requ"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9c599db0-2e09-4a1b-9a78-2342a2a30d5d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 52, "token_count": 68, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "dbcb51ea-941f-409c-9207-62af48568249", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4bc659550c7e4f0c20697a411a45bca6c7728702f9b513f87fe5ed7542aafa53", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9c599db0-2e09-4a1b-9a78-2342a2a30d5d", "text": "%) patients treated with JARDIANCE and placebo, respectively. No severe hypoglycemic events occurred (severe hypoglycemia was defined as an event requiring the assistance of another person to actively administer carbohydrates, glucagon or take other corrective actions)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8db7e9f9-4903-4537-8490-d9ff4a25b938", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 53, "token_count": 26, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "e71e67eb-2c3d-45af-bd94-3272c1770d3b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "da160ba87200466cda1ded4df3004bf80d8462696516412d048ca8100b7d1ff6", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "8db7e9f9-4903-4537-8490-d9ff4a25b938", "text": "No new adverse reactions were identified in EMPEROR-Reduced or EMPEROR-Preserved heart failure trials."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1f798732-7a4f-4455-a9f4-cbfa3689aee3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 54, "token_count": 117, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7ef3b9c8-c592-4dc7-a32e-65dcbc6668fc", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ed311f809eb2fe988150bc83d492ba1cda0be0310b220748e1c1006939efd582", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "1f798732-7a4f-4455-a9f4-cbfa3689aee3", "text": "The safety profile in patients with chronic kidney disease was generally consistent with that observed across the studied indications. In a long-term cardio-renal outcome trial [see Clinical Studies 14.5] , in patients with chronic kidney disease, the occurrence of lower limb amputations was reported with event rates of 2.9, and 4.3 events per 1,000 patient-years in the placebo, and JARDIANCE 10 mg treatment arms, respectively [see Warnings and Precautions (5.5)]."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:eaec10b9-c3d6-431c-ac24-bf4150b6b5a5", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 55, "token_count": 145, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "916a86f8-435c-4a8e-a5b1-853bb4c3c12f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "349d1f2dca065e8646c835f1665023a8cb93716bd21f3ae40b724c84fdb7a4ae", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "eaec10b9-c3d6-431c-ac24-bf4150b6b5a5", "text": "Initiation of JARDIANCE causes an increase in serum creatinine and decrease in eGFR within weeks of starting therapy and then these changes stabilize. In a trial of adults with moderate renal impairment, larger mean changes were observed. In a long-term cardiovascular outcomes trial, the increase in serum creatinine and decrease in eGFR generally did not exceed 0.1 mg/dL and -9.0 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , respectively, at Week 4, and reversed after treatment discontinuation, suggesting acute hemodynamic changes may play a role in the renal function changes observed with JARDIANCE."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:19865d13-03eb-4e4f-8045-3cd234fee693", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 56, "token_count": 83, "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "1ac9d7d6-0522-4aab-92ad-c24087b338c0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "e534a68e90080170e6690c637ecb3d99892b6586871882c713b14840991ad481", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "19865d13-03eb-4e4f-8045-3cd234fee693", "text": "Dose-related increases in low-density lipoprotein cholesterol (LDL-C) were observed in adults treated with JARDIANCE.  LDL-C increased by 2.3%, 4.6%, and 6.5% in patients treated with placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively.  The range of mean baseline LDL-C levels was 90.3 to 90.6 mg/dL across treatment groups."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e7d7c5ca-a789-4223-b8fc-cbf65b101c24", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 57, "token_count": 106, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "6f8d1cd4-a078-4aef-944f-095b1e158302", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "51d1c621d2a0e5151bd4c92482e75939ef87ecc0907c2b35e522c9a467cc71f5", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "e7d7c5ca-a789-4223-b8fc-cbf65b101c24", "text": "In a pool of four placebo-controlled trials in adults, median hematocrit decreased by 1.3% in placebo and increased by 2.8% in JARDIANCE 10 mg and 2.8% in JARDIANCE 25 mg treated patients.  At the end of treatment, 0.6%, 2.7%, and 3.5% of patients with hematocrits initially within the reference range had values above the upper limit of the reference range with placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d26f8f7a-132f-4da9-a00b-c25acdea3a37", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 58, "token_count": 158, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "e1f75249-dc3c-4c04-9ddd-37d58d923549", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "413e1d0c84f0cb6353fe17d2af417ab6a09e2072cef91a67bf6198e1f8275a6b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "d26f8f7a-132f-4da9-a00b-c25acdea3a37", "text": "Additional adverse reactions have been identified during postapproval use of JARDIANCE. Because these reactions are reported voluntarily from a population of uncertain size, it is generally not possible to reliably estimate their frequency or establish a causal relationship to drug exposure.\n\nGastrointestinal Disorders:\n\nConstipation\n\nInfections:\n\nNecrotizing fasciitis of the perineum (Fournier's gangrene), urosepsis and pyelonephritis\n\nMetabolism and Nutrition Disorders:\n\nKetoacidosis\n\nRenal and Urinary Disorders:\n\nAcute kidney injury\n\nSkin and Subcutaneous Tissue Disorders: Angioedema, skin reactions (e.g., rash, urticaria)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:586d8fce-0bad-4903-bab4-57692564566b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 59, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7b001011-32f3-4040-b4ff-2baa77dee29b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "8c37b4ff1ca13e7f82115f8dbd55af25fb3d41f2f6accbd345eb9d77d20eab88", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "586d8fce-0bad-4903-bab4-57692564566b", "text": "See Table 4 for clinically relevant interactions with JARDIANCE.\n\nTable 4 Clinically Relevant Interactions with JARDIANCE\n\n| Diuretics                                            | Diuretics                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n|------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Clinical Impact                                      | Coadministration of empagliflozin with diuretics resulted in increased urine volume and frequency of voids, which might enhance the potential for volume depletion.                                                                                           |\n| Intervention                                         | Before initiating JARDIANCE, assess volume status and renal function. In patients"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cb7e3d6c-00e6-4033-ab80-e8c489cd546c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 60, "token_count": 297, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7b001011-32f3-4040-b4ff-2baa77dee29b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5e7e37f40b19a61c03ff74ea2bd55440627e12ccdb6309a7e962e5e5e2f2f396", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "cb7e3d6c-00e6-4033-ab80-e8c489cd546c", "text": "|\n| Intervention                                         | Before initiating JARDIANCE, assess volume status and renal function. In patients with volume depletion, correct this condition before initiating JARDIANCE. Monitor for signs and symptoms of volume depletion, and renal function after initiating therapy. |\n| Insulin or Insulin Secretagogues                     | Insulin or Insulin Secretagogues                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| Clinical Impact                                      | The risk of hypoglycemia is increased when JARDIANCE is used in combination with insulin secretagogues (e.g., sulfonylurea) or insulin.                                                                                                                       |\n| Intervention                                         | Coadministration of JARDIANCE with an insulin secretagogue (e.g., sulfonylurea) or insulin may require lower dosages of the insulin secretagogue or insulin to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:395759dd-fed4-4aa3-b254-c9a4eedafdcd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 61, "token_count": 296, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7b001011-32f3-4040-b4ff-2baa77dee29b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "2bccac956ad61bc995bdb8374620908a9e8313881f18e6669c8e88b32ec67809", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "395759dd-fed4-4aa3-b254-c9a4eedafdcd", "text": "lin secretagogue (e.g., sulfonylurea) or insulin may require lower dosages of the insulin secretagogue or insulin to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia.                                                               |\n| Lithium                                              | Lithium                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| Clinical Impact                                      | Concomitant use of an SGLT2 inhibitor with lithium may decrease serum lithium concentrations.                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| Intervention                                         | Monitor serum lithium concentration more frequently during JARDIANCE initiation and dosage changes.                                                                                                                                                           |\n| Positive Urine Glucose Test"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4f737e72-eebc-4f28-9b94-77bea6f37104", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 62, "token_count": 262, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7b001011-32f3-4040-b4ff-2baa77dee29b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "e5b37a7401c2bf4dc8000673c99cfa6ed465ce71c064eca6e8fb306e5b08d5a0", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "4f737e72-eebc-4f28-9b94-77bea6f37104", "text": "|\n| Positive Urine Glucose Test                          | Positive Urine Glucose Test                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Clinical Impact                                      | SGLT2 inhibitors increase urinary glucose excretion and will lead to positive urine glucose tests.                                                                                                                                                            |\n| Intervention                                         | Monitoring glycemic control with urine glucose tests is not recommended in patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors. Use alternative methods to monitor glycemic control.                                                                                             |\n| Interference with 1,5-anhydroglucitol (1,5-AG) Assay | Interference with 1,5-anhydroglucitol (1,5-AG) Assay"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:81b4d589-615b-40c6-89cf-e627726e6603", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 63, "token_count": 154, "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7b001011-32f3-4040-b4ff-2baa77dee29b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "d9500a6598be481b239a8c71774be1de0214f3d03d1f88ecdcca6f1c0f8d80ae", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "81b4d589-615b-40c6-89cf-e627726e6603", "text": "erence with 1,5-anhydroglucitol (1,5-AG) Assay | Interference with 1,5-anhydroglucitol (1,5-AG) Assay                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| Clinical Impact                                      | Measurements of 1,5-AG are unreliable in assessing glycemic control in patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors.                                                                                                                                                      |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7f78a6d6-ef02-4a05-81d4-d2b320aad931", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 64, "token_count": 30, "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "61a7d8e6-605a-4699-9ef9-5b16b6a47781", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "7b5768f83ab6eb9b0bfdf5549caa8ffc68ab5d2f4e68f3da35dd867dd4342bfa", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "7f78a6d6-ef02-4a05-81d4-d2b320aad931", "text": "Monitoring glycemic control with 1,5-AG assay is not recommended. Use alternative methods to monitor glycemic control."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2126cee4-d230-4bd5-b499-1e045205adf9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 65, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "f1c332db-7ac2-4fb6-84ab-cc0dd78dd0df", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "424a89458b6157818c851c5e4d79e0bbe08ab7aebfd0949eb165713b613eaec2", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "2126cee4-d230-4bd5-b499-1e045205adf9", "text": "Based on animal data showing adverse renal effects, JARDIANCE is not recommended during the second and third trimesters of pregnancy.\n\nThe limited available data with JARDIANCE in pregnant women are not sufficient to determine a drugassociated risk for major birth defects and miscarriage.  There are risks to the mother and fetus associated with poorly controlled diabetes in pregnancy [see Clinical Considerations] .\n\nIn animal studies, adverse renal changes were observed in rats when empagliflozin was administered during a period of renal development corresponding to the late second and third trimesters of human pregnancy. Doses approximately 13-times the maximum clinical dose caused renal pelvic and tubule dilatations that were reversible [see Data] .\n\nThe estimated background risk of major birth defects is 6% to 10% in women with pre-gestational diabetes with a HbA1c &gt;7 and has been reported to be as high as 20% to 25% in women with HbA1c &gt;10. The estimated background risk of miscarriage for the indicated population is unknown. In the U.S. general population, the estimated background risk of major birth defects and miscarriage in clinically recognized pregnancies is 2% to 4%"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c62a4e26-59c7-44cf-8398-6e1e4bd0d186", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 66, "token_count": 45, "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "f1c332db-7ac2-4fb6-84ab-cc0dd78dd0df", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "373617e3780a244eba3dfe27b44fb1e56863985b7cf59d59de26b7004ea83893", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c62a4e26-59c7-44cf-8398-6e1e4bd0d186", "text": "In the U.S. general population, the estimated background risk of major birth defects and miscarriage in clinically recognized pregnancies is 2% to 4% and 15% to 20%, respectively."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6d03282b-ed24-440c-93ac-3153050c6711", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 67, "token_count": 75, "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "e9c3217b-d587-42c7-8946-3905ba015379", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "cb9b93d24389c7f2ff26327ce86c47777c9b83c790fbefb2b3f92689913dee44", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "6d03282b-ed24-440c-93ac-3153050c6711", "text": "Poorly controlled diabetes in pregnancy increases the maternal risk for diabetic ketoacidosis, pre-eclampsia, spontaneous abortions, preterm delivery, and delivery complications. Poorly controlled diabetes increases the fetal risk for major birth defects, stillbirth, and macrosomia related morbidity."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e49411eb-6fc5-4cf8-a0f6-e32606c9f3e7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 68, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "1ca0e6d4-ca50-486a-9495-26c95a4cc98c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "224a4e160c288fc556764d8cd2fbc0dcd49ba42f0f5c7342a8fe03d849fe5b2a", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "e49411eb-6fc5-4cf8-a0f6-e32606c9f3e7", "text": "Empagliflozin dosed directly to juvenile rats from postnatal day (PND) 21 until PND 90 at doses of 1, 10, 30, and 100 mg/kg/day caused increased kidney weights and renal tubular and pelvic dilatation at 100 mg/kg/day, which approximates 13-times the maximum clinical dose of 25 mg, based on AUC.  These findings were not observed after a 13-week, drug-free recovery period. These outcomes occurred with drug exposure during periods of renal development in rats that correspond to the late second and third trimester of human renal development.\n\nIn embryo-fetal development studies in rats and rabbits, empagliflozin was administered for intervals coinciding with the first trimester period of organogenesis in humans. Doses up to 300 mg/kg/day, which approximates 48times (rats) and 128-times (rabbits) the maximum clinical dose of 25 mg (based on AUC), did not result in adverse developmental effects. In rats, at higher doses of empagliflozin causing maternal toxicity, malformations of limb bones increased in fetuses at 700 mg/kg/day or 154-times the 25 mg maximum clinical dose. Empagliflozin crosses the placenta and reaches fetal tissues in rats. In the rabbit, higher doses of empagliflozin r"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ce384ff9-23ea-472c-b72b-6c87747d84e6", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 69, "token_count": 63, "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "1ca0e6d4-ca50-486a-9495-26c95a4cc98c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "fddb41ae467313f57512e3e079485e5ac353210532abe34487e118f4b139ec65", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "ce384ff9-23ea-472c-b72b-6c87747d84e6", "text": "the 25 mg maximum clinical dose. Empagliflozin crosses the placenta and reaches fetal tissues in rats. In the rabbit, higher doses of empagliflozin resulted in maternal and fetal toxicity at 700 mg/kg/day, or 139-times the 25 mg maximum clinical dose."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c29d0ffd-3fb5-4212-9321-26f31d8d49ae", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 70, "token_count": 101, "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "b74d2511-2d96-4d12-bbed-f2fccf06f712", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "9c4a5c67403b8780d1e64a2792b1b797587befb6675da0c1c0444b84fe8d4435", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c29d0ffd-3fb5-4212-9321-26f31d8d49ae", "text": "In pre- and postnatal development studies in pregnant rats, empagliflozin was administered from gestation day 6 through to lactation day 20 (weaning) at up to 100 mg/kg/day (approximately 16-times the 25 mg maximum clinical dose) without maternal toxicity.  Reduced body weight was observed in the offspring at greater than or equal to 30 mg/kg/day (approximately 4-times the 25 mg maximum clinical dose)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:59941ace-0402-48e5-953c-38092f3114d9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 71, "token_count": 160, "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "d983b26b-1391-4ac9-b2f9-8a9d3e371541", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "8e8e460c2925931b3dacd9c42cf97b8be38cb1b2b9ae93cb941a11e6e1c17dc6", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "59941ace-0402-48e5-953c-38092f3114d9", "text": "There is limited information regarding the presence of JARDIANCE in human milk, the effects of JARDIANCE on the breastfed infant or the effects on milk production.  Empagliflozin is present in the milk of lactating rats [see Data] .  Since human kidney maturation occurs in utero and during the first 2 years of life when lactational exposure may occur, there may be risk to the developing human kidney.\n\nBecause of the potential for serious adverse reactions in a breastfed infant, including the potential for empagliflozin to affect postnatal renal development, advise patients that use of JARDIANCE is not recommended while breastfeeding."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7ed238fd-08c6-4f77-889f-e8e16cac5f09", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 72, "token_count": 128, "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "a602a2a9-9fd3-48f9-ad90-c8dad5c9727a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5973584e7fba28fd513a4f948f33413ad40bc13cccb6d5a880961755ed82224a", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "7ed238fd-08c6-4f77-889f-e8e16cac5f09", "text": "Empagliflozin was present at a low level in rat fetal tissues after a single oral dose to the dams at gestation day 18. In rat milk, the mean milk to plasma ratio ranged from 0.634 to 5, and was greater than one from 2 to 24 hours post-dose. The mean maximal milk to plasma ratio of 5 occurred at 8 hours post-dose, suggesting accumulation of empagliflozin in the milk. Juvenile rats directly exposed to empagliflozin showed a risk to the developing kidney (renal pelvic and tubular dilatations) during maturation."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cae74f9f-b7c2-4fe3-9925-c8c7bc4c6e11", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 73, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "47449479-3aa8-43ae-9a37-fcacdc51ce2d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "f800af4beca1ebbfcaa591a7d45254115fa092917e5978d7e312437385a764b0", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "cae74f9f-b7c2-4fe3-9925-c8c7bc4c6e11", "text": "The safety and effectiveness of JARDIANCE as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in type 2 diabetes mellitus have been established in pediatric patients aged 10 years and older. Use of JARDIANCE for this indication is supported by evidence from a 26-week double-blind, placebo-controlled clinical trial, with a double-blind active treatment safety extension period of up to 52 weeks in 157 pediatric patients aged 10 to 17 years with type 2 diabetes mellitus and a pediatric pharmacokinetic study [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.3) and Clinical Studies (14.2)] . The safety profile of pediatric patients treated with JARDIANCE was similar to that observed in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus, with the exception of hypoglycemia risk which was higher in pediatric patients treated with JARDIANCE regardless of concomitant insulin use [see Warnings and Precautions (5.4) and Adverse Reactions (6.1)].\n\nThe safety and effectiveness of JARDIANCE have not been established in pediatric patients less than 10 years of age as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in type 2 diabetes mellitus.\n\nThe safety and effectiveness of JARDIANCE have not been establis"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a8263b31-469b-4ca9-a627-48e96a796d58", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 74, "token_count": 141, "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "47449479-3aa8-43ae-9a37-fcacdc51ce2d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "657dac75129ca09bf990835a3e8f6730314d0126f3a7f101e01a3d48b0b2a1aa", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "a8263b31-469b-4ca9-a627-48e96a796d58", "text": "djunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in type 2 diabetes mellitus.\n\nThe safety and effectiveness of JARDIANCE have not been established in pediatric patients to reduce the risk of:\n\n- x cardiovascular death and hospitalization for heart failure in patients with heart failure.\n- x sustained decline in eGFR, end-stage kidney disease, cardiovascular death, and hospitalization in patients with chronic kidney disease at risk of progression.\n- x cardiovascular death in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and established cardiovascular disease."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2102be4a-d037-4724-b135-e0de418fa9e2", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 75, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "3a1ea206-6d25-414f-be52-b5efee0d41df", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "fa0170b157a6ff32a269fbcb75ada0f76af0a0d2f5be3e63de810635a143c72b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "2102be4a-d037-4724-b135-e0de418fa9e2", "text": "In glycemic control trials in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, a total of 2,721 (32%) patients treated with JARDIANCE were 65 years of age and older, and 491 (6%) were 75 years of age and older.  JARDIANCE is expected to have diminished glycemic efficacy in elderly patients with renal impairment [see Use in Specific Populations (8.6)] .  The risk of volume depletion-related adverse reactions increased in patients who were 75 years of age and older to 2.1%, 2.3%, and 4.4% for placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg. The risk of urinary tract infections increased in patients who were 75 years of age and older to 10.5%, 15.7%, and 15.1% in patients randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2) and Adverse Reactions (6.1)] .\n\nIn the EMPEROR-Reduced, EMPEROR-Preserved, and EMPA-KIDNEY trials, no overall differences in safety and effectiveness have been observed between patients 65 years of age and older and younger adult patients. EMPEROR-Reduced included 1,188 (64%) patients treated with JARDIANCE 65 years of age and older, and 503 (27%) patients 75 years of age and older. EMPEROR-Preserved included 2,403 (80%"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8152c4bb-3c00-45fe-b8d7-08a30ade70a7", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 76, "token_count": 101, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "3a1ea206-6d25-414f-be52-b5efee0d41df", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "cad2aba6c46079b48ecd3a5d284dcf6cf5c2b476f998e51dfe363624ee77d0bb", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "8152c4bb-3c00-45fe-b8d7-08a30ade70a7", "text": "4%) patients treated with JARDIANCE 65 years of age and older, and 503 (27%) patients 75 years of age and older. EMPEROR-Preserved included 2,403 (80%) patients treated with JARDIANCE 65 years of age and older, and 1,281 (43%) patients 75 years of age and older. EMPA-KIDNEY included 1,803 (55%) patients treated with JARDIANCE 65 years of age and older, and 758 (23%) patients 75 years of age and older."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b612944f-8d98-4c32-bc67-74c5329b2106", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 77, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "36c838fb-19f2-490d-aeec-391f25570fc0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "41c422029980a6b30513b83924708553c95704b84bbfab58ce2f6a7c3fcba851", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b612944f-8d98-4c32-bc67-74c5329b2106", "text": "The efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE for glycemic control were evaluated in a trial of adult patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus with mild and moderate renal impairment (eGFR 30 to less than 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ) [see Clinical Studies (14.1)] .  In this trial, 195 adult patients exposed to JARDIANCE had an eGFR between 60 and 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 91 adult patients exposed to JARDIANCE had an eGFR between 45 and 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , and 97 patients exposed to JARDIANCE had an eGFR between 30 and 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . The glucose lowering benefit of JARDIANCE 25 mg decreased in adult patients with worsening renal function. The risks of renal impairment, volume depletion adverse reactions and urinary tract infection-related adverse reactions increased with worsening renal function [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2)] . Use of JARDIANCE for glycemic control in patients without established cardiovascular disease or cardiovascular risk factors is not recommended when eGFR is less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .\n\nJARDIANCE was evaluated in 7,020 adult patients with type 2 diabetes and established cardiovascular disease (eGFR greater than or equal to 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ) in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9ef017e4-7216-46d4-8f77-3a5488331806", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 78, "token_count": 252, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "36c838fb-19f2-490d-aeec-391f25570fc0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "56fa220ad783f7c4846e49da0321decbeed12c9054205e72e1867951bc8bc217", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9ef017e4-7216-46d4-8f77-3a5488331806", "text": "adult patients with type 2 diabetes and established cardiovascular disease (eGFR greater than or equal to 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ) in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial, in a total of 9,718 patients with heart failure (eGFR greater than or equal to 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ) in the EMPEROR-Reduced and EMPEROR-Preserved trials, and in 6,609 adult patients with chronic kidney disease (eGFR 20 to 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ) in the EMPA-KIDNEY study.  The safety profile across eGFR subgroups in these trials was consistent with the known safety profile [see Adverse Reactions (6.1) and Clinical Studies (14.3, 14.4, 14.5)].\n\nEfficacy and safety trials with JARDIANCE did not enroll adult patients with an eGFR less than 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2  or on dialysis. Once enrolled, adult patients in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME, EMPERORReduced, EMPEROR-Preserved, and EMPA-KIDNEY trials were not required to discontinue therapy for worsening of eGFR to less than 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 or initiation of dialysis [see Clinical Studies (14.3, 14.4, 14.5)]."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:13958bd4-6dd8-419e-bde0-842ce3600ddf", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 79, "token_count": 24, "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "b0c46249-a646-4284-b06e-b5736ef77747", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "56581d4eef28aec0ab843b98c60d295de3ab8ae3e8e4bacd91fefc3815d48f63", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "13958bd4-6dd8-419e-bde0-842ce3600ddf", "text": "JARDIANCE may be used in patients with hepatic impairment [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.3)] ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7a08def9-ee4f-4ceb-9fa3-57d9de44e85a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 80, "token_count": 142, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "9ebf02f8-7173-4283-be60-50bf32266b9b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "14504c4c7db834fc2d4174ebbcf1915bf4de371158ccd91664ca840fbcd7e2bc", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "7a08def9-ee4f-4ceb-9fa3-57d9de44e85a", "text": "Urinary Glucose Excretion In patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, urinary glucose excretion increased immediately following a dose of empagliflozin and was maintained at the end of a 4-week treatment period averaging at approximately 64 grams per day with 10 mg empagliflozin and 78 grams per day with 25 mg empagliflozin once daily [see Clinical Studies (14)]. Data from single oral doses of empagliflozin in healthy subjects indicate that, on average, the elevation in urinary glucose excretion approaches baseline by about 3 days for the 10 mg and 25 mg doses."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c370d557-a00d-4cab-b0a6-a47242bef3be", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 81, "token_count": 173, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "53c62fb7-5380-42ba-b6fe-51f232aa0a7b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "0ee6b96f6cf45bc37bf0a85f34b65210336630897d7e0d8854500bcc306cf05f", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c370d557-a00d-4cab-b0a6-a47242bef3be", "text": "Empagliflozin also reduces sodium reabsorption and increases the delivery of sodium to the distal tubule. This may influence several physiological functions including, but not restricted to, increasing tubuloglomerular feedback and reducing intraglomerular pressure, lowering both pre- and afterload of the heart and downregulating sympathetic activity.\n\nEmpagliflozin is an inhibitor of SGLT2, the predominant transporter responsible for reabsorption of glucose from the glomerular filtrate back into the circulation. By inhibiting SGLT2, empagliflozin reduces renal reabsorption of filtered glucose and lowers the renal threshold for glucose, and thereby increases urinary glucose excretion."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6e6f87f6-f2af-4743-9b95-dac7fc16bd0f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 82, "token_count": 264, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "de848317-55b5-421d-9dbd-f9ef02245e98", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "947ebc5e9d1978ca3d38174a280475c96208218ccba7222501f61ef9e30aadbc", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "6e6f87f6-f2af-4743-9b95-dac7fc16bd0f", "text": "dioxide.\n\nEach film-coated tablet of JARDIANCE contains 10 mg or 25 mg of empagliflozin (free base) and the following inactive ingredients: colloidal silicon dioxide, croscarmellose sodium, hydroxypropyl cellulose, lactose monohydrate, magnesium stearate, and microcrystalline cellulose.  In addition, the film coating contains the following inactive ingredients: ferric oxide yellow, hypromellose, polyethylene glycol, talc, and titanium practically insoluble in toluene.\n\nsoluble in methanol, slightly soluble in ethanol and acetonitrile, soluble in 50% acetonitrile/water, and Empagliflozin is a white to yellowish, non-hygroscopic powder.  It is very slightly soluble in water, sparingly OH\n\nHO\n\nOH\n\nHO\n\nO\n\nI/\n\nCl\n\n~\n\nO\n\nO\n\nc5\n\nIts molecular formula is C23H27ClO7 and the molecular weight is 450.91. The structural formula is:\n\nThe chemical name of empagliflozin is D-Glucitol,1,5-anhydro-1-C-[4-chloro-3-[[4-[[(3S)-tetrahydro-3furanyl]oxy]phenyl]methyl]phenyl]-, (1S).\n\nJARDIANCE tablets for oral use contain empagliflozin, an inhibitor of the SGLT2."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:01ffb02c-e104-4d88-812d-4fb7cb68e51a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 83, "token_count": 1, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "de848317-55b5-421d-9dbd-f9ef02245e98", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "51925171c4e66ea822a519b92aadfde8e72c2a296c4fa6ae48c81157bc24a54b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "01ffb02c-e104-4d88-812d-4fb7cb68e51a", "text": "GLT2."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1667933c-ff4c-44fb-865c-2acd3015a80a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 84, "token_count": 62, "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7ae03919-8b67-4efd-8da4-8a93bed16280", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "499d4b862c2149125912c670bc912fa873d30765b2e78c693b7d1be8cc4fe13d", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "1667933c-ff4c-44fb-865c-2acd3015a80a", "text": "In the event of an overdose with JARDIANCE, consider contacting the Poison Help line (1-800-222-1222) or a medical toxicologist for additional overdosage management recommendations. Removal of empagliflozin by hemodialysis has not been studied.\n\n10"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c589f855-8b67-4fbe-92a7-7cbf19111817", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 85, "token_count": 38, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ada0dd92-bf58-4831-810e-5e5d12bc2798", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "bf7173aa33c9faa3f9192d083bf99b73bcdf1cfd7603c431d6faafdfa5edd801", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c589f855-8b67-4fbe-92a7-7cbf19111817", "text": "In a 5-day study, mean 24-hour urine volume increase from baseline was 341 mL on Day 1 and 135 mL on Day 5 of empagliflozin 25 mg once daily treatment."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7a22dfde-1265-4d6c-855f-fa92588fc6b0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 86, "token_count": 76, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "e2e02bc7-3ea3-4739-9363-958c4e89810a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "73950b5d5300f1601f7cb1dfa9c2539c44388b64abd47edc696d6456a833db2a", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "7a22dfde-1265-4d6c-855f-fa92588fc6b0", "text": "In a randomized, placebo-controlled, active-comparator, crossover study, 30 healthy subjects were administered a single oral dose of empagliflozin 25 mg, empagliflozin 200 mg (8 times the maximum dose), moxifloxacin, and placebo.  No increase in QTc was observed with either 25 mg or 200 mg empagliflozin."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:065825db-e0fd-4a32-8d16-481a25485cb3", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 87, "token_count": 186, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "75e24a75-eeca-44c9-8778-473889172003", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4ae34be18afc8fb954183360b808aa7d48b811de6cc8edfc36cd54f4c7d67a84", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "065825db-e0fd-4a32-8d16-481a25485cb3", "text": "The pharmacokinetics of empagliflozin has been characterized in healthy volunteers and patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and no clinically relevant differences were noted between the two populations.  The steadystate mean plasma AUC and Cmax were 1,870 nmol ā h/L and 259 nmol/L, respectively, with 10 mg empagliflozin once daily treatment, and 4,740 nmol ā h/L and 687 nmol/L, respectively, with 25 mg empagliflozin once daily treatment.  Systemic exposure of empagliflozin increased in a dose-proportional manner in the therapeutic dose range. Empagliflozin does not appear to have time-dependent pharmacokinetic characteristics. Following oncedaily dosing, up to 22% accumulation, with respect to plasma AUC, was observed at steady-state."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5f93cd53-3d74-4ab7-9de2-5eca3a8f3f22", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 88, "token_count": 125, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0244872a-86b2-40ef-9fc0-9d3f3db4751a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "b0bc3f39099183a370dd351c3e28602617d5c1b3f0a6535841c4f8b50ad33ed2", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "5f93cd53-3d74-4ab7-9de2-5eca3a8f3f22", "text": "After oral administration, peak plasma concentrations of empagliflozin were reached at 1.5 hours post-dose. Administration of 25 mg empagliflozin after intake of a high-fat and high-calorie meal resulted in slightly lower exposure; AUC decreased by approximately 16% and Cmax decreased by approximately 37%, compared to fasted condition.  The observed effect of food on empagliflozin pharmacokinetics was not considered clinically relevant and empagliflozin may be administered with or without food."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b0c48b2b-ce8f-4be1-a3fc-eb9ea778d50e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 89, "token_count": 76, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "4394941f-3ac8-4009-ace0-5de9a8b205b5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "30894369418324b88d6563b3cc71822ed69149728ccd08206a1a0b06a3040892", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b0c48b2b-ce8f-4be1-a3fc-eb9ea778d50e", "text": "The apparent steady-state volume of distribution was estimated to be 73.8 L based on a population pharmacokinetic analysis.  Following administration of an oral [ 14 C]-empagliflozin solution to healthy subjects, the red blood cell partitioning was approximately 36.8% and plasma protein binding was 86.2%."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3d471b80-aa17-4fb3-89a0-6622a308cc0d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 90, "token_count": 44, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "781407d7-99cd-4bc3-ab69-5b6090e53863", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "d78fa83fcb4fcb9ff4924616f699ab1ae8a1177f1623c703975afb27dc18287d", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "3d471b80-aa17-4fb3-89a0-6622a308cc0d", "text": "The apparent terminal elimination half-life of empagliflozin was estimated to be 12.4 h and apparent oral clearance was 10.6 L/h based on the population pharmacokinetic analysis."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9f34dba4-bb1b-4b74-abdb-6120cbeae161", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 91, "token_count": 114, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "1edb0a65-778d-4bb9-85b1-1cedbce04122", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "787b669f3f3283da597f4ee7efee0b4316d16b89872da1669a86a157cb040e13", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9f34dba4-bb1b-4b74-abdb-6120cbeae161", "text": "No major metabolites of empagliflozin were detected in human plasma and the most abundant metabolites were three glucuronide conjugates (2-O-, 3-O-, and 6-O-glucuronide). Systemic exposure of each metabolite was less than 10% of total drug-related material. In vitro studies suggested that the primary route of metabolism of empagliflozin in humans is glucuronidation by the uridine 5'-diphospho-glucuronosyltransferases UGT2B7, UGT1A3, UGT1A8, and UGT1A9."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b2e5c1ff-b9c9-4e05-b4a3-2577e85b7a2b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 92, "token_count": 94, "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "5cfc38ce-789a-4a9e-bf9e-59f27c3011b9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4821357009440ffc1b51a9f73d7a250ee1a6769522a265df434c104cdfb88cc3", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b2e5c1ff-b9c9-4e05-b4a3-2577e85b7a2b", "text": "Following administration of an oral [ 14 C]-empagliflozin solution to healthy subjects, approximately 95.6% of the drug-related radioactivity was eliminated in feces (41.2%) or urine (54.4%). The majority of drug-related radioactivity recovered in feces was unchanged parent drug and approximately half of drug-related radioactivity excreted in urine was unchanged parent drug."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c89ff6ba-39bc-440c-a80f-70a6656dc004", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 93, "token_count": 68, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "661eaa1b-0147-4b8d-9284-822350db014b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "6902b7b10f835d20cddadb520e7a5d6cb1eabb581f8069a36d2ad7b159a975ef", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c89ff6ba-39bc-440c-a80f-70a6656dc004", "text": "The pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of empagliflozin were investigated in pediatric patients aged 10 to 17 years with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Oral administration of empagliflozin at 10 mg and 25 mg resulted in exposure within the range observed in adult patients."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4461a48e-08ad-4026-b940-3cf3c6e2f22c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 94, "token_count": 39, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "d7dcd5c5-d899-46d6-9f75-485fb9b6c99e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "6d09e27fe748a87906f27b600080d3fbc57ba537a1a69ec36acbddc9c3734ec6", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "4461a48e-08ad-4026-b940-3cf3c6e2f22c", "text": "Age, body mass index (BMI), gender and race (Asians versus primarily Whites) do not have a clinically meaningful effect on pharmacokinetics of empagliflozin."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0faa8c45-ba83-4ef9-99be-7c46f661d23b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 95, "token_count": 74, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "aff7b731-329d-4ae8-a471-c0c44168e3d3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "bb5ff0ff989246d3e010159df229bc89834eb2c135fcf352d50c320b057dd154", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "0faa8c45-ba83-4ef9-99be-7c46f661d23b", "text": "In adult patients with mild, moderate, and severe hepatic impairment according to the Child-Pugh classification, AUC of empagliflozin increased by approximately 23%, 47%, and 75%, and Cmax increased by approximately 4%, 23%, and 48%, respectively, compared to subjects with normal hepatic function."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f85ecbdc-d025-430e-a4dc-e0b37c980999", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 96, "token_count": 266, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "9bfee2bf-dea5-4cc8-9a80-e55d22e2c17c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "c290619b229299d3fe4d971a0ad6b1e1b464fc4b4e54a0f6c5fb76e2594327ec", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "f85ecbdc-d025-430e-a4dc-e0b37c980999", "text": "In adult patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus with mild (eGFR: 60 to less than 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ), moderate (eGFR: 30 to less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ), and severe (eGFR: less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ) renal impairment and patients on dialysis due to kidney failure, AUC of empagliflozin increased by approximately 18%, 20%, 66%, and 48%, respectively, compared to subjects with normal renal function. Peak plasma levels of empagliflozin were similar in patients with moderate renal impairment and patients on dialysis due to kidney failure compared to subjects with normal renal function. Peak plasma levels of empagliflozin were roughly 20% higher in patients with mild and severe renal impairment as compared to patients with normal renal function. Population pharmacokinetic analysis showed that the apparent oral clearance of empagliflozin decreased, with a decrease in eGFR leading to an increase in drug exposure.  However, the fraction of empagliflozin that was excreted unchanged in urine, and urinary glucose excretion, declined with decrease in eGFR."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:22fa2cb0-565d-4514-a613-eba5074aba99", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 97, "token_count": 4, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "9bfee2bf-dea5-4cc8-9a80-e55d22e2c17c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "842a458c00f4ad9f5e3ad576a87b21230c981666e889c19ba87d76b80678a6fc", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "22fa2cb0-565d-4514-a613-eba5074aba99", "text": "crease in eGFR."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:28391a0b-8a53-43f0-81d2-30412807208d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 98, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "baa3468a-450f-43fa-bff8-89e28dbe7cbf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "41ba2b392b8477e7ba18c55f74c131975b41dc95db41de641b81f1279d1edd27", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "28391a0b-8a53-43f0-81d2-30412807208d", "text": "Empagliflozin does not inhibit, inactivate, or induce CYP450 isoforms. In vitro data suggest that the primary route of metabolism of empagliflozin in humans is glucuronidation by the uridine 5'-diphosphoglucuronosyltransferases UGT1A3, UGT1A8, UGT1A9, and UGT2B7. Empagliflozin does not inhibit UGT1A1, UGT1A3, UGT1A8, UGT1A9, or UGT2B7. Therefore, no effect of empagliflozin is anticipated on concomitantly administered drugs that are substrates of the major CYP450 isoforms or UGT1A1, UGT1A3, UGT1A8, UGT1A9, or UGT2B7. The effect of UGT induction (e.g., induction by rifampicin or any other UGT enzyme inducer) on empagliflozin exposure has not been evaluated.\n\nEmpagliflozin is a substrate for P-glycoprotein (P-gp) and breast cancer resistance protein (BCRP), but it does not inhibit these efflux transporters at therapeutic doses. Based on in vitro studies, empagliflozin is considered unlikely to cause interactions with drugs that are P-gp substrates. Empagliflozin is a substrate of the human uptake transporters OAT3, OATP1B1, and OATP1B3, but not OAT1 and OCT2. Empagliflozin does not inhibit any of these human uptake transporters at clinically relevant plasma concentrations and, therefo"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b732a325-a0bd-49de-8a38-30aa55c3277f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 99, "token_count": 70, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "baa3468a-450f-43fa-bff8-89e28dbe7cbf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "1b4329cdf10705ad3263b720c71ccccb341e02c3e5794754c32de4f2364c6d7d", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b732a325-a0bd-49de-8a38-30aa55c3277f", "text": "but not OAT1 and OCT2. Empagliflozin does not inhibit any of these human uptake transporters at clinically relevant plasma concentrations and, therefore, no effect of empagliflozin is anticipated on concomitantly administered drugs that are substrates of these uptake transporters."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5e69dc42-c53b-430a-9061-852774de084a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 100, "token_count": 162, "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "17475fa5-d03b-46d2-949d-b119029a5861", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "2929fb8d86c22c264c6cd036530f67109c1660d61731b9f081cdb7e045b9b3d5", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "5e69dc42-c53b-430a-9061-852774de084a", "text": "Empagliflozin pharmacokinetics were similar with and without coadministration of metformin, glimepiride, pioglitazone, sitagliptin, linagliptin, warfarin, verapamil, ramipril, and simvastatin in healthy volunteers and with or without coadministration of hydrochlorothiazide and torsemide in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus (see Figure 1). In subjects with normal renal function, coadministration of empagliflozin with probenecid resulted in a 30% decrease in the fraction of empagliflozin excreted in urine without any effect on 24-hour urinary glucose excretion. The relevance of this observation to patients with renal impairment is unknown."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6637b1bc-fb5a-43f7-9379-5a45141b939b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 101, "token_count": 165, "page_number": 18, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0b4444c9-1358-46c8-8d19-de51c430646e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4e06267224d3a94d5416587a83a179c0afd25f9b6888821ba2fd12eabd0da7b1", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "6637b1bc-fb5a-43f7-9379-5a45141b939b", "text": "Figure 1 Effect of Various Medications on the Pharmacokinetics of Empagliflozin as Displayed as 90% Confidence Interval of Geometric Mean AUC and Cmax Ratios [reference lines indicate 100% (80% - 125%)]\n\n<!-- image -->\n\na empagliflozin, 50 mg, once daily; b empagliflozin, 25 mg, single dose; c empagliflozin, 25 mg, once daily; d empagliflozin, 10 mg, single dose Empagliflozin had no clinically relevant effect on the pharmacokinetics of metformin, glimepiride, pioglitazone, sitagliptin, linagliptin, warfarin, digoxin, ramipril, simvastatin, hydrochlorothiazide, torsemide, and oral contraceptives when coadministered in healthy volunteers (see Figure 2)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9495d1b5-4908-44dc-80fa-0313c4b25cbf", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 102, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 19, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0967321b-7f9a-4902-a781-d55029681c2e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "1dadb3fabff7f44731345edbf28da405a1999c0dd651e0b77e13a12e283d10cb", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9495d1b5-4908-44dc-80fa-0313c4b25cbf", "text": "Figure 2 Effect of Empagliflozin on the Pharmacokinetics of Various Medications as Displayed as 90% Confidence Interval of Geometric Mean AUC and  Cmax Ratios [reference lines indicate 100% (80% - 125%)]\n\nGeometric  mean ratio  (90% confidence interval)\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n| Antidiabetic drugs   | Metformin, 1000 mg, twice daily\"          | AUC Cmax   |\n|----------------------|-------------------------------------------|------------|\n|                      | Glimepiride, 1 mg, single dose•           | AUC Cmax   |\n|                      | Pioglitazone, 45 mg, once daill           | AUC Cmax   |\n|                      | Sitagliptin , 100 mg, once daily\"         | AUC Cmax   |\n|                      | Linagliptin , 5 mg, once daily\"           | AUC Cmax   |\n| Oral contraceptives  | Ethin ylestradiol, 30 mcg, once daily'· 1 | AUC Cmax   |\n|                      | Levonorgestrel, 150 mcg, once daily'· 1   | AUC Cmax   |\n| Others               | Simvastatin, 40 mg, single dosec          | AUC Gmax   |\n|                      | Simvastatin acidd                         | AUG Gmax   |\n|                      | R-Warfarin, 25 mg, single doseb,e         | AUG Cmax   |\n|                      | S-"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7acf3f87-8d62-4d0f-9f0f-9230964d6025", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 103, "token_count": 174, "page_number": 19, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0967321b-7f9a-4902-a781-d55029681c2e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "f0d518fc519edce4c68657ff3529e13be233c59d6c7337944365783f98c9cf7b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "7acf3f87-8d62-4d0f-9f0f-9230964d6025", "text": "d                         | AUG Gmax   |\n|                      | R-Warfarin, 25 mg, single doseb,e         | AUG Cmax   |\n|                      | S-Warfarin, 25 mg, single doseb,e         | AUG Cmax   |\n|                      | Ramipril, 5 mg, once daill                | AUG Gmax   |\n|                      | Ramiprilat9                               | AUG        |\n|                      | Digoxin, 0.5 mg, single doseb             | AUC Gmax   |\n|                      | Hydrochlorothiazide, 25 mg, once dailyb   | AUG Gmax   |\n|                      | Torsemide, 5 mg, once dailyb              | AUG        |\n|                      |                                           | Gmax       |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:07c0302f-89ad-4c9d-9416-37dc8163cbce", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 104, "token_count": 218, "page_number": 19, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "68df8237-036f-4b4d-8457-53b84ec4c145", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "7a05983eaf89945b39bc672103b096b4f30ddda469527a048569ea446e74183f", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "07c0302f-89ad-4c9d-9416-37dc8163cbce", "text": "Carcinogenesis was evaluated in 2-year studies conducted in CD-1 mice and Wistar rats.  Empagliflozin did not increase the incidence of tumors in female rats dosed at 100, 300, or 700 mg/kg/day (up to 72 times the exposure from the maximum clinical dose of 25 mg). In male rats, hemangiomas of the mesenteric lymph node were increased significantly at 700 mg/kg/day or approximately 42 times the exposure from a 25 mg clinical dose.  Empagliflozin did not increase the incidence of tumors in female mice dosed at 100, 300, or 1,000 mg/kg/day (up to 62 times the exposure from a 25 mg clinical dose). Renal tubule adenomas and carcinomas were observed in male mice at 1,000 mg/kg/day, which is approximately 45 times the exposure of the maximum clinical dose of 25 mg. These tumors may be associated with a metabolic pathway predominantly present in the male mouse kidney."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:08d01a13-29a9-4283-a925-113dd3ef67bb", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 105, "token_count": 57, "page_number": 20, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0fe1ee70-e860-4012-8bb3-37db5468f1eb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "02d1de0b320d978c85254cd19d88805e808e2028bc149d8fac11ee0f5262f4b6", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "08d01a13-29a9-4283-a925-113dd3ef67bb", "text": "Empagliflozin was not mutagenic or clastogenic with or without metabolic activation in the in vitro Ames bacterial mutagenicity assay, the in vitro L5178Y tk +/mouse lymphoma cell assay, and an in vivo micronucleus assay in rats."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f597ab25-1a07-424d-86a0-0643ab7c2905", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 106, "token_count": 58, "page_number": 20, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "950fa678-14a1-40e2-8375-206d1804f896", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "10809b688516b44f740aa63a49d6e4cb144a45834d6d522b60194442927ef1a5", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "f597ab25-1a07-424d-86a0-0643ab7c2905", "text": "Empagliflozin had no effects on mating, fertility or early embryonic development in treated male or female rats up to the high dose of 700 mg/kg/day (approximately 155 times the 25 mg clinical dose in males and females, respectively)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a89b83af-4978-47ee-bf2d-f0aea7d370a0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 107, "token_count": 135, "page_number": 20, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "deeb8f74-74d8-4212-bde8-2cef7ade32c7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "45d7ea81f30876cf7a6387bb7c7307a62d928508708fed881a29121a789ddbc8", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "a89b83af-4978-47ee-bf2d-f0aea7d370a0", "text": "JARDIANCE has been studied as monotherapy and in combination with metformin, sulfonylurea, pioglitazone, linagliptin, and insulin.  JARDIANCE has also been studied in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus with mild or moderate renal impairment.\n\nIn adult patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, treatment with JARDIANCE reduced hemoglobin A1c (HbA1c), compared to placebo. The reduction in HbA1c for JARDIANCE compared with placebo was observed across subgroups including sex, race, geographic region, baseline BMI and duration of disease."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cdf99165-51da-499a-b3e2-8162e39fd099", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 108, "token_count": 182, "page_number": 20, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "85ebaa6a-b2f3-49f3-9a07-3d65ce3b9e34", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a427faacef41197e885d9db65f94a9f15dcd6b2cdc28cb3e56f24480f220c027", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "cdf99165-51da-499a-b3e2-8162e39fd099", "text": "A total of 986 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus participated in a double-blind, placebo-controlled trial to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE monotherapy.\n\nTreatment-naïve patients with inadequately controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus entered an open-label placebo run-in for 2 weeks. At the end of the run-in period, patients who remained inadequately controlled and had an HbA1c between 7% and 10% were randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, or a reference comparator.\n\nAt Week 24, treatment with JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg daily provided statistically significant reductions in HbA1c (p-value &lt;0.0001), fasting plasma glucose (FPG), and body weight compared with placebo (see Table 5 and Figure 3)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e24d56aa-4545-460b-882c-ca6197cf9c7d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 109, "token_count": 299, "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "b5bd9257-0761-4d29-9c05-53ec2cc3e13f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "386349074a58c38d63d3433c0b22d5d2273a31d4c45a2e6d509cb5714e123e22", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "e24d56aa-4545-460b-882c-ca6197cf9c7d", "text": "Table 5 Results at Week 24 From a Placebo-Controlled Monotherapy Trial of JARDIANCE\n\n|                                                    | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=224   | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=224   | Placebo N=228   |\n|----------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|-------------------------|-----------------|\n| HbA1c (%) a                                        |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                    | 7.9                     | 7.9                     | 7.9             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)               | -0.7                    | -0.8                    | 0.1             |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (97.5% CI) | -0.7 b (-0.9, -0.6)     | -0.9 b (-1.0, -0.7)     | --              |\n| Patients [n (%)] achieving HbA1c <7%               | 72 (35%)                | 88 (44%)                | 25 (12%)        |\n| FPG (mg/dL) c                                      |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                    | 153                     | 153                     | 155"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bd0c31bd-211f-4e7c-92e7-2907977e7fda", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 110, "token_count": 296, "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "b5bd9257-0761-4d29-9c05-53ec2cc3e13f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "2b23a7374486364055867a4bced6a64d241c13f611092ad403ec9a0b4d100a6a", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "bd0c31bd-211f-4e7c-92e7-2907977e7fda", "text": "|                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                    | 153                     | 153                     | 155             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)               | -19                     | -25                     | 12              |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI)   | -31 (-37, -26)          | -36 (-42, -31)          | --              |\n| Body Weight                                        |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean) in kg                              | 78                      | 78                      | 78              |\n| % change from baseline (adjusted mean)             | -2.8                    | -3.2                    | -0.4            |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI)   | -2.5 b (-3.1, -1.9)     | -2.8 b (-3.4, -2.2)     | --              |\n\na Modified intent-to-treat population.  Last observation on trial (LOCF) was used to impute missing data at Week 24.  At Week 24, 9.4%, 9.4%, and 30.7% was imputed for patients randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, and placebo, respectively. b ANCOVA derived p-value &lt;0.0001 ("}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:50c3fe32-f1eb-4dd4-83d0-ec370eeba454", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 111, "token_count": 171, "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "b5bd9257-0761-4d29-9c05-53ec2cc3e13f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "e9322b9e9628fe70ddefefd09288ebfab0101d32dcaf02d84245a420a9af1161", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "50c3fe32-f1eb-4dd4-83d0-ec370eeba454", "text": "%, and 30.7% was imputed for patients randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, and placebo, respectively. b ANCOVA derived p-value &lt;0.0001 (HbA1c: ANCOVA model includes baseline HbA1c, treatment, renal function, and region.  Body weight and FPG: same model used as for HbA1c but additionally including baseline body weight/baseline FPG, respectively.) c FPG (mg/dL); for JARDIANCE 10 mg, n=223, for JARDIANCE 25 mg, n=223, and for placebo, n=226\n\nFigure 3 Adjusted Mean HbA1c Change at Each Time Point (Completers) and at Week 24 (mITT Population) - LOCF\n\n1\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n'Mean change from baseline adjusted for baseline HbA1c, geographical region, and eGFR at baseline."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:66cfbbd3-a65d-4236-9f5e-799746d0783b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 112, "token_count": 73, "page_number": 22, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0efa4a18-ab94-4e1a-95e4-0391b226f43f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "6314a4d5bc5a6689c5a7c4991d4868d62c638e814845edbbccc28469e7ddf4b6", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "66cfbbd3-a65d-4236-9f5e-799746d0783b", "text": "At Week 24, the systolic blood pressure was statistically significantly reduced compared to placebo by -2.6 mmHg (placebo-adjusted, p-value=0.0231) in patients randomized to 10 mg of JARDIANCE and by -3.4 mmHg (placebo-corrected, p-value=0.0028) in patients randomized to 25 mg of JARDIANCE."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ebe87e42-8b37-4058-a63f-9c002cf57b03", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 113, "token_count": 294, "page_number": 22, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "21d9dc76-75a4-4354-ab64-bc988d0c6f32", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a2a04aba6416f1f7796fa4a098dfe466a8fadb2e92964bd2e359a5e9b13c9292", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "ebe87e42-8b37-4058-a63f-9c002cf57b03", "text": "A total of 637 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus participated in a double-blind, placebo-controlled trial to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE in combination with metformin.\n\nPatients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on at least 1,500 mg of metformin per day entered an open-label 2-week placebo run-in. At the end of the run-in period, patients who remained inadequately controlled and had an HbA1c between 7% and 10% were randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, or JARDIANCE 25 mg.\n\nAt Week 24, treatment with JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg daily provided statistically significant reductions in HbA1c (p-value &lt;0.0001), FPG, and body weight compared with placebo (see Table 6).\n\nTable 6 Results at Week 24 From a Placebo-Controlled Trial for JARDIANCE used in Combination with Metformin\n\n|                                                              | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=217   | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=213   | Placebo N=207   |\n|--------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|-------------------------|-----------------|\n| HbA1c (%) a                                                  |                         |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:629cbee7-5886-4f3d-ae6f-2cf0b5a75299", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 114, "token_count": 296, "page_number": 22, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "21d9dc76-75a4-4354-ab64-bc988d0c6f32", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5e11e40fadf650dd5955d353c1c33922e2eedb225a86223ac0af1bfb16e19a14", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "629cbee7-5886-4f3d-ae6f-2cf0b5a75299", "text": "---------------|-----------------|\n| HbA1c (%) a                                                  |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              | 7.9                     | 7.9                     | 7.9             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)                         | -0.7                    | -0.8                    | -0.1            |\n| Difference from placebo + metformin (adjusted mean) (95% CI) | -0.6 b (-0.7, -0.4)     | -0.6 b (-0.8, -0.5)     | --              |\n| Patients [n (%)] achieving HbA1c <7%                         | 75 (38%)                | 74 (39%)                | 23 (13%)        |\n| FPG (mg/dL) c                                                |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              | 155                     | 149                     | 156             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)                         | -20                     | -22                     | 6               |\n| Difference from placebo + metformin (adjusted mean)          | -26"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:99758d07-4604-4e44-b3c5-ea22ba203705", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 115, "token_count": 242, "page_number": 22, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "21d9dc76-75a4-4354-ab64-bc988d0c6f32", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "54ee1fa14c1e6c217c4b1ae032decb46a2d5b93335992845e4b27004a32e6359", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "99758d07-4604-4e44-b3c5-ea22ba203705", "text": "| -22                     | 6               |\n| Difference from placebo + metformin (adjusted mean)          | -26                     | -29                     | --              |\n| Body Weight                                                  |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline mean in kg                                          | 82                      | 82                      | 80              |\n| % change from baseline (adjusted mean)                       | -2.5                    | -2.9                    | -0.5            |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI)             | -2.0 b (-2.6, -1.4)     | -2.5 b (-3.1, -1.9)     | --              |\n\nAt Week 24, the systolic blood pressure was statistically significantly reduced compared to placebo by -4.1 mmHg (placebo-corrected, p-value &lt;0.0001) for JARDIANCE 10 mg and -4.8 mmHg (placebo-corrected, pvalue &lt;0.0001) for JARDIANCE 25 mg."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2670b523-be76-426b-a7da-bd4b7b994e69", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 116, "token_count": 66, "page_number": 22, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "495711bf-833e-4520-8ef3-6d4774e7ef7e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ee36c53185bfbd5b1d3712ce1ae4a5b435c1d7358c3574b25185b5654d519984", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "2670b523-be76-426b-a7da-bd4b7b994e69", "text": "A total of 1,364 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus participated in a double-blind, randomized, activecontrolled trial to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE in combination with metformin as initial therapy compared to the corresponding individual components."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:25fb6ec5-e1d2-4f05-8237-a0fbcf70ec98", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 117, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "25ad1cc1-11e6-4b22-9551-82f85a0684f1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "f074a9374ea7ff69b5adca6254254d0c8e7f36d924aab2a0002087ee8b08b192", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "25fb6ec5-e1d2-4f05-8237-a0fbcf70ec98", "text": "Treatment-naïve patients with inadequately controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus entered an open-label placebo run-in for 2 weeks. At the end of the run-in period, patients who remained inadequately controlled and had an HbA1c between 7% and 10.5% were randomized to one of 8 active-treatment arms: JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg; metformin 1,000 mg, or 2,000 mg; JARDIANCE 10 mg in combination with 1,000 mg or 2,000 mg metformin; or JARDIANCE 25 mg in combination with 1,000 mg or 2,000 mg metformin.\n\nAt Week 24, initial therapy of JARDIANCE in combination with metformin provided statistically significant reductions in HbA1c (p-value &lt;0.01) compared to the individual components (see Table 7).\n\nTable 7 Glycemic Parameters at 24 Weeks in a Trial Comparing JARDIANCE and Metformin to the Individual Components as Initial Therapy\n\n|                                                  | JARDIANCE 10 mg + Metformin 1,000 mg a N=161   | JARDIANCE 10 mg + Metformin 2,000 mg a N=167   | JARDIANCE 25 mg + Metformin 1,000 mg a N=165   | JARDIANCE 25 mg + Metformin 2,000 mg a N=169   | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=169   | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=163   | Metformin 1,000 mg a N=167   | Metformin 2,000 mg a N=162   |\n|-------"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f79ebd98-e074-4637-9f37-54dbe128c11e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 118, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "25ad1cc1-11e6-4b22-9551-82f85a0684f1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "245d8e2037f224751cf00c049b4e383079fa1e87ff653e0e703eefd77a25a4ce", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "f79ebd98-e074-4637-9f37-54dbe128c11e", "text": "formin 2,000 mg a N=169   | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=169   | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=163   | Metformin 1,000 mg a N=167   | Metformin 2,000 mg a N=162   |\n|--------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|-------------------------|------------------------------|------------------------------|\n| HbA1c (%)                                        |                                                |                                                |                                                |                                                |                         |                         |                              |                              |\n| Baseline (mean)                                  | 8.7                                            | 8.7                                            | 8.8                                            | 8.7                                            | 8.6                     | 8.9                     | 8.7                          |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8ecd83c7-213e-4294-bd6c-9bb4dbe73c87", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 119, "token_count": 292, "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "25ad1cc1-11e6-4b22-9551-82f85a0684f1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "87439f0d21f839126e1711a0bf8b0c4537b657a3ea30d6b0496bc05ac5f2569b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "8ecd83c7-213e-4294-bd6c-9bb4dbe73c87", "text": "| 8.7                                            | 8.6                     | 8.9                     | 8.7                          | 8.6                          |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)             | -2.0                                           | -2.1                                           | -1.9                                           | -2.1                                           | -1.4                    | -1.4                    | -1.2                         | -1.8                         |\n| Comparison vs JARDIANCE (adjusted mean) (95% CI) | -0.6 b (-0.9, -0.4)                            | -0.7 b (-1.0, -0.5)                            | -0.6 c (-0.8, -0.3)                            | -0.7 c (-1.0, -0.5)                            | --                      | --                      | --                           | --                           |\n| Comparison vs metformin (adjusted mean) (95% CI) | -0.8 b (-1.0, -0.6)                            | -0.3 b (-0.6, -0.1)                            | -0.8 c (-1.0, -0.5)                            | -0.3 c (-0.6, -0.1)                            | --                      | --"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ff81d1c7-4794-437e-b4ac-df2db4529137", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 120, "token_count": 168, "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "25ad1cc1-11e6-4b22-9551-82f85a0684f1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5e09326a47260ccb5ebdcb3981fbca9bd6ad5be863853101cceaaed5d125be44", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "ff81d1c7-4794-437e-b4ac-df2db4529137", "text": "| -0.8 c (-1.0, -0.5)                            | -0.3 c (-0.6, -0.1)                            | --                      | --                      | --                           | --                           |\n\na Metformin total daily dose, administered in two equally divided doses per day.\n\nb p-value ≤ 0.0062 (modified intent-to-treat population [observed case] MMRM model included treatment, renal function, region, visit, visit by treatment interaction, and baseline HbA1c).\n\nc p-value ≤ 0.0056 (modified intent-to-treat population [observed case] MMRM model included treatment, renal function, region, visit, visit by treatment interaction, and baseline HbA1c)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:31301b98-206f-4aca-af07-201d46f8d870", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 121, "token_count": 182, "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "683d622e-803b-4b75-858f-5971f1392173", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "fad737512332f8cb1dbd10459e64569f15a3cc953efd068d8c0d07c5ceb845b5", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "31301b98-206f-4aca-af07-201d46f8d870", "text": "A total of 666 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus participated in a double-blind, placebo-controlled trial to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE in combination with metformin plus a sulfonylurea.\n\nPatients with inadequately controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus on at least 1,500 mg per day of metformin and on a sulfonylurea, entered a 2-week open-label placebo run-in. At the end of the run-in, patients who remained inadequately controlled and had an HbA1c between 7% and 10% were randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, or JARDIANCE 25 mg.\n\nTreatment with JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg daily provided statistically significant reductions in HbA1c (pvalue &lt;0.0001), FPG, and body weight compared with placebo (see Table 8)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f7695977-d2b4-4b3d-a039-98789c315972", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 122, "token_count": 297, "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7813c836-07ca-4129-b01e-5064d3d9e08d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "f5f9d0d676b8ef6cb1e32c6cf8403ab6e5e1ed73daca29fb9a38f56c3aa9a4f8", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "f7695977-d2b4-4b3d-a039-98789c315972", "text": "Table 8 Results at Week 24 from a Placebo-Controlled Trial for JARDIANCE in Combination with Metformin and Sulfonylurea\n\n|                                                  | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=225   | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=216   | Placebo N=225   |\n|--------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|-------------------------|-----------------|\n| HbA1c (%) a                                      |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                  | 8.1                     | 8.1                     | 8.2             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)             | -0.8                    | -0.8                    | -0.2            |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI) | -0.6 b (-0.8, -0.5)     | -0.6 b (-0.7, -0.4)     | --              |\n| Patients [n (%)] achieving HbA1c <7%             | 55 (26%)                | 65 (32%)                | 20 (9%)         |\n| FPG (mg/dL) c                                    |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                  | 151                     | 156"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5a4f7421-22cb-4100-97d7-a25fc5c73a19", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 123, "token_count": 298, "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7813c836-07ca-4129-b01e-5064d3d9e08d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "563ce446beeb1a1f4a749b451ab48302243f88efedb3641582eddaa3bc35e502", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "5a4f7421-22cb-4100-97d7-a25fc5c73a19", "text": "|                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                  | 151                     | 156                     | 152             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)             | -23                     | -23                     | 6               |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean)          | -29                     | -29                     | --              |\n| Body Weight                                      |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline mean in kg                              | 77                      | 78                      | 76              |\n| % change from baseline (adjusted mean)           | -2.9                    | -3.2                    | -0.5            |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI) | -2.4 b (-3.0, -1.8)     | -2.7 b (-3.3, -2.1)     | --              |\n\na Modified intent-to-treat population.  Last observation on trial (LOCF) was used to impute missing data at Week 24.  At Week 24, 17.8%, 16.7%, and 25.3% was imputed for patients randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, and placebo, respectively.\n\nb ANCOVA p-value &lt;0.0001"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:52c05028-d494-4e4a-8199-db6c0fd99ea6", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 124, "token_count": 113, "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7813c836-07ca-4129-b01e-5064d3d9e08d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "41de6f1905d51b06609a09997fd981e0cc83cfc7222615ad669c0557ce4050cc", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "52c05028-d494-4e4a-8199-db6c0fd99ea6", "text": "8%, 16.7%, and 25.3% was imputed for patients randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, and placebo, respectively.\n\nb ANCOVA p-value &lt;0.0001 (HbA1c: ANCOVA model includes baseline HbA1c, treatment, renal function, and region.  Body weight and FPG: same model used as for HbA1c but additionally including baseline body weight/baseline FPG, respectively.) c FPG (mg/dL); for JARDIANCE 10 mg, n=225, for JARDIANCE 25 mg, n=215, for placebo, n=224"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:beccd1d4-a43b-4817-91f7-a354b85daa00", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 125, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "49794be1-b6f1-40d3-b963-0d7a73c90dce", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "f31e564c0c6faf1f1867508b955dc696bfc7c435a56f9fa96e66757515d14850", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "beccd1d4-a43b-4817-91f7-a354b85daa00", "text": "A total of 686 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus participated in a double-blind, active-controlled trial to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg in combination with linagliptin 5 mg compared to the individual components.\n\nPatients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on at least 1,500 mg of metformin per day entered a single-blind placebo run-in period for 2 weeks. At the end of the run-in period, patients who remained inadequately controlled and had an HbA1c between 7% and 10.5% were randomized 1:1:1:1:1 to one of 5 active-treatment arms of JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg, linagliptin 5 mg, or linagliptin 5 mg in combination with 10 mg or 25 mg JARDIANCE as a fixed-dose combination tablet.\n\nAt Week 24, JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg used in combination with linagliptin 5 mg provided statistically significant improvement in HbA1c (p-value &lt;0.0001) and FPG (p-value &lt;0.001) compared to the individual components in patients who had been inadequately controlled on metformin. Treatment with JARDIANCE/linagliptin 25 mg/5 mg or JARDIANCE/linagliptin 10 mg/5 mg daily also resulted in a statistically significant reduction in body weight compared to linagliptin 5"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8b3914b2-cd8a-4751-b37f-3c2f14b748c9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 126, "token_count": 67, "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "49794be1-b6f1-40d3-b963-0d7a73c90dce", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "c4a82ff9f57aa49b3ed0765a90eb942bbaa04b259e08e80dc3b4cd0f47a4eef6", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "8b3914b2-cd8a-4751-b37f-3c2f14b748c9", "text": "25 mg/5 mg or JARDIANCE/linagliptin 10 mg/5 mg daily also resulted in a statistically significant reduction in body weight compared to linagliptin 5 mg (p-value &lt;0.0001). There was no statistically significant difference in body weight compared to JARDIANCE alone."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2825ee5f-c72c-4cca-9ffe-5fab8d4cda08", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 127, "token_count": 176, "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "0a241a31-9700-46ed-b899-41172af63339", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "15eaa6054155355b79a117353fe95e93c02de3905fb9d2467c73e49737795f80", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "2825ee5f-c72c-4cca-9ffe-5fab8d4cda08", "text": "The efficacy of JARDIANCE was evaluated in a double-blind, glimepiride-controlled, trial in 1,545 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus with insufficient glycemic control despite metformin therapy.\n\nPatients with inadequate glycemic control and an HbA1c between 7% and 10% after a 2-week run-in period were randomized to glimepiride or JARDIANCE 25 mg.\n\nAt Week 52, JARDIANCE 25 mg and glimepiride lowered HbA1c and FPG (see Table 9, Figure 4).  The difference in observed effect size between JARDIANCE 25 mg and glimepiride excluded the pre-specified non- inferiority margin of 0.3%.  The mean daily dosage of glimepiride was 2.7 mg and the maximal approved dosage in the United States is 8 mg per day."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8cac6a46-cb0b-44c9-af11-bc47ede00ef9", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 128, "token_count": 297, "page_number": 25, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "93decd45-6be5-4208-af22-2cc182378675", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "de393224e3e630c40c8887e2e3a10ca39558ceba051bd38e3710d7fd31f6b281", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "8cac6a46-cb0b-44c9-af11-bc47ede00ef9", "text": "Table 9 Results at Week 52 from an Active-Controlled Trial Comparing JARDIANCE to Glimepiride as Add-On Therapy in Patients Inadequately Controlled on Metformin\n\n|                                                        | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=765   | Glimepiride N=780   |\n|--------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|---------------------|\n| HbA1c (%) a                                            |                         |                     |\n| Baseline (mean)                                        | 7.9                     | 7.9                 |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)                   | -0.7                    | -0.7                |\n| Difference from glimepiride (adjusted mean) (97.5% CI) | -0.07 b (-0.15, 0.01)   | --                  |\n| FPG (mg/dL) d                                          |                         |                     |\n| Baseline (mean)                                        | 150                     | 150                 |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)                   | -19                     | -9                  |\n| Difference from glimepiride (adjusted mean)            | -11"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:684ba72b-63a0-4b81-a467-80200d5d3132", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 129, "token_count": 152, "page_number": 25, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "93decd45-6be5-4208-af22-2cc182378675", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "6926e740535915ea73a4a098a245b57778569489a78ae7cc1506bfd339871ef4", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "684ba72b-63a0-4b81-a467-80200d5d3132", "text": "mean)                   | -19                     | -9                  |\n| Difference from glimepiride (adjusted mean)            | -11                     | --                  |\n| Body Weight                                            |                         |                     |\n| Baseline mean in kg                                    | 82.5                    | 83                  |\n| % change from baseline (adjusted mean)                 | -3.9                    | 2.0                 |\n| Difference from glimepiride (adjusted mean) (95% CI)   | -5.9 c (-6.3, -5.5)     | --                  |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:82af0cd8-e8f1-43e4-97f9-3dcc821d95ba", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 130, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "6921c4f8-c30e-4354-8ca7-5d99328df9ec", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a8ab09ebb6d2a7f1ff4c84a610f90f342db3db6976e67230ebe3d963709fdd8f", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "82af0cd8-e8f1-43e4-97f9-3dcc821d95ba", "text": "Figure 4 Adjusted mean HbA1c Change at Each Time Point (Completers) and at Week 52 (mITT Population) - LOCF\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n*Mean change from baseline adjusted for baseline HbA1c, geographical region, and eGFR at baseline.\n\nAt Week 52, the adjusted mean change from baseline in systolic blood pressure was -3.6 mmHg, compared to 2.2 mmHg for glimepiride.  The differences between treatment groups for systolic blood pressure was statistically significant (p-value &lt;0.0001).\n\nAt Week 104, the adjusted mean change from baseline in HbA1c was -0.75% for JARDIANCE 25 mg and -0.66% for glimepiride. The adjusted mean treatment difference was -0.09% with a 97.5% confidence interval of (-0.32%, 0.15%), excluding the pre-specified non-inferiority margin of 0.3%.  The mean daily dosage of glimepiride was 2.7 mg and the maximal approved dosage in the United States is 8 mg per day. The Week 104 analysis included data with and without concomitant glycemic rescue medication, as well as off-treatment data. Missing data for patients not providing any information at the visit were imputed based on the observed offtreatment data.  In this multiple imputation analysis, 13.9% of the data were imputed fo"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:28fa3dc7-94f6-440f-b879-d3755c5aeb6b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 131, "token_count": 109, "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "6921c4f8-c30e-4354-8ca7-5d99328df9ec", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "b1ba7414a56e41702000d854dac7457bf8f1e2212637a19ae400957a2deed9cb", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "28fa3dc7-94f6-440f-b879-d3755c5aeb6b", "text": "nformation at the visit were imputed based on the observed offtreatment data.  In this multiple imputation analysis, 13.9% of the data were imputed for JARDIANCE 25 mg and 12.9% for glimepiride.\n\nAt Week 104, JARDIANCE 25 mg daily resulted in a statistically significant difference in change from baseline for body weight compared to glimepiride (-3.1 kg for JARDIANCE 25 mg vs. +1.3 kg for glimepiride; ANCOVA-LOCF, p-value &lt;0.0001)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2fe0d0ab-fb90-497d-9ae6-69ea3de63e96", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 132, "token_count": 296, "page_number": 27, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "720db087-1b90-4fb5-be02-ed9b6f5cfb50", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "69e43bb71a565cb131ebbe2412c884087d78112c88bda8e156a467f9f6a91c05", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "2fe0d0ab-fb90-497d-9ae6-69ea3de63e96", "text": "A total of 498 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus participated in a double-blind, placebo-controlled trial to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE in combination with pioglitazone, with or without metformin.\n\nPatients with inadequately controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus on metformin at a dose of at least 1,500 mg per day and pioglitazone at a dose of at least 30 mg per day were placed into an open-label placebo run-in for 2 weeks.  Patients with inadequate glycemic control and an HbA1c between 7% and 10% after the run-in period were randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, or JARDIANCE 25 mg.\n\nTreatment with JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg daily resulted in statistically significant reductions in HbA1c (pvalue &lt;0.0001), FPG, and body weight compared with placebo (see Table 10).\n\nTable 10 Results of Placebo-Controlled Trial for JARDIANCE in Combination Therapy with Pioglitazone\n\n|                                                                   | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=165   | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=168   | Placebo N=165   |\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|-------------------------|-----------------|\n| HbA1c (%) a"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1607cf53-465f-4cb7-97a2-9b0fc1512e7c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 133, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 27, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "720db087-1b90-4fb5-be02-ed9b6f5cfb50", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "69cd3e44f52dc02994eac081bbae9f120bd188628bdfb8cafd55a45abc6928b2", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "1607cf53-465f-4cb7-97a2-9b0fc1512e7c", "text": "-----------------------------------------------|-------------------------|-------------------------|-----------------|\n| HbA1c (%) a                                                       |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                                   | 8.1                     | 8.1                     | 8.2             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)                              | -0.6                    | -0.7                    | -0.1            |\n| Difference from placebo + pioglitazone (adjusted mean) (95% CI)   | -0.5 b (-0.7, -0.3)     | -0.6 b (-0.8, -0.4)     | --              |\n| Patients [n (%)] achieving HbA1c <7%                              | 36 (24%)                | 48 (30%)                | 12 (8%)         |\n| FPG (mg/dL) c                                                     |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                                   | 152                     | 152                     | 152             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)                              | -17                     | -22"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:901e47bc-cbf5-4db4-a4b9-436a03eb68da", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 134, "token_count": 221, "page_number": 27, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "720db087-1b90-4fb5-be02-ed9b6f5cfb50", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "797e555cec2062b0a5a7852a55d465851893f9f178f5583550188ff1ebd16815", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "901e47bc-cbf5-4db4-a4b9-436a03eb68da", "text": "| 152                     | 152             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)                              | -17                     | -22                     | 7               |\n| Difference from placebo + pioglitazone (adjusted mean) (97.5% CI) | -23 b (-31.8, -15.2)    | -28 b (-36.7, -20.2)    | --              |\n| Body Weight                                                       |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline mean in kg                                               | 78                      | 79                      | 78              |\n| % change from baseline (adjusted mean)                            | -2.0                    | -1.8                    | 0.6             |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI)                  | -2.6 b (-3.4, -1.8)     | -2.4 b (-3.2, -1.6)     | --              |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b8be4914-2d1a-48eb-9402-8b120d6e7a5e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 135, "token_count": 235, "page_number": 27, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "2f964092-1915-4e95-9f8d-893d45c8e24f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "be742e33fba2f45bf9a2f9b942514d2b07b3460ca2a6eb3974ef9e1bd4ca2c97", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b8be4914-2d1a-48eb-9402-8b120d6e7a5e", "text": "A total of 494 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on insulin, or insulin in combination with oral drugs participated in a double-blind, placebo-controlled trial to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE as add-on therapy to insulin over 78 weeks.\n\nPatients entered a 2-week placebo run-in period on basal insulin (e.g., insulin glargine, insulin detemir, or NPH insulin) with or without metformin and/or sulfonylurea background therapy. Following the run-in period, patients with inadequate glycemic control were randomized to the addition of JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, or placebo. Patients were maintained on a stable dose of insulin prior to enrollment, during the run-in period, and during the first 18 weeks of treatment.  For the remaining 60 weeks, insulin could be adjusted. The mean total daily insulin dose at baseline for JARDIANCE 10 mg, 25 mg, and placebo was 45 IU, 48 IU, and 48 IU, respectively."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9af1ed1a-c34d-4e61-ac03-cab6654f9c88", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 136, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ebe7f2b9-9425-4bf2-8bde-1df3419b96b8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "e5ca277bac8417c09c439e2ef5f931da03f4d3e3ce74738600a6bfa6e31bcd47", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9af1ed1a-c34d-4e61-ac03-cab6654f9c88", "text": "JARDIANCE used in combination with insulin (with or without metformin and/or sulfonylurea) provided statistically significant reductions in HbA1c and FPG compared to placebo after both 18 and 78 weeks of treatment (see Table 11). JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg daily also resulted in statistically significantly greater percent body weight reduction compared to placebo.\n\nTable 11 Results at Week 18 and 78 for a Placebo-Controlled Trial for JARDIANCE in Combination with Insulin\n\n|                                                    | 18 weeks (no insulin adjustment)   | 18 weeks (no insulin adjustment)   | 18 weeks (no insulin adjustment)   | 78 weeks (adjustable insulin dose after 18 weeks)   | 78 weeks (adjustable insulin dose after 18 weeks)   | 78 weeks (adjustable insulin dose after 18 weeks)   |\n|----------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------|------------------------------------|------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|\n|                                                    | JARDIANCE 10 m"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b5e01162-4c32-40c3-9b6d-9cc5cac07226", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 137, "token_count": 299, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ebe7f2b9-9425-4bf2-8bde-1df3419b96b8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "0c315e28280d293a524a5312abbae23cf16a8df06563bed0e1dfb1f9bf01cde8", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b5e01162-4c32-40c3-9b6d-9cc5cac07226", "text": "-------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|\n|                                                    | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=169              | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=155              | Placebo N=170                      | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=169                               | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=155                               | Placebo N=170                                       |\n| HbA1c (%) a                                        |                                    |                                    |                                    |                                                     |                                                     |                                                     |\n| Baseline (mean)                                    | 8.3                                | 8.3                                | 8.2                                | 8.3                                                 | 8.3                                                 | 8.2                                                 |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)               | -0.6                               | -0.7                               | 0"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d1430976-5bf4-4381-8211-14c7448db4cc", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 138, "token_count": 288, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ebe7f2b9-9425-4bf2-8bde-1df3419b96b8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5ff08b956e542cce06ea700356d9fbbcdc745d32a6b80c69d0c648bafc052114", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "d1430976-5bf4-4381-8211-14c7448db4cc", "text": "|\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)               | -0.6                               | -0.7                               | 0                                  | -0.4                                                | -0.6                                                | 0.1                                                 |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (97.5% CI) | -0.6 b (-0.8, -0.4)                | -0.7 b (-0.9, -0.5)                | --                                 | -0.5 b (-0.7, -0.3)                                 | -0.7 b (-0.9, -0.5)                                 | --                                                  |\n| Patients (%) achieving HbA1c <7%                   | 18.0                               | 19.5                               | 5.5                                | 12.0                                                | 17.5                                                | 6.7                                                 |\n| FPG (mg/dL)                                        |                                    |                                    |                                    |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3522a6aa-2cc3-493a-a519-c6b291b6f189", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 139, "token_count": 293, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ebe7f2b9-9425-4bf2-8bde-1df3419b96b8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "469bf10c11a5cb2139f4094447be84d9b4327fe137a3ac71b37e7a83c1358dcb", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "3522a6aa-2cc3-493a-a519-c6b291b6f189", "text": "|                                    |                                    |                                    |                                                     |                                                     |                                                     |\n| Baseline (mean)                                    | 138                                | 146                                | 142                                | 138                                                 | 146                                                 | 142                                                 |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean, SE)           | -17.9 (3.2)                        | -19.1 (3.3)                        | 10.4 (3.1)                         | -10.1 (3.2)                                         | -15.2 (3.4)                                         | 2.8 (3.2)                                           |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI)   | -28.2 b (-37.0, -19.5)             | -29.5 b (-38.4, -20.6)             | --                                 | -12.9 c (-21.9, 3.9)                                | -17.9 b (-27.0, -8.8)"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1649249f-82f9-418b-b4b4-ce0713d92b4a", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 140, "token_count": 298, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ebe7f2b9-9425-4bf2-8bde-1df3419b96b8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "4b7e21b2e71b8d19f9035ed0cd7812b4fd8fbcf8f87ddc35592f83893258c958", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "1649249f-82f9-418b-b4b4-ce0713d92b4a", "text": "| --                                 | -12.9 c (-21.9, 3.9)                                | -17.9 b (-27.0, -8.8)                               | --                                                  |\n| Body Weight                                        |                                    |                                    |                                    |                                                     |                                                     |                                                     |\n| Baseline mean in kg                                | 92                                 | 95                                 | 90                                 | 92                                                  | 95                                                  | 90                                                  |\n| % change from baseline (adjusted mean)             | -1.8                               | -1.4                               | -0.1                               | -2.4                                                | -2.4                                                | 0.7                                                 |\n| Dif"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6861ec81-f833-4a8c-b771-d7eee515a622", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 141, "token_count": 291, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ebe7f2b9-9425-4bf2-8bde-1df3419b96b8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "c859d49271d916d3cff1d4de6bfe288d3d1aa6f111f261efcad6d3f11f97f6f9", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "6861ec81-f833-4a8c-b771-d7eee515a622", "text": "| -2.4                                                | 0.7                                                 |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI)   | -1.7 d (-3.0, -0.5)                | -1.3 e (-2.5, -0.0)                | --                                 | -3.0 b (-4.4, -1.7)                                 | -3.0 b (-4.4, -1.6)                                 | --                                                  |\n\na Modified intent-to-treat population.  Last observation on trial (LOCF) was used to impute missing data at Week 18 and 78.  At Week 18, 21.3%, 30.3%, and 21.8% was imputed for patients randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, and placebo, respectively.  At Week 78, 32.5%, 38.1% and 42.4% was imputed for patients randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, and placebo, respectively.\n\nb ANCOVA p-value &lt;0.0001 (HbA1c: ANCOVA model includes baseline HbA1c, treatment, and region; FPG: MMRM model includes baseline FPG, baseline HbA1c, treatment, region, visit and visit by treatment interaction.  Body weight: MMRM model includes baseline body weight, baseline HbA1c, treatment, region, visit and visit by treat"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:baa59bc5-e0ba-4783-9e0e-e6eb30587c40", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 142, "token_count": 55, "page_number": 28, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ebe7f2b9-9425-4bf2-8bde-1df3419b96b8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "6d7a8c8f22b28d9e2b2988d7c29b197d2aa13bd2105d6f55264a5a9167be1318", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "baa59bc5-e0ba-4783-9e0e-e6eb30587c40", "text": "nd visit by treatment interaction.  Body weight: MMRM model includes baseline body weight, baseline HbA1c, treatment, region, visit and visit by treatment interaction.\n\nc p-value=0.0049\n\nd p-value=0.0052\n\ne p-value=0.0463"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c48def9a-29bd-42fe-ac5d-ea06a7043d95", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 143, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 29, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "86478f4e-897e-41f8-8bfe-7728bfbe57b1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "2d4709c831c62153ab9889e2f47e8e66d1448f1371b26497102022be9a94095c", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c48def9a-29bd-42fe-ac5d-ea06a7043d95", "text": "A total of 563 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on multiple daily injections (MDI) of insulin (total daily dose &gt;60 IU), alone or in combination with metformin, participated in a double-blind, placebo-controlled trial to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE as add-on therapy to MDI insulin over 18 weeks.\n\nPatients entered a 2-week placebo run-in period on MDI insulin with or without metformin background therapy. Following the run-in period, patients with inadequate glycemic control were randomized to the addition of JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, or placebo. Patients were maintained on a stable dose of insulin prior to enrollment, during the run-in period, and during the first 18 weeks of treatment. The mean total daily insulin dose at baseline for JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, and placebo was 88.6 IU, 90.4 IU, and 89.9 IU, respectively.\n\nJARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg daily used in combination with MDI insulin (with or without metformin) provided statistically significant reductions in HbA1c compared to placebo after 18 weeks of treatment (see Table 12).\n\nTable 12 Results at Week 18 for a Placebo-Controlled Trial for JARDIANCE in Combination with In"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e528d650-e8cd-449d-8f42-b63b5820a7f8", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 144, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 29, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "86478f4e-897e-41f8-8bfe-7728bfbe57b1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "bb49f630a524a0ed11e52bc055883d996fab6fb121e921462f0579a4ae9fe4b3", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "e528d650-e8cd-449d-8f42-b63b5820a7f8", "text": "o placebo after 18 weeks of treatment (see Table 12).\n\nTable 12 Results at Week 18 for a Placebo-Controlled Trial for JARDIANCE in Combination with Insulin and with or without Metformin\n\n|                                                  | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=186   | JARDIANCE 25 mg N=189   | Placebo N=188   |\n|--------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|-------------------------|-----------------|\n| HbA1c (%) a                                      |                         |                         |                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                  | 8.4                     | 8.3                     | 8.3             |\n| Change from baseline (adjusted mean)             | -0.9                    | -1.0                    | -0.5            |\n| Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI) | -0.4 b (-0.6, -0.3)     | -0.5 b (-0.7, -0.4)     | --              |\n\na Modified intent-to-treat population.  Last observation on trial (LOCF) was used to impute missing data at Week 18.  At Week 18, 23.7%, 22.8% and 23.4% was imputed for patients randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, and placebo, respectively.\n\nb ANCOVA p-value &lt"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cdce0379-901f-4a1d-b645-28229b05962f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 145, "token_count": 196, "page_number": 29, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "86478f4e-897e-41f8-8bfe-7728bfbe57b1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "428d4d8e6857e5e5bb29d8c1e343b01c3b87efc9a430319370fea71f1da0eda0", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "cdce0379-901f-4a1d-b645-28229b05962f", "text": "k 18, 23.7%, 22.8% and 23.4% was imputed for patients randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg, JARDIANCE 25 mg, and placebo, respectively.\n\nb ANCOVA p-value &lt;0.0001 (HbA1c: ANCOVA model includes baseline HbA1c, treatment, renal function, geographical region, and background medication).\n\nDuring an extension period with treatment for up to 52 weeks, insulin could be adjusted to achieve defined glucose target levels. The change from baseline in HbA1c was maintained from 18 to 52 weeks with both JARDIANCE 10 mg and 25 mg. After 52 weeks, JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg daily resulted in statistically greater percent body weight reduction compared to placebo (p-value &lt;0.0001). The mean change in body weight from baseline was -1.95 kg for JARDIANCE 10 mg, and -2.04 kg for JARDIANCE 25 mg."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:10783c5e-f3ad-469a-8ec9-b4851f7de938", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 146, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 29, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "2360abe8-468f-437a-bcae-2790234c0646", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "5787a53890424bc92f8af09685f49135bae80445b5ee463aff89381dbd9382ac", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "10783c5e-f3ad-469a-8ec9-b4851f7de938", "text": "A total of 738 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and a baseline eGFR less than 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 participated in a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, parallel-group trial to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and renal impairment.  The trial population comprised of 290 patients with mild renal impairment (eGFR 60 to less than 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ), 374 patients with moderate renal impairment (eGFR 30 to less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ), and 74 with severe renal impairment (eGFR less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ). A total of 194 patients with moderate renal impairment had a baseline eGFR of 30 to less than 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 and 180 patients had a baseline eGFR of 45 to less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .\n\nAt Week 24, JARDIANCE 25 mg provided statistically significant reduction in HbA1c relative to placebo in patients with mild to moderate renal impairment (see Table 13). A statistically significant reduction relative to placebo was also observed with JARDIANCE 25 mg in patients with either mild [-0.7 (95% CI: -0.9, -0.5)] or moderate [-0.4 (95% CI: -0.6, -0.3)] renal impairment and with JARDIANCE 10 mg in patients with mild [-0.5 (95%"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:50140ab9-ef91-41ac-8eba-69bda3ba0609", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 147, "token_count": 46, "page_number": 29, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "2360abe8-468f-437a-bcae-2790234c0646", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "6ad8e7d27740d8cf7c64a0441e705747845ab8e7bc24ad2e76ed81033c746431", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "50140ab9-ef91-41ac-8eba-69bda3ba0609", "text": "r mild [-0.7 (95% CI: -0.9, -0.5)] or moderate [-0.4 (95% CI: -0.6, -0.3)] renal impairment and with JARDIANCE 10 mg in patients with mild [-0.5 (95% CI: -0.7, -0.3)] renal impairment."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ac33bdf9-29ad-4f0d-81aa-0445fac4ba05", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 148, "token_count": 299, "page_number": 30, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "a464c0ff-2705-44be-9999-d15c29867182", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "2b2749eaa3591c7b3cf938616e3ba67ae34aede76d7e9b0e5b1e2c3f2d8d0efd", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "ac33bdf9-29ad-4f0d-81aa-0445fac4ba05", "text": "The glucose lowering efficacy of JARDIANCE 25 mg decreased with decreasing level of renal function in the mild to moderate range. Least square mean HbA1c changes at 24 weeks were -0.6%, -0.5%, and -0.2% for those with a baseline eGFR of 60 to less than 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 45 to less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , and 30 to less than 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ,  respectively [see Dosage and Administration (2) and Use in Specific Populations (8.6)] . For placebo, least square mean HbA1c changes at 24 weeks were 0.1%, -0.1%, and 0.2% for patients with a baseline eGFR of 60 to less than 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 45 to less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , and 30 to less than 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ,  respectively.\n\nTable 13 Results at Week 24 (LOCF) of Placebo-Controlled Trial for JARDIANCE in Adults with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus and Renal Impairment\n\n|                                                | Mild and Moderate Impairment b   |\n|------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|\n|                                                | JARDIANCE 25 mg                  |\n| HbA1c                                          |                                  |\n| Number of patients"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2192c2fe-145e-45de-b258-fe54b6138e9d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 149, "token_count": 299, "page_number": 30, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "a464c0ff-2705-44be-9999-d15c29867182", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "985cfa87c0fef0b596c9329ce6af3a0b9400547dbcf7d3c4c2e39a88efb84e38", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "2192c2fe-145e-45de-b258-fe54b6138e9d", "text": "| JARDIANCE 25 mg                  |\n| HbA1c                                          |                                  |\n| Number of patients                             | n=284                            |\n| Comparison vs placebo (adjusted mean) (95% CI) | -0.5 a (-0.6, -0.4)              |\n\na p-value &lt;0.0001 (HbA1c: ANCOVA model includes baseline HbA1c, treatment, renal function, and background medication) b eGFR 30 to less than 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2  - Modified intent-to-treat population. Last observation on trial (LOCF) was used to impute missing data at Week 24.  At Week 24, 24.6% and 26.2% was imputed for patients randomized to JARDIANCE 25 mg and placebo, respectively.\n\nFor patients with severe renal impairment, the analyses of changes in HbA1c and FPG showed no discernible treatment effect of JARDIANCE 25 mg compared to placebo [see Indications and Usage (1), Dosage and Administration (2.1, 2.2) and Use in Specific Populations (8.6)] .\n\n14.2 Glycemic Control Trial in Pediatric Patients Aged 10 to 17 Years with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus DINAMO (NCT03429543) was a 26-week, double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled, parallel group trial, with a double-blind active trea"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:90f997f2-5ae8-402f-ae78-4caf09415537", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 150, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 30, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "a464c0ff-2705-44be-9999-d15c29867182", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "dba9e76fff8cae5c96dcebbcfbe13905d07b3fa5ac62881febfe0821ba850a95", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "90f997f2-5ae8-402f-ae78-4caf09415537", "text": "betes Mellitus DINAMO (NCT03429543) was a 26-week, double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled, parallel group trial, with a double-blind active treatment safety extension period up to 52 weeks to assess the efficacy of JARDIANCE. The trial enrolled pediatric patients aged 10 to 17 years with inadequately controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus (HbA1c 6.5 to 10.5%). Patients treated with metformin (at least 1,000 mg daily or maximally tolerated dose), with or without insulin therapy, and those with a history of intolerance to metformin therapy were enrolled. Patients were randomized to 3 treatment arms (JARDIANCE 10 mg, a dipeptidyl peptidase-4 (DPP-4) inhibitor or placebo), over 26 weeks. Patients in the JARDIANCE 10 mg group who failed to achieve HbA1c &lt;7.0% at Week 12 underwent a second randomization at Week 14 to remain on the 10 mg dose or increase to 25 mg. Patients on placebo were re-randomized at Week 26 to one of the JARDIANCE doses (10 mg or 25 mg) or a DPP-4 inhibitor.\n\nA total of 157 patients were treated with either JARDIANCE (10 mg or 25 mg; N=52), a DPP-4 inhibitor (N=52), or placebo (N=53). Background therapies as adjunct to diet and exercise included metformin (51%"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9e328a0b-1a3e-4be5-9b02-fb0f53ee3ab0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 151, "token_count": 222, "page_number": 30, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "a464c0ff-2705-44be-9999-d15c29867182", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a3929285d2e6dff2d5f24aca1a2c2ff4ba0b7a6cf82956b4fccb8b2b451d261b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9e328a0b-1a3e-4be5-9b02-fb0f53ee3ab0", "text": "ANCE (10 mg or 25 mg; N=52), a DPP-4 inhibitor (N=52), or placebo (N=53). Background therapies as adjunct to diet and exercise included metformin (51%), a combination of metformin and insulin (40.1%), insulin (3.2%), or none (5.7%). The mean HbA1c at baseline was 8.0% and the mean duration of type 2 diabetes mellitus was 2.1 years. The mean age was 14.5 years (range: 10-17 years) and 51.6% were aged 15 years and older. Approximately, 50% were White, 6% were Asian, 31% were Black or African American, and 38% were of Hispanic or Latino ethnicity. The mean BMI was 36.0 kg/m 2 and mean BMI Z-score was 3.0. Patients with an eGFR less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 were not enrolled in the trial. Approximately 25% of the study population had microalbuminuria or macroalbuminuria.\n\nAt Week 26, treatment with JARDIANCE was superior in reducing HbA1c from baseline versus placebo (see Table 14)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6fd64bbd-0aeb-4431-a767-d3bc25848b58", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 152, "token_count": 296, "page_number": 31, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "21bb1e43-cff4-479d-9d0e-900642548a72", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "69c3e4d96f2e0464125c650c96814f3f4bf1898b19b7f1af5dab91254ae23624", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "6fd64bbd-0aeb-4431-a767-d3bc25848b58", "text": "Table 14 Results at Week 26 for a Placebo-Controlled Trial for JARDIANCE in Combination with Metformin and/or Insulin or as Monotherapy in Pediatric Patients Aged 10 to 17 Years with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus a\n\n|                                    | JARDIANCE 10 mg and 25 mg   | Placebo   |\n|------------------------------------|-----------------------------|-----------|\n| HbA1c (%) b                        |                             |           |\n| Number of patients                 | n=52                        | n=53      |\n| Baseline (mean)                    | 8.0                         | 8.1       |\n| Change from baseline c             | -0.2                        | 0.7       |\n| Difference from placebo c (95% CI) | -0.8 e (-1.5, -0.2)         | --        |\n| FPG (mg/dL) b,d                    |                             |           |\n| Number of patients                 | n=48                        | n=52      |\n| Baseline (mean)                    | 154                         | 159       |\n| Change from baseline c             | -19                         | 17        |\n| Difference from placebo c (95% CI) | -36 (-60.7, -10.7)          | --        |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b57c67e9-590b-4320-931e-426e52eeadcd", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 153, "token_count": 31, "page_number": 31, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "21bb1e43-cff4-479d-9d0e-900642548a72", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "0b13e3896d1509e69b0c21645d1b6e2a61d3fbc5fc7a40e4a36701c60cab060e", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b57c67e9-590b-4320-931e-426e52eeadcd", "text": "| -19                         | 17        |\n| Difference from placebo c (95% CI) | -36 (-60.7, -10.7)          | --        |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1912a60a-70f4-48ed-9c4c-d60f6a4d9b91", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 154, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 31, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "60a8f800-fc0a-48cf-9014-998161e169e6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ca38b0ebd455bfdb403efed0b03530df2c2e1ca8216dfbcdd67b347cf9356c9f", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "1912a60a-70f4-48ed-9c4c-d60f6a4d9b91", "text": "The effect of JARDIANCE on cardiovascular (CV) risk in adult patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus and established, stable, atherosclerotic CV disease was evaluated in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial, a multicenter, multinational, randomized, double-blind parallel group trial.  The trial compared the risk of experiencing a major adverse cardiovascular event (MACE) between JARDIANCE and placebo when these were added to and used concomitantly with standard of care treatments for diabetes mellitus and atherosclerotic CV disease. Concomitant antidiabetic medications were to be kept stable for the first 12 weeks of the trial. Thereafter, antidiabetic and atherosclerotic therapies could be adjusted, at the discretion of investigators, to ensure participants were treated according to the standard care for these diseases.\n\nA total of 7,020 patients were treated (JARDIANCE 10 mg = 2,345; JARDIANCE 25 mg = 2,342; placebo = 2,333) and followed for a median of 3.1 years. Approximately 72% of the trial population was White, 22% was Asian, and 5% was Black. The mean age was 63 years and approximately 72% were male.\n\nAll patients in the trial had inadequately controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus at ba"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9a56b85a-b0ec-4532-994a-0a15915cb5ec", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 155, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 31, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "60a8f800-fc0a-48cf-9014-998161e169e6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "66a5a96b67bcd6fca2da71539521a8c6f9883d2c453fad3019ff4b64510f4e92", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9a56b85a-b0ec-4532-994a-0a15915cb5ec", "text": "lack. The mean age was 63 years and approximately 72% were male.\n\nAll patients in the trial had inadequately controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus at baseline (HbA1c greater than or equal to 7%). The mean HbA1c at baseline was 8.1% and 57% of participants had diabetes mellitus for more than 10 years. Approximately 31%, 22% and 20% reported a past history of neuropathy, retinopathy and nephropathy to investigators, respectively and the mean eGFR was 74 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . At baseline, patients were treated with one (~30%) or more (~70%) antidiabetic medications including metformin (74%), insulin (48%), and sulfonylurea (43%).\n\nAll patients had established atherosclerotic CV disease at baseline including one (82%) or more (18%) of the following: a documented history of coronary artery disease (76%), stroke (23%) or peripheral artery disease (21%). At baseline, the mean systolic blood pressure was 136 mmHg, the mean diastolic blood pressure was 76 mmHg, the mean LDL was 86 mg/dL, the mean HDL was 44 mg/dL, and the mean urinary albumin to creatinine ratio (UACR) was 175 mg/g. At baseline, approximately 81% of patients were treated with renin angiotensin system inhibitors, 65% with beta-blo"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a9f71278-5e62-4b6a-81d6-e4fefdc7108c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 156, "token_count": 61, "page_number": 31, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "60a8f800-fc0a-48cf-9014-998161e169e6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "bbaf469df983126065d2cae71f87456d14d6e27233708f23078d6bd0bbeeede8", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "a9f71278-5e62-4b6a-81d6-e4fefdc7108c", "text": "atinine ratio (UACR) was 175 mg/g. At baseline, approximately 81% of patients were treated with renin angiotensin system inhibitors, 65% with beta-blockers, 43% with diuretics, 77% with statins, and 86% with antiplatelet agents (mostly aspirin)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5864a06b-70ba-4018-b4a4-29b4cc48e2ee", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 157, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 32, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "aa122e32-acb0-4ed0-b8cb-402045f53ab7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "b5859c44807e16c4ad5ea558be736ee1149fa22a9f7f2316a8c0950e6941a8be", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "5864a06b-70ba-4018-b4a4-29b4cc48e2ee", "text": "The primary endpoint in EMPA-REG OUTCOME was the time to first occurrence of a Major Adverse Cardiac Event (MACE).  A major adverse cardiac event was defined as occurrence of either a CV death or a non-fatal myocardial infarction (MI) or a non-fatal stroke.  The statistical analysis plan had pre-specified that the 10 and 25 mg doses would be combined.  A Cox proportional hazards model was used to test for non-inferiority against the pre-specified risk margin of 1.3 for the hazard ratio of MACE and superiority on MACE if non-inferiority was demonstrated. Type-1 error was controlled across multiples tests using a hierarchical testing strategy.\n\nJARDIANCE significantly reduced the risk of first occurrence of primary composite endpoint of CV death, non-fatal myocardial infarction, or non-fatal stroke (HR: 0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99).  The treatment effect was due to a significant reduction in the risk of CV death in subjects randomized to empagliflozin (HR: 0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77), with no change in the risk of non-fatal myocardial infarction or non-fatal stroke (see Table 15 and Figures 5 and 6).  Results for the 10 mg and 25 mg empagliflozin dosages were consistent with results for t"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:44eec7c8-c635-4bf4-86f2-7a067b2ea827", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 158, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 32, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "aa122e32-acb0-4ed0-b8cb-402045f53ab7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "1c9d5928efcdd969abdb0c6a227e02153e75d6e20f79235dd171bdd38a8e3dca", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "44eec7c8-c635-4bf4-86f2-7a067b2ea827", "text": "tion or non-fatal stroke (see Table 15 and Figures 5 and 6).  Results for the 10 mg and 25 mg empagliflozin dosages were consistent with results for the combined dosage groups.\n\nTable 15 Treatment Effect for the Primary Composite Endpoint and its Components a\n\n|                                                                                                       | Placebo N=2,333   | JARDIANCE N=4,687   | Hazard ratio vs placebo (95% CI)   |\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|---------------------|------------------------------------|\n| Composite of CV death, non-fatal myocardial infarction, non-fatal stroke (time to first occurrence) b | 282 (12.1%)       | 490 (10.5%)         | 0.86 (0.74, 0.99)                  |\n| Non-fatal myocardial infarction c                                                                     | 121 (5.2%)        | 213 (4.5%)          | 0.87 (0.70, 1.09)                  |\n| Non-fatal stroke c                                                                                    | 60 (2.6%)         | 150 (3.2%)          | 1.24 (0.92, 1.67)                  |\n| CV death c"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:74fdc25d-2104-457a-b3a9-fbb71cdf8aaa", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 159, "token_count": 66, "page_number": 32, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "aa122e32-acb0-4ed0-b8cb-402045f53ab7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "d50eb9e247eb2e0b60f0b057b6aa0a5d8a0195d0d1af93e6850ff2f3488e07fe", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "74fdc25d-2104-457a-b3a9-fbb71cdf8aaa", "text": "| 60 (2.6%)         | 150 (3.2%)          | 1.24 (0.92, 1.67)                  |\n| CV death c                                                                                            | 137 (5.9%)        | 172 (3.7%)          | 0.62 (0.49, 0.77)                  |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0aa248ca-c02d-4c86-91ec-9db29651b90d", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 160, "token_count": 36, "page_number": 33, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "4a710ab7-1126-4650-a746-ab0a94cd229f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "2bf14236521c08b726df1e4268198cef8176db5108a81f78f4a7ceab0c1a5bda", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "0aa248ca-c02d-4c86-91ec-9db29651b90d", "text": "Figure 5 Estimated Cumulative Incidence of First MACE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nFigure 6 Estimated Cumulative Incidence of CV Death\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n48"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:90605e38-b098-4d99-88e3-68c97c763b0c", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 161, "token_count": 122, "page_number": 34, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "288bed8c-91fe-4ffb-a867-0f3e0d89742a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "beaebdcaec83dfad7e1ecb7be9217d52bd183f80a4ca09ef4bd591d519bb4a15", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "90605e38-b098-4d99-88e3-68c97c763b0c", "text": "The efficacy of JARDIANCE on CV death was generally consistent across major demographic and disease subgroups.\n\nVital status was obtained for 99.2% of subjects in the trial. A total of 463 deaths were recorded during the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial.  Most of these deaths were categorized as CV deaths. The non-CV deaths were only a small proportion of deaths and were balanced between the treatment groups (2.1% in patients treated with JARDIANCE, and 2.4% of patients treated with placebo)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e3bc0998-5e81-4a13-bbfa-a7cc21347202", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 162, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 34, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "5a32b221-9744-49f6-b5d1-701d7ca083e9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "3782d4ffefa83d135a80b9291fecbe261138d3bbac98b77835ca82a865bb67d2", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "e3bc0998-5e81-4a13-bbfa-a7cc21347202", "text": "EMPEROR-Reduced (NCT03057977) was a double-blind trial conducted in adults with chronic heart failure (New York Heart Association [NYHA] functional class II-IV) with left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≤ 40% to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE as adjunct to standard of care heart failure therapy.\n\nOf 3,730 patients, 1,863 were randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg and 1,867 to placebo and were followed for a median of 16 months. The mean age of the trial population was 67 years (range: 25 to 94 years) and 76% were men, 24% were women, and 27% were 75 years of age or older. Approximately 71% of the trial population were White, 18% Asian, and 7% Black or African American. At baseline, 50% of the patients had type 2 diabetes mellitus.\n\nAt randomization, 75% of patients were NYHA class II, 24% were class III, and 0.5% were class IV. The mean LVEF was 28%. At baseline, the mean eGFR was 62 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and the median urinary albumin to creatinine ratio (UACR) was 22 mg/g. Approximately half of the patients (52%) had eGFR equal to or above 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 24% had eGFR 45 to less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 19% had eGFR 30 to less than 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , and 5% had eGFR 20 to les"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bd4951ee-6910-4271-874f-929826ad51c4", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 163, "token_count": 246, "page_number": 34, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "5a32b221-9744-49f6-b5d1-701d7ca083e9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "b84987cb5c22224c08e763c9c7d371ff8af1f58f8a7f448fbf712705c0f0db30", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "bd4951ee-6910-4271-874f-929826ad51c4", "text": "ove 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 24% had eGFR 45 to less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 19% had eGFR 30 to less than 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , and 5% had eGFR 20 to less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .\n\nAt baseline, 88% of patients were treated with angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors, angiotensin receptor blockers (ARB), or angiotensin receptor-neprilysin inhibitors (ARNI), 95% with beta-blockers, 71% with mineralocorticoid receptor antagonists (MRA), and 95% with diuretics.\n\nThe primary endpoint was the time to first event of either cardiovascular (CV) death or hospitalization for heart failure (HHF). First and recurrent HHF was assessed as a key secondary endpoint.\n\nJARDIANCE was superior in reducing the risk of the primary composite endpoint of cardiovascular death or hospitalization for heart failure compared with placebo, mostly through a reduction in hospitalization for heart failure.  JARDIANCE reduced the risk of first and recurrent HHF (see Table 16 and Figures 7 and 8)."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9124de4c-2d02-490e-86e1-e2d7cbe01868", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 164, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 35, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "979f7f26-316c-4f0f-93ed-8d597562009f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "8b39cdc32e0edd71adcb7b0fd7ebdcb7eb3a8ea234376b1f847123cfd5f8f455", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "9124de4c-2d02-490e-86e1-e2d7cbe01868", "text": "Table 16 Treatment Effect for the Primary Composite Endpoint, its Components, and Key Secondary Endpoints\n\n|                           | Placebo N=1,867        | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=1,863   | Hazard ratio vs placebo (95% CI)   | p-value   |\n|---------------------------|------------------------|---------------------------|------------------------------------|-----------|\n|                           | Number of Patients (%) | Number of Patients (%)    |                                    |           |\n| CV death or HHF a         | 462 (24.7%)            | 361 (19.4%)               | 0.75 (0.65, 0.86)                  | <0.0001   |\n| CV death a,b              | 202 (10.8%)            | 187 (10.0%)               | 0.92 (0.75, 1.12)                  |           |\n| HHF a                     | 342 (18.3%)            | 246 (13.2%)               | 0.69 (0.59, 0.81)                  |           |\n|                           | Number of Events       | Number of Events          |                                    |           |\n| First and recurrent HHF c | 553                    | 388                       | 0.70 (0.58, 0.85)                  | 0.0003    |\n\nFigure 7 Time to First Occurrence of"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8c0134d6-10ee-428e-b58a-adbfd5cc23d0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 165, "token_count": 62, "page_number": 35, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "979f7f26-316c-4f0f-93ed-8d597562009f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "fdf33a3452bd6413ce24669966f1836f369d4d7205aae4138bab6b4d7669329f", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "8c0134d6-10ee-428e-b58a-adbfd5cc23d0", "text": "nt HHF c | 553                    | 388                       | 0.70 (0.58, 0.85)                  | 0.0003    |\n\nFigure 7 Time to First Occurrence of the Primary Composite Endpoint of CV Death or Hospitalization for Heart Failure\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:63155405-a72b-4d10-9069-0dc895a8d55e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 166, "token_count": 24, "page_number": 36, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "d334de6c-01fc-429a-9a43-650ae16862c0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "a5c599fad94864e61c36f03e578f8df28e7fca8f13a6e8fb8227002ea7ada1c8", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "63155405-a72b-4d10-9069-0dc895a8d55e", "text": "Figure 8 Time to Event of Hospitalization for Heart Failure (First and Recurrent)\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b722df51-6d6d-42bd-9a31-13097bd07339", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 167, "token_count": 298, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "231526cc-ce9b-4feb-a597-02d6b06aa41f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "b62e00d28fdd12b04c733b6f9e2c0d2b85c990295ee72be353b044743ac1063c", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b722df51-6d6d-42bd-9a31-13097bd07339", "text": "The results of the primary composite were generally consistent across the pre-specified subgroups (see Figure 9).\n\nFigure 9 Treatment Effects for the Primary Composite Endpoint (CV Death and Hospitalization for Heart Failure) Subgroup Analysis (EMPEROR-Reduced)\n\n| Subgroup Category                 | N with event/ N Empagliflozin 10 mg VS Placebo   | analyzed   | Hazard ratio (95%CI)   | Empagliflozin 10 mg better   | Placebo better   |\n|-----------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|------------|------------------------|------------------------------|------------------|\n| Overall                           | 361/1863                                         | 462/1867   | 0.75 (0.65,0.86)       | 1-e,                         |                  |\n| Diabetes at baseline              |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| Diabetic                          | 200/ 927                                         | 265/ 929   | 0.72 (0.60,0.87)       | 1-----1                      |                  |\n| Non-Diabetic                      | 161/ 936"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:731b217f-68e3-407e-b009-921c54058106", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 168, "token_count": 298, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "231526cc-ce9b-4feb-a597-02d6b06aa41f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "c2d668b56b3ced5ea37445f7775c4e6cd85884526e46040372f224587f744560", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "731b217f-68e3-407e-b009-921c54058106", "text": "| 265/ 929   | 0.72 (0.60,0.87)       | 1-----1                      |                  |\n| Non-Diabetic                      | 161/ 936                                         | 197/ 938   | 0.78 (0.64,0.97)       | I-+--!                       |                  |\n| Age                               |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| < 65                              | 128/ 675                                         | 193/ 740   | 0.71 (0.57,0.89)       | 1-----1                      |                  |\n| 2: 65                             | 233/1188                                         | 269/1127   | 0.78 (0.66,0.93)       | f--e-j                       |                  |\n| Sex                               |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| Male                              | 294/1426                                         | 353/1411   | 0.80 (0.68,0.93)       | 1-a-l                        |                  |\n| Female                            | 67"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a7620479-faa1-4f94-bb9d-f2e5b7d60511", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 169, "token_count": 289, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "231526cc-ce9b-4feb-a597-02d6b06aa41f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ea6f3e2137e579b97f493f3788f65a88b7724f39b3f96904914515cf50e10c55", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "a7620479-faa1-4f94-bb9d-f2e5b7d60511", "text": "| 353/1411   | 0.80 (0.68,0.93)       | 1-a-l                        |                  |\n| Female                            | 67/ 437                                          | 109/ 456   | 0.59 (0.44,0.80)       | 1--------,                   |                  |\n| Race                              |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| White                             | 264/1325                                         | 289/1304   | 0.88 (0.75, 1.04)      |                              |                  |\n| Black/ African-American           | 24/ 123                                          | 48/ 134    | 0.46 (0.28,0. 75)      |                              |                  |\n| Asian                             | 62/ 337                                          | 99/ 335    | 0.57 (0.41 ,0.78)      |                              |                  |\n| Other including mixed race        | 5/ 51                                            | 14/ 63     | 0.41 (0.15,1.14)       |                              |                  |\n| BMI"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c7fab94b-edbc-416b-a69b-1e50608afb78", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 170, "token_count": 291, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "231526cc-ce9b-4feb-a597-02d6b06aa41f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "70066fb51a40a668de024205aac383bc456cbbde2a6cf413ad107622260c29ac", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c7fab94b-edbc-416b-a69b-1e50608afb78", "text": "| 14/ 63     | 0.41 (0.15,1.14)       |                              |                  |\n| BMI                               |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| <30                               | 226/1263                                         | 322/1300   | 0.70 (0.59,0.83)       |                              |                  |\n| 2:30                              | 135/ 600                                         | 140/ 567   | 0.85 (0.67, 1.08)      |                              |                  |\n| eGFR at baseline                  |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| 2:90                              | 31/ 229                                          | 55/ 220    | 0.51 (0.33,0.80)       |                              |                  |\n| 60 to <90                         | 128/ 740                                         | 169/ 740   | 0.73 (0.58,0.92)       |                              |                  |\n| 45 to <60"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:906acb1b-e556-44da-9f5f-2d0916405c18", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 171, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "231526cc-ce9b-4feb-a597-02d6b06aa41f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ee3e8a593ac3a216d0fb00754c46c0110c33b0dbc2ce890f08d7bcf51c9a71b9", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "906acb1b-e556-44da-9f5f-2d0916405c18", "text": "740                                         | 169/ 740   | 0.73 (0.58,0.92)       |                              |                  |\n| 45 to <60                         | 80/ 433                                          | 108/ 467   | 0.76 (0.57, 1.02)      |                              |                  |\n| 30 to <45                         | 87/ 345                                          | 96/ 349    | 0.92 (0.69, 1.23)      |                              |                  |\n| <30                               | 35/ 115                                          | 33/ 90     | 0.68 (0.42, 1.09)      |                              |                  |\n| NYHA at baseline                  |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| II                                | 220/1399                                         | 299/1401   | 0.71 (0.59,0.84)       |                              |                  |\n| Ill/IV                            | 141/ 464                                         | 163/ 466   | 0.83 (0.66, 1.04)      |                              |                  |\n| He"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a312851a-fff8-4ffd-b943-5897375acd6f", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 172, "token_count": 296, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "231526cc-ce9b-4feb-a597-02d6b06aa41f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "8b72da93308ae2cf8d4e6ad6c05172038e172a6fafe33d5b001c2c45b3d57c2b", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "a312851a-fff8-4ffd-b943-5897375acd6f", "text": "| 141/ 464                                         | 163/ 466   | 0.83 (0.66, 1.04)      |                              |                  |\n| Heart failure physiology          |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| LVEF s 30% and NTproBNP < median  | 80/ 699                                          | 115/ 724   | 0.70 (0.53,0.93)       | f----+----1                  |                  |\n| LVEF s 30% and NTproBNP 2: median | 169/ 631                                         | 249/ 661   | 0.65 (0.53,0.79)       | 1------,                     |                  |\n| LVEF > 30%                        | 108/ 526                                         | 97/ 475    | 0.99 (0.76, 1.31)      |                              |                  |\n| Baseline use of MRA               |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| No                                | 118/ 557                                         | 132/ 512   | 0.76 (0.59,0.97)       | f-----1                      |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c2ce9e06-c42e-435a-8bb4-6bf37818d15b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 173, "token_count": 296, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "231526cc-ce9b-4feb-a597-02d6b06aa41f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "b6f406a2c6609ab7cc5e434d909df3ce9751f0be2a7ba5985c903d61902eb631", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "c2ce9e06-c42e-435a-8bb4-6bf37818d15b", "text": "| 118/ 557                                         | 132/ 512   | 0.76 (0.59,0.97)       | f-----1                      |                  |\n| Yes                               | 243/1306                                         | 330/1355   | 0.75 (0.63,0.88)       | HI-I                         |                  |\n| Baseline use of ARNi              |                                                  |            |                        |                              |                  |\n| No                                | 310/1523                                         | 369/1480   | 0.77 (0.66,0.90)       | 1-a-l                        |                  |\n| Yes                               | 51/ 340                                          | 93/ 387    | 0.64 (0.45,0.89)       |                              |                  |\n|                                   |                                                  |            |                        | 0.125 0.25 0.5               | 2 4              |\n\nHazard ratio\n\nLVEF &gt;30%: Includes both above and below the median NT-proBNP. To be eligible for inclusion, patients with an LVEF &gt;30% were required to"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5852ba9e-4e14-482c-b01c-defa02d9c31b", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 174, "token_count": 71, "page_number": 37, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "231526cc-ce9b-4feb-a597-02d6b06aa41f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "df96bcc61452fe97910a564be3c9af488988ce19de44e32eaeb314c88b93e67d", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "5852ba9e-4e14-482c-b01c-defa02d9c31b", "text": "ratio\n\nLVEF &gt;30%: Includes both above and below the median NT-proBNP. To be eligible for inclusion, patients with an LVEF &gt;30% were required to meet a higher NT-proBNP threshold than those with LVEF ≤ 30%, unless they additionally had a history of HHF within the past 12 months."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6bd7553d-91c2-415f-b8b1-ac27778906e0", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 175, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 38, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "87148f81-b514-4a9a-925c-50c8573d2199", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "907c95b78fbe6c8385b9a5572a37feb3677571886c04920c8ab9c059cda08ca7", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "6bd7553d-91c2-415f-b8b1-ac27778906e0", "text": "EMPEROR-Preserved (NCT03057951) was a double-blind trial conducted in adults with chronic heart failure NYHA Class II-IV with LVEF &gt;40% to evaluate the efficacy of JARDIANCE as adjunct to standard of care therapy.\n\nOf 5,988 patients, 2,997 were randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg and 2,991 to placebo and were followed for a median of 26 months. The mean age of the trial population was 72 years (range: 22 to 100 years) and 55% were men, 45% were women, and 43% were 75 years of age or older. Approximately 76% of the trial population were White, 14% Asian, and 4% Black or African American.\n\nAt randomization, 82% of patients were NYHA class II, 18% were class III, and 0.3% were class IV. The EMPEROR-Preserved trial population included patients with a LVEF &lt;50% (33.1%), with a LVEF 50 to &lt;60% (34.4%) and a LVEF ≥ 60% (32.5%). At baseline, the mean eGFR was 61 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and the median urinary albumin to creatinine ratio (UACR) was 21 mg/g. Approximately half of the patients (50%) had eGFR equal to or above 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 26% had eGFR 45 to less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 19% had eGFR 30 to less than 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , and 5% had eGFR 20 to less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ."}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:25bd08d8-8406-4bc3-b89e-0d28f248f2fe", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 176, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 38, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "87148f81-b514-4a9a-925c-50c8573d2199", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "db6b4c6ca53757eaed1f15bbcb109b5ca5be3f173650a2d19cef40efcb59f8bc", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "25bd08d8-8406-4bc3-b89e-0d28f248f2fe", "text": "had eGFR 45 to less than 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 19% had eGFR 30 to less than 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , and 5% had eGFR 20 to less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .\n\nAt baseline, 81% of patients were treated with ACE inhibitors, ARBs, or ARNI, 86% with beta-blockers, 38% with MRAs, and 86% with diuretics.\n\nThe primary endpoint was the time to first event of either CV death or HHF. First and recurrent HHF was assessed as a key secondary endpoint.\n\nJARDIANCE was superior in reducing the risk of the primary composite endpoint compared with placebo, mostly through a reduction in hospitalization for heart failure. JARDIANCE reduced the risk of first and recurrent HHF (see Table 17 and Figures 10 and 11).\n\nTable 17 Treatment Effect for the Primary Composite Endpoint, its Components, and Key Secondary Endpoints\n\n|                           | Placebo N=2,991        | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=2,997   | Hazard ratio vs placebo (95% CI)   |   p-value |\n|---------------------------|------------------------|---------------------------|------------------------------------|-----------|\n|                           | Number of Patients (%) | Number of Patients (%)    |                                    |           |\n|"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f9df29d3-db7d-4c45-8ab1-aeb3a9f0072e", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 177, "token_count": 202, "page_number": 38, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "87148f81-b514-4a9a-925c-50c8573d2199", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "d750f2366ba1fb0e972019ff0e39350eb97cfa9c9e58e42388120895c61ff22c", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "f9df29d3-db7d-4c45-8ab1-aeb3a9f0072e", "text": "--|-----------|\n|                           | Number of Patients (%) | Number of Patients (%)    |                                    |           |\n| CV death or HHF a         | 511 (17.1%)            | 415 (13.8%)               | 0.79 (0.69, 0.90)                  |    0.0003 |\n| CV death a,b              | 244 (8.2%)             | 219 (7.3%)                | 0.91 (0.76, 1.09)                  |           |\n| HHF a                     | 352 (11.8%)            | 259 (8.6%)                | 0.71 (0.60, 0.83)                  |           |\n|                           | Number of Events       | Number of Events          |                                    |           |\n| First and recurrent HHF c | 541                    | 407                       | 0.73 (0.61, 0.88)                  |    0.0009 |"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:da7e6221-d55d-45c7-ab38-103d2298f512", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 178, "token_count": 58, "page_number": 39, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "5bbd65f7-fe3e-430e-894f-fa2c39e4261e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "521b48ff401fd67c2244b26d2fde5fb2f9a29f1a11c865a2060185f6e2456a38", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "da7e6221-d55d-45c7-ab38-103d2298f512", "text": "Figure 10 Time to First Occurrence of the Primary Composite Endpoint of CV Death or Hospitalization for Heart Failure\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nFigure 11 Time to Event of Hospitalization for Heart Failure (First and Recurrent)\n\n<!-- image -->"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d7cfbae3-f5e5-4a3b-98ee-ae6266e33bcf", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 179, "token_count": 300, "page_number": 40, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "4dc7a36e-6ebe-440c-ac60-e3b566432bd5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "bae4df6fca59e8b029a69acd5a8878ad3e82bfc0b371940bd9aa7f43d1bfeefd", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "d7cfbae3-f5e5-4a3b-98ee-ae6266e33bcf", "text": "The results of the primary composite endpoint were consistent across the pre-specified subgroups (see Figure 12).\n\nFigure 12 Treatment Effects for the Primary Composite Endpoint (CV Death or Hospitalization for Heart Failure) Subgroup Analysis (EMPEROR-Preserved)\n\n| Subgroup Category          | N with event/ N analyzed   | N with event/ N analyzed   | Hazard ratio (95%CI)   | Empagliflozin 10 mg better   | Placebo better   |\n|----------------------------|----------------------------|----------------------------|------------------------|------------------------------|------------------|\n|                            | Empagliflozin 10 mg        | vs Placebo                 |                        |                              | -                |\n| Overall                    | 415/2997                   | 511/2991                   | 0.79 (0.69,0.90)       | i-----,                      |                  |\n| Diabetes at baseline       |                            |                            |                        |                              |                  |\n| Diabetic                   | 239/1466                   | 291/1472                   | 0.79 (0.67,0.94)       | f"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b65c450e-6462-4f5b-a1b9-4bce95f9b425", "@type": "Chunk", "graphScope": "brand", "chunk_index": 180, "token_count": 294, "page_number": 40, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "4dc7a36e-6ebe-440c-ac60-e3b566432bd5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_hash": "ce79bd32e8a6470ec7db2a93b3ce8dcb7938646065dee7ae81ca3a0c382cbc78", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "chunk_id": "b65c450e-6462-4f5b-a1b9-4bce95f9b425", "text": "|                  |\n| Diabetic                   | 239/1466                   | 291/1472                   | 0.79 (0.67,0.94)       | f----+---l                   |                  |\n| Non-Diabetic               | 176/1531                   | 220/1519                   | 0.78 (0.64,0.95)       | I------+----,                |                  |\n| Age                        |                            |                            |                        |                              |               