n very commonly (may affect more than 1 in 10 people)", "page_number": 53, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "07c6cd0c-8842-459f-b919-2413aafe6359", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The signs of dehydration are not specific, but may include:\n\n- unusual thirst\n- lightheadedness or dizziness upon standing\n- fainting or loss of consciousness", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:07c6cd0c-8842-459f-b919-2413aafe6359"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:2f6b0a4e-e178-4642-a9ed-fd659f97f3ba", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Hypoglycaemia", "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2f6b0a4e-e178-4642-a9ed-fd659f97f3ba", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The frequency of hypoglycaemia depended on the background therapy in the respective studies and was similar for empagliflozin and placebo as monotherapy, add-on to metformin, add-on to pioglitazone with or without metformin, as add-on to linagliptin and metformin, and as adjunct to standard care therapy and for the combination of empagliflozin with metformin in drug-naïve patients compared to those treated with empagliflozin and metformin as individual components. An increased frequency was noted when given as add-on to metformin and a sulphonylurea (empagliflozin 10 mg: 16.1%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 11.5%, placebo: 8.4%), add-on to basal insulin with or without metformin and with or without a sulphonylurea (empagliflozin 10 mg: 19.5%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 28.4%, placebo: 20.6% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg: 36.1%, placebo 35.3% over the 78-week trial), and add-on to MDI insulin with or without metformin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 39.8%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 41.3%, placebo: 37.2% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg: 51.1%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 57.7%, placebo: 58% over the 52-week trial).\n\nIn the EMPEROR heart failure studies, similar frequency of hypoglycaemia was noted when used addon to sulphonylurea or insulin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 6.5%, placebo: 6.7%).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2f6b0a4e-e178-4642-a9ed-fd659f97f3ba"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:73635b7c-201c-46a8-b5ec-fc01d7db4d2d", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Other side effects while taking Jardiance:", "page_number": 54, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "73635b7c-201c-46a8-b5ec-fc01d7db4d2d", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:73635b7c-201c-46a8-b5ec-fc01d7db4d2d"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:3089470f-9d4f-4eee-b7c3-c19414db4b2c", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "ANNEX I", "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "3089470f-9d4f-4eee-b7c3-c19414db4b2c", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3089470f-9d4f-4eee-b7c3-c19414db4b2c"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7c8a9094-1048-4d00-a039-940e371e55d5", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "SUMMARY OF PRODUCT CHARACTERISTICS", "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7c8a9094-1048-4d00-a039-940e371e55d5", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7c8a9094-1048-4d00-a039-940e371e55d5"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:19f44440-fcc3-4a75-8e22-4b3e40bc492d", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "1. NAME OF THE MEDICINAL PRODUCT", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "19f44440-fcc3-4a75-8e22-4b3e40bc492d", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance 10 mg film-coated tablets Jardiance 25 mg film-coated tablets", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:19f44440-fcc3-4a75-8e22-4b3e40bc492d"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:90bd8fae-26e2-4a70-a698-c08c6d35b1c3", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "2. QUALITATIVE AND QUANTITATIVE COMPOSITION", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "90bd8fae-26e2-4a70-a698-c08c6d35b1c3", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:90bd8fae-26e2-4a70-a698-c08c6d35b1c3"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:72043664-d5b7-4ed9-8e8a-39ffb1cf44e7", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Jardiance 10 mg film-coated tablets", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "72043664-d5b7-4ed9-8e8a-39ffb1cf44e7", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains 10 mg empagliflozin.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:72043664-d5b7-4ed9-8e8a-39ffb1cf44e7"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7be759b0-c4fa-439c-a15e-c495d012756f", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Excipients with known effect", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7be759b0-c4fa-439c-a15e-c495d012756f", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains lactose monohydrate equivalent to 154.3 mg lactose anhydrous.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7be759b0-c4fa-439c-a15e-c495d012756f"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:6e8e9f19-0b50-42ea-9fd5-15a3af72ac59", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Jardiance 25 mg film-coated tablets", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6e8e9f19-0b50-42ea-9fd5-15a3af72ac59", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains 25 mg empagliflozin.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6e8e9f19-0b50-42ea-9fd5-15a3af72ac59"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:74cea541-8458-48ca-8d92-587141b0c022", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Excipients with known effect", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "74cea541-8458-48ca-8d92-587141b0c022", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains lactose monohydrate equivalent to 107.4 mg lactose anhydrous.\n\nFor the full list of excipients, see section 6.1.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:74cea541-8458-48ca-8d92-587141b0c022"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:ccf52c08-9cc3-4ba6-97eb-27dc4abe7bde", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "ccf52c08-9cc3-4ba6-97eb-27dc4abe7bde", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Film-coated tablet (tablet).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ccf52c08-9cc3-4ba6-97eb-27dc4abe7bde"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7561f639-7882-454b-b411-23c90ede7334", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Jardiance 10 mg film-coated tablets", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7561f639-7882-454b-b411-23c90ede7334", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Round, pale yellow, biconvex, bevel-edged film-coated tablet debossed with 'S10' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim logo on the other (tablet diameter: 9.1 mm).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7561f639-7882-454b-b411-23c90ede7334"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:992b6b63-1c8e-47a7-a308-aee1fa43582d", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Jardiance 25 mg film-coated tablets", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "992b6b63-1c8e-47a7-a308-aee1fa43582d", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Oval, pale yellow, biconvex film-coated tablet debossed with 'S25' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim logo on the other (tablet length: 11.1 mm, tablet width: 5.6 mm).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:992b6b63-1c8e-47a7-a308-aee1fa43582d"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:2824ee35-3b1d-4792-964f-a58c8c8bbaa4", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2824ee35-3b1d-4792-964f-a58c8c8bbaa4", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2824ee35-3b1d-4792-964f-a58c8c8bbaa4"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:b8c312fb-18d3-4b42-9a88-06355658f720", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.1 Therapeutic indications", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b8c312fb-18d3-4b42-9a88-06355658f720", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b8c312fb-18d3-4b42-9a88-06355658f720"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:37fabc6d-48b2-45a0-9a39-7d25dd312d9f", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "37fabc6d-48b2-45a0-9a39-7d25dd312d9f", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance is indicated in adults and children aged 10 years and above for the treatment of insufficiently controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise\n\n- -as monotherapy when metformin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance\n- -in addition to other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes\n\nFor study results with respect to combination of therapies, effects on glycaemic control, cardiovascular and renal events, and the populations studied, see sections 4.4, 4.5 and 5.1.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:37fabc6d-48b2-45a0-9a39-7d25dd312d9f"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:916d3dd8-0293-4e83-a95d-5d42266303f7", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Heart failure", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "916d3dd8-0293-4e83-a95d-5d42266303f7", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance is indicated in adults for the treatment of symptomatic chronic heart failure.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:916d3dd8-0293-4e83-a95d-5d42266303f7"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:edf8c677-dbdf-4d72-a9f0-142c0ed443c5", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Chronic kidney disease", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "edf8c677-dbdf-4d72-a9f0-142c0ed443c5", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance is indicated in adults for the treatment of chronic kidney disease.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:edf8c677-dbdf-4d72-a9f0-142c0ed443c5"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:93d8a775-9a92-4470-a919-6a3968e676f1", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.2 Posology and method of administration", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "93d8a775-9a92-4470-a919-6a3968e676f1", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:93d8a775-9a92-4470-a919-6a3968e676f1"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:17a62dc7-6880-44b9-bb60-2e75ce412461", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Posology", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "17a62dc7-6880-44b9-bb60-2e75ce412461", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:17a62dc7-6880-44b9-bb60-2e75ce412461"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:6255a9e3-f098-4b96-9800-27a1d1f3afb3", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6255a9e3-f098-4b96-9800-27a1d1f3afb3", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The recommended starting dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily for monotherapy and add-on combination therapy with other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes. In patients tolerating empagliflozin 10 mg once daily who have an eGFR ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and need tighter glycaemic control, the dose can be increased to 25 mg once daily. The maximum daily dose is 25 mg (see below and section 4.4).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6255a9e3-f098-4b96-9800-27a1d1f3afb3"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:2dd90f41-cf84-43aa-83c1-268af0ba8aa9", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Heart failure", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2dd90f41-cf84-43aa-83c1-268af0ba8aa9", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The recommended dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2dd90f41-cf84-43aa-83c1-268af0ba8aa9"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:b9f3eb9a-be8b-4f96-8f20-210ffeeee15a", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Chronic kidney disease", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b9f3eb9a-be8b-4f96-8f20-210ffeeee15a", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The recommended dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b9f3eb9a-be8b-4f96-8f20-210ffeeee15a"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:8cc6c1c4-80dc-49ed-b160-634d92f0d22e", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "All indications", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "8cc6c1c4-80dc-49ed-b160-634d92f0d22e", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "When empagliflozin is used in combination with a sulphonylurea or with insulin, a lower dose of the sulphonylurea or insulin may be considered to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia (see sections 4.5 and 4.8).\n\nIf a dose is missed, it should be taken as soon as the patient remembers; however, a double dose should not be taken on the same day.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:8cc6c1c4-80dc-49ed-b160-634d92f0d22e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:93e251f3-c73e-4e5d-a924-a72a680b13db", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Special populations", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "93e251f3-c73e-4e5d-a924-a72a680b13db", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:93e251f3-c73e-4e5d-a924-a72a680b13db"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:6ff36a3a-d2f6-48b1-812d-240c5ca947ab", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Renal impairment", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6ff36a3a-d2f6-48b1-812d-240c5ca947ab", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Due to limited experience, it is not recommended to initiate treatment with empagliflozin in patients with an eGFR &lt; 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .\n\nIn patients with an eGFR &lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 the daily dose of empagliflozin is 10 mg.\n\nIn patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, the glucose lowering efficacy of empagliflozin is reduced in patients with an eGFR &lt; 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and likely absent in patients with an eGFR &lt; 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . Therefore, if eGFR falls below 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , additional glucose lowering treatment should be considered if needed (see sections 4.4, 4.8, 5.1 and 5.2).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6ff36a3a-d2f6-48b1-812d-240c5ca947ab"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:4bec51e7-0d92-43f3-a4a8-8188f3276c3f", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Hepatic impairment", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4bec51e7-0d92-43f3-a4a8-8188f3276c3f", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "No dose adjustment is required for patients with hepatic impairment. Empagliflozin exposure is increased in patients with severe hepatic impairment. Therapeutic experience in patients with severe hepatic impairment is limited and therefore not recommended for use in this population (see section 5.2).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4bec51e7-0d92-43f3-a4a8-8188f3276c3f"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:974f594b-d029-4008-9b2c-524455fde10f", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Elderly", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "974f594b-d029-4008-9b2c-524455fde10f", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "No dose adjustment is recommended based on age. In patients 75 years and older, an increased risk for volume depletion should be taken into account (see sections 4.4 and 4.8).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:974f594b-d029-4008-9b2c-524455fde10f"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:b0c0a9ca-1f49-4fb1-ba69-09b754e34493", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Paediatric population", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b0c0a9ca-1f49-4fb1-ba69-09b754e34493", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The recommended starting dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily. In patients tolerating empagliflozin 10 mg once daily and requiring additional glycaemic control, the dose can be increased to 25 mg once daily (see sections 5.1 and 5.2). No data are available for children with eGFR &lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and children below 10 years of age.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b0c0a9ca-1f49-4fb1-ba69-09b754e34493"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:b325c700-365c-4b74-9351-65100b30929a", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b325c700-365c-4b74-9351-65100b30929a", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The safety and efficacy of empagliflozin for the treatment of heart failure or for the treatment of chronic kidney disease in children under 18 years of age have not been established. No data are available.", "PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:b325c700-365c-4b74-9351-65100b30929a"}], "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b325c700-365c-4b74-9351-65100b30929a"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:37017a54-58ee-4218-bc2f-8d85988565e8", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Method of administration", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "37017a54-58ee-4218-bc2f-8d85988565e8", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The tablets can be taken with or without food, swallowed whole with water.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:37017a54-58ee-4218-bc2f-8d85988565e8"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:5655cbfa-9679-42c6-893b-4f48369d1bd5", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.3 Contraindications", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "5655cbfa-9679-42c6-893b-4f48369d1bd5", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients listed in section 6.1.", "PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:5655cbfa-9679-42c6-893b-4f48369d1bd5"}], "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:5655cbfa-9679-42c6-893b-4f48369d1bd5"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:4409b123-117a-48d4-975c-378f436de1ff", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.4 Special warnings and precautions for use", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4409b123-117a-48d4-975c-378f436de1ff", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:4409b123-117a-48d4-975c-378f436de1ff"}], "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4409b123-117a-48d4-975c-378f436de1ff"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:dff5d609-8387-412f-adb6-6b2ee91fbe2f", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "General", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "dff5d609-8387-412f-adb6-6b2ee91fbe2f", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus (see 'Ketoacidosis' in section 4.4).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:dff5d609-8387-412f-adb6-6b2ee91fbe2f"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:6b6e7cbf-c89e-484c-b82c-de150615604e", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Ketoacidosis", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6b6e7cbf-c89e-484c-b82c-de150615604e", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Cases of ketoacidosis, including life-threatening and fatal cases, have been reported in patients with diabetes mellitus treated with SGLT2 inhibitors, including empagliflozin. In a number of cases, the presentation of the condition was atypical with only moderately increased blood glucose values, below 14 mmol/L (250 mg/dL). It is not known if ketoacidosis is more likely to occur with higher doses of empagliflozin. Although ketoacidosis is less likely to occur in patients without diabetes mellitus, cases have also been reported in these patients.\n\nThe risk of ketoacidosis must be considered in the event of non-specific symptoms such as nausea, vomiting, anorexia, abdominal pain, excessive thirst, difficulty breathing, confusion, unusual fatigue or sleepiness. Patients should be assessed for ketoacidosis immediately if these symptoms occur, regardless of blood glucose level.\n\nIn patients where ketoacidosis is suspected or diagnosed, treatment with empagliflozin should be discontinued immediately.\n\nTreatment should be interrupted in patients who are hospitalised for major surgical procedures or acute serious medical illnesses. Monitoring of ketones is recommended in these patients. Measurement of blood ketone levels is preferred to urine. Treatment with empagliflozin may be restarted when the ketone values are normal and the patient's condition has stabilised.\n\nBefore initiating empagliflozin, factors in the patient history that may predispose to ketoacidosis should be considered.\n\nProlonged ketoacidosis and prolonged glucosuria have been observed with empagliflozin. Ketoacidosis may last longer after discontinuation of empagliflozin than expected from the plasma half-life (see section 5.2). Empagliflozin-independent factors, such as insulin deficiency, might be involved in prolonged periods of ketoacidosis.\n\nPatients who may be at higher risk of ketoacidosis include patients with a low beta-cell function reserve (e.g. type 2 diabetes patients with low C-peptide or latent autoimmune diabetes in adults (LADA) or patients with a history of pancreatitis), patients with conditions that lead to restricted food intake or severe dehydration, patients for whom insulin doses are reduced and patients with increased insulin requirements due to acute medical illness, surgery or alcohol abuse. SGLT2 inhibitors should be used with caution in these patients.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6b6e7cbf-c89e-484c-b82c-de150615604e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:60a8b15c-9c71-4687-9f8c-b515fc74a374", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "60a8b15c-9c71-4687-9f8c-b515fc74a374", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Restarting SGLT2 inhibitor treatment in patients with previous ketoacidosis while on SGLT2 inhibitor treatment is not recommended, unless another clear precipitating factor is identified and resolved.\n\nJardiance should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes. Data from a clinical trial program in patients with type 1 diabetes showed increased ketoacidosis occurrence with common frequency in patients treated with empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg as an adjunct to insulin compared to placebo.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:60a8b15c-9c71-4687-9f8c-b515fc74a374"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:9a7a5961-1e81-4f2f-8886-ceccb3a44061", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Renal impairment", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "9a7a5961-1e81-4f2f-8886-ceccb3a44061", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Due to limited experience, it is not recommended to initiate treatment with empagliflozin in patients with an eGFR &lt; 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .\n\nIn patients with an eGFR &lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 the daily dose of empagliflozin is 10 mg (see section 4.2).\n\nThe glucose lowering efficacy of empagliflozin is dependent on renal function, and is reduced in patients with an eGFR &lt; 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and is likely absent in patients with an eGFR &lt; 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2  (see section 4.2, 5.1 and 5.2).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:9a7a5961-1e81-4f2f-8886-ceccb3a44061"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:b0a2edfb-2315-4618-b86d-09b5ed86d2c6", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Monitoring of renal function", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b0a2edfb-2315-4618-b86d-09b5ed86d2c6", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Assessment of renal function is recommended as follows:\n\n- -Prior to empagliflozin initiation and periodically during treatment, i.e. at least yearly (see sections 4.2, 4.8, 5.1 and 5.2).\n- -Prior to initiation of any concomitant medicinal product that may have a negative impact on renal function.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b0a2edfb-2315-4618-b86d-09b5ed86d2c6"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:4586acf2-883e-4de4-b333-63abd53adec3", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Risk for volume depletion", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4586acf2-883e-4de4-b333-63abd53adec3", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Based on the mode of action of SGLT2 inhibitors, osmotic diuresis accompanying glucosuria may lead to a modest decrease in blood pressure (see section 5.1). Therefore, caution should be exercised in patients for whom an empagliflozin-induced drop in blood pressure could pose a risk, such as patients with known cardiovascular disease, patients on anti-hypertensive therapy with a history of hypotension or patients aged 75 years and older.\n\nIn case of conditions that may lead to fluid loss (e.g. gastrointestinal illness), careful monitoring of volume status (e.g. physical examination, blood pressure measurements, laboratory tests including haematocrit) and electrolytes is recommended for patients receiving empagliflozin. Temporary interruption of treatment with empagliflozin should be considered until the fluid loss is corrected.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4586acf2-883e-4de4-b333-63abd53adec3"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:475e338e-bf52-4973-aa24-ff7b4f8be0a6", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Elderly", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "475e338e-bf52-4973-aa24-ff7b4f8be0a6", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The effect of empagliflozin on urinary glucose excretion is associated with osmotic diuresis, which could affect the hydration status. Patients aged 75 years and older may be at an increased risk of volume depletion. A higher number of these patients treated with empagliflozin had adverse reactions related to volume depletion as compared to placebo (see section 4.8). Therefore, special attention should be given to their volume intake in case of co-administered medicinal products which may lead to volume depletion (e.g. diuretics, ACE inhibitors).", "PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:475e338e-bf52-4973-aa24-ff7b4f8be0a6"}], "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:475e338e-bf52-4973-aa24-ff7b4f8be0a6"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7e20fc68-1213-476f-b61f-bdcd7057e1d2", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Complicated urinary tract infections", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7e20fc68-1213-476f-b61f-bdcd7057e1d2", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Cases of complicated urinary tract infections including pyelonephritis and urosepsis have been reported in patients treated with empagliflozin (see section 4.8). Temporary interruption of empagliflozin should be considered in patients with complicated urinary tract infections.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7e20fc68-1213-476f-b61f-bdcd7057e1d2"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:d7aa5df9-51be-4cc9-8074-350839411d7e", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Necrotising fasciitis of the perineum (Fournier's gangrene)", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d7aa5df9-51be-4cc9-8074-350839411d7e", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Cases of necrotising fasciitis of the perineum, (also known as Fournier's gangrene), have been reported in female and male patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors, including empagliflozin. This is a rare but serious and potentially life-threatening event that requires urgent surgical intervention and antibiotic treatment.\n\nPatients should be advised to seek medical attention if they experience a combination of symptoms of pain, tenderness, erythema, or swelling in the genital or perineal area, with fever or malaise. Be aware that either uro-genital infection or perineal abscess may precede necrotising fasciitis. If Fournier´s gangrene is suspected, Jardiance should be discontinued and prompt treatment (including antibiotics and surgical debridement) should be instituted.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d7aa5df9-51be-4cc9-8074-350839411d7e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:e623f3a3-e582-4c07-bdb5-383b763c7849", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.9 Overdose", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e623f3a3-e582-4c07-bdb5-383b763c7849", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e623f3a3-e582-4c07-bdb5-383b763c7849"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:5556d121-5d2f-42f5-b6cb-3847d4b3223a", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Lower limb amputations", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "5556d121-5d2f-42f5-b6cb-3847d4b3223a", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "An increase in cases of lower limb amputation (primarily of the toe) has been observed in long-term clinical studies with another SGLT2 inhibitor. It is unknown whether this constitutes a class effect. Like for all diabetic patients it is important to counsel patients on routine preventative foot-care.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:5556d121-5d2f-42f5-b6cb-3847d4b3223a"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:8e7aa7a7-a2fc-4f07-bc81-4bc7d82f836f", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Hepatic injury", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "8e7aa7a7-a2fc-4f07-bc81-4bc7d82f836f", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Cases of hepatic injury have been reported with empagliflozin in clinical trials. A causal relationship between empagliflozin and hepatic injury has not been established.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:8e7aa7a7-a2fc-4f07-bc81-4bc7d82f836f"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:8d5b8aa6-3e6a-4322-9090-a3afe8d4122a", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Elevated haematocrit", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "8d5b8aa6-3e6a-4322-9090-a3afe8d4122a", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Haematocrit increase was observed with empagliflozin treatment (see section 4.8). Patients with pronounced elevations in haematocrit should be monitored and investigated for underlying haematological disease.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:8d5b8aa6-3e6a-4322-9090-a3afe8d4122a"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:9fbfe13b-d7e9-47c8-b364-22200e5553b5", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Chronic kidney disease", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "9fbfe13b-d7e9-47c8-b364-22200e5553b5", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Patients with albuminuria may benefit more from treatment with empagliflozin.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:9fbfe13b-d7e9-47c8-b364-22200e5553b5"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:e4c9d7e4-676c-4ba6-bd7a-a90f0344acc1", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Infiltrative disease or Takotsubo cardiomyopathy", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e4c9d7e4-676c-4ba6-bd7a-a90f0344acc1", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Patients with infiltrative disease or with Takotsubo cardiomyopathy have not been specifically studied. Therefore, efficacy in these patients has not been established.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e4c9d7e4-676c-4ba6-bd7a-a90f0344acc1"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:0b339ebd-6013-461d-a133-bd7675c8493b", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Urine laboratory assessments", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "0b339ebd-6013-461d-a133-bd7675c8493b", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Due to its mechanism of action, patients taking Jardiance will test positive for glucose in their urine.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:0b339ebd-6013-461d-a133-bd7675c8493b"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:77d73b63-98f8-4f3b-b9ad-840ab3692dc6", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Interference with 1,5-anhydroglucitol (1,5-AG) assay", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "77d73b63-98f8-4f3b-b9ad-840ab3692dc6", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Monitoring glycaemic control with 1,5-AG assay is not recommended as measurements of 1,5-AG are unreliable in assessing glycaemic control in patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors. Use of alternative methods to monitor glycaemic control is advised.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:77d73b63-98f8-4f3b-b9ad-840ab3692dc6"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:74ddfc00-f218-4899-bfc5-81fa0c1e64da", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Lactose", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "74ddfc00-f218-4899-bfc5-81fa0c1e64da", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The tablets contain lactose. Patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medicinal product.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:74ddfc00-f218-4899-bfc5-81fa0c1e64da"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:d26fc014-0c55-4945-b1cc-c866c2258dc3", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Sodium", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d26fc014-0c55-4945-b1cc-c866c2258dc3", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains less than 1 mmol sodium (23 mg), that is to say essentially 'sodium free'.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d26fc014-0c55-4945-b1cc-c866c2258dc3"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:678b0bd7-8669-4ae5-bf44-a37a85fedf3e", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.5 Interaction with other medicinal products and other forms of interaction", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "678b0bd7-8669-4ae5-bf44-a37a85fedf3e", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:678b0bd7-8669-4ae5-bf44-a37a85fedf3e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:979dfd35-ddd0-460f-a004-36045a8c4e8e", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Pharmacodynamic interactions", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "979dfd35-ddd0-460f-a004-36045a8c4e8e", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:979dfd35-ddd0-460f-a004-36045a8c4e8e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:b9908a1a-c9e1-4cfc-ad05-9bd4f2b282f3", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Diuretics", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b9908a1a-c9e1-4cfc-ad05-9bd4f2b282f3", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin may add to the diuretic effect of thiazide and loop diuretics and may increase the risk of dehydration and hypotension (see section 4.4).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b9908a1a-c9e1-4cfc-ad05-9bd4f2b282f3"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:e0799d46-0074-47d9-b4db-2580f1a1d3ff", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Insulin and insulin secretagogues", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e0799d46-0074-47d9-b4db-2580f1a1d3ff", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Insulin and insulin secretagogues, such as sulphonylureas, may increase the risk of hypoglycaemia. Therefore, a lower dose of insulin or an insulin secretagogue may be required to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia when used in combination with empagliflozin (see sections 4.2 and 4.8).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e0799d46-0074-47d9-b4db-2580f1a1d3ff"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:8dab208a-f8a2-47b5-bb65-db75a1933883", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Pharmacokinetic interactions", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "8dab208a-f8a2-47b5-bb65-db75a1933883", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:8dab208a-f8a2-47b5-bb65-db75a1933883"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:f92f4b0d-f96a-4cd5-9830-ecd27c66c021", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Effects of other medicinal products on empagliflozin", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "f92f4b0d-f96a-4cd5-9830-ecd27c66c021", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In vitro data suggest that the primary route of metabolism of empagliflozin in humans is glucuronidation by uridine 5'-diphosphoglucuronosyltransferases UGT1A3, UGT1A8, UGT1A9, and UGT2B7. Empagliflozin is a substrate of the human uptake transporters OAT3, OATP1B1, and OATP1B3, but not OAT1 and OCT2. Empagliflozin is a substrate of P-glycoprotein (P-gp) and breast cancer resistance protein (BCRP).\n\nCo-administration of empagliflozin with probenecid, an inhibitor of UGT enzymes and OAT3, resulted in a 26% increase in peak empagliflozin plasma concentrations (Cmax) and a 53% increase in area under the concentration-time curve (AUC). These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.\n\nThe effect of UGT induction (e.g. induction by rifampicin or phenytoin) on empagliflozin has not been studied. Co-treatment with known inducers of UGT enzymes is not recommended due to a potential risk of decreased efficacy. If an inducer of these UGT enzymes must be co-administered, monitoring of glycaemic control to assess response to Jardiance is appropriate.\n\nAn interaction study with gemfibrozil, an in vitro inhibitor of OAT3 and OATP1B1/1B3 transporters, showed that empagliflozin Cmax increased by 15% and AUC increased by 59% following coadministration. These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.\n\nInhibition of OATP1B1/1B3 transporters by co-administration with rifampicin resulted in a 75% increase in Cmax and a 35% increase in AUC of empagliflozin. These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.\n\nEmpagliflozin exposure was similar with and without co-administration with verapamil, a P-gp inhibitor, indicating that inhibition of P-gp does not have any clinically relevant effect on empagliflozin.\n\nInteraction studies suggest that the pharmacokinetics of empagliflozin were not influenced by coadministration with metformin, glimepiride, pioglitazone, sitagliptin, linagliptin, warfarin, verapamil, ramipril, simvastatin, torasemide and hydrochlorothiazide.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:f92f4b0d-f96a-4cd5-9830-ecd27c66c021"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:4108c328-e013-4b32-8dd6-9c87d990eeb6", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Effects of empagliflozin on other medicinal products", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4108c328-e013-4b32-8dd6-9c87d990eeb6", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin may increase renal lithium excretion and the blood lithium levels may be decreased. Serum concentration of lithium should be monitored more frequently after empagliflozin initiation and dose changes. Please refer the patient to the lithium prescribing doctor in order to monitor serum concentration of lithium.\n\nBased on in vitro studies, empagliflozin does not inhibit, inactivate, or induce CYP450 isoforms. Empagliflozin does not inhibit UGT1A1, UGT1A3, UGT1A8, UGT1A9, or UGT2B7. Drug-drug interactions involving the major CYP450 and UGT isoforms with empagliflozin and concomitantly administered substrates of these enzymes are therefore considered unlikely.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4108c328-e013-4b32-8dd6-9c87d990eeb6"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:e8158717-c350-4032-bda0-9a654038afcd", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Common", "page_number": 54, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e8158717-c350-4032-bda0-9a654038afcd", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "- genital yeast infection (thrush)\n- passing more urine than usual or needing to pass urine more often\n- itching\n- rash or red skin - this may be itchy and include raised bumps, oozing fluid or blisters\n- thirst\n- blood tests may show an increase in blood fat (cholesterol) levels in your blood\n- constipation", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e8158717-c350-4032-bda0-9a654038afcd"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:a0ddb39b-c2b1-4561-99f1-7dc562743052", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Major hypoglycaemia (events requiring assistance)", "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "a0ddb39b-c2b1-4561-99f1-7dc562743052", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "No increase in major hypoglycaemia was observed with empagliflozin compared to placebo as monotherapy, add-on to metformin, add-on to metformin and a sulphonylurea, add-on to pioglitazone with or without metformin, add-on to linagliptin and metformin, as adjunct to standard care therapy and for the combination of empagliflozin with metformin in drug-naïve patients compared to those treated with empagliflozin and metformin as individual components. An increased frequency was noted when given as add-on to basal insulin with or without metformin and with or without a sulphonylurea (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 1.3%, placebo: 0% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg: 0%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 1.3%, placebo 0% over the 78-week trial), and add-on to MDI insulin with or without metformin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0.5%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 0.5%, placebo: 0.5% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg: 1.6%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 0.5%, placebo: 1.6% over the 52-week trial).\n\nIn the EMPEROR heart failure studies, major hypoglycaemia was observed at similar frequencies in patients with diabetes mellitus when treated with empagliflozin and placebo as add-on to sulphonylurea or insulin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 2.2%, placebo: 1.9%).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:a0ddb39b-c2b1-4561-99f1-7dc562743052"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:10a7c9c3-041a-4930-8c48-78dcb2a4d4e5", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Vaginal moniliasis, vulvovaginitis, balanitis and other genital infection", "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "10a7c9c3-041a-4930-8c48-78dcb2a4d4e5", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Vaginal moniliasis, vulvovaginitis, balanitis and other genital infections were reported more frequently in patients treated with empagliflozin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 4.0%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 3.9%) compared to placebo (1.0%). These infections were reported more frequently in females treated with empagliflozin compared to placebo, and the difference in frequency was less pronounced in males. The genital tract infections were mild or moderate in intensity.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:10a7c9c3-041a-4930-8c48-78dcb2a4d4e5"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:04735944-4719-46b2-961f-4a9e5e6e4bf2", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "04735944-4719-46b2-961f-4a9e5e6e4bf2", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In the EMPEROR heart failure studies, the frequency of these infections was more pronounced in patients with diabetes mellitus (empagliflozin 10 mg: 2.3%; placebo: 0.8%) than in patients without diabetes mellitus (empagliflozin 10 mg: 1.7%; placebo: 0.7%) when treated with empagliflozin compared to placebo.\n\nCases of phimosis/acquired phimosis have been reported concurrent with genital infections and in some cases, circumcision was required.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:04735944-4719-46b2-961f-4a9e5e6e4bf2"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:d5de7e51-25cd-47f4-847d-80a99d4d79fb", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Increased urination", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d5de7e51-25cd-47f4-847d-80a99d4d79fb", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Increased urination (including the predefined terms pollakiuria, polyuria, and nocturia) was observed at higher frequencies in patients treated with empagliflozin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 3.5%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 3.3%) compared to placebo (1.4%). Increased urination was mostly mild or moderate in intensity. The frequency of reported nocturia was similar for placebo and empagliflozin (&lt; 1%).\n\nIn the EMPEROR heart failure studies, increased urination was observed at similar frequencies in patients treated with empagliflozin and placebo (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0.9%, placebo 0.5%).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d5de7e51-25cd-47f4-847d-80a99d4d79fb"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:6ce25d94-8bf5-405d-9cb2-1dde894dd61e", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Urinary tract infection", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6ce25d94-8bf5-405d-9cb2-1dde894dd61e", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The overall frequency of urinary tract infection reported as adverse event was similar in patients treated with empagliflozin 25 mg and placebo (7.0% and 7.2%) and higher in empagliflozin 10 mg (8.8%). Similar to placebo, urinary tract infection was reported more frequently for empagliflozin in patients with a history of chronic or recurrent urinary tract infections. The intensity (mild, moderate, severe) of urinary tract infection was similar in patients treated with empagliflozin and placebo. Urinary tract infection was reported more frequently in females treated with empagliflozin compared to placebo; there was no difference in males.", "PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:6ce25d94-8bf5-405d-9cb2-1dde894dd61e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6ce25d94-8bf5-405d-9cb2-1dde894dd61e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:12f4b3f5-2014-4e1c-8cec-ce62be529fa7", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Volume depletion", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "12f4b3f5-2014-4e1c-8cec-ce62be529fa7", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The overall frequency of volume depletion (including the predefined terms blood pressure (ambulatory) decreased, blood pressure systolic decreased, dehydration, hypotension, hypovolaemia, orthostatic hypotension, and syncope) was similar in patients treated with empagliflozin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0.6%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 0.4%) and placebo (0.3%). The frequency of volume depletion events was increased in patients 75 years and older treated with empagliflozin 10 mg (2.3%) or empagliflozin 25 mg (4.3%) compared to placebo (2.1%).", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:12f4b3f5-2014-4e1c-8cec-ce62be529fa7"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:11d431cf-486f-4bdb-9a4c-9005159978d5", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Blood creatinine increased/Glomerular filtration rate decreased", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "11d431cf-486f-4bdb-9a4c-9005159978d5", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The overall frequency of patients with increased blood creatinine and decreased glomerular filtration rate were similar between empagliflozin and placebo (blood creatinine increased: empagliflozin 10 mg 0.6%, empagliflozin 25 mg 0.1%, placebo 0.5%; glomerular filtration rate decreased: empagliflozin 10 mg 0.1%, empagliflozin 25 mg 0%, placebo 0.3%).\n\nInitial increases in creatinine and initial decreases in estimated glomerular filtration rates in patients treated with empagliflozin were generally transient during continuous treatment or reversible after drug discontinuation of treatment.\n\nConsistently, in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME study, patients treated with empagliflozin experienced an initial fall in eGFR (mean: 3 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ). Thereafter, eGFR was maintained during continued treatment. Mean eGFR returned to baseline after treatment discontinuation suggesting acute haemodynamic changes may play a role in these renal function changes. This phenomenon is also observed in the EMPEROR heart failure studies and the EMPA-KIDNEY study.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:11d431cf-486f-4bdb-9a4c-9005159978d5"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:0281fd9a-8e55-40c7-8e53-0667bee248d3", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Serum lipids increased", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "0281fd9a-8e55-40c7-8e53-0667bee248d3", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Mean percent increases from baseline for empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg versus placebo, respectively, were total cholesterol 4.9% and 5.7% versus 3.5%; HDL-cholesterol 3.3% and 3.6% versus 0.4%; LDL-cholesterol 9.5% and 10.0% versus 7.5%; triglycerides 9.2% and 9.9% versus 10.5%.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:0281fd9a-8e55-40c7-8e53-0667bee248d3"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:96d7c009-ca57-4dd5-9150-c27544ad94b2", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Haematocrit increased", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "96d7c009-ca57-4dd5-9150-c27544ad94b2", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Mean changes from baseline in haematocrit were 3.4% and 3.6% for empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg, respectively, compared to 0.1% for placebo. In the EMPA-REG Outcome study, haematocrit values returned towards baseline values after a follow-up period of 30 days after treatment stop.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:96d7c009-ca57-4dd5-9150-c27544ad94b2"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:592209f6-6bc2-414a-98b7-ec19c04a83ef", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Paediatric population", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "592209f6-6bc2-414a-98b7-ec19c04a83ef", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In the DINAMO trial 157 children aged 10 years and above with type 2 diabetes were treated, in which 52 patients received empagliflozin, 52 linagliptin and 53 placebo (see section 5.1). During the placebo-controlled phase, the most frequent adverse drug reaction was hypoglycaemia with higher overall rates for patients in the empagliflozin pooled group compared with placebo (empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg, pooled: 23.1%, placebo: 9.4%). None of these events was severe or required assistance.\n\nOverall, the safety profile in children was similar to the safety profile in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus.", "PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:592209f6-6bc2-414a-98b7-ec19c04a83ef"}], "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:592209f6-6bc2-414a-98b7-ec19c04a83ef"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:4b506e4d-9c65-44eb-a962-96d6ca04ac0e", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Reporting of suspected adverse reactions", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4b506e4d-9c65-44eb-a962-96d6ca04ac0e", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Reporting suspected adverse reactions after authorisation of the medicinal product is important. It allows continued monitoring of the benefit/risk balance of the medicinal product. Healthcare professionals are asked to report any suspected adverse reactions via the national reporting system listed in Appendix V.", "PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:4b506e4d-9c65-44eb-a962-96d6ca04ac0e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4b506e4d-9c65-44eb-a962-96d6ca04ac0e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:1e76e7fd-d001-43a5-a0a5-01ecc9f886f4", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Mechanism of action", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "1e76e7fd-d001-43a5-a0a5-01ecc9f886f4", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin is a reversible, highly potent (IC50 of 1.3 nmol) and selective competitive inhibitor of sodium-glucose co-transporter 2 (SGLT2). Empagliflozin does not inhibit other glucose transporters important for glucose transport into peripheral tissues and is 5 000 times more selective for SGLT2 versus SGLT1, the major transporter responsible for glucose absorption in the gut. SGLT2 is highly expressed in the kidney, whereas expression in other tissues is absent or very low. It is responsible, as the predominant transporter, for the reabsorption of glucose from the glomerular filtrate back into the circulation. In patients with type 2 diabetes and hyperglycaemia a higher amount of glucose is filtered and reabsorbed.\n\nEmpagliflozin improves glycaemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes by reducing renal glucose reabsorption. The amount of glucose removed by the kidney through this glucuretic mechanism is dependent on blood glucose concentration and GFR. Inhibition of SGLT2 in patients with type 2 diabetes and hyperglycaemia leads to excess glucose excretion in the urine. In addition, initiation of empagliflozin increases excretion of sodium resulting in osmotic diuresis and reduced intravascular volume.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:1e76e7fd-d001-43a5-a0a5-01ecc9f886f4"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:deecb14f-6525-4bb3-819d-fd6e87487433", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "", "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "deecb14f-6525-4bb3-819d-fd6e87487433", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In patients with type 2 diabetes, urinary glucose excretion increased immediately following the first dose of empagliflozin and is continuous over the 24 hour dosing interval. Increased urinary glucose excretion was maintained at the end of the 4-week treatment period, averaging approximately 78 g/day. Increased urinary glucose excretion resulted in an immediate reduction in plasma glucose levels in patients with type 2 diabetes.\n\nEmpagliflozin improves both fasting and post-prandial plasma glucose levels. The mechanism of action of empagliflozin is independent of beta cell function and insulin pathway and this contributes to a low risk of hypoglycaemia. Improvement of surrogate markers of beta cell function including Homeostasis Model Assessment-β (HOMA-β) was noted. In addition, urinary glucose excretion triggers calorie loss, associated with body fat loss and body weight reduction. The glucosuria observed with empagliflozin is accompanied by diuresis which may contribute to sustained and moderate reduction of blood pressure.\n\nEmpagliflozin also reduces sodium reabsorption and increases the delivery of sodium to the distal tubule. This may influence several physiological functions including, but not restricted to: increasing tubuloglomerular feedback and reducing intraglomerular pressure, lowering both pre- and afterload of the heart, downregulating of sympathetic activity and reducing left ventricular wall stress as evidenced by lower NT-proBNP values which may have beneficial effects on cardiac remodeling, filling pressures and diastolic function as well as preserving kidney structure and function. Other effects such as an increase in haematocrit, a reduction in body weight and blood pressure may further contribute to the beneficial cardiac and renal effects.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:deecb14f-6525-4bb3-819d-fd6e87487433"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:d624b43c-483f-4835-982f-ebfc6b4bcfc2", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Clinical efficacy and safety", "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d624b43c-483f-4835-982f-ebfc6b4bcfc2", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:d624b43c-483f-4835-982f-ebfc6b4bcfc2"}], "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d624b43c-483f-4835-982f-ebfc6b4bcfc2"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:2a5be72d-81f0-4e49-b100-65202149e3a2", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus", "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2a5be72d-81f0-4e49-b100-65202149e3a2", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Both improvement of glycaemic control and reduction of cardiovascular morbidity and mortality are an integral part of the treatment of type 2 diabetes.\n\nGlycaemic efficacy and cardiovascular outcomes have been assessed in a total of 14 663 patients with type 2 diabetes who were treated in 12 double-blind, placebo- and active-controlled clinical studies, of which 9 295 received empagliflozin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 4 165 patients; empagliflozin 25 mg: 5 130 patients). Five studies had treatment durations of 24 weeks; extensions of those and other studies had patients exposed to empagliflozin for up to 102 weeks.\n\nTreatment with empagliflozin as monotherapy and in combination with metformin, pioglitazone, a sulphonylurea, DPP-4 inhibitors, and insulin lead to clinically relevant improvements in HbA1c, fasting plasma glucose (FPG), body weight, and systolic and diastolic blood pressure. Administration of empagliflozin 25 mg resulted in a higher proportion of patients achieving HbA1c goal of less than 7% and fewer patients needing glycaemic rescue compared to empagliflozin 10 mg and placebo. Higher baseline HbA1c was associated with a greater reduction in HbA1c. In addition, empagliflozin as adjunct to standard care therapy reduced cardiovascular mortality in patients with type 2 diabetes and established cardiovascular disease.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2a5be72d-81f0-4e49-b100-65202149e3a2"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:75c96592-f767-4df2-9e70-b76cf412ebf1", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Monotherapy", "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "75c96592-f767-4df2-9e70-b76cf412ebf1", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The efficacy and safety of empagliflozin as monotherapy was evaluated in a double-blind, placebo- and active-controlled study of 24 weeks duration in treatment-naïve patients. Treatment with empagliflozin resulted in a statistically significant (p &lt; 0.0001) reduction in HbA1c compared to placebo (Table 2) and a clinically meaningful decrease in FPG.\n\nIn a pre-specified analysis of patients (N = 201) with a baseline HbA1c ≥ 8.5%, treatment resulted in a reduction in HbA1c from baseline of -1.44% for empagliflozin 10 mg, -1.43% for empagliflozin 25 mg, -1.04% for sitagliptin, and an increase of 0.01% for placebo.", "PI_SECTION_CONTAINS_SAFETY": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:75c96592-f767-4df2-9e70-b76cf412ebf1"}], "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:75c96592-f767-4df2-9e70-b76cf412ebf1"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:fbac01df-4a29-4b24-9891-f9197379ea6e", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "", "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "fbac01df-4a29-4b24-9891-f9197379ea6e", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In the double-blind placebo-controlled extension of this study, reductions of HbA1c, body weight and blood pressure were sustained up to Week 76.\n\nTable 2: Efficacy results of a 24 week placebo-controlled study of empagliflozin as monotherapy a\n\n|                                                              |   Placebo | Jardiance             | Jardiance             | Sitagliptin            |\n|--------------------------------------------------------------|-----------|-----------------------|-----------------------|------------------------|\n|                                                              |           | 10 mg                 | 25 mg                 | 100 mg                 |\n| N                                                            |       228 | 224                   | 224                   | 223                    |\n| HbA1c (%)                                                    |           |                       |                       |                        |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              |      7.91 | 7.87                  | 7.86                  | 7.85                   |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       |      0.08 | -0.66                 | -0.78                 | -0.66                  |\n| Difference from placebo 1 (97.5% CI)                         |           | -0.74* (-0.90, -0.57) | -0.85* (-1.01, -0.69) | -0.73 (-0.88, -0.59) 3 |\n| N                                                            |       208 | 204                   | 202                   | 200                    |\n| Patients (%) achieving HbA1c < 7% with baseline HbA1c ≥ 7% 2 |      12.0 | 35.3                  | 43.6                  | 37.5                   |\n| N                                                            |       228 | 224                   | 224                   | 223                    |\n| Body Weight (kg)                                             |           |                       |                       |                        |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              |     78.23 | 78.35                 | 77.80                 | 79.31                  |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       |     -0.33 | -2.26                 | -2.48                 | 0.18                   |\n| Difference from placebo 1 (97.5% CI)                         |           | -1.93* (-2.48, -1.38) | -2.15* (-2.70, -1.60) | 0.52 (-0.04, 1.00) 3   |\n| N                                                            |       228 | 224                   | 224                   | 223                    |\n| SBP (mmHg) 4                                                 |           |                       |                       |                        |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              |     130.4 | 133.0                 | 129.9                 | 132.5                  |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       |      -0.3 | -2.9                  | -3.7                  | 0.5                    |\n| Difference from placebo 1 (97.5% CI)                         |           | -2.6* (-5.2, -0.0)    | -3.4* (-6.0, -0.9)    | 0.8 (-1.4, 3.1) 3      |\n\na Full analysis set (FAS) using last observation carried forward (LOCF) prior to glycaemic rescue therapy\n\n1 Mean adjusted for baseline value\n\n2 Not evaluated for statistical significance as a result of the sequential confirmatory testing procedure 3 95% CI\n\n4 LOCF, values after antihypertensive rescue censored\n\n* p-value &lt; 0.0001", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:fbac01df-4a29-4b24-9891-f9197379ea6e"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:691c0d49-486d-4575-8859-432aa3d2c8b7", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Combination therapy", "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "691c0d49-486d-4575-8859-432aa3d2c8b7", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:691c0d49-486d-4575-8859-432aa3d2c8b7"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:5e98039a-f382-497c-9aae-2db86ec89dc1", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Empagliflozin as add-on to metformin, sulphonylurea, pioglitazone", "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "5e98039a-f382-497c-9aae-2db86ec89dc1", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin as add-on to metformin, metformin and a sulphonylurea, or pioglitazone with or without metformin resulted in statistically significant (p &lt; 0.0001) reductions in HbA1c and body weight compared to placebo (Table 3). In addition it resulted in a clinically meaningful reduction in FPG, systolic and diastolic blood pressure compared to placebo.\n\nIn the double-blind placebo-controlled extension of these studies, reduction of HbA1c, body weight and blood pressure were sustained up to Week 76.", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:5e98039a-f382-497c-9aae-2db86ec89dc1"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:e300cce3-3c80-4879-b4e9-84a0ed4ef53b", "@type": "PISection", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "", "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e300cce3-3c80-4879-b4e9-84a0ed4ef53b", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Table 3: Efficacy results of 24 week placebo-controlled studies a\n\n|                                                              | Add-on to metformin therapy                     | Add-on to metformin therapy                     | Add-on to metformin therapy                     |\n|--------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|\n|                                                              | Placebo                                         | 10 mg                                           | 25 mg                                           |\n| N                                                            | 207                                             | 217                                             | 213                                             |\n| HbA1c (%)                                                    |                                                 |                                                 |                                                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              | 7.90                                            | 7.94                                            | 7.86                                            |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       | -0.13                                           | -0.70                                           | -0.77                                           |\n| Difference from placebo 1 (97.5% CI)                         |                                                 | -0.57*                                          | -0.64*                                          |\n| N                                                            |                                                 | (-0.72, -0.42)                                  | (-0.79, -0.48)                                  |\n|                                                              | 184                                             | 199                                             | 191                                             |\n| Patients (%) achieving HbA1c < 7% with baseline HbA1c ≥ 7% 2 | 12.5                                            | 37.7                                            | 38.7                                            |\n| N                                                            | 207                                             | 217                                             | 213                                             |\n| Body Weight (kg)                                             |                                                 |                                                 |                                                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              | 79.73                                           | 81.59                                           | 82.21                                           |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       | -0.45                                           | -2.08                                           | -2.46                                           |\n| Difference from placebo 1                                    |                                                 | -1.63*                                          | -2.01*                                          |\n| (97.5% CI)                                                   |                                                 | (-2.17, -1.08)                                  | (-2.56, -1.46)                                  |\n| N                                                            | 207                                             | 217                                             | 213                                             |\n| SBP (mmHg) 2                                                 |                                                 |                                                 |                                                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              | 128.6                                           | 129.6                                           | 130.0                                           |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       | -0.4                                            | -4.5                                            | -5.2                                            |\n| Difference from placebo 1                                    |                                                 | -4.1*                                           | -4.8*                                           |\n| (95% CI)                                                     |                                                 | (-6.2, -2.1)                                    | (-6.9, -2.7)                                    |\n| Add-on to metformin and a sulphonylurea therapy              | Add-on to metformin and a sulphonylurea therapy | Add-on to metformin and a sulphonylurea therapy | Add-on to metformin and a sulphonylurea therapy |\n|                                                              | Placebo                                         | 10 mg                                           | 25 mg                                           |\n| N                                                            | 225                                             | 225                                             | 216                                             |\n| HbA1c (%)                                                    |                                                 |                                                 |                                                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              | 8.15                                            | 8.07                                            | 8.10                                            |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       | -0.17                                           | -0.82                                           | -0.77                                           |\n| Difference from placebo 1                                    |                                                 | -0.64*                                          | -0.59*                                          |\n| (97.5% CI)                                                   |                                                 | (-0.79, -0.49)                                  | (-0.74, -0.44)                                  |\n| N                                                            | 216                                             | 209                                             | 202                                             |\n| Patients (%) achieving HbA1c < 7% with baseline HbA1c ≥ 7% 2 | 9.3                                             | 26.3                                            | 32.2                                            |\n| N                                                            | 225                                             | 225                                             | 216                                             |\n| Body Weight (kg)                                             |                                                 |                                                 |                                                 |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              | 76.23                                           | 77.08                                           | 77.50                                           |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       | -0.39                                         