 "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:safety:ae47ec96-f72f-4c68-bc08-df055c0da0ec", "@type": "SafetyStatement", "graphScope": "brand", "page_number": 53, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "ae47ec96-f72f-4c68-bc08-df055c0da0ec", "statement_text": "Ketoacidosis, seen uncommonly (may affect up to 1 in 100 people)", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "DERIVED_FROM_SECTION": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ae47ec96-f72f-4c68-bc08-df055c0da0ec"}], "DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Sheet", "section_type": "sheet", "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx", "sheet_name": "Sheet", "source_document_id": "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc", "text": "# Sheet\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000958 | Match Text: In patients with CKD, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of CV death or kidney disease progression by 28% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPA-KIDNEY trial, a randomised, parallel-group, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 6609 patients with CKD, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=3304) were evaluated vs placebo (n=3305). Patients were adults with an eGFR ≥ 20, < 45 mL/min/1.73 m2 ; or an eGFR ≥ 45, < 90 mL/min/1.73 m2 with a uACR ≥ 200 mg/g. The primary endpoint in the EMPA-KIDNEY trial was a composite of CV death or progression of kidney disease defined as end-stage kidney disease (the initiation of maintenance dialysis or receipt of a kidney transplant), a sustained decrease in the eGFR to <10 ml/min/1.73 m2, a sustained decrease in eGFR of ≥40% from baseline, or death from renal causes. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 28% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.72; 95% CI: 0.64, 0.82; p<0.001).  CI=confidence interval; CKD=chronic kidney disease; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration;  HR=hazard ratio; RRR=relative risk reduction; T2D=type 2 diabetes; uACR=urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio. | Reference: Herrington 2022 NEJM, Nov 4, 2022 | AMA Style Guide References: Herrington 2022 N Engl J Med, Nov 4, 2022. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: CPNT-CRP-100323 JARDIANCE (v3.0)\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000960 | Match Text: In patients with HF with LVEF >40%, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of CV death or HHF by 21% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) was evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).  CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular;  HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure; HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction;  NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction. | Reference: RD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461 | AMA Style Guide References: Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: CPNT-CRP-100331 JARDIANCE (v1.0)\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000964 | Match Text: In patients with CKD, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of first and recurrent all-cause hospitalisation by 14% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPA-KIDNEY trial, a randomised, parallel-group, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 6609 patients with CKD, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=3304) were evaluated vs placebo (n=3305). Patients were adults with an eGFR ≥ 20, < 45 mL/min/1.73 m2 ; or an eGFR ≥ 45, < 90 mL/min/1.73 m2 with a uACR ≥ 200 mg/g. The primary endpoint in the EMPA-KIDNEY trial was a composite of CV death or progression of kidney disease defined as end-stage kidney disease (the initiation of maintenance dialysis or receipt of a kidney transplant), a sustained decrease in the eGFR to <10 ml/min/1.73 m2, a sustained decrease in eGFR of ≥40% from baseline, or death from renal causes. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 28% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.72; 95% CI: 0.64, 0.82; p<0.001).  Hospitalisation for any cause was a key secondary outcome of the EMPA-KIDNEY trial. The analysis of hospitalisations for any cause included the first and all subsequent events (JARDIANCE, 1611 hospitalisations in 960 patients; placebo, 1895 hospitalisations in 1035 patients).  CI=confidence interval; CKD=chronic kidney disease; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration;  HR=hazard ratio; RRR=relative risk reduction; uACR=urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio. | Reference: Herrington 2022 NEJM, Nov 4, 2022 | AMA Style Guide References: Herrington 2022 N Engl J Med, Nov 4, 2022. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: \nCPNT-CRP-100326 JARDIANCE (v1.0)\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000966 | Match Text: In patients with LVEF ≤ 40%, JARDIANCE slowed the decline of renal function by 4 times | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 3730 patients with HFrEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=1863) was evaluated vs placebo (n=1867). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤ 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Reduced trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 25% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.75; 95% CI: 0.65, 0.86; p<0.001).   The rate of decline in eGFR was a prespecified secondary outcome of the EMPEROR-Reduced trial.  CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate; HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure; HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction;  NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction | Reference: RD-157832 JARDIANCE M. Packer, S.D. Anker, J. Butler; Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli | AMA Style Guide References: Packer M, Anker SD, Butler J. Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000968 | Match Text: In patients with LVEF > 40%, JARDIANCE slowed the decline of renal function by 2 times | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) was evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).  The rate of decline in eGFR was a prespecified secondary outcome of the EMPEROR-Preserved trial.  CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate; HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure; HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction;  NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction | Reference: RD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461 | AMA Style Guide References: Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000969 | Match Text: In patients with T2D and CVD, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of CV death by 38% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: The primary composite outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial was 3-point MACE, composed of death from CV causes, nonfatal MI, or nonfatal stroke, as analyzed in the pooled JARDIANCE group vs the placebo group. Patients were adults with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke. The 14% RRR in 3-point MACE (HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99; p<0.001 for noninferiority; p=0.04 for superiority) was driven by a reduction in the risk of CV death (HR=0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77) and 38% RRR in CV death was achieved in the overall EMPA-REG OUTCOME population for the duration of the trial.  Pooled data from 10-mg and 25-mg doses of JARDIANCE; both doses showed a comparable reduction in the risk of CV death.  In addition to reducing the risk of CV death when added to the standard of care, JARDIANCE also lowered HbA1c. In addition, JARDIANCE demonstrated reduction in weight and blood pressure. JARDIANCE is not indicated for weight loss or reduction of blood pressure.  CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; HR=hazard ratio; MACE=major adverse cardiovascular events; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; RRR=relative risk reduction; SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor; T2D=type 2 diabetes. | Reference: \nRD-103048 Zinman B, Wanner C, Lachin JM, et al. New Eng J Med. 2016;373:2117-28. | AMA Style Guide References: Zinman B, Wanner C, Lachin JM, et al. N Engl J Med. 2016;373:2117-28. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: \nCPNT-CRP-100327 JARDIANCE (v2.0)\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000959 | Match Text: In patients with HF with LVEF ≤40%, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of CV death or HHF by 25% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 3730 patients with HFrEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=1863) was evaluated vs placebo (n=1867). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤ 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Reduced trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 25% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.75; 95% CI: 0.65, 0.86; p<0.001).  CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular;  HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure; HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction;  NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction | Reference: RD-157832 JARDIANCE M. Packer, S.D. Anker, J. Butler; Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli | AMA Style Guide References: Packer M, Anker SD, Butler J. Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: CPNT-CRP-100329 JARDIANCE (v1.0)\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000965 | Match Text: In patients with LVEF ≤ 40%, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of first and recurrent HHF by 30% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 3730 patients with HFrEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=1863) was evaluated vs placebo (n=1867). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤ 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Reduced trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 25% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.75; 95% CI: 0.65, 0.86; p<0.001).   The occurrence of all HHF, including first and recurrent events, was a prespecified secondary outcome of the EMPEROR-Reduced trial.  In addition to the RRR of all HHF, including first and recurrent events, the risk of total hospitalisations for any reason was also significantly reduced (HR=0.85, 95% CI: 0.75, 0.95).  CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular;  HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure; HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction;  NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction | Reference: RD-157832 JARDIANCE M. Packer, S.D. Anker, J. Butler; Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli | AMA Style Guide References: Packer M, Anker SD, Butler J. Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: CPNT-CRP-100330 JARDIANCE (v2.0)\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000967 | Match Text: In patients with LVEF > 40%, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of first and recurrent HHF by 27% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) was evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).  The occurrence of all HHF, including first and recurrent events, was a prespecified secondary outcome of the EMPEROR-Preserved trial.  CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular;  HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure; HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction;  NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction | Reference: RD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461 | AMA Style Guide References: Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: CPNT-CRP-100332 JARDIANCE (v1.0)\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000971 | Match Text: The interconnected nature of cardio, renal and metabolic diseases ampliﬁes and accelerates risk. | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Reference: 2020 - Cardiorenal Syndrome in Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus - Rational Use f Sodium-glucose Cotransporte | AMA Style Guide References: Cardiorenal Syndrome in Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus - Rational Use f Sodium-glucose Cotransporte. 2020. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000973 | Match Text: JARDIANCE has a proven safety and tolerability profile across multiple trials. | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Safety | Footnotes: Please see the SmPC for the full list of AEs and full list of special warnings and precautions for use, as well as dosing details.  AE=adverse event; SmPC=Summary of Product Characteristics | Reference: Jardiance - EU/SmPC  | AMA Style Guide References: - EU/SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000978 | Match Text: Adopting guideline-recommended treatments improves patient outcomes. | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | Reference: 2023 - Contemporary Use of Sodium-Glucose Cotransporter-2 Inhibitor Therapy Among Patients Hospitali  | AMA Style Guide References: Contemporary Use of Sodium-Glucose Cotransporter-2 Inhibitor Therapy Among Patients Hospitali. 2023. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000979 | Match Text: Despite their proven potential, evidence-based recommendations are often underutilized | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | Reference: 2023 - Contemporary Use of Sodium-Glucose Cotransporter-2 Inhibitor Therapy Among Patients Hospitali \n\n2019 - Reasons for Lack of Improvement in Treatment With Evidence-Based Therapies in Heart Failure | AMA Style Guide References: Contemporary Use of Sodium-Glucose Cotransporter-2 Inhibitor Therapy Among Patients Hospitali. 2023.\n\nReasons for Lack of Improvement in Treatment With Evidence-Based Therapies in Heart Failure. 2019. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001161 | Match Text: In patients with HF, JARDIANCE delivered consistent efficacy regardless of T2D or CKD status | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 3730 patients with HFrEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=1863) was evaluated vs placebo (n=1867). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤ 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Reduced trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 25% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.75; 95% CI: 0.65, 0.86; p<0.001).   Results of prespecified subgroup analyses in the EMPEROR-Reduced trial. Diabetes at baseline (HR=0.72; 95% CI: 0.60, 0.87); no diabetes at baseline (HR=0.78; 95% CI: 0.64, 0.97). eGFR (CKD-EPI) ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 at baseline (HR=0.67; 95% CI: 0.55, 0.83); eGFR (CKD-EPI) < 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 at baseline (HR=0.83; 95% CI: 0.69, 1.00).  In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) was evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).  Results of prespecified subgroup analyses in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial. Diabetes at baseline (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.67, 0.94); no diabetes at baseline (HR=0.78; 95% CI: 0.64, 0.95). eGFR (CKD-EPI) ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 at baseline (HR=0.81; 95% CI: 0.65, 1.00); eGFR (CKD-EPI) < 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 at baseline (HR=0.78; 95% CI: 0.66, 0.91).  CI=confidence interval;  CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration;  HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalisation for heart failure;  HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction; T2D=type 2 diabetes.. | Reference: RD-142505 JARDIANCE Packer 2020_Cardiovascular and renal outcomes \n\nRD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461 | AMA Style Guide References: Packer 2020 Cardiovascular and renal outcomes.\n\nAnker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001157 | Match Text: JARDIANCE protected patients with HF by reducing the risk of CV death or HHF | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 3730 patients with HFrEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=1863) was evaluated vs placebo (n=1867). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤ 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Reduced trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 25% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.75; 95% CI: 0.65, 0.86; p<0.001).  In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) was evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).  CI=confidence interval;  CV=cardiovascular; HF=heart failure; HHFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalisation for heart failure;  HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction. | Reference: RD-142505 JARDIANCE Packer 2020_Cardiovascular and renal outcomes\n\nRD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461 | AMA Style Guide References: Packer 2020 Cardiovascular and renal outcomes.\n\nAnker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001158 | Match Text: In patients with HF, JARDIANCE protected the kidneys by slowing the decline of renal function | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 3730 patients with HFrEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=1863) was evaluated vs placebo (n=1867). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤ 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Reduced trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 25% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.75; 95% CI: 0.65, 0.86; p<0.001).  In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) was evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).  The rate of decline in eGFR was a prespecified secondary outcome of the EMPEROR-Preserved and EMPEROR-Reduced trials.  CI=confidence interval;  CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration; HF=heart failure; HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalisation for heart failure;  HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction. | Reference: RD-142505 JARDIANCE Packer 2020_Cardiovascular and renal outcomes\n\nRD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461 | AMA Style Guide References: Packer 2020 Cardiovascular and renal outcomes.\n\nAnker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001160 | Match Text: JARDIANCE demonstrated early benefits when initiated in the hospital | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Safety | Footnotes: In the EMPULSE trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 530 patients with chronic heart failure regardless of LVEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=265) were evaluated in the hospital setting vs placebo (n=265). The primary endpoint in the EMPULSE trial was clinical benefit, defined as a hierarchical composite of death from any cause, number of heart failure events and time to first heart failure event, or a 5-point or greater difference in change from baseline in the KCCQ-TSS at 90 days, as assessed using a win ratio. Patients treated with JARDIANCE were 36% more likely to experience clinical benefit compared with placebo (win ratio=1.36; 95% CI: 1.09, 1.68; p=0.0054).  In the EMPULSE trial, the initiation of empagliflozin for acute HF produced clinical benefit regardless of the degree of symptomatic impairment at baseline and improved symptoms, physical limitations, and quality of life, with benefits seen as early as 15 days and maintained through 90 days.  CI=confidence interval; KCCQ-TSS=Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire Total Symptom Score; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; NYHA=New York Heart Association. | Reference: \nRD-157613 JARDIANCE Voors Nature Medicines\n\n\n25. Kosiborod MN. Circulation. 2022;146(4):279-288.\n | AMA Style Guide References: Voors Nat Med.\n\nKosiborod MN. Circulation. 2022;146(4):279-288. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001172 | Match Text: In patients with T2D and eCVD, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of incident or worsening nephropathy by 39% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 7720 patients with T2D at high cardiovascular risk, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg (n=4867) were evaluated vs placebo (n=2333). Patients were adults with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke. The primary composite outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial was 3-point MACE, composed of death from CV causes, nonfatal MI, or nonfatal stroke, as analysed in the pooled JARDIANCE group vs the placebo group. The result was 14% RRR (1.6% ARR) in 3-point MACE (HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99; p<0.001 for noninferiority; p=0.04 for superiority).   Incident or worsening nephropathy is defined as progression to macroalbuminuria, doubling of serum creatinine, eGFR of ≤ 45 mL/min/1.73 m2; initiation of renal replacement therapy; death from renal disease. Incident or worsening nephropathy was a prespecified component of the secondary microvascular outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial.  CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular;  eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration; HR=hazard ratio; MACE=major adverse cardiovascular events; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; RRR=relative risk reduction; T2D=type 2 diabetes. | Reference: 2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes\n\nRD-149832 JARDIANCE Christoph Wanner The New England Journal of Medicine | AMA Style Guide References: Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes. 2015.\n\nChristoph Wanner The New England Journal of Medicine. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: \nCPNT-CRP-100328 JARDIANCE (v1.0)\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001165 | Match Text: Prescribe JARDIANCE to reduce kidney disease progression or risk of CV death in patients with CKD | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPA-KIDNEY trial, a randomised, parallel-group, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 6609 patients with CKD, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=3304) were evaluated vs placebo (n=3305). Patients were adults with an eGFR ≥ 20, < 45 mL/min/1.73 m2 ; or an eGFR ≥ 45, < 90 mL/min/1.73 m2 with a uACR ≥ 200 mg/g. The primary endpoint in the EMPA-KIDNEY trial was a composite of CV death or progression of kidney disease defined as end-stage kidney disease (the initiation of maintenance dialysis or receipt of a kidney transplant), a sustained decrease in the eGFR to <10 ml/min/1.73 m2, a sustained decrease in eGFR of ≥40% from baseline, or death from renal causes. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 28% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.72; 95% CI: 0.64, 0.82; p<0.001).2  CI=confidence interval; CKD=chronic kidney disease; CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate; HR=hazard ratio; RRR=relative risk reduction uACR=urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio. | Reference: Herrington 2022 NEJM, Nov 4, 2022 \n\nJardiance - SmPC | AMA Style Guide References: Herrington 2022 N Engl J Med, Nov 4, 2022.\n\n- SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001166 | Match Text: EMPA-KIDNEY was the largest and broadest SGLT2i trial of its kind | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: CKD=chronic kidney disease; SGLT2i=sodium glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitor | Reference: Herrington 2022 NEJM, Nov 4, 2022 \n\nEMPA-KIDNEY Collaborative Group Nephrol Dial Transplant 2022 | AMA Style Guide References: Herrington 2022 N Engl J Med, Nov 4, 2022.\n\nEMPA-KIDNEY Collaborative Group Nephrol Dial Transplant. 2022. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001171 | Match Text: In patients with T2D and CVD, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of HHF by 35% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: The primary composite outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial was 3-point MACE, composed of death from CV causes, nonfatal MI, or nonfatal stroke, as analyzed in the pooled JARDIANCE group vs the placebo group. Patients were adults with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke. The 14% RRR in 3-point MACE (HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99; p<0.001 for noninferiority; p=0.04 for superiority) was driven by a reduction in the risk of CV death (HR=0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77).  Hospitalisation for heart failure was a secondary CV outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial (HR=0.65; 95% CI: 0.50, 0.85).  CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure; HR=hazard ratio; MACE=major adverse cardiovascular events; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; RRR=relative risk reduction; T2D=type 2 diabetes. | Reference: 2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes | AMA Style Guide References: Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes. 2015. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001184 | Match Text: JARDIANCE offers triple protection for cardiovascular, renal, and metabolic conditions | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Reference: Herrington 2022 NEJM, Nov 4, 2022\n\n2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes\n\nRD-142505 JARDIANCE Packer 2020_Cardiovascular and renal outcomes\n\nRD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461 | AMA Style Guide References: Herrington 2022 N Engl J Med, Nov 4, 2022.\n\nEmpagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes. 2015.\n\nPacker 2020 Cardiovascular and renal outcomes.\n\nAnker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001188 | Match Text: JARDIANCE may provide the greatest kidney benefit and delay of dialysis when initiated early | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: According to a calculation based on the hypothetical transformation of chronic eGFR slopes into time to kidney failure in an independent publication.  Estimated from each baseline eGFR value by applying the chronic eGFR slopes corresponding to participants on placebo vs JARDIANCE within the prespecified eGFR subgroups (eGFR cutoff points to define subgroups).  CKD=chronic kidney disease; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate. | Reference: 2023 - EMPA-KIDNEY: expanding the range of kidney protection by SGLT2 inhibitors | AMA Style Guide References: EMPA-KIDNEY: expanding the range of kidney protection by SGLT2 inhibitors. 2023. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001192 | Match Text: CKD is a silent, progressive disease often missed and untreated in early phases | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: CKD=chronic kidney disease. | Reference: \n2024 KDIGO Guidelines  | AMA Style Guide References: 2024 KDIGO Guidelines. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001196 | Match Text: JARDIANCE is an easy choice to help protect your patients by reducing CV and renal risk | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Dosing and Administration | Footnotes: CV=cardiovascular | Reference: \nJardiance - EU/SmPC | AMA Style Guide References: - EU/SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001197 | Match Text: JARDIANCE is easy to use across a broad spectrum of patients | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Reference: \nJardiance - EU/SmPC | AMA Style Guide References: - EU/SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001195 | Match Text: Proactively assess kidney health using uACR and eGFR in patients with hypertension or T2D | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic, Disease Awareness | Footnotes: eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate; T2D=type 2 diabetes; uACR=urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio | Reference: 2024 KDIGO Guidelines \n\nGaitonde Am Fam Physician 2017 | AMA Style Guide References: 2024 KDIGO Guidelines.\n\nGaitonde Am Fam Physician. 2017. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001193 | Match Text: Risk of CV death increases with declining kidney function | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic, Disease Awareness | Footnotes: CV=cardiovascular | Reference: 2012 - Chronic Kidney Disease Prognosis Consortium. Association of kidney disease measures with mort  | AMA Style Guide References: Chronic Kidney Disease Prognosis Consortium. Association of kidney disease measures with mort. 2012. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001198 | Match Text: JARDIANCE dosing recommendation based on indication and kidney function | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Dosing and Administration | Footnotes: CV=cardiovascular | Reference: \nJardiance - EU/SmPC | AMA Style Guide References: - EU/SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001201 | Match Text: More than 100 nephrology, endocrinology, and cardiology guidelines, worldwide, endorse the foundational use of SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | Footnotes: SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitor. | Reference: 2023 - Local/regional guidelines where Empagliflozin/SGLT-2i are recommended | AMA Style Guide References: Local/regional guidelines where Empagliflozin/SGLT-2i are recommended. 2023. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001200 | Match Text: JARDIANCE is 1A recommended for first-line treatment of CKD, with or without T2D | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic, Disease Awareness | Footnotes: CKD=chronic kidney disease; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2024 KDIGO Guidelines | AMA Style Guide References: 2024 KDIGO Guidelines. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001202 | Match Text: International CKD, T2D, and HF guidelines recommend the use of an SGLT2i, such as JARDIANCE, as early as first line | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: CKD=chronic kidney disease; CV=cardiovascular HF=heart failure; SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitor. T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2022 - ADAEASD ConsensusReport_Davies MJ et al, Diabetes Care 2022\n\n2022 - de Boer IH et al., Diabetes Care 2022; 45(12): 3075–90\n\n2024 KDIGO Guidelines\n\nRD-151098 JARDIANCE McDonagh, Metra 2021 ESC HF Guidelines\n\nMcDonagh TA, Metra M, Adamo M, et al. Eur Heart J 2023 \n\nFreinkel Standard of care in Diabetes 2025\n\nSeidu S i wsp. Prim Care Diabetes 2022;16:223\n\nRD-169473 McDonagh TA et al. 2021 Eur Heart J. 2021;42(36):3599-3726\n\nMarx Eur Heart J 2023 | AMA Style Guide References: ADAEASD ConsensusReport Davies MJ et al, Diabetes Care 2022. 2022.\n\nde Boer IH et al., Diabetes Care 2022. 45(12): 3075–90. 2022.\n\n2024 KDIGO Guidelines.\n\nMcDonagh, Metra 2021 ESC HF Guidelines.\n\nMcDonagh TA, Metra M, Adamo M, et al. Eur Heart J. 2023.\n\nFreinkel Standard of care in Diabetes 2025.\n\nSeidu S i wsp. Prim Care Diabetes. 2022;16:223.\n\nMcDonagh TA et al. 2021 Eur Heart J. 2021;42(36):3599-3726.\n\nMarx Eur Heart J. 2023. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001203 | Match Text: Heart failure, regardless of rEF or pEF, is a progressive condition that needs urgent, optimal intervention | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | Footnotes: pEF=preserved ejection fraction; rEF=reduced ejection fraction | Reference: 11. Shah KS et al. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2017;70(20):2476-2486\n\nRD-171272 Schwinger_Cardiovascular Diagnosis and Therapy_2021\n\nAbdin ESC Heart Fail 2021\n\nMaddox JACC 2024 | AMA Style Guide References: Shah KS et al. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2017;70(20):2476-2486.\n\nSchwinger Cardiovascular Diagnosis and Therapy. 2021.\n\nAbdin ESC Heart Fail. 2021.\n\nMaddox J Am Coll Cardiol. 2024. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001204 | Match Text: 1 in 10 patients will die within 1 year after diagnosis of HF | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Footnotes: HF=heart failure | Reference: 2015 - Mortality in heart failure patients | AMA Style Guide References: Mortality in heart failure patients. 2015. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001207 | Match Text: Reduced eGFR is associated with increased risk of all-cause mortality, CV death, and HHF in patients with HF | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Footnotes: CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filatration rate; HF=heart failure; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure | Reference: \n2019 - Heart failure in chronic kidney disease: conclusions from a Kidney Disease | AMA Style Guide References: Heart failure in chronic kidney disease: conclusions from a Kidney Disease. 2019. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001211 | Match Text: In adult patients with HF across the LVEF spectrum, JARDIANCE demonstrated early benefits when initiated in hospital within 1-5 days after stabilization | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Safety | Footnotes: Adult patients with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤40%).  Adult patients with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF >40%).  In the EMPULSE trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 530 patients with chronic heart failure regardless of LVEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=265) were evaluated in the hospital setting vs placebo (n=265). The primary endpoint in the EMPULSE trial was clinical benefit, defined as a hierarchical composite of death from any cause, number of heart failure events and time to first heart failure event, or a 5-point or greater difference in change from baseline in the KCCQ-TSS at 90 days, as assessed using a win ratio. Patients treated with JARDIANCE were 36% more likely to experience clinical benefit compared with placebo (win ratio=1.36; 95% CI: 1.09, 1.68; p=0.0054).   CI=confidence interval; KCCQ-TSS=Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire Total Symptom Score; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; NYHA=New York Heart Association. | Reference: RD-157832 JARDIANCE M. Packer, S.D. Anker, J. Butler; Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli \n\nRD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461\n\nRD-157613 JARDIANCE Voors Nature Medicines | AMA Style Guide References: Packer M, Anker SD, Butler J. Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli.\n\nAnker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461.\n\nVoors Nat Med. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001205 | Match Text: Approximately 1 in 4 patients hospitalized for HF are readmitted within 30 days | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Footnotes: HF=heart failure; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction | Reference: 2020 - Reducing All-cause 30-day Hospital Readmissions for Patients Pres | AMA Style Guide References: Reducing All-cause 30-day Hospital Readmissions for Patients Pres. 2020. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001206 | Match Text: Patients with HF had lower HRQoL compared to those at risk of HF | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Footnotes: HF=heart failure;HRQoL=health-related quality of life | Reference: 2020 - Change of Health-Related Quality of Life Over Time and Its Association With Patient Outcomes | AMA Style Guide References: Change of Health-Related Quality of Life Over Time and Its Association With Patient Outcomes. 2020. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001210 | Match Text: JARDIANCE delivered consistent efficacy regardless of T2D or CKD status of patients with LVEF >40% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) was evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).  Results of prespecified subgroup analyses in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial. Diabetes at baseline (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.67, 0.94); no diabetes at baseline (HR=0.78; 95% CI: 0.64, 0.95). eGFR (CKD-EPI) ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 at baseline (HR=0.81; 95% CI: 0.65, 1.00); eGFR (CKD-EPI) < 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 at baseline (HR=0.78; 95% CI: 0.66, 0.91).  CI=confidence interval;  CKD=chronic kidney disease; CKD-EPI=Chronic Kidney Disease Epidemiology Collaboration; CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration; HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalisation for heart failure;  HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction; T2D=type 2 diabetes. | Reference: RD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461 | AMA Style Guide References: Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001208 | Match Text: JARDIANCE demonstrated significant protection as early as 2 weeks by reducing the risk of CV death or HHF across the LVEF spectrum | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 3730 patients with HFrEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=1863) was evaluated vs placebo (n=1867). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤ 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Reduced trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 25% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.75; 95% CI: 0.65, 0.86; p<0.001).  In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, the effect of empagliflozin to reduce the combined risk of death, hospitalisation for heart failure, or an emergent or urgent heart failure visit was statistically significant at 12 days after randomisation and statistical significance was sustained from day 12 onward (HR, 0.70; 95% CI, 0.63-0.78; p<0.0001).  In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) was evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).   In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, the effect of empagliflozin on time to cardiovascular death or heart failure hospitalization was statistically significant at 18 days after randomisation and statistical significance was sustained from day 18 onward (HR=0.41, 95% CI 0.17–0.99; p=0.0476).  CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; HF=heart failure; HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalisation for heart failure;  HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction | Reference: RD-157832 JARDIANCE M. Packer, S.D. Anker, J. Butler; Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli \n\n2021 - Effect of Empagliflozin on the Clinical Stability of Patients With Heart Failure and a Reduce\n\nRD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461\n\n2022 - Early benefit with empagliflozin in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: insights | AMA Style Guide References: Packer M, Anker SD, Butler J. Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli.\n\nEffect of Empagliflozin on the Clinical Stability of Patients With Heart Failure and a Reduce. 2021.\n\nAnker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461.\n\nEarly benefit with empagliflozin in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: insights. 2022. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001212 | Match Text: JARDIANCE is an easy choice to protect your patients with HF by reducing CV and renal risk | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: CV=cardiovascular; HF=heart failure | Reference: Jardiance - EU/SmPC | AMA Style Guide References: - EU/SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001214 | Match Text: SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, are Class 1 recommended for first-line use in patients with eCVD and T2D like Joana to reduce the risk of CV death and hospitalizations, independent of glucose control | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | Footnotes: CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: Marx Eur Heart J 2023 | AMA Style Guide References: Marx Eur Heart J. 2023. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001218 | Match Text: JARDIANCE reduced the risk of CV death independent of glucose-lowering effects and baseline HbA1c, weight, or eGFR | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c. | Reference: 2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes | AMA Style Guide References: Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes. 2015. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001221 | Match Text: By the time hypertension or T2D is diagnosed, structural kidney damage may already be underway | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: eGFR=estimated  glomerular filtration rate; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2020 - Cardiorenal Syndrome in Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus - Rational Use f Sodium-glucose Cotransporte\n\nMárquez Nefrologia (Engl Ed) 2022\n\n2024 KDIGO Guidelines\n\n\n | AMA Style Guide References: Cardiorenal Syndrome in Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus - Rational Use f Sodium-glucose Cotransporte. 2020.\n\nMárquez Nefrologia (Engl Ed). 2022.\n\n2024 KDIGO Guidelines. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001229 | Match Text: In patients with CKD, JARDIANCE slowed the eGFR decline across the spectrum of uACR | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPA-KIDNEY trial, a randomised, parallel-group, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 6609 patients with CKD, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=3304) were evaluated vs placebo (n=3305). Patients were adults with an eGFR ≥ 20, < 45 mL/min/1.73 m2 ; or an eGFR ≥ 45, < 90 mL/min/1.73 m2 with a uACR ≥ 200 mg/g. The primary endpoint in the EMPA-KIDNEY trial was a composite of CV death or progression of kidney disease defined as end-stage kidney disease (the initiation of maintenance dialysis or receipt of a kidney transplant), a sustained decrease in the eGFR to <10 ml/min/1.73 m2, a sustained decrease in eGFR of ≥40% from baseline, or death from renal causes. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 28% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.72; 95% CI: 0.64, 0.82; p<0.001).  Annual rate of change in eGFR was a prespecified exploratory outcome in the EMPA-KIDNEY trial. Shown are the results of long-term slope, representing the mean (±SE) changes from 2 months after the first dose of JARDIANCE or placebo to the final follow-up visit.   CI=confidence interval; CKD=chronic kidney disease; CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration; HR=hazard ratio; RRR=relative risk reduction; SE=standard error; uACR=urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio. | Reference: Herrington 2022 NEJM, Nov 4, 2022 | AMA Style Guide References: Herrington 2022 N Engl J Med, Nov 4, 2022. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001233 | Match Text: 2024 KDIGO guidelines reinforce SGLT2is as an early and foundational therapy for the management of CKD | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | Footnotes: CKD=chronic kidney disease; KDIGO=Kidney Disease: Improving Global Outcomes; SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor | Reference: 2024 KDIGO Guidelines | AMA Style Guide References: 2024 KDIGO Guidelines. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001235 | Match Text: Early intervention is key to help protect patients with T2D and eCVD by reducing the risk of cardio-renal complications | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Guidelines | Footnotes: eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2022 - Management of Hyperglycemia in Type 2 Diabetes, 2022. A Consensus Report by the American Diab\n\nRD-151098 JARDIANCE McDonagh, Metra 2021 ESC HF Guidelines\n\n2022 - 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure. JACC\n\n2020 - Global, regional, and national burden of chronic kidney disease, 1990–2017: a systematic anal | AMA Style Guide References: Management of Hyperglycemia in Type 2 Diabetes, 2022. A Consensus Report by the American Diab. 2022.\n\nMcDonagh, Metra 2021 ESC HF Guidelines.\n\n2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2022.\n\nGlobal, regional, and national burden of chronic kidney disease, 1990–2017: a systematic anal. 2020. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001236 | Match Text: Complications can begin to develop even before diagnosis of T2D | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic, Disease Awareness | Reference: RD-118297 Diabetes Ramlo-Halsted BA, Edelman SV 5. Ramlo-Halsted BA, Edelman SV. Prim Care. 1999;26\n\nRD-143020 JARDIANCE Perspectives in Diabetes U.K. Prospective Diabetes Study 16 Overview of 6 Years' | AMA Style Guide References: Diabetes Ramlo-Halsted BA, Edelman SV 5. Ramlo-Halsted BA, Edelman SV. Prim Care. 1999;26.\n\nPerspectives in Diabetes Prospective UK Diabetes Study 16 Overview of 6 Years'. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001237 | Match Text: Prescribe JARDIANCE as early, foundational T2D treatment | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: Jardiance - EU/SmPC | AMA Style Guide References: - EU/SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001238 | Match Text: In patients with T2D and eCVD, JARDIANCE reduced the risk of CV death independent of multiple baseline characteristics | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: In the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 7720 patients with T2D at high cardiovascular risk, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE® 10 mg or 25 mg (n=4867) were evaluated vs placebo (n=2333). Patients were adults with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke. The primary composite outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial was 3-point MACE, composed of death from CV causes, nonfatal MI, or nonfatal stroke, as analysed in the pooled JARDIANCE group vs the placebo group. The 14% RRR (1.6% ARR) in 3-point MACE (HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99; p<0.001 for noninferiority; p=0.04 for superiority) was driven by a reduction in the risk of CV death (HR=0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77); there was no change in risk of nonfatal MI (HR=0.87; 95% CI: 0.70, 1.09) or nonfatal stroke (HR=1.24; 95% CI: 0.92, 1.67).  A post hoc analysis of data from the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial by baseline HbA1c subgroups. EMPA-REG OUTCOME was not powered to show differences between subgroups.  Hazard ratios are related to CV death: HbA1c <7% (HR=0.30; 95% CI: 0.12, 0.80); HbA1c 7% to <8% (HR=0.59; 95% CI: 0.42, 0.83); HbA1c 8% to <9% (HR=0.67; 95% CI: 0.45, 0.99); HbA1c ≥9% (HR=0.76; 95% CI: 0.44, 1.31); p=0.41 for interaction. BMI <30 kg/m2 (HR=0.50; 95% CI: 0.37, 0.68); BMI ≥30 kg/m2 (HR=0.78; 95% CI: 0.56, 1.08); p=0.05 for interaction.5 SBP ≥140 mm Hg and/or DBP ≥90 mm Hg (HR=0.56; 95% CI: 0.40, 0.79); SBP <140 mm Hg and DBP <90 mm Hg (HR=0.67; 95% CI: 0.50, 0.91); p=0.44 for interaction. eGFR ≥90 mL/min/1.73 m2 (HR=0.70; 95% CI: 0.39, 1.25); eGFR 60 to <90 mL/min/1.73 m2 (HR=0.49; 95% CI: 0.35, 0.68); eGFR <60 mL/min/1.73 m2 (HR=0.78; 95% CI: 0.54, 1.12); p=0.15 for interaction.  ARR=absolute risk reduction; BMI=body mass index; BP=blood pressure; CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; DBP=diastolic blood pressure; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; HR=hazard ratio; MACE=major adverse cardiovascular events; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; SBP=systolic blood pressure; T2D=type 2 diabetes. | Reference: 2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes\n\nRD-154658 JARDIANCE INZUCCHI CIRCULATION\n | AMA Style Guide References: Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes. 2015.\n\nINZUCCHI CIRCULATION. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001240 | Match Text: In insulin-naive patients with T2D and eCVD, JARDIANCE reduced the need for insulin initiation | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: Adult patients with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke  Outcome of insulin initiation was defined to be maintained on ≥ 2 consecutive visits ≥ 13 weeks apart. Cox regression model adjusted for baseline HbA1c, time since T2D diagnosis, BMI, eGFR, geographic region, and treatment status.Kaplan-Meier estimates  BMI=body mass index; CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate; HR=hazard ratio; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; RRR=relative risk reduction; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes\n\nRD-152033 JARDIANCE Vaduganathan Vaduganathan DOM 2021  | AMA Style Guide References: Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes. 2015.\n\nVaduganathan Vaduganathan Diabetes Obes Metab. 2021. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001241 | Match Text: In insulin-treated patients with T2D and eCVD, JARDIANCE reduced the need for large increases in insulin dose | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: Adult patients with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke.  Sustained insulin dose increase was defined as time to first increase in total daily insulin dose by >20% from baseline total daily insulin dose, sustained for at least 2 consecutive visits at a minimum of 13 weeks apart, analysed in patients treated with insulin at baseline  CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; HR=hazard ratio; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; RRR=relative risk reduction; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes\n\nRD-152033 JARDIANCE Vaduganathan Vaduganathan DOM 2021  | AMA Style Guide References: Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes. 2015.\n\nVaduganathan Vaduganathan Diabetes Obes Metab. 2021. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001242 | Match Text: JARDIANCE provides multiple metabolic benefits to patients with T2D while also reducing CV and renal risk | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: In a 24-week, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 637 patients with T2D, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=217) and JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=213) as add-on therapy to metformin ≥1500 mg were evaluated vs placebo added to metformin (n=207). The primary endpoint was adjusted mean change (SE) from baseline in HbA1c (%); weight loss and blood pressure reduction were key secondary and exploratory endpoints, respectively.  CV=cardiovascular; SE=standard error of the mean; T2D=type 2 diabetes. | Reference: 5. Häring HU, Merker L, Seewaldt-Becker E, et al Diabetes Care. 2014;36:1650-1659. RD-105019\n\nRD-145767 Inzucchi SE, Davies MJ, Khunti K, et al. Empagliflozin treatment 2021;33:425-433.\n\nJardiance - EU/SmPC | AMA Style Guide References: Häring HU, Merker L, Seewaldt-Becker E, et al. Diabetes Care. 2014;36:1650-1659.\n\nInzucchi SE, Davies MJ, Khunti K, et al. Empagliflozin treatment 2021;33:425-433.\n\n- EU/SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001243 | Match Text: JARDIANCE can be used down to an eGFR of 30 mL/min/1.73 m2 in patients with T2D | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: Please see the SmPC for the full list of AEs and full list of special warnings and precautions for use.  AE=adverse event; eGFR=estimated glomerular ﬁltration rate; SmPC=summary of product characteristics; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: Jardiance - EU/SmPC | AMA Style Guide References: - EU/SmPC. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001244 | Match Text: Diabetes guidelines recommend early use of SGLT2is in patients with T2D regardless of metabolic parameters | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Guidelines | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: In addition to comprehensive CV risk management  ASCVD has been defined differently across CVOTs but all included individuals with eCVD (eg, MI, stroke, any revascularisation procedure). Variably included: conditions such as transient ischaemic attack, unstable angina, amputation, symptomatic or asymptomatic coronary artery disease. A strong recommendation is warranted for people with CVD and a weaker recommendation for those with indicators of high CV risk. While definitions of high risk vary, most comprise ≥55 years of age with 2 or more additional risk factors (including obesity, hypertension, smoking, dyslipidaemia, or albuminuria). Current or prior symptoms of HF with documented HFrEF or HFpEF. eGFR <60 mL/min/1.73 m2 OR albuminuria (ACR ≥3.0 mg/mmol [30 mg/g]). These measurements may vary over time; thus, a repeat measure is required to document CKD.   ACR=albumin to creatinine ratio; ASCVD=atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease; ADA=American Diabetes Association; CV=cardiovascular; CVD=cardiovascular disease; CVOT=cardiovascular outcomes trial; CKD=chronic kidney disease; EASD=European Association for the Study of Diabetes; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate; HF=heart failure; HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction; SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitor; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2022 - Management of Hyperglycemia in Type 2 Diabetes, 2022. A Consensus Report by the American Diab | AMA Style Guide References: Management of Hyperglycemia in Type 2 Diabetes, 2022. A Consensus Report by the American Diab. 2022. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA\nResource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001245 | Match Text: JARDIANCE demonstrated its proven safety profile across a broad population of patients with CKD. | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Safety | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: Adult patients with