l medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPEROR-Preserved | 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.97; 2026 Card iVA p.34; 2026 Card iVA p.57; 2026 Card iVA p.70; 2026 Card iVA p.73; 2026 Card iVA p.76; 2026 Card iVA p.85; 2026 Card iVA p.141; 2026 Card iVA p.169; 2026 Card iVA p.172; 2026 PCP iVA p.117\n#: 101 | Final Corrected Claim: *EMPEROR-Reduced included adult patients with chronic HF (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤40%).1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 40% | Study/programme: EMPEROR-Reduced | Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.97; 2026 Card iVA p.12; 2026 Card iVA p.28; 2026 Card iVA p.31; 2026 Card iVA p.34; 2026 Card iVA p.42; 2026 Card iVA p.76; 2026 Card iVA p.141; 2026 Card iVA p.166; 2026 Card iVA p.172; 2026 PCP iVA p.117 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPEROR-Reduced | 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.97; 2026 Card iVA p.12; 2026 Card iVA p.28; 2026 Card iVA p.31; 2026 Card iVA p.34; 2026 Card iVA p.42; 2026 Card iVA p.76; 2026 Card iVA p.141; 2026 Card iVA p.166; 2026 Card iVA p.172; 2026 PCP iVA p.117\n#: 102 | Final Corrected Claim: *EMPEROR-Reduced included adult patients with chronic HF (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤40%). | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 40% | Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.55 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 PCP iVA p.55\n#: 103 | Final Corrected Claim: Despite being a guideline-recommended treatment across LVEF, \nSGLT2is remain underutilised to treat HF. | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.60 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.60\n#: 104 | Final Corrected Claim: In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 3730 patients with HFrEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=1863) were evaluated vs placebo (n=1867). Patients were adults with chronic HF (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR- Reduced trial was a composite of CV death or hospitalisation for HF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 25% RRR in this endpoint \n(HR=0.75; 95% CI: 0.65, 0.86; p<0.001). | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 40% | Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.21; 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 PCP iVA p.29; 2026 PCP iVA p.111 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.21; 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 PCP iVA p.29; 2026 PCP iVA p.111\n#: 105 | Final Corrected Claim: In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) were evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF >40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint \n(HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001). | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 40% | Specialty context: Cardio-Renal, Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.70; 2026 Card iVA p.73; 2026 Card iVA p.104 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.70; 2026 Card iVA p.73; 2026 Card iVA p.104\n#: 106 | Final Corrected Claim: Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤40%). | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 40% | Specialty context: Cardio-Renal, Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.28; 2026 Card iVA p.31; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.104 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.28; 2026 Card iVA p.31; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.104\n#: 107 | Final Corrected Claim: In addition to the RRR of all HHF, including first and recurrent events, the risk of total hospitalisations for any reason was also significantly reduced (HR=0.85; 95% CI: 0.75, 0.95).1 \n\nII Standard of care: All patients received appropriate treatments for heart failure, including diuretics, inhibitors of the renin-angiotensin system and neprilysin, beta blockers, mineralocorticoid receptor antagonists and, when indicated, cardiac devices.1 | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 95%; HR=0.85; 95% CI: 0 | Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.31 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.31\n#: 108 | Final Corrected Claim: †Adult patients with chronic HF (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF >40%).2 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 40% | Specialty context: Cardiology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.55 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 2 | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 PCP iVA p.55\n#: 109 | Final Corrected Claim: Key inclusion criteria included a chronic HF (NYHA class II-IV) diagnosis, an elevated NT-proBNP level, and structural heart changes or documented hospitalisation for HF within 12 months. Elevated NT-proBNP is defined as a level of >300 pg/mL or, for patients with atrial fibrillation at baseline, a level of >900 pg/mL.2 | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.85; 2026 Card iVA p.157; 2026 PCP iVA p.105 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 12 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.85; 2026 Card iVA p.157; 2026 PCP iVA p.105\n#: 110 | Final Corrected Claim: ‡Standard of care: All patients received appropriate treatments for heart failure, including diuretics, inhibitors of the renin-angiotensin system and neprilysin, beta blockers, | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.91; 2026 Endo iVA p.94; 2026 Card iVA p.163; 2026 PCP iVA p.111; 2026 PCP iVA p.114 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.91; 2026 Endo iVA p.94; 2026 Card iVA p.163; 2026 PCP iVA p.111; 2026 PCP iVA p.114\n#: 111 | Final Corrected Claim: International T2D guidelines recommend the use of an | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinolog