Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.31; 2026 Card iVA p.107; 2026 PCP iVA p.33 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.31; 2026 Card iVA p.107; 2026 PCP iVA p.33\n#: 115 | Final Corrected Claim: In the EMPA-KIDNEY trial, a randomised, parallel-group, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 6609 patients with CKD, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=3304) were evaluated vs placebo (n=3305). | Status: Corrected | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg | Study/programme: EMPA-KIDNEY | Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.78; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.104; 2026 Card iVA p.181; 2026 PCP iVA p.41 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY | 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.78; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.104; 2026 Card iVA p.181; 2026 PCP iVA p.41\n#: 116 | Final Corrected Claim: §In the EMPA-KIDNEY trial, a randomised, parallel-group, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 6609 patients with CKD, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=3304) were evaluated vs placebo (n=3305). | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg | Study/programme: EMPA-KIDNEY | Specialty context: Cardio-Renal, Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.21; 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 PCP iVA p.29 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.21; 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 PCP iVA p.29\n#: 117 | Final Corrected Claim: ¶¶Sustained insulin dose increase was defined as time to first increase in total daily insulin dose by >20% from baseline total daily insulin dose, sustained for at least 2 consecutive visits at a minimum of 13 weeks apart, analysed in patients treated with insulin at baseline.8 ##Incident or worsening nephropathy is defined as progression to macroalbuminuria, doubling of serum creatinine, eGFR of ≤45 mL/min/1.73 m2; initiation of renal replacement therapy; death from renal disease. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 20% | Specialty context: Endocrinology | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.32 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.32\n#: 118 | Final Corrected Claim: There were no significant differences between the placebo and JARDIANCE groups of nonfatal MI (HR=0.87; 95% CI: 0.70, 1.09; p=0.22) or nonfatal stroke (HR=1.24; 95% CI: 0.92, 1.67; p=0.16).5 ||Pooled data from 10-mg and 25-mg doses of JARDIANCE; both doses showed a comparable reduction in the risk of CV death.5 ¶Standard of care included CV medications and glucose-lowering agents given at the discretion of healthcare providers and according to recommendations of local guidelines.5 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 95%; HR=0.87; HR=1.24; 95% CI: 0; p=0.22; p=0.16 | Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.107 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 5 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.107\n#: 119 | Final Corrected Claim: #In a double-blind extension trial, adjusted mean changes in weight for patients with baseline BMI ≥35 at Week 76 were 0.23 kg for placebo (n=29), -3.74 kg for JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=33), and -4.77 kg for JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=41). | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg; 25 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36\n#: 120 | Final Corrected Claim: *Key inclusion criteria included a chronic HF (NYHA class II-IV) diagnosis, an elevated NT-proBNP level, and therapy with the appropriate doses of HF medication. Elevated NT-proBNP is defined as a level of ≥1000 pg/mL in those with an ejection fraction of 31% to 35% or a level of ≥2500 pg/mL in those with an ejection fraction of 36% to 40%, as compared with a level of ≥600 pg/mL in those with an ejection fraction of ≤30%. | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.85; 2026 Card iVA p.157; 2026 PCP iVA p.105 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.85; 2026 Card iVA p.157; 2026 PCP iVA p.105\n#: 121 | Final Corrected Claim: In a subgroup analysis at 24 weeks of patients with baseline BMI ≥35, adjusted mean changes in weight were -0.34 kg for placebo (n=29), -2.63 kg for JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=33), and -3.35 kg for JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=41). Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) was -2.28 for JARDIANCE 10 mg and -3.01 for JARDIANCE 25 mg. | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 25 mg; 10 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 3 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36\n#: 122 | Final Corrected Claim: A convenient, easy-to-use option with once-daily, oral dosing1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.47; 2026 Card iVA p.90; 2026 Card iVA p.119 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.47; 2026 Card iVA p.90; 2026 Card iVA p.119\n#: 123 | Final Corrected Claim: Initiate with JARDIANCE 10 mg. Continue with 10 mg in patients already taking JARDIANCE. | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.47; 2026 PCP iVA p.44 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.47; 2026 PCP iVA p.44\n#: 124 | Final Corrected Claim: In a double-blind extension trial, adjusted mean changes in weight for patients with baseline BMI ≥35 at Week 76 were 0.23 kg for placebo (n=29), -3.74 kg for JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=33), and -4.77 kg for JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=41). Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) was -3.96 kg for JARDIANCE 10 mg and -4.99 kg for JARDIANCE 25 mg. Missing data were imputed using the LOCF approach.3 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg; 25 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36\n#: 125 | Final Corrected Claim: Initiate with JARDIANCE 10 mg. \nIn patients tolerating 10 mg and requiring additional glycaemic control, the dose can be increased to 25 mg. | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg; 25 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.47 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.47\n#: 126 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=48). Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) was -0.73% for JARDIANCE 10 mg and -1.0% for JARDIANCE 25 mg. Missing data were imputed using the LOCF | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 0.73%; 1.0%; 25 mg; 10 mg | Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.36 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.36\n#: 127 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE reduced the need for large increases in insulin dose¶¶8 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.29 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 8 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.29\n#: 128 | Final Corrected Claim: for JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=213), respectively. Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) was -0.6% for both JARDIANCE 10 mg and 25 mg; p<0.001 vs placebo for both doses.2 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 0.6%; p<0.001; 25 mg; 10 mg | Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.36 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnote