-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) were evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg | Study/programme: EMPEROR-Preserved | Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 Card iVA p.70; 2026 Card iVA p.73 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 Card iVA p.70; 2026 Card iVA p.73\n#: 137 | Final Corrected Claim: In a 24-week, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 637 patients with T2D, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=217) and JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=213) as add-on therapy to metformin ≥1500 mg were evaluated vs placebo added to metformin (n=207). | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg; 25 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36\n#: 138 | Final Corrected Claim: *Increase to 25 mg once daily in patients with T2D who tolerate 10 mg and need additional glycaemic control.1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 25 mg; 10 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.46; 2026 PCP iVA p.43 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.46; 2026 PCP iVA p.43\n#: 139 | Final Corrected Claim: In patients with T2D tolerating 10 mg and requiring additional glycaemic control, the dose can be increased to 25 mg. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg; 25 mg | Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.44 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.44\n#: 140 | Final Corrected Claim: Adjusted mean changes of -0.1% from baseline HbA1c 7.9% for placebo (n=207), -0.7% from baseline HbA1c 7.9% for JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=217), and -0.8% from baseline HbA1c 7.9% for JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=213), respectively. Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) was -0.6% for both JARDIANCE 10 mg and 25 mg; p<0.001 vs placebo for both doses. | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 0.1%; 7.9%; 0.7%; 0.8%; 10 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36\n#: 141 | Final Corrected Claim: In a subgroup analysis at 24 weeks of patients with baseline ≥8.5%, adjusted mean changes in HbA1c were -0.5% for placebo (n=50), -1.2% for JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=57), and -1.5% for JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=48). Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) was -0.73% for JARDIANCE 10 mg and -1.0% for JARDIANCE 25 mg. | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 8.5%; 0.5%; 1.2%; 1.5%; 10 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.57 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.57\n#: 142 | Final Corrected Claim: Continue with 10 mg in patients with T2D + eCVD already taking JARDIANCE. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.47 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.47\n#: 143 | Final Corrected Claim: Initiate with JARDIANCE 10 mg for treatment of T2D + eCVD. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 10 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.47 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.47\n#: 144 | Final Corrected Claim: Pooled data from the 10 mg and 25 mg doses of JARDIANCE showed a comparable reduction in the risk of hospitalisation for heart failure. | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.93 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.93\n#: 145 | Final Corrected Claim: Pooled data from 10-mg and 25-mg doses of JARDIANCE; both doses showed a comparable reduction in the risk of CV death. | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.96 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.96\n#: 146 | Final Corrected Claim: 2024 KDIGO guidelines on CKD management recommend SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, for first-line treatment. | Status: Corrected | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.42; 2026 PCP iVA p.24 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.42; 2026 PCP iVA p.24\n#: 147 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE, an SGLT2i, is recommended to reduce cardio-renal risk in high-risk patients with: \n• T2D + ASCVD\n• T2D + indicators of high risk\n• T2D + HF\n• T2D + CKD | Status: Corrected | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.41 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.41\n#: 148 | Final Corrected Claim: SGLT2is consistently improved cardio-renal outcomes across a wide \nrange of patients | Status: Corrected | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.129 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.129\n#: 149 | Final Corrected Claim: EMPA-KIDNEY is the largest dedicated SGLT2i trial, evaluating JARDIANCE across a broad population with CKD | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Study/programme: EMPA-KIDNEY | Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.180 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY | 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.180\n#: 150 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE is the first and only SGLT2i to show positive outcomes when initiated in the hospital within 1-5 days after stabilisation | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.33; 2026 Card iVA p.75; 2026 Card iVA p.138 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.33; 2026 Card iVA p.75; 2026 Card iVA p.138\n#: 151 | Final Corrected Claim: International T2D guidelines recommend the use of an SGLT2i such as JARDIANCE as early as first line2-5 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.40 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 2-5 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.40\n#: 152 | Final Corrected Claim: SGLT2is are a Class I, Level A-recommended therapy for patients with HFrEF to reduce the risk of heart failure hospitalisation or cardiovascular death, making JARDIANCE 1 of 4 foundational treatments \nfor HFrEF6 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.43; 2026 PCP iVA p.25 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.43; 2026 PCP iVA p.25\n#: 153 | Final Corrected Claim: SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, are 1A recommended for first-line use4,5 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.25 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 4,5 | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.25\n#: 154 | Final Corrected Claim: SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, are Class I recommended \nfor first-line use in patients with CVD + T2D to reduce \nthe risk of CV events*3 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.17; 2026 Card iVA p.62 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.17; 2026 Card iVA p.62\n#: 155 | Final Corrected Claim: SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, are Class I recommended for first-line use in patients with CVD + T2D to reduce the risk of CV events, independent of glucose control1 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.99 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.99\n#: 156 | Final Corrected Claim: Your patients with HF require urgent and appropriate \nintervention with foundational treatments, like SGLT2is1 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.60 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1,2 | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.60\n#: 157 | Final Corrected Claim: International T2D, CKD, and HF guidelines recommend the use of an SGLT2i such as JARDIANCE as early as first line2-9 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.22 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 2-9 | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.22\n#: 158 | Final Corrected Claim: More than 100 nephrology, endocrinology, and cardiology guidelines \nworldwide endorse the foundational use of SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE1 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.40; 2026 PCP iVA p.22 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.40; 2026 PCP iVA p.22\n#: 159 | Final Corrected Claim: Used alone” is defined as giving JARDIANCE without insulin or sulphonylureas.2 \n\n|| The mechanism of action of JARDIANCE is dependent on blood glucose levels, meaning it only removes glucose when levels are elevated. The risk of hypoglycaemia only increases when it’s combined with other medications that can cause low blood sugar, such as insulin or sulphonylureas.2,3 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.114 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.114\n#: 160 | Final Corrected Claim: Based on claims data sources of adult patients with HFrEF in Japan (Medical Data Vision claims registry), Sweden (nationwide administrative registries), and the United States (C212Optum de-identified Market Clarity Data). At study onset, dapagliflozin was the available SGLT2i approved for use in patients with HFrEF in the United States.2 | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.127 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 2 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.127\n#: 161 | Final Corrected Claim: As an SGLT2i, JARDIANCE is a Class I, Level A-recommended therapy for patients with HFmrEF and HFpEF to reduce the risk of heart failure hospitalisation or cardiovascular death2 | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.17; 2026 Card iVA p.62 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.17; 2026 Card iVA p.62\n#: 162 | Final Corrected Claim: In the 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of HF JARDIANCE, as an SGLT2i, is recommended for adult patients with HFrEF1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.14 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.14\n#: 163 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE, as an SGLT2i, is recommended for adult patients with HFpEF1 In the 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of HF | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.59 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.59\n#: 164 | Final Corrected Claim: Rapid sequencing rationale: Drugs should be prioritised based on efficacy, safety, and ease of use, initiating an additional GDMT class likely yields a greater benefit than titrating a class in use, and background therapy can facilitate the use of other drugs by enhancing safety.1 | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.22 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.22\n#: 165 | Final Corrected Claim: ESC Guidelines: As an SGLT2i, JARDIANCE is a Class I, Level A-recommended therapy for patients with HFpEF to reduce the risk of CV death or HHF.2 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Heart failure; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.63 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 2 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.63\n#: 166 | Final Corrected Claim: ESC Guidelines: As an SGLT2i, JARDIANCE is a Class I, Level A-recommended therapy for patients with HFrEF to reduce the risk of CV death or HHF.1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Heart failure; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.18 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.18\n#: 167 | Final Corrected Claim: ARR was estimated as the absolute difference in the proportion of events by treatment arm. NNT=1/ARR. NNT is per 2 years at risk.\n\n‖ Standard of care: All patients received a RAASi unless an investigator judged that a RAASi was not indicated or tolerated. | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.181 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.181\n#: 168 | Final Corrected Claim: *Based on a consortium that was tasked with compiling and meta-analysing the best available data to provide a more comprehensive assessment of the independent and combined associations of eGFR and albuminuria with mortality and kidney outcomes. Results are from the findings from a collaborative meta-analysis of the 21 general population cohorts for all-cause and cardiovascular mortality, which included >100,000 individuals with uACR measurements and 1.1 million participants with dipstick measurements | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.9 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.9\n#: 169 | Final Corrected Claim: Primary care guidelines recommend including SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, as part of initial therapy for patients with T2D at high or very high cardiovascular risk7 ESC guidelines include SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, as Class I, Level A-recommended therapy for patients with eCVD and T2D to reduce cardiovascular events, independent of baseline or target HbA1c6 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.23 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 6 | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.23\n#: 170 | Final Corrected Claim: SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, are Class I recommended for first-line use in patients with eCVD + T2D to reduce the risk of CV events8 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.43 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 8 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.43\n#: 171 | Final Corrected Claim: SGLT2is reduced the risk of composite HHF or CV mortality by 22% In a meta-analysis examining 15 studies with SGLT2is in CVD, T2D, and CKD | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 22% | Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.130 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.130\n#: 172 | Final Corrected Claim: Very common AEs: hypoglycaemia (when used with sulphonylurea or insulin). JARDIANCE has a placebo-like incidence of hypoglycaemia when added to metformin; volume \ndepletion. Selected uncommon AE: diabetic ketoacidosis. Rare AE: necrotising fasciitis of the perineum (Fournier’s gangrene). | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.37 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.37\n#: 173 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE is contraindicated in patients with hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients of JARDIANCE. JARDIANCE should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes or for the treatment of DKA. JARDIANCE should be used with caution in patients who may be at a higher risk of ketoacidosis while taking JARDIANCE. In patients where DKA is suspected or diagnosed, treatment with JARDIANCE should be discontinued immediately. For use in patients with renal impairment, please refer to the dosing page of this document and the SmPC.1 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardio-Renal, Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.54; 2026 Card iVA p.48; 2026 Card iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.120; 2026 PCP iVA p.51 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.54; 2026 Card iVA p.48; 2026 Card iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.120; 2026 PCP iVA p.51\n#: 174 | Final Corrected Claim: Rates of hypoglycaemia were similar between JARDIANCE and placebo1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.65; 2026 PCP iVA p.98 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.65; 2026 PCP iVA p.98\n#: 175 | Final Corrected Claim: Rates of hypoglycaemia‡ were similar between JARDIANCE \nand placebo in patients with or without T2D1 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.96; 2026 Card iVA p.41; 2026 Card iVA p.84; 2026 Card iVA p.171; 2026 PCP iVA p.116 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.96; 2026 Card iVA p.41; 2026 Card iVA p.84; 2026 Card iVA p.171; 2026 PCP iVA p.116\n#: 176 | Final Corrected Claim: Very common AEs: hypoglycaemia (when used with sulphonylurea or insulin). JARDIANCE has a placebo-like incidence of hypoglycaemia when added to metformin; volume depletion. Selected uncommon AE: diabetic ketoacidosis. Rare AE: necrotising fasciitis of the perineum (Fournier’s gangrene | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.47 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.47\n#: 177 | Final Corrected Claim: When used alone,§ JARDIANCE does not inherently cause hypoglycaemia||2 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.113 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA p.113\n#: 178 | Final Corrected Claim: the risk of hypoglycaemia when used in combination with JARDIANCE.1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.48; 2026 PCP iVA p.45 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.48; 2026 PCP iVA p.45\n#: 179 | Final Corrected Claim: †Ketoacidosis occurred in one patient (in the JARDIANCE group) without diabetes at baseline.2 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.81; 2026 PCP iVA p.83 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 2 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.81; 2026 PCP iVA p.83\n#: 180 | Final Corrected Claim: ‡Hypoglycaemic AEs with a plasma glucose value of ≤70 mg/dL (3.9 mmol/L) or that required assistance.1,2 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 70 mg | Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.66; 2026 Endo iVA p.97; 2026 Card iVA p.42 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1,2 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.66; 2026 Endo iVA p.97; 2026 Card iVA p.42\n#: 181 | Final Corrected Claim: ‡Ketoacidosis occurred in 1 patient (in the JARDIANCE group) without diabetes at baseline. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardio-Renal, Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.187 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Card iVA p.187\n#: 182 | Final Corrected Claim: The mechanism of action of JARDIANCE is dependent on blood glucose levels, meaning it only removes glucose when levels are elevated. The risk of hypoglycaemia only increases when it’s combined with other medications that can cause low blood sugar, such as insulin or sulphonylureas.2 | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.114 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.114\n#: 183 | Final Corrected Claim: Treat early to reduce the risk of hospitalisation or CV death in your patients3 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Campaign / Messaging | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.5; 2026 Card iVA p.50 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 3 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.5; 2026 Card iVA p.50\n#: 184 | Final Corrected Claim: reduce their risk of hospitalisation or CV death5,6 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Campaign / Messaging | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.57 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 5,6 | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.57\n#: 185 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE can help you stay committed by: offering protection by reducing the risk of CV death for adult patients with T2D + eCVD; reducing the risk of CV death and HHF for adult patients with HF; reducing the risk of kidney disease progression or CV death in adult patients with CKD; and lowering HbA1c in adult patients with T2D.1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Campaign / Messaging | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.1; 2026 PCP iVA p.1 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.1; 2026 PCP iVA p.1\n#: 186 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE can help you stay committed by: offering protection by reducing the risk of CV death for adult patients with eCVD + T2D; reducing the risk of CV death and HHF for adult patients with HF; reducing the risk of kidney disease progression or CV death in adult patients with CKD; and lowering HbA1c in adult patients with T2D.1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Campaign / Messaging | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.1 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.1\n#: 187 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE can help you stay committed by: offering protection by reducing the risk of CV death for adult patients with T2D + eCVD; reducing the risk of CV death and HHF for adult patients with HF; reducing the risk of kidney disease progression or CV death in adult patients with CKD; and lowering HbA1c in adult patients with T2D. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: 2026 Nephrology iVA overarching benefit statement. Local label and mandatory qualifiers must be checked before reuse. Source: PC-CRP-105591, page 1. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: JARDIANCE Summary of Product Characteristics, June 2025 | PC-CRP-105591 Nephrology iVA 2026, p.1\n#: 188 | Final Corrected Claim: Your patients with CKD are more likely to die from CVD than to progress to kidney failure. Nearly 1 in 2 patients with CKD will die from CVD before reaching end-stage kidney disease and requiring dialysis. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Disease-burden statement; not a product efficacy claim. Source: PC-CRP-105591 Nephrology iVA 2026, page 5. | Footnotes: 1,2 | Reference: PC-CRP-105591 Nephrology iVA 2026, p.5\n#: 189 | Final Corrected Claim: CV mortality risk is elevated even at low albuminuria levels. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: CKD disease-risk statement based on albuminuria and kidney function risk stratification. Source: PC-CRP-105591, page 8. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: PC-CRP-105591 Nephrology iVA 2026, p.8\n#: 190 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE provides kidney and CV protection as demonstrated in multiple clinical trials spanning a decade. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Umbrella statement linked to EMPA-REG OUTCOME, EMPEROR-Reduced, EMPEROR-Preserved and EMPA-KIDNEY. Must be used with indication-specific outcomes and footnotes. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 14–17. | Footnotes: 1-5 | Reference: EMPA-REG OUTCOME | EMPEROR-Reduced | EMPEROR-Preserved | EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.14-17\n#: 191 | Final Corrected Claim: In EMPA-KIDNEY, JARDIANCE reduced the risk of kidney disease progression or cardiovascular death by 28% versus placebo. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: EMPA-KIDNEY primary composite endpoint: HR=0.72; 95% CI: 0.64, 0.82; p<0.001. Use with complete trial population and standard-of-care qualifiers. Source: PC-CRP-105591, page 18. | Footnotes: 1,3 | Reference: Herrington WG et al. N Engl J Med. 2023; 388:117-127 | EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.18-20\n#: 192 | Final Corrected Claim: EMPA-KIDNEY studied JARDIANCE across a broad spectrum of patients with CKD, including understudied patient populations. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Clinical evidence / Study population | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Includes patients across a wide uACR and eGFR range, with and without T2D or CVD, and with or without RAAS inhibitor use. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 21–23. | Footnotes: 1-3 | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.21-23\n#: 193 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE slowed eGFR decline over time in patients with CKD with or without type 2 diabetes. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Long-term eGFR slope outcome from EMPA-KIDNEY. Annual decline presented in the asset: -1.37 with JARDIANCE versus -2.75 mL/min/1.73 m²/year with placebo. Use the complete outcome qualification. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 27–29. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.27-29\n#: 194 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE can help protect kidney function in patients with CKD who have low albuminuria. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Linked to slowed eGFR decline across the uACR spectrum. The primary composite subgroup result was not statistically significant in the uACR <30 mg/g subgroup; retain the eGFR-slope qualification. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 33–36. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.33-36\n#: 195 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE reduced kidney disease progression regardless of diabetes status. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Based on a subsidiary EMPA-KIDNEY analysis across causes of CKD. The analysis type and outcome definition must remain linked. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 37–39. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY subsidiary analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.37-39\n#: 196 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE may slow the onset of dialysis by more than 20 years in selected patients with CKD. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Modelled extrapolation based on EMPA-KIDNEY eGFR slope, not an observed clinical-trial endpoint. Must always be described as extrapolated and not as a guaranteed individual outcome. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 40–46. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: Extrapolated EMPA-KIDNEY eGFR-slope analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.40-46\n#: 197 | Final Corrected Claim: In the EMPOWER meta-analysis, JARDIANCE reduced the risk of acute kidney injury by 27% and the risk of a 50% or greater increase in serum creatinine by 20%. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Heart failure; Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Meta-analysis across CKD, HF and T2D + eCVD populations. AKI HR=0.73; 95% CI: 0.63, 0.85. Creatinine increase HR=0.80; 95% CI: 0.72, 0.88. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 60–62. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPOWER meta-analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.60-62\n#: 198 | Final Corrected Claim: In the EMPOWER meta-analysis, JARDIANCE reduced the risk of kidney failure by 34% and kidney disease progression by 30%. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Heart failure; Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Meta-analysis across CKD, HF and T2D + eCVD populations. Kidney failure HR=0.66; 95% CI: 0.55, 0.79. Kidney disease progression HR=0.70; 95% CI: 0.63, 0.78. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 63–65. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPOWER meta-analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.63-65\n#: 199 | Final Corrected Claim: The risk of selected serious adverse events with JARDIANCE remained low and comparable with placebo in more than 20,000 patients. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Heart failure; Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Meta-analysis statement covering selected serious adverse events. It does not replace the complete locally approved safety information. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 66–68. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: Safety outcomes meta-analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.66-68\n#: 200 | Final Corrected Claim: The 2024 KDIGO guideline reinforces SGLT2 inhibitors as an early and foundational therapy for the management of CKD. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Class-level recommendation applying to defined patient groups by eGFR, albuminuria, T2D and HF status. Avoid implying an exclusive recommendation for JARDIANCE. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 72–75. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for CKD | PC-CRP-105591, pp.72-75\n#: 201 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE is a once-daily oral treatment with no titration, can be taken at any time of day with or without food, and can be initiated down to an eGFR of 20 mL/min/1.73 m². | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: The asset presents 10 mg once daily as the starting and recommended dose. Initiation and continuation thresholds must be checked against the current local label. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 76–78. | Footnotes: 1,2 | Reference: JARDIANCE Summary of Product Characteristics, June 2025 | PC-CRP-105591, pp.76-78\n#: 202 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE works by inhibiting SGLT2\" which is the title of the slide and next point is \"JARDIANCE reduces glucose and sodium reabsorption and increases delivery of sodium to the distal tubule | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Chronic kidney disease; Heart failure | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Linked in the asset to increased urinary glucose excretion, tubuloglomerular feedback and reduced intraglomerular pressure. Proposed cardiovascular mechanisms should not be presented as proven clinical mediators. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 79–81. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: JARDIANCE Summary of Product Characteristics | PC-CRP-105591, pp.79-81\n#: 203 | Final Corrected Claim: In EMPA-KIDNEY, JARDIANCE reduced first and recurrent all-cause hospitalisation by 14% versus placebo. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Key secondary outcome including first and all subsequent all-cause hospitalisations. HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.78, 0.95; p=0.003. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 121–123. | Footnotes: 1,2 | Reference: Herrington WG et al. N Engl J Med. 2023; 388:117-127 | Data on file | PC-CRP-105591, pp.121-123", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:67e73694-bb4c-40ab-b0f5-2176e5d3d832"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a4cbfa69-4a9b-472e-bc23-56640590546d"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:94f9663f-76b8-480b-881b-b80b507192ff"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6db579d5-cda6-4fcd-b523-7737b24c7357"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:88cbcce8-3010-470b-9244-1df43a0b4401"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:164cae6a-767e-4343-b33c-82c64fddb8f5"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:fcb4ba63-cee4-4ee6-8d43-8cba23db5435"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:26ca616c-65b9-4e74-abec-236fc2f1a5e3"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cc3e9727-0942-480d-ad58-9e570bc89f6a"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:17497247-efd7-4428-858c-cbeb3dca8f8c"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b8325548-6c42-473a-aec1-35d910cc0ee2"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:10a7badb-9c26-4e9c-a994-d05cd0998eea"}, {"@id": "urn:k