ation: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.100\n#: 56 | Original Extracted Text: CVD=cardiovascular disease; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; HF=heart failure; SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor; T2D=type 2 diabetes. | Reason for Exclusion (Observation): This is not the claim, this are abbreviations  | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.10", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0161314c-b793-4cc3-8c85-f201e7bb4b8d"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8285cc88-0e7e-4167-afa2-664a3e207fe7"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e857b6ed-d8c8-4e8a-b92a-6a516264c52c"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1ab3ad3d-5980-4dc1-a6ae-bd19d0147568"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f94b565f-bef0-45a8-a551-df55ba131c8a"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2fec29d4-1656-40b8-8c8d-a6854a0af2b1"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:64a1dbf1-17c5-4bb0-9b0c-192861e5e826"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:25ea11ec-a36a-4179-8cf6-e2d8e9b9dede"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cb96b620-ec8d-4671-8c4b-c04461921c48"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:46f56b2b-c579-470f-8a9a-ee2e7a744e21"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1415e5a8-c91c-4931-8a76-513f3c38cb57"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2bcecfff-195b-49eb-a6a8-77728db57689"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:67349ef4-c45c-40f4-b954-327ec874c055"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2116c511-248e-4395-bd03-4ac8808a5033"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8ddf11c9-e63c-47fc-8610-7f68f0dd9142"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f7e9ca07-3d96-401b-a65b-54739659d2b7"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:856b8602-e2d7-4c0a-b070-cd794bb5dee5"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7411417c-3cc3-4f5b-a381-0bc258caa2ee"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0f40fb53-288c-4329-a2cc-788edabb26c9"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:766f1235-1e01-458c-8503-23564811e737"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9ff6f3fb-0637-4fd6-bea4-fb3dc8602ae4"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d9d58d4c-974c-473f-af01-3506e57c7f81"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ad597ba0-c8e7-488a-9c89-78810c48371f"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f8413b1f-821c-4cd2-8f1b-d016aab41c2e"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c17e0588-7cc1-4a76-be46-f8249b999a2c"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9e717d35-1cbc-4c88-8087-f085a7f47335"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:bb36123a-d730-4de4-9c46-becccb5ec790", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Summary", "section_type": "sheet", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "claims_content_modules", "section_id": "bb36123a-d730-4de4-9c46-becccb5ec790", "extraction_method": "openpyxl", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE_Claims_Corrected_Final-1 (1) 2.xlsx", "sheet_name": "Summary", "source_document_id": "13ae0354-6211-4820-b97a-7634167e0ed0", "text": "# Summary\nJARDIANCE Claims — Correction Summary: Metric | col_2: Count\nJARDIANCE Claims — Correction Summary: Total claims in original file | col_2: 274\nJARDIANCE Claims — Correction Summary: Claims confirmed complete & substantiated (no change) | col_2: 123\nJARDIANCE Claims — Correction Summary: Claims corrected to complete/accurate wording | col_2: 80\nJARDIANCE Claims — Correction Summary: Duplicate fragments merged into a single corrected claim | col_2: 15\nJARDIANCE Claims — Correction Summary: Claims excluded (not valid standalone claims — references, footnotes, abbreviations, titles, etc.) | col_2: 56\nJARDIANCE Claims — Correction Summary: Final corrected claims list count | col_2: 203", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c619c141-7e0a-46ad-9080-adbdabc6f242"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4ce6cbd0-0c93-4a62-b820-b73442b78ab2", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "4ce6cbd0-0c93-4a62-b820-b73442b78ab2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f6fcc9f2-6571-4cb6-882e-f1a441a88a32"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b183a7db-f218-4b5b-ab8d-d952dfe126cd", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "WHAT IS JARDIANCE?", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "b183a7db-f218-4b5b-ab8d-d952dfe126cd", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "JARDIANCE is a prescription medicine used to:\n\n-   reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization for heart failure in adults with heart failure, when the heart cannot pump enough blood to the rest of your body\n-   reduce the risk of further worsening of kidney disease, end-stage kidney disease (ESKD), death due to cardiovascular disease, and hospitalization in adults with chronic kidney disease\n-   reduce the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes who also have known cardiovascular disease\n-   lower blood sugar along with diet and exercise in adults and children who are 10 years of age and older with type 2 diabetes\n\nJARDIANCE is not for use to lower blood sugar in people with type 1 diabetes. It may increase their risk of diabetic ketoacidosis (increased ketones in the blood or urine).\n\nJARDIANCE is not for use to lower blood sugar in people with type 2 diabetes who have severe kidney problems, because it may not work.\n\nJARDIANCE is not for people with polycystic kidney disease, or who are taking or have recently received certain types of immunosuppressive therapy to treat kidney disease. JARDIANCE is not expected to work if you have these conditions.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cc65a59d-af73-4b11-b9ae-7bf21f45edba"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:22e41fac-85f2-4a2a-9834-ab98bfdbfd22"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ee6385fa-66f0-4e80-8d55-14fcc499e183", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "IMPORTANT SAFETY INFORMATION", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "ee6385fa-66f0-4e80-8d55-14fcc499e183", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "Do not take JARDIANCE if you are allergic to empagliflozin or any of the ingredients in JARDIANCE.\n\nSymptoms of a serious allergic reaction may include:\n\n- rash\n-   raised, red areas on your skin (hives)\n-   swelling of your face, lips, mouth, and throat that may cause difficulty in breathing or swallowing\n\nIf you have any of these symptoms, stop taking JARDIANCE and call your healthcare provider right away or go to the nearest hospital emergency room.\n\nPlease see additional Important Safety Information for JARDIANCE throughout, and Prescribing Information and Medication Guide.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1f63801b-d2e2-4be5-b89d-2ea34c029891"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:11b4ff6d-dcf6-4bb4-80d1-88d0bb4f9c3e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "WHAT TO KNOW ABOUT ®", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "11b4ff6d-dcf6-4bb4-80d1-88d0bb4f9c3e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "JARDIANCE ( empagliflozin ) TABLETS\n\nYou're taking an important step in managing your chronic kidney disease (CKD), and we're here to help you get started with JARDIANCE. You may know JARDIANCE as a treatment to lower blood sugar in adults with type 2 diabetes, along with diet and exercise-but it's also for adults with chronic kidney disease. In fact, JARDIANCE reduces the risk of further worsening of kidney disease, end-stage kidney disease (ESKD), cardiovascular death, and hospitalization in adults with chronic kidney disease.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2837a1b6-c37f-4f3d-91a4-23346450526a"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:be2ef901-f86d-4028-80b1-982e816c84f8", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "FOR ADULTS WITH CKD, JARDIANCE IS A ONCE-DAILY PILL PROVEN TO:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "be2ef901-f86d-4028-80b1-982e816c84f8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\nSlow the progression of chronic kidney disease\n\nReduce the risk of kidney failure, which can lead to dialysis\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nLower the risk of cardiovascular death\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nJARDIANCE is not for use to lower blood sugar in people with type 1 diabetes. It may increase their risk of diabetic ketoacidosis (increased ketones in the blood or urine).\n\nJARDIANCE is not for use to lower blood sugar in people with type 2 diabetes who have severe kidney problems, because it may not work.\n\nJARDIANCE is not for people with polycystic kidney disease, or who are taking or have recently received certain types of immunosuppressive therapy to treat kidney disease. JARDIANCE is not expected to work if you have these conditions.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3b442f96-0ad8-4836-9e4f-29b3cad0ea44"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:bf39c3c2-80c3-4479-98a8-b94a7b055689", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "IMPORTANT SAFETY INFORMATION (cont'd)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "bf39c3c2-80c3-4479-98a8-b94a7b055689", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:71aec688-601e-4093-9c01-c98bbca6997e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "JARDIANCE can cause serious side effects, including:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "71aec688-601e-4093-9c01-c98bbca6997e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "-   Diabetic ketoacidosis (increased ketones in your blood or urine) in people with type 1 and other ketoacidosis. JARDIANCE can cause ketoacidosis that can be life-threatening and may lead to death. Ketoacidosis is a serious condition which needs to be treated in a hospital. People with type 1 diabetes have a high risk of getting ketoacidosis. People with type 2 diabetes or pancreas problems also have an increased risk of getting ketoacidosis. Ketoacidosis can also happen in people who are sick, cannot eat or drink as usual, skip meals, and are on a diet high in fat and low in carbohydrates (ketogenic diet), take less than the usual amount of insulin or miss insulin doses, drink too much alcohol, have a loss of too much fluid from the body (volume depletion), or who have surgery. Ketoacidosis can happen even if your blood sugar is less than 250 mg/dL. Your healthcare provider may ask you to periodically check ketones in your urine or blood. Stop taking JARDIANCE and call your healthcare provider or get medical help right away if you get any of the following. If possible, check for ketones in your urine or blood, even if your blood sugar is less than 250 mg/dL:\n- nausea\n- tiredness\n- vomiting\n- trouble breathing\n- stomach-area (abdominal) pain\n- ketones in your urine or blood", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6f2710c0-f4d5-4292-b41f-daf9e49f4e00"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8e1263c8-203d-4e09-8647-c97e9c9194a3"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6d56d6a2-97f4-4928-b58a-51e01ee8ebb8", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "6d56d6a2-97f4-4928-b58a-51e01ee8ebb8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1ed574d9-1770-4522-86c3-e1be8bf84f83"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6f88edcf-f7e3-4942-ac60-44307dca16f5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "STAYING PROACTIVE WITH CKD", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "6f88edcf-f7e3-4942-ac60-44307dca16f5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:925977ed-cb4a-443a-9514-7a7baed3bec4", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "1. TAKING JARDIANCE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "925977ed-cb4a-443a-9514-7a7baed3bec4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "JARDIANCE is one pill, so it's easy to fit into your daily routine. Take JARDIANCE in the morning with or without food, exactly as your healthcare provider tells you to take it. Be sure to talk to your healthcare provider about all the medications you're taking and any noticeable changes you experience while taking a new medication.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:faea89db-3073-43d5-947c-1849a73d090d"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3d280301-e331-482f-b3a9-f2dd8668e5d3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "2. MANAGING POSSIBLE SIDE EFFECTS", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "3d280301-e331-482f-b3a9-f2dd8668e5d3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "The most common side effects with JARDIANCE are urinary tract infections and yeast infections. These are not all the possible side effects of JARDIANCE. Tell your healthcare provider if you experience these or other side effects.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2fd1dac9-b61e-4504-ab86-27f4104aa897"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2d730f0f-cf87-4291-a823-52c7e765c5a3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "IMPORTANT SAFETY INFORMATION (cont'd)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "2d730f0f-cf87-4291-a823-52c7e765c5a3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "-   Dehydration. JARDIANCE can cause some people to become dehydrated (the loss of body water and salt). Dehydration may cause you to feel dizzy, faint, light-headed, or weak, especially when you stand up. Sudden worsening of kidney function has happened in people who are taking JARDIANCE.\n\nYou may be at a higher risk of dehydration if you:\n\n- take medicines to lower your blood pressure, including water pills (diuretics)          · are on a low salt diet\n- have kidney problems          · are 65 years of age or older\n\nTalk to your healthcare provider about what you can do to prevent dehydration, including how much fluid you should drink on a daily basis. Call your healthcare provider right away if you reduce the amount of food or liquid you drink, if you are sick or cannot eat, or start to lose liquids from your body from vomiting, diarrhea, or being in the sun too long.\n\n-   Genital and urinary tract infections. JARDIANCE can cause serious infections in your genital area or urinary tract that could require hospitalization. A rare but serious bacterial infection called necrotizing fasciitis can cause damage to the tissue under the skin in the area between and around the anus and genitals (perineum). This infection may require hospitalization, multiple surgeries, and could lead to death. Seek medical attention immediately if you have a fever or you are feeling very weak, tired, or uncomfortable (malaise), and you develop pain or tenderness, swelling, or redness of skin (erythema) in the area between and around your anus and genitals. Also tell your healthcare provider if you have any of these signs or symptoms of infections:", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8011a40e-70e4-4dcc-8790-ba62ce7c6722"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bef938cf-abcf-4ffe-9a9c-5e190c3fa99b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:504e9008-c52e-4c6e-b4dc-f06d028aa725", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Urinary tract infection:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "504e9008-c52e-4c6e-b4dc-f06d028aa725", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "- burning feeling when you urinate\n- need to urinate often or right away\n- pain in the lower part of your stomach (pelvis)\n- blood in your urine\n\nYou may also have a fever, back pain, nausea, or vomiting.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:49d1c548-0c92-47ac-8e2d-474cbd8a4973"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3053a12f-e9a2-40a7-ae31-630a152d6b8b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "3053a12f-e9a2-40a7-ae31-630a152d6b8b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ed276646-be92-4038-9ab5-0285e63a74e8"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7326f5d3-205f-472d-b25f-d188a566d7b0", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "3. STAYING ON TOP OF APPOINTMENTS", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "7326f5d3-205f-472d-b25f-d188a566d7b0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "Staying on top of doctor appointments and understanding your kidney health is an important step in managing your condition. Your doctor will monitor your kidney health with routine lab tests you may already be familiar with:\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:770604cd-dd01-41c0-bd6e-acbc9199ab47"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2c3ae1b7-9edb-4706-a9ff-6b789a40c9b6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "UACR", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "2c3ae1b7-9edb-4706-a9ff-6b789a40c9b6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "A UACR (urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio) is a urine test that checks for how much small protein, called albumin, is in your urine, which is a sign of kidney damage.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bdd33a8d-9cb3-471d-90d7-1eec045dbe78"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3fe3aa9f-add4-46e9-9d52-e3ab7b4c5df6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "eGFR", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "3fe3aa9f-add4-46e9-9d52-e3ab7b4c5df6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "An eGFR (estimated glomerular filtration rate) is a blood test that measures kidney function and how well the kidneys can filter blood.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nWorking with your doctor to understand your kidney numbers can help you get a better handle on your chronic kidney disease.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:45f9a966-9381-4d50-a000-0375f35763a7"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:f9b45727-5c79-4754-b483-dc668585129a", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "IMPORTANT SAFETY INFORMATION (cont'd)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "f9b45727-5c79-4754-b483-dc668585129a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2e1f57ad-fe75-4432-8d1f-5baad4d223f2", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Vaginal yeast infection:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "2e1f57ad-fe75-4432-8d1f-5baad4d223f2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "- vaginal odor           · white or yellowish vaginal discharge (may be lumpy or look like cottage cheese)\n- vaginal itching\n\nYeast infection of the skin around the penis: Swelling of an uncircumcised penis may make it difficult to pull back the skin around the tip of your penis. Other symptoms include:\n\n- redness, itching, or swelling of the penis\n- rash on the penis\n- bad smelling discharge from the penis\n- pain in the skin around the penis\n\nTalk to your healthcare provider about what to do if you get symptoms of a yeast infection. They may suggest you use an over-the-counter antifungal medicine. Contact your healthcare provider right away if your symptoms do not improve after using an over-the-counter antifungal medicine.\n\n-   Low blood sugar (hypoglycemia): In adults, if you take JARDIANCE with another medicine that can cause low blood sugar, such as sulfonylurea or insulin, your risk of low blood sugar is higher. In children 10 years of age and older, the risk for low blood sugar is higher with JARDIANCE regardless of use with another medicine that can also lower blood sugar. The dose of your sulfonylurea or insulin may need to be lowered. Symptoms of low blood sugar may include:\n- headache\n- drowsiness\n- weakness\n- dizziness\n- confusion\n- irritability\n- hunger\n- fast heartbeat\n- sweating\n- shaking or feeling jittery\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b12b4272-5ea1-4b65-b31f-1dc8270bf626"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1d5d7c47-c14d-4b84-9796-ce9bb0bfd867"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4210806a-362f-4b12-a6d3-5824c80e8594", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "4210806a-362f-4b12-a6d3-5824c80e8594", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c05454e6-b3fc-4c3b-a1db-a4d360c6a110"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:c54b0ff4-55a0-4302-8363-bb00fd01d785", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "SUPPORT EVERY STEP OF THE WAY", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "c54b0ff4-55a0-4302-8363-bb00fd01d785", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\nThe My JARDIANCE Support™ Program is there to support you on your journey, with healthy tips, lifestyle ideas, and keeping you on track with treatment.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nSave with the JARDIANCE Savings Card. With a JARDIANCE Savings Card, eligible commercially insured patients can pay $0 for a 30- to 90-day prescription. And don't worry - we'll also automatically re-enroll you after 12 months as long as you still qualify.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nGet started at JARDIANCE.COM or scan this QR code.\n\n*To view the full terms and conditions, please visit  JARDIANCE.com/savings.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f2041f00-b85b-40fa-b705-dc6d65abffa8"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:60712e8c-29fb-4365-90e4-c87edc014b2d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "WHAT IS JARDIANCE?", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "60712e8c-29fb-4365-90e4-c87edc014b2d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "JARDIANCE is a prescription medicine used to:\n\n- reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization for heart failure in adults with heart failure, when the heart cannot pump enough blood to the rest of your body\n-   reduce the risk of further worsening of kidney disease, end-stage kidney disease (ESKD), death due to cardiovascular disease, and hospitalization in adults with chronic kidney disease\n-   reduce the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes who also have known cardiovascular disease\n-   lower blood sugar along with diet and exercise in adults and children who are 10 years of age and older with type 2 diabetes\n\nJARDIANCE is not for use to lower blood sugar in people with type 1 diabetes. It may increase their risk of diabetic ketoacidosis (increased ketones in the blood or urine).\n\nJARDIANCE is not for use to lower blood sugar in people with type 2 diabetes who have severe kidney problems, because it may not work.\n\nJARDIANCE is not for people with polycystic kidney disease, or who are taking or have recently received certain types of immunosuppressive therapy to treat kidney disease. JARDIANCE is not expected to work if you have these conditions.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7c2a3cdb-2e4e-4be7-b7bb-29868496b0f9"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:48f6c32c-f106-4644-a08b-1adc9fb3d872"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:a4c15f9f-a518-4034-8328-017f9e14749c", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "IMPORTANT SAFETY INFORMATION", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "a4c15f9f-a518-4034-8328-017f9e14749c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "Do not take JARDIANCE if you are allergic to empagliflozin or any of the ingredients in JARDIANCE. Symptoms of a serious allergic reaction may include:\n\n- rash\n- raised, red areas on your skin (hives)\n- swelling of your face, lips, mouth, and throat that may cause difficulty in breathing or swallowing\n\nIf you have any of these symptoms, stop taking JARDIANCE and call your healthcare provider right away or go to the nearest hospital emergency room.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:69e5c7e3-1a36-4bc5-8b44-4b9464671626"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6b45bf0f-c94a-4355-9c5e-86286962dfaf", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "JARDIANCE can cause serious side effects, including:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "6b45bf0f-c94a-4355-9c5e-86286962dfaf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "-   Diabetic ketoacidosis (increased ketones in your blood or urine) in people with type 1 and other ketoacidosis.\n\nJARDIANCE can cause ketoacidosis that can be life-threatening and may lead to death. Ketoacidosis is a serious condition which needs to be treated in a hospital. People with type 1 diabetes have a high risk of getting ketoacidosis. People with type 2 diabetes or pancreas problems also have an increased risk of getting ketoacidosis. Ketoacidosis can also happen in people who are sick, cannot eat or drink as usual, skip meals, and are on a diet high in fat and low in carbohydrates (ketogenic diet), take less than the usual amount of insulin or miss insulin doses, drink too much alcohol, have a loss of too much fluid from the body (volume depletion), or who have surgery. Ketoacidosis can happen even if your blood sugar is less than 250 mg/dL. Your healthcare provider may ask you to periodically check ketones in your urine or blood. Stop taking JARDIANCE and call your healthcare provider or get medical help right away if you get any of the following. If possible, check for ketones in your urine or blood, even if your blood sugar is less than 250 mg/dL :\n\n- nausea\n- tiredness\n- vomiting\n- trouble breathing\n- stomach-area (abdominal) pain\n- ketones in your urine or blood\n-   Dehydration. JARDIANCE can cause some people to become dehydrated (the loss of body water and salt). Dehydration may cause you to feel dizzy, faint, light-headed, or weak, especially when you stand up. Sudden worsening of kidney function has happened in people who are taking JARDIANCE .\n\nYou may be at a higher risk of dehydration if you:\n\n-   take medicines to lower your blood pressure, including water pills (diuretics)\n- have kidney problems · are 65 years of age or older\n\nTalk to your healthcare provider about what you can do to prevent dehydration, including how much fluid you should drink on a daily basis. Call your healthcare provider right away if you reduce the amount of food or liquid you drink, if you are sick or cannot eat, or start to lose liquids from your body from vomiting, diarrhea, or being in the sun too long.\n\n-   Genital and urinary tract infections. JARDIANCE can cause serious infections in your genital area or urinary tract that could require hospitalization. A rare but serious bacterial infection called necrotizing fasciitis can cause damage to the tissue under the skin in the area between and around the anus and genitals (perineum) . This infection may require hospitalization, multiple surgeries, and could lead to death. Seek medical attention immediately if you have a fever or you are feeling very weak, tired, or uncomfortable (malaise), and you develop pain or tenderness, swelling, or redness of skin (erythema) in the area between and around your anus and genitals. Also tell your healthcare provider if you have any of these signs or symptoms of infections:", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:39146075-0c21-4025-8a23-c7d614ba44b4"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d35b9ba3-66ed-4e15-b3ee-d1bbf222038d"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e72ba9e3-b34b-4219-8322-4ad4558c957a"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:84c4defd-870b-4c7b-8ab3-7cec0630f837", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Urinary tract infection:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "84c4defd-870b-4c7b-8ab3-7cec0630f837", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "- burning feeling when you urinate\n- need to urinate often or right away\n- pain in the lower part of your stomach (pelvis)\n- blood in your urine\n\nYou may also have a fever, back pain, nausea, or vomiting.\n\n- are on a low salt diet\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5b68e9cf-665c-4957-93e0-5c0791de2091"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:34aa06bb-b0b5-404e-babc-a416dde90d8b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "IMPORTANT SAFETY INFORMATION (cont'd)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "34aa06bb-b0b5-404e-babc-a416dde90d8b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:a37f08d6-bcd4-4981-9e0c-a7fc25c3403d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Vaginal yeast infection:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "a37f08d6-bcd4-4981-9e0c-a7fc25c3403d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "- vaginal odor           · white or yellowish vaginal discharge (may be lumpy or look like cottage cheese)\n- vaginal itching\n\nYeast infection of the skin around the penis: Swelling of an uncircumcised penis may make it difficult to pull back the skin around the tip of your penis. Other symptoms include:\n\n- redness, itching, or swelling of the penis\n- rash on the penis\n- bad smelling discharge from the penis\n- pain in the skin around the penis\n\nTalk to your healthcare provider about what to do if you get symptoms of a yeast infection. They may suggest you use an over-the-counter antifungal medicine. Contact your healthcare provider right away if your symptoms do not improve after using an over-the-counter antifungal medicine.\n\n-   Low blood sugar (hypoglycemia): In adults, if you take JARDIANCE with another medicine that can cause low blood sugar, such as sulfonylurea or insulin, your risk of low blood sugar is higher. In children 10 years of age and older, the risk for low blood sugar is higher with JARDIANCE regardless of use with another medicine that can also lower blood sugar. The dose of your sulfonylurea or insulin may need to be lowered. Symptoms of low blood sugar may include:\n- headache · weakness  · confusion  · hunger\n- sweating\n- drowsiness · dizziness · irritability · fast heartbeat  · shaking or feeling jittery\n-   Amputations. SGLT2 inhibitors may increase your risk of lower limb amputations. You may be at a higher risk of lower limb amputation if you:\n- have a history of amputation · have had blocked or narrowed blood vessels, usually in your leg\n- have had diabetic foot infection, ulcers, or sores\n\nCall your healthcare provider right away if you have new pain or tenderness, any sores, ulcers, or infections in your leg or foot. Talk to your healthcare provider about proper foot care.\n\n-   Serious allergic reactions. If you have any symptoms of a serious allergic reaction, stop taking JARDIANCE and call your healthcare provider right away or go to the nearest hospital emergency room.\n\nThe most common side effects of JARDIANCE include urinary tract infections and yeast infections in females.\n\nThese are not all the possible side effects of JARDIANCE. For more information, ask your healthcare provider or pharmacist.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1342dc73-688f-4081-8c0d-0f1a3edaa23b"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:539b1722-6df6-4949-8ae1-140725bc7c9a"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:22d2b8d3-6bb0-4535-a733-49eec307ed35"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:49ff4dee-75cf-4628-bd4a-b5aa5f111a96", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Before taking JARDIANCE, tell your healthcare provider about all of your medical conditions, including if you:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "49ff4dee-75cf-4628-bd4a-b5aa5f111a96", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "- have type 1 diabetes or have had diabetic ketoacidosis\n- have a decrease in your insulin dose\n- have a serious infection\n- have a history of infection of the vagina or penis\n- have a history of amputation\n- have kidney problems\n- have liver problems\n-   have a history of urinary tract infections or problems with urination\n-   are on a low sodium (salt) diet. Your healthcare provider may change your diet or dose\n-   are going to have surgery. Your healthcare provider may stop JARDIANCE before you have surgery. Talk to your healthcare provider if you are having surgery about when to stop taking JARDIANCE and when to start it again\n- are eating less, or there is a change in your diet\n- are dehydrated\n-   have or have had problems with your pancreas, including pancreatitis or surgery on your pancreas\n-   drink alcohol very often, or drink a lot of alcohol in the short term ('binge' drinking)\n- have ever had an allergic reaction to JARDIANCE\n-   are pregnant or plan to become pregnant. JARDIANCE may harm your unborn baby. Tell your healthcare provider right away if you become pregnant during treatment with JARDIANCE\n-   are breastfeeding or are planning to breastfeed. JARDIANCE may pass into your breast milk and may harm your baby. Do not breastfeed while taking JARDIANCE\n\nTell your healthcare provider about all the medicines you take, including prescription and over-the-counter medicines, vitamins, and herbal supplements.\n\nYou are encouraged to report negative side effects of prescription drugs to the FDA. Visit www.fda.gov/medwatch or call 1-800-FDA-1088.\n\nPlease see Prescribing Information and Medication Guide for JARDIANCE.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nCL-JAR-100211 10.24.2025\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c5cf54ff-4a5b-49e6-9e3b-4f836bc49cdb"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0672d479-918d-4669-bf66-93d95eff7d77"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:04b0373f-e976-42fc-ac92-abef59354cfd", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "04b0373f-e976-42fc-ac92-abef59354cfd", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d8b7db96-e0af-45b8-81a8-fd574d93bd75"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:bdf76d57-62ab-4497-bcfe-ff1e21b5d856", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "IMPORTANT SAFETY INFORMATION", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "disease_brochure", "section_id": "bdf76d57-62ab-4497-bcfe-ff1e21b5d856", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "CKD_Brochure.pdf", "source_document_id": "c66d5608-a1a9-4ea5-8044-6599b515b904", "text": "Do not take JARDIANCE if you are allergic to empagliflozin or any of the ingredients in JARDIANCE. Symptoms of a serious allergic reaction may include:\n\n- rash\n-   raised, red areas on your skin (hives)\n-   swelling of your face, lips, mouth, and throat that may cause difficulty in breathing or swallowing\n\nIf you have any of these symptoms, stop taking JARDIANCE and call your healthcare provider right away or go to the nearest hospital emergency room.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4b102d8c-5891-4084-a699-bb96d4877059"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:77ce92c3-94ad-4458-b297-1524eb7cf503", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "JARDIANCE ®  and the JARDIANCE ®  family global branding guidelines", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "77ce92c3-94ad-4458-b297-1524eb7cf503", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "text": "Utilise the branding system exactly as described in these global branding guidelines. Consistent use of these elements is critical to ensure a meaningful and recognisable brand experience for JARDIANCE and the JARDIANCE family worldwide.\n\nOctober 2025", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3c512f12-6309-4b29-8423-0b75c83d672e"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b4aae777-ca81-42d2-af78-09316ff61110", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "b4aae777-ca81-42d2-af78-09316ff61110", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "text": "All content in the global branding guidelines is strictly confidential and not to be distributed externally. It is neither the intention of the authors of the global branding guidelines nor of the Boehringer Ingelheim/ Lilly Alliance to discuss, strategise, or implement marketing communications that fall beyond the approved indications for this product. Any promotional activities must be consistent with the approved label and carried out in compliance with all company policies, applicable laws, and regulations. Any promotional materials must be reviewed and approved locally for compliance with all company policies, applicable laws, and regulations.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:364e2ec5-9166-4c25-8e64-31495586280c"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:be877221-3c90-42fb-b97f-a5011550fbdf", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Contents", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "be877221-3c90-42fb-b97f-a5011550fbdf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf", "source_document_id": "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b", "text": "| 1. JARDIANCE vision . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .        |   4 |\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------|