        |                              |                  |\n| White                      | 310/2286                   | 370/2256                   | 0.81 (0.69,0.94)       | ~                            |                  |\n| Black/ African-American    | 24/ 133                    | 28/ 125                    | 0.73 (0.42, 1.25)      |                              |                  |\n| Asian                      | 54/ 413                    | 77/ 411                    | 0.65 (0.46,0.92)       |                              |                  |\n| Other including mixed race | 27/ 164                    | 36/ 198                    | 0.95 (0.58, 1.57)      |                              |                  |\n| BMI                        |                            |                            |                        |                              |                  |\n| <30                        | 223/1654                   | 292/1642                   | 0.74 (0.62,0.88)       | f----+---l                   |                  |\n| 2:30                       | 192/1343                   | 219/1349                   | 0.85 (0. 70, 1 03)     | 1-----i                      |                  |\n| eGFR at baseline           |                            |                            |                        |                              |                  |\n| 2:90                       | 22/ 231                    | 28/ 237                    | 0.83 (0.48, 1.46)      |                              |                  |\n| 60 to <90                  | 130/1262                   | 161/1268                   | 0.80 (0.64, 1.01)      | -                            |                  |\n| 45 to <60                  | 112/ 792                   | 143/ 773                   | 0.73 (0.57,0.93)       |                              |                  |\n| 30 to <45                  | 106/ 564                   | 123/ 550                   | 0.82 (0.64, 1.07)      |                              |                  |\n| <30                        | 45/ 148                    | 55/ 161                    | 0.81 (0.55, 1.21)      |                              |                  |\n| NYHA at baseline           |                            |                            |                        |                              |                  |\n| II                         | 275/2435                   | 361/2452                   | 0.75 (0.64,0.87)       | 1--+---l                     |                  |\n| Ill/IV                     | 140/ 562                   | 150/ 539                   | 0.86 (0.68, 1.09)      |                              |                  |\n| LVEF at baseline           |                            |                            |                        |                              |                  |\n| >40% to <50%               | 145/ 995                   | 193/ 988                   | 0.71 (0.57,0.88)       | I ■ I                        |                  |\n| 50% to <60%                | 138/1028                   | 173/1030                   | 0.80 (0.64,0.99)       |                              |                  |\n| 2:60%                      | 132/ 974                   | 145/ 973                   | 0.87 (0.69, 1.10)      |                              |                  |\n| NT-proBNP                  |                            |                            |                        |                              |                  |\n| < median                   | 126/1477                   | 168/1508                   | 0.76 (0.61 ,0.96)      | I ■ I                        |                  |\n| 2: median                  | 288/1516                   | 341/1476                   | 0.78 (0.67,0.91)       | i----1                       |                  |\n| Baseline use of MRA        |                            |                            |                        |                              |                  |\n| No                         | 233/1878                   | 306/1866                   | 0.73 (0.62,0.87)       | f----+---l                   |                  |\n| Yes                        | 182/1119                   | 205/1125                   | 0.87 (0. 71 , 1.06)    | I----+- --l                  |                  |\n|                            |                            |                            |                        | I I 0.25 0.5                 | I 2              |\n\nHazard ratio", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d7cfbae3-f5e5-4a3b-98ee-ae6266e33bcf"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b65c450e-6462-4f5b-a1b9-4bce95f9b425"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:be8b4a44-5ebe-42c3-bb43-bd6ad49c4243"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1a7a6753-fd03-49de-b8b6-001ec0fba26f"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:91a0e70c-28e5-436e-b691-5dd236c12d31"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5418b230-75ed-4eee-8a21-bfc2a5d14150"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6c2eefa1-c807-4743-8c24-33c3bc8ee200"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d264d769-bb13-4f96-a14e-76ee1de70c51", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "14.5  Chronic Kidney Disease Trial in Adults", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 41, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "d264d769-bb13-4f96-a14e-76ee1de70c51", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "EMPA-KIDNEY (NCT03594110) was a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial conducted in adults with chronic kidney disease (eGFR ≥ 20 to &lt;45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ; or eGFR ≥ 45 to &lt;90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 with urine albumin to creatinine ratio [UACR] ≥ 200 mg/g). The trial excluded patients with polycystic kidney disease or patients requiring intravenous immunosuppressive therapy in the preceding three months or &gt;45 mg of prednisone (or equivalent) at the time of screening. The primary objective of the trial was to assess the effects of empagliflozin as an adjunct to standard of care therapy, including RAS-inhibitor therapy when appropriate, on time to kidney disease progression or cardiovascular death.\n\nA total of 6,609 patients, were equally randomized to JARDIANCE 10 mg or placebo and were followed for a median of 24 months.\n\nThe mean age of the study population was 63 years (range: 18 to 94 years) and 67% were male. Approximately 58% of the study population were White, 36% Asian, and 4% Black or African American. Approximately 44% of the patients had type 2 diabetes mellitus.\n\nAt baseline, the mean eGFR was 37 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 21% of patients had an eGFR equal to or above 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 44% had an eGFR 30 to less than 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , and 35% had an eGFR less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . The median UACR was 329 mg/g, 20% of patients had a UACR &lt;30 mg/g, 28% had a UACR 30 to ≤ 300mg/g, and 52% had a UACR &gt;300 mg/g. Approximately 1% of patients had type 1 diabetes at baseline. The most common etiologies of CKD were diabetic nephropathy/diabetic kidney disease (31%), glomerular disease (25%), hypertensive/renovascular disease (22%) and other/unknown (22%).\n\nAt baseline, 85% of patients were treated with ACE inhibitor or ARB, 64% with statins, and 34% with antiplatelet agents.\n\nJARDIANCE was superior to placebo in reducing the risk of the primary composite endpoint of sustained ≥ 40% eGFR decline, sustained eGFR &lt;10 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , progression to end-stage kidney disease, or CV or renal death. The treatment effect reflected a reduction in a sustained ≥ 40% eGFR decline, sustained eGFR &lt;10 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , progression to end-stage kidney disease, and CV death. There were few renal deaths during the trial. JARDIANCE also reduced the risk of first and recurrent hospitalization (see Table 18 and Figure 13); information collected on the reason for hospitalization was insufficient to further characterize the benefit.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5c05d428-069c-4a22-b56b-d79a7b693d85"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b6d44474-12db-46c0-a36c-5b4ebeacb6f2"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:89249716-31d5-4658-a445-ece2378f0957"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3c08935e-ad6c-42ca-8aa1-31c7cd8730c3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "3c08935e-ad6c-42ca-8aa1-31c7cd8730c3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Table 18 Treatment Effect for the Primary Composite Endpoint, its Components and Key Secondary Endpoints\n\n|                                                                                                                                          | Placebo N=3,305        | JARDIANCE 10 mg N=3,304   | Hazard ratio vs placebo (95% CI)   | p-value   |\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------|---------------------------|------------------------------------|-----------|\n|                                                                                                                                          | Number of Patients (%) | Number of Patients (%)    |                                    |           |\n| Composite of sustained ≥ 40% eGFR decline, sustained eGFR <10 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , ESKD a , or CV or renal death (time to first occurrence) | 558 (16.9)             | 432 (13.1)                | 0.72 (0.64, 0.82)                  | <0.0001   |\n| Sustained ≥ 40% eGFR decline                                                                                                             | 474 (14.3)             | 359 (10.9)                | 0.70 (0.61, 0.81)                  |           |\n| ESKD a or sustained eGFR <10 mL/min/1.73 m 2                                                                                             | 221 (6.7)              | 157 (4.8)                 | 0.69 (0.56, 0.84)                  |           |\n| Renal death b                                                                                                                            | 4 (0.1)                | 4 (0.1)                   |                                    |           |\n| CV death                                                                                                                                 | 69 (2.1)               | 59 (1.8)                  | 0.84 (0.60, 1.19)                  |           |\n|                                                                                                                                          | Number of Events       | Number of Events          |                                    |           |\n| First and recurrent hospitalization c                                                                                                    | 1,895                  | 1,611                     | 0.86 (0.78, 0.95)                  | 0.0025    |\n\nFigure 13 Time to First Occurrence of the Primary Composite Endpoint, Sustained ≥ 40% eGFR Decline, Sustained eGFR &lt;10 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , ESKD or Renal Death, or CV Death\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6a70e28e-0ddd-4eef-86c6-0e1f13b87823"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:718cacd9-ea0d-451e-a57a-1330b81374c9"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3c653e75-4f8d-4ed5-a2b8-aeebc65998ad"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e9926b95-b9be-4616-8439-b94fe1fbed2c", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "e9926b95-b9be-4616-8439-b94fe1fbed2c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "The results of the primary composite endpoint were generally consistent across the pre-specified subgroups examined, including eGFR categories, underlying cause of kidney disease, diabetes status, or background use of RAS inhibitors (see Figure 14).  The treatment benefit with JARDIANCE on the primary composite endpoint was not evident in patients with very low levels of albuminuria, however there were few events in these patients.\n\nFigure 14 Treatment Effects for the Primary Composite Endpoint (Sustained ≥ 40% eGFR Decline, Sustained eGFR &lt;10 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , ESKD or Renal Death, or CV Death) Subgroup Analysis (EMPA-KIDNEY)\n\n| Subgroup                          | N with event/ N        | analyzed   | Hazard ratio       | Interaction   | Empagliflozin 1 O mg better ~   | Placebo better   |\n|-----------------------------------|------------------------|------------|--------------------|---------------|---------------------------------|------------------|\n| Category                          | Empagliflozin 10 mg vs | Placebo    | (95%CI)            | p-value       |                                 |                  |\n| Overall                           | 432/3304               | 558/3305   | 0. 72 (0.64,0.82)  |               | f---9--1                        |                  |\n| Diabetes at base I ine            |                        |            |                    | 0.0598        |                                 |                  |\n| Diabetic                          | 218/1525               | 306/1515   | 0.64 (0.54,0.77)   |               | f-------1                       |                  |\n| Non-Diabetic                      | 214/1779               | 252/1790   | 0.82 (0.68,0.99)   |               |                                 |                  |\n| Baseline eGFR (CKD-EPI)           |                        |            |                    | 0.7800*       |                                 |                  |\n| <30                               | 247/1131               | 317/1151   | 0. 73 (0.62,0.86)  |               | f----+-----l                    |                  |\n| 30 to <45                         | 140/1467               | 175/1461   | 0. 78 (0.62,0.97)  |               | I • I                           |                  |\n| 2:45                              | 45/ 706                | 66/ 693    | 0.64 (0.44,0.93)   |               |                                 |                  |\n| Baseline UACR [mg/g)              |                        |            |                    | 0.0174*       |                                 |                  |\n| Normal (<30)                      | 42/ 665                | 42/ 663    | 1.01 (0.66, 1.55)  |               |                                 |                  |\n| Microalbuminuria (30 to s300)     | 67/ 927                | 78/ 937    | 0.91 (0.65, 1.26)  |               |                                 |                  |\n| Macroalbuminuria (>300)           | 323/1712               | 438/1705   | 0.67 (0.58,0.78)   |               | f---a---1                       |                  |\n| Age (years)                       |                        |            |                    | 0.5392        |                                 |                  |\n| <65                               | 231/1501               | 288/1501   | 0. 75 (0.63,0.89)  |               | f-------1                       |                  |\n| 2:65                              | 201/1803               | 270/1804   | 0.69 (0.58,0.83)   |               | 1-----+----l                    |                  |\n| Sex                               |                        |            |                    | 0.3620        |                                 |                  |\n| Male                              | 307/2207               | 394/2210   | 0. 75 (0.65,0.87)  |               | i------1                        |                  |\n| Female                            | 125/1097               | 164/1095   | 0.66 (0.52,0.83)   |               | I • I                           |                  |\n| Race                              |                        |            |                    | 0.0833        |                                 |                  |\n| White                             | 245/1939               | 273/1920   | 0.83 (0.70,0.99)   |               | f----                           |                  |\n| Black/ African-American           | 20/ 128                | 31/ 134    | 0.65 (0.37, 1.14)  |               |                                 |                  |\n| Asian Other including mixed race  | 163/1194               | 245/1199   | 0.62 (0.51 ,0.76)  |               | I • I                           |                  |\n| History of renal disease          |                        |            |                    | 0.5578        |                                 |                  |\n| Diabetic kidney disease           | 161/1032               | 223/1025   | 0.65 (0.53,0.80)   |               | I • I                           |                  |\n| Glomerular disease                | 117/ 853               | 142/ 816   |                    |               |                                 |                  |\n| Hypertensive/renovascular disease |                        | 96/ 739    |                    |               |                                 |                  |\n|                                   | 72/ 713                |            | 0.73 (0.54, 1.00)  |               |                                 |                  |\n|                                   |                        |            |                    | 0.5159        |                                 |                  |\n| No                                |                        |            | 0. 77 (0.60,0.98)  |               |                                 |                  |\n|                                   | 82/ 706                |            |                    |               |                                 |                  |\n|                                   |                        |            | 0.82(0.61 ,1.11)   |               |                                 |                  |\n| Other/unknown                     |                        | 97/ 725    |                    |               |                                 |                  |\n| RAS inhibitor                     |                        |            |                    |               |                                 |                  |\n|                                   | 81/ 473                | 98/ 508    | 0. 79 (0.59, 1.06) |               |                                 |                  |\n| Yes                               | 351/2831               | 460/2797   | 0. 71 (0.62,0.82)  |               | I-+-!                           |                  |\n|                                   |                        |            |                    | 0.25          | 0.5                             |                  |\n\n*=Trend test Hazard ratio", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f7d24202-33b1-4823-8bcf-d457b2e87bd1"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:40583a0d-6356-49c7-a41d-311347191149"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b8a8a6b3-080e-4799-857c-b5ccbcf3bea9"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f0fe44d7-4a8a-4693-a365-b35c4339b560"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2406c808-33c5-40ac-ace5-8a0b2ab11fb7"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ae8f2ab2-4fe4-4f2c-a0d7-10d516021072"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cbb69480-992e-4ec6-beaf-5c31f623f4cd"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:652afa90-80df-4715-8e48-8ecde4cb2229", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "16 HOW SUPPLIED/STORAGE AND HANDLING", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 44, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "652afa90-80df-4715-8e48-8ecde4cb2229", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "JARDIANCE tablets are available as follows:\n\n10 mg tablets: pale yellow, round, biconvex, and bevel-edged film-coated tablets debossed with 'S 10' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol on the other side.\n\nBottles of 30 (NDC 0597-0152-30)\n\nBottles of 90 (NDC 0597-0152-90)\n\nCartons containing 3 blister cards of 10 tablets each (3 x 10) (NDC 0597-0152-37), institutional pack.\n\n25 mg tablets: pale yellow, oval, biconvex film-coated tablets, debossed with 'S 25' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol on the other side.\n\nBottles of 30 (NDC 0597-0153-30)\n\nBottles of 90 (NDC 0597-0153-90)\n\nCartons containing 3 blister cards of 10 tablets each (3 x 10) (NDC 0597-0153-37), institutional pack.\n\nDispense in a well-closed container as defined in the USP.\n\nStorage\n\nStore at 20°C to 25°C (68°F to 77°F); excursions permitted to 15°C to 30°C (59°F to 86°F) [see USP Controlled Room Temperature].", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:93b8ca5c-c5f0-40b7-bd69-25be667a4c2d"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:041b6961-ee30-4f10-8f28-0239df8c1f91", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "17 PATIENT COUNSELING INFORMATION", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 44, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "041b6961-ee30-4f10-8f28-0239df8c1f91", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Advise the patient to read the FDA-approved patient labeling (Medication Guide).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2783f1c2-fca5-45f4-bebc-77f7d6e67e1f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:f430cf41-ad92-483b-9cfb-1b4209a59d03", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Diabetic Ketoacidosis in Patients with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus and Other Ketoacidosis", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 44, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "f430cf41-ad92-483b-9cfb-1b4209a59d03", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "In patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus, inform them that using JARDIANCE can increase their risk of lifethreatening diabetic ketoacidosis and that fatal ketoacidosis has occurred. For all other patients, inform them that JARDIANCE can cause potentially fatal ketoacidosis and that type 2 diabetes mellitus and pancreatic disorders (e.g., history of pancreatitis or pancreatic surgery) are risk factors.\n\nEducate all patients on precipitating factors (such as insulin dose reduction or missed insulin doses, infection, reduced caloric intake, ketogenic diet, surgery, dehydration, and alcohol abuse) and symptoms of ketoacidosis (including nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, tiredness, and labored breathing). Inform patients that blood glucose may be normal even in the presence of ketoacidosis.\n\nAdvise patients that they may be asked to monitor ketones. If symptoms of ketoacidosis occur, instruct patients to discontinue JARDIANCE and seek medical attention immediately [see Warnings and Precautions (5.1)] .", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:37ffb3f7-a004-418f-abb5-ce873217552f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3889e0a3-dc8a-43bb-abe6-68e537cc0585", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Volume Depletion", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 44, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "3889e0a3-dc8a-43bb-abe6-68e537cc0585", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Inform patients that symptomatic hypotension may occur with JARDIANCE and advise them to contact their healthcare provider if they experience such symptoms [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2)] .  Inform patients that dehydration may increase the risk for hypotension, and to maintain adequate fluid intake.\n\nGenitourinary Infections, including Urosepsis, Pyelonephritis, Necrotizing Fasciitis of the Perineum (Fournier's Gangrene), and Genital Mycotic Infections\n\nCounsel patients that genitourinary infections may occur when taking JARDIANCE and may become serious. Educate them on the symptoms and advise them to seek medical advice if symptoms occur. Specifically, advise patients to promptly seek medical attention if they develop pain or tenderness, redness, or swelling of the genitals or the area from the genitals back to the rectum, along with a fever above 100.4 q F or malaise [see Warnings and Precautions (5.3)] .", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c7df109c-6cf6-4c87-b61b-308db334b908"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:55565e14-66ad-4c40-98a8-5d571ad91ec5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Hypoglycemia", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "55565e14-66ad-4c40-98a8-5d571ad91ec5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Inform patients that hypoglycemia has been reported when JARDIANCE is used with insulin secretagogues or insulin. Hypoglycemia may occur in pediatric patients regardless of concomitant antidiabetic treatment. Educate patients or caregivers on the signs and symptoms of hypoglycemia [see Warnings and Precautions (5.4)] .", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ffe72020-d6e5-44e2-a3a8-4294a55af1d1"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d7dfdd26-4552-4293-8258-e2072ec11206", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Lower Limb Amputation", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "d7dfdd26-4552-4293-8258-e2072ec11206", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Counsel patients about the importance of routine preventative foot care. Instruct patients to monitor for new pain or tenderness, sores or ulcers, or infections involving the leg or foot and to seek medical advice immediately if such signs or symptoms develop [see Warnings and Precautions (5.5)] .", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:65ea8ce3-5446-446a-8242-c2dda6e5718a"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ac4340ca-6dae-4f02-be4f-14c2652fa86c", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Hypersensitivity Reactions", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "ac4340ca-6dae-4f02-be4f-14c2652fa86c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Inform patients that serious hypersensitivity reactions, such as urticaria and angioedema, have been reported with JARDIANCE.  Advise patients to report immediately any skin reaction or angioedema, and to discontinue drug until they have consulted prescribing healthcare provider [see Warnings and Precautions (5.6)] .", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c43bf4c6-453f-4bfa-a041-57c321500508"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3ee888be-37b7-4307-9b88-2910b826d5a8", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Laboratory Tests", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "3ee888be-37b7-4307-9b88-2910b826d5a8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Inform patients that elevated glucose in urinalysis is expected when taking JARDIANCE [see Drug Interactions (7)] .", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:01246dac-8526-46a5-93af-ea879640671f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3391912a-4b4c-4df4-91d5-478b776dc9a7", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Pregnancy", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "3391912a-4b4c-4df4-91d5-478b776dc9a7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Advise pregnant patients, and patients of reproductive potential, of the potential risk to a fetus with treatment with JARDIANCE [see Use in Specific Populations (8.1)] .  Instruct patients to report pregnancies to their healthcare provider as soon as possible.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2f08b89d-aa61-4ff8-848f-e563b46bc0e7"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7f835f2f-3003-4cfa-b1b8-1505cbd7c6d3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Lactation", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "7f835f2f-3003-4cfa-b1b8-1505cbd7c6d3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Advise patients that breastfeeding is not recommended during treatment with JARDIANCE [see Use in Specific Populations (8.2)].", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9054176e-d4e5-4238-a198-74a9ed4a0268"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:1c21d6f8-fbc7-4178-88f4-1d341f47a2c0", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Missed Dose", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "1c21d6f8-fbc7-4178-88f4-1d341f47a2c0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Instruct patients to take JARDIANCE only as prescribed. If a dose is missed, it should be taken as soon as the patient remembers.  Advise patients not to double their next dose [see Dosage and Administration (2.4)] .", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b096e5f3-9c65-4789-9933-7839be4b7acf"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:fba32ae7-9fe1-4d58-8ca2-f64e74b29a90", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Distributed by:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "fba32ae7-9fe1-4d58-8ca2-f64e74b29a90", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc. Ridgefield, CT 06877 USA\n\nMarketed by: Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc. Ridgefield, CT 06877 USA and Eli Lilly and Company Indianapolis, IN 46285 USA", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:44c0651d-2130-4b48-9351-9d13ae62c596"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:354e21c3-60eb-497b-b0c5-7cbb9b0369e4", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Licensed from:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "354e21c3-60eb-497b-b0c5-7cbb9b0369e4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim International GmbH, Ingelheim, Germany JARDIANCE is a registered trademark of and used under license from Boehringer Ingelheim International GmbH.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5cdf4fbd-7c00-4a89-8aa9-8a270dad3e30"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:dcc12fc8-1267-4e86-9b10-12a9d07130e7", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "dcc12fc8-1267-4e86-9b10-12a9d07130e7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc. either owns or uses the EMPA-REG OUTCOME ® , EMPERORReduced ® , EMPEROR-Preserved ® , and EMPA-KIDNEY ®  trademarks under license.\n\nThe other brands listed are trademarks of their respective owners and are not trademarks of Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc.\n\nCopyright © 2025 Boehringer Ingelheim International GmbH ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\nCOL8914PI262025", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c3a23ef1-6201-4e92-be45-9e9c9ae08c88"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:26c55f7b-565d-4f2a-bc03-a295e890b773", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "MEDICATION GUIDE JARDIANCE ®  (jar DEE ans) (empagliflozin tablets)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 47, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "26c55f7b-565d-4f2a-bc03-a295e890b773", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "for oral use", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:391210d1-8d13-40fe-aeb3-62b2d1cf4b07"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:945687f7-25b7-470a-9d34-e975c33aa89d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "What is the most important information I should know about JARDIANCE?", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 47, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "945687f7-25b7-470a-9d34-e975c33aa89d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "JARDIANCE can cause serious side effects, including:\n\n- x Diabetic ketoacidosis (increased ketones in your blood or urine) in people with type 1 and other ketoacidosis. JARDIANCE can cause ketoacidosis that can be life-threatening and may lead to death. Ketoacidosis is a serious condition which needs to be treated in a hospital. People with type 1 diabetes have a high risk of getting ketoacidosis. People with type 2 diabetes or pancreas problems also have an increased risk of getting ketoacidosis. Ketoacidosis can also happen in people who: are sick, cannot eat or drink as usual, skip meals, are on a diet high in fat and low in carbohydrates (ketogenic diet), take less than the usual amount of insulin or miss insulin doses, drink too much alcohol, have a loss of too much fluid from the body (volume depletion), or who have surgery. Ketoacidosis can happen even if your blood sugar is less than 250 mg/dL. Your healthcare provider may ask you to periodically check ketones in your urine or blood.\n\nStop taking JARDIANCE and call your healthcare provider or get medical help right away if you get any of the following. If possible, check for ketones in your urine or blood, even if your blood sugar is less than 250 mg/dL:\n\n- o nausea\n- o vomiting\n- o stomach-area (abdominal) pain\n- o tiredness\n- o trouble breathing\n- o ketones in your urine or blood\n- x Dehydration. JARDIANCE can cause some people to become dehydrated (the loss of body water and salt). Dehydration may cause you to feel dizzy, faint, light-headed, or weak, especially when you stand up (orthostatic hypotension). There have been reports of sudden worsening of kidney function in people who are taking JARDIANCE. You may be at higher risk of dehydration if you:\n- o take medicines to lower your blood pressure, including diuretics (water pills)\n- o are on low sodium (salt) diet\n- o have kidney problems\n- o are 65 years of age or older\n\nTalk to your healthcare provider about what you can do to prevent dehydration including how much fluid you should drink on a daily basis. Call your healthcare provider right away if you reduce the amount of food or liquid you drink, for example if you are sick or you cannot eat, or start to lose liquids from your body, for example from vomiting, diarrhea or being in the sun too long.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2ee1eb03-2623-44cc-b2aa-3d1ae88a0b2e"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8309a83f-5248-462c-95aa-0b2d89119d68"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d1bd2cff-8fb4-4e13-b837-092e40d5f776"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4b4e6350-99ff-45ff-a826-8ace6c0ef9e8", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "What is JARDIANCE?", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 47, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "4b4e6350-99ff-45ff-a826-8ace6c0ef9e8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "JARDIANCE is a prescription medicine used to:\n\n- o reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization for heart failure in adults with heart failure, when the heart cannot pump enough blood to the rest of your body.\n- o reduce the risk of further worsening of kidney disease, end-stage kidney disease (ESKD), death due to cardiovascular disease, and hospitalization in adults with chronic kidney disease.\n- o reduce the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes and who also have known cardiovascular disease.\n- o lower blood sugar (glucose) along with diet and exercise in adults and children who are 10 years of age and older with type 2 diabetes.\n\nJARDIANCE is not for use to lower blood sugar (glucose) in people with type 1 diabetes. It may increase their risk of diabetic ketoacidosis (increased ketones in blood or urine).\n\nJARDIANCE is not for use to lower blood sugar (glucose) in people with type 2 diabetes who have severe kidney problems, because it may not work.\n\nJARDIANCE is not for people with polycystic kidney disease, or who are taking or have recently received certain types of immunosuppressive therapy to treat kidney disease. JARDIANCE is not expected to work if you have these conditions.\n\nIt is not known if JARDIANCE is safe and effective in children under 10 years of age.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:062bef30-8d62-4afd-b17c-dcddfbc70f59"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:62522549-4f2b-4fbe-b377-517e5630d8e0"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d0f2844b-c0f3-4aa4-8777-83acbe8f7d04", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Who should not take JARDIANCE? Do not take JARDIANCE if you:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 48, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "d0f2844b-c0f3-4aa4-8777-83acbe8f7d04", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "- x are allergic to empagliflozin or any of the ingredients in JARDIANCE.  See the end of this Medication Guide for a complete list of ingredients in JARDIANCE. Symptoms of a serious allergic reaction to JARDIANCE may include:\n- o rash\n- o raised, red areas on your skin (hives)\n- o swelling of your face, lips, mouth, and throat that may cause difficulty in breathing or swallowing\n\nIf you have any of these symptoms, stop taking JARDIANCE and call your healthcare provider right away or go to the nearest hospital emergency room.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:abad7581-4e54-4074-a642-4e084e57ec0d"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b4fe4c71-c92e-46d6-a989-762b2dda16e1", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "What should I tell my healthcare provider before taking JARDIANCE?", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 48, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "b4fe4c71-c92e-46d6-a989-762b2dda16e1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:edc92f27-a46a-41a8-896b-3ac34f080a55", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Before taking JARDIANCE, tell your healthcare provider about all of your medical conditions, including if you:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 48, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "edc92f27-a46a-41a8-896b-3ac34f080a55", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "- x have type 1 diabetes or have had diabetic ketoacidosis.\n- x have a serious infection.\n- x have a decrease in your insulin dose.\n- x have a history of infection of the vagina or penis.\n- x have kidney problems.\n- x have a history of amputation.\n- x have liver problems.\n- x are on a low sodium (salt) diet. Your healthcare provider may change your diet or your dose.\n- x have a history of urinary tract infections or problems with urination.\n- x are going to have surgery. Your healthcare provider may stop your JARDIANCE before you have surgery. Talk to your healthcare provider if you are having surgery about when to stop taking JARDIANCE and when to start it again.\n- x are eating less, or there is a change in your diet.\n- x have or have had problems with your pancreas, including pancreatitis or surgery on your pancreas.\n- x are dehydrated.\n- x drink alcohol very often or drink a lot of alcohol in the short term ('binge' drinking).\n- x are pregnant or plan to become pregnant. JARDIANCE may harm your unborn baby. If you become pregnant while taking JARDIANCE, tell your healthcare provider as soon as possible. Talk with your healthcare provider about the best way to control your blood sugar while you are pregnant.\n- x have ever had an allergic reaction to JARDIANCE.\n- x are breastfeeding or plan to breastfeed. JARDIANCE may pass into your breast milk and may harm your baby. Talk with your healthcare provider about the best way to feed your baby if you are taking JARDIANCE.  Do not breastfeed while taking JARDIANCE.\n\nTell your healthcare provider about all the medicines you take, including prescription and over-the-counter medicines, vitamins, and herbal supplements.\n\nJARDIANCE may affect the way other medicines work, and other medicines may affect how JARDIANCE works. Know the medicines you take. Keep a list of them to show your healthcare provider and pharmacist when you get a new medicine.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9236a975-a3ac-43d8-b441-e02e21b5b96c"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1ff876ad-73d5-415f-a940-72208c20e852"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:cf165962-d35c-4b5a-9b2d-3d3a85ba44e5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "How should I take JARDIANCE?", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 48, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "cf165962-d35c-4b5a-9b2d-3d3a85ba44e5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "- x Take JARDIANCE exactly as your healthcare provider tells you to take it.\n- x Your healthcare provider will tell you how much JARDIANCE to take and when to take it.  Your healthcare provider may change your dose if needed.\n- x Take JARDIANCE by mouth 1 time in the morning each day, with or without food.\n- x Your healthcare provider may tell you to take JARDIANCE along with other diabetes medicines. Low blood sugar can happen more often when JARDIANCE is taken with certain other diabetes medicines. See 'What are the possible side effects of JARDIANCE?'\n- x If you miss a dose, take it as soon as you remember.  If it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and take the medicine at the next regularly scheduled time.  Do not take two doses of JARDIANCE at the same time.  Talk with your healthcare provider if you have questions about a missed dose.\n- x If you take too much JARDIANCE, call your healthcare provider or Poison Help line at 1-800-222-1222, or go to the nearest hospital emergency room right away.\n- x When taking JARDIANCE, you may have sugar in your urine, which will show up on a urine test.\n- x When your body is under some types of stress, such as fever, trauma (such as a car accident), infection, or surgery, the amount of diabetes medicine you need may change. Tell your healthcare provider right away if you have any of these conditions and follow your healthcare provider's instructions.\n- x Your healthcare provider may do certain blood tests before you start JARDIANCE and during treatment as needed.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:abaca656-fbca-4f25-a449-40b1e07040d9"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ff26443e-080a-4188-bd69-22c5aff82130"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:539f090d-cafc-4acf-9233-4f9e29eda3ad", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "What are the possible side effects of JARDIANCE?", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "539f090d-cafc-4acf-9233-4f9e29eda3ad", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "JARDIANCE may cause serious side effects, including:\n\n- x See 'What is the most important information I should know about JARDIANCE?'\n- x Genital and urinary tract infections. JARDIANCE can cause serious infections in your genital area or urinary tract that could require hospitalization. A rare but serious bacterial infection called necrotizing fasciitis can cause damage to the tissue under the skin in the area between and around the anus and genitals (perineum). This infection may require hospitalization, multiple surgeries, and could lead to death. Seek medical attention immediately if you have a fever or you are feeling very weak, tired or uncomfortable (malaise), and you develop any of the following symptoms in the area between and around your anus and genitals:\n- o pain or tenderness\n- o swelling\n- o redness of skin (erythema)\n\nAlso tell your healthcare provider if you have any of these signs or symptoms of urinary tract infections or yeast infections:\n\n- o Urinary tract infection:\n- • burning feeling when you urinate\n- • need to urinate often or right away\n- • pain in the lower part of your stomach (pelvis)\n- • blood in your urine\n\nYou may also have a fever, back pain, nausea, or vomiting.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:36bd3426-bb51-4f7a-9f75-1f022721e420"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1981d054-dd6f-49e9-a34c-189868adf5ec"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2796491c-659c-45dd-b146-3db0a810fdc0", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "o Vaginal yeast infection :", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "2796491c-659c-45dd-b146-3db0a810fdc0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "- • vaginal odor\n- • white or yellowish vaginal discharge (may be lumpy or look like cottage cheese)\n- • vaginal itching\n- o Yeast infection of the skin around the penis (balanitis or balanoposthitis): If you are uncircumcised, swelling may make it difficult to pull back the skin around the tip of your penis. Other symptoms include:\n- • redness, itching, or swelling of the penis\n- • bad smelling discharge from the penis\n- • rash on the penis\n- • pain in the skin around the penis\n\nTalk to your healthcare provider about what to do if you get symptoms of a yeast infection. They may suggest you use an over-the-counter antifungal medicine. Contact your healthcare provider right away if your symptoms do not improve after using an over-the-counter antifungal medicine.\n\n- x Low blood sugar (hypoglycemia). In adults, if you take JARDIANCE with another medicine that can cause low blood sugar, such as a sulfonylurea or insulin, your risk of getting low blood sugar is higher. In children 10 years of age and older, the risk for low blood sugar is higher with JARDIANCE even if you do not use another medicine that can also lower blood sugar. The dose of your sulfonylurea medicine or insulin may need to be lowered while you take JARDIANCE.\n\nSigns and symptoms of low blood sugar may include:\n\n- [ ] o headache\n\n- o drowsiness\n- o weakness\n\n- [ ] o irritability\n\n- [ ] o hunger\n\n- [ ] o fast heartbeat\n\n- [ ] o confusion\n\n- [ ] o shaking or feeling jittery\n\n- x Amputations. SGLT2 inhibitors may increase your risk of lower limb amputations.\n\nYou may be at a higher risk of lower limb amputation if you:\n\n- o have a history of amputation\n- o have had blocked or narrowed blood vessels, usually in your leg\n- o have had diabetic foot infection, ulcers or sores\n\nCall your healthcare provider right away if you have new pain or tenderness, any sores, ulcers, or infections in your leg or foot. Talk to your healthcare provider about proper foot care.\n\n- x Serious allergic reactions. If you have any symptoms of a serious allergic reaction, stop taking JARDIANCE and call your healthcare provider right away or go to the nearest hospital emergency room. See 'Who should not take JARDIANCE?' .", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:52b5b3e1-b046-42c1-8600-996b7ac1c3d1"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7bf57bf2-7040-4fc7-acbe-a56450c2642b"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:41d7f204-2292-4d6c-a8ad-30a3fa66ea53"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:fb426d13-8394-4ca1-b703-ad9d540e3563", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "The most common side effects of JARDIANCE include:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "fb426d13-8394-4ca1-b703-ad9d540e3563", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "- x urinary tract infections\n- x yeast infections in females\n\nThese are not all the possible side effects of JARDIANCE.  For more information, ask your healthcare provider or pharmacist.\n\nCall your doctor for medical advice about side effects.  You may report side effects to FDA at 1-800-FDA-1088.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bb032b7d-dbfd-46b8-976e-723f330d963f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2f899d66-7223-4338-b35c-107b9e1214e6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "How should I store JARDIANCE?", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "2f899d66-7223-4338-b35c-107b9e1214e6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "- x Store JARDIANCE at room temperature between 68 q F to 77 q F (20 q C to 25 q C).\n- x Keep JARDIANCE and all medicines out of the reach of children.\n\n- [ ] o dizziness\n\n- [ ] o sweating", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:38171f1a-4516-42ae-8bd9-0c069be5c9f2"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:68556df2-2f98-423d-a7f0-6a36483737de", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "General information about the safe and effective use of JARDIANCE.", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 50, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "68556df2-2f98-423d-a7f0-6a36483737de", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Medicines are sometimes prescribed for purposes other than those listed in a Medication Guide. Do not use JARDIANCE for a condition for which it is not prescribed.  Do not give JARDIANCE to other people, even if they have the same symptoms you have.  It may harm them.\n\nYou can ask your pharmacist or healthcare provider for information about JARDIANCE that is written for health professionals.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c389108f-c0eb-4f97-b845-83b4cf2e7b62"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:aa23cb55-fc24-45a4-a907-dfe2f13974de", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "What are the ingredients in JARDIANCE?", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 50, "source_document_type": "prescribing_information", "section_id": "aa23cb55-fc24-45a4-a907-dfe2f13974de", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "Jardiance_PI.pdf", "source_document_id": "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0", "text": "Active Ingredient:\n\nempagliflozin\n\nInactive Ingredients: colloidal silicon dioxide, croscarmellose sodium, hydroxypropyl cellulose, lactose monohydrate, magnesium stearate, and microcrystalline cellulose.  In addition, the film coating contains the following inactive ingredients: ferric oxide yellow, hypromellose, polyethylene glycol, talc, and titanium dioxide.\n\nDistributed by: Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc.; Ridgefield, CT 06877 USA\n\nMarketed by: Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc.; Ridgefield, CT 06877 USA and Eli Lilly and Company, Indianapolis, IN 46285 USA\n\nLicensed from: Boehringer Ingelheim International GmbH, Ingelheim, Germany\n\nJARDIANCE is a registered trademark of and used under license from Boehringer Ingelheim International GmbH.\n\nBoehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc. either owns or uses the EMPA-REG OUTCOME ® , EMPEROR-Reduced ® , EMPEROR-Preserved ® , and EMPA-KIDNEY ® trademarks under license.\n\nThe other brands listed are trademarks of their respective owners and are not trademarks of Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc.\n\nCopyright © 2025 Boehringer Ingelheim International GmbH ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\nCOL8914PI262025\n\nFor more information about JARDIANCE, including current prescribing information and Medication Guide, go to www.jardiance.com , scan the code, or call Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc. at 1-800-542-6257.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nThis Medication Guide has been approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.\n\nRevised: October 2025", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cfccc40e-0b73-45aa-b595-c9d93c6480a8"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:813d897b-4acf-410d-a5c2-e69f3f2fd20c"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d3fca4fc-a137-4db8-948c-2ccefaee47d0", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Symptoms", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d3fca4fc-a137-4db8-948c-2ccefaee47d0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In controlled clinical studies single doses of up to 800 mg empagliflozin in healthy volunteers and multiple daily doses of up to 100 mg empagliflozin in patients with type 2 diabetes did not show any toxicity. Empagliflozin increased urine glucose excretion leading to an increase in urine volume. The observed increase in urine volume was not dose-dependent and is not clinically meaningful. There is no experience with doses above 800 mg in humans.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2ee5ae2b-05e9-479e-a8fa-89939f42a7cb"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:8610d9ea-399f-4ffe-9cc9-5121bbae9331", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Therapy", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "8610d9ea-399f-4ffe-9cc9-5121bbae9331", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In the event of an overdose, treatment should be initiated as appropriate to the patient's clinical status. The removal of empagliflozin by haemodialysis has not been studied.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1da3352c-957e-41d4-9b28-870576c8ce0d"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:14a9c970-f818-4e05-9d0d-ebc48cdc8062", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "5. PHARMACOLOGICAL PROPERTIES", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "14a9c970-f818-4e05-9d0d-ebc48cdc8062", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:624b4b2e-33e8-4a00-9d5a-28758c42af71", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "624b4b2e-33e8-4a00-9d5a-28758c42af71", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Pharmacotherapeutic group: Drugs used in diabetes, Sodium-glucose co-transporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors, ATC code: A10BK03", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f646612f-a9c1-4ce3-a8bf-3b38e013876d"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:df6f1ec4-ed31-428c-96e4-b3942a882073", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "df6f1ec4-ed31-428c-96e4-b3942a882073", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin does not inhibit P-gp at therapeutic doses. Based on in vitro studies, empagliflozin is considered unlikely to cause interactions with active substances that are P-gp substrates. Coadministration of digoxin, a P-gp substrate, with empagliflozin resulted in a 6% increase in AUC and 14% increase in Cmax of digoxin. These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.\n\nEmpagliflozin does not inhibit human uptake transporters such as OAT3, OATP1B1, and OATP1B3 in vitro at clinically relevant plasma concentrations and, as such, drug-drug interactions with substrates of these uptake transporters are considered unlikely.\n\nInteraction studies conducted in healthy volunteers suggest that empagliflozin had no clinically relevant effect on the pharmacokinetics of metformin, glimepiride, pioglitazone, sitagliptin, linagliptin, simvastatin, warfarin, ramipril, digoxin, diuretics and oral contraceptives.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:21f22924-ce3e-4ec1-85c5-d7b32485150b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:cb2b9b2f-45b4-4e99-845e-431bd31dce18", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Paediatric population", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "cb2b9b2f-45b4-4e99-845e-431bd31dce18", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Interaction studies have only been performed in adults.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a0a256d6-17cc-471d-aa8e-0d063637a465"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:fbfebb7a-9404-4d0d-b93f-a352164cf99c", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.6 Fertility, pregnancy and lactation", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "fbfebb7a-9404-4d0d-b93f-a352164cf99c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:689d954c-5fa0-4db4-a085-143676834c2e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Pregnancy", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "689d954c-5fa0-4db4-a085-143676834c2e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "There are no data from the use of empagliflozin in pregnant women. Animal studies show that empagliflozin crosses the placenta during late gestation to a very limited extent but do not indicate direct or indirect harmful effects with respect to early embryonic development. However, animal studies have shown adverse effects on postnatal development (see section 5.3). As a precautionary measure, it is preferable to avoid the use of Jardiance during pregnancy.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:678dd59e-4249-438e-b9f5-4e8c42ea6ecc"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:c37b5864-2d1a-4473-9a4b-60505cdcb9de", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Breast-feeding", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "c37b5864-2d1a-4473-9a4b-60505cdcb9de", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "No data in humans are available on excretion of empagliflozin into milk. Available toxicological data in animals have shown excretion of empagliflozin in milk. A risk to the newborns/infants cannot be excluded. Jardiance should not be used during breast-feeding.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0d446b35-c4ef-4b47-89c0-9364003dec2b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:962bc2f9-25df-4d79-9e71-ac8e9c5c24e1", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Fertility", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "962bc2f9-25df-4d79-9e71-ac8e9c5c24e1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "No studies on the effect on human fertility have been conducted for Jardiance. Animal studies do not indicate direct or indirect harmful effects with respect to fertility (see section 5.3).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2e4beaf8-c05f-4119-bed1-853e7ecf4274"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b9b6bedd-2c81-45d4-aec9-4e0963368e04", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.7 Effects on ability to drive and use machines", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b9b6bedd-2c81-45d4-aec9-4e0963368e04", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance has minor influence on the ability to drive and use machines. Patients should be advised to take precautions to avoid hypoglycaemia while driving and using machines, in particular when Jardiance is used in combination with a sulphonylurea and/or insulin.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9b2f2330-1b44-4683-8d29-4e6382386cb9"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:98f9a64a-ec89-4782-a3d3-64da57abffb6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.8 Undesirable effects", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "98f9a64a-ec89-4782-a3d3-64da57abffb6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:c2ab14c0-3072-4f94-a2ec-6527b4c31c4f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Summary of the safety profile", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "c2ab14c0-3072-4f94-a2ec-6527b4c31c4f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:bc93c8a3-3eb1-4c6d-bf5b-9db9c5014c62", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "bc93c8a3-3eb1-4c6d-bf5b-9db9c5014c62", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "A total of 15 582 patients with type 2 diabetes were included in clinical studies to evaluate the safety of empagliflozin, of which 10 004 patients received empagliflozin, either alone or in combination with metformin, a sulphonylurea, pioglitazone, DPP-4 inhibitors, or insulin.\n\nIn 6 placebo-controlled trials of 18 to 24 weeks duration, 3 534 patients were included of which 1 183", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7661a4a7-33eb-49b0-9db8-0a22712b3866"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d298fc33-3414-4a64-bbf1-6c158b856f90", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d298fc33-3414-4a64-bbf1-6c158b856f90", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "were treated with placebo and 2 351 with empagliflozin. The overall incidence of adverse events in patients treated with empagliflozin was similar to placebo. The most frequently reported adverse reaction was hypoglycaemia when used with sulphonylurea or insulin (see description of selected adverse reactions).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:684fd73b-9067-4046-87a2-b56d5157409a"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e9e280b4-7d10-4662-aa4f-cd53e6d91934", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Heart failure", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e9e280b4-7d10-4662-aa4f-cd53e6d91934", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The EMPEROR studies included patients with heart failure and either reduced ejection fraction (N = 3 726) or preserved ejection fraction (N = 5 985) treated with empagliflozin 10 mg or placebo. Approximately half of the patients had type 2 diabetes mellitus. The most frequent adverse reaction of the pooled EMPEROR-Reduced and EMPEROR-Preserved studies was volume depletion (empagliflozin 10 mg: 11.4%. placebo: 9.7%).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:07bc97f0-8b8a-4cfb-9cc7-b22d0b881d9b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:cb94014e-4890-475c-a97d-12b74bc2cc8b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Chronic kidney disease", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "cb94014e-4890-475c-a97d-12b74bc2cc8b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The EMPA-KIDNEY study included patients with chronic kidney disease (N = 6 609) treated with 10 mg empagliflozin or placebo. About 44% of the patients had type 2 diabetes mellitus. The most frequent adverse events in the EMPA-KIDNEY study were gout (empagliflozin 7.0% vs placebo 8.0%), and acute kidney injury (empagliflozin 2.8% vs placebo 3.5%) which were more frequently reported in patients on placebo.\n\nThe overall safety profile of empagliflozin was generally consistent across the studied indications.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5e876b5d-994a-4ee4-a7bc-7aa6c2a3a1e5"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:cf5e0a21-9448-4866-865b-4a09a323a124", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Tabulated list of adverse reactions", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "cf5e0a21-9448-4866-865b-4a09a323a124", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Adverse reactions classified by system organ class and MedDRA preferred terms reported in patients who received empagliflozin in placebo-controlled studies are presented in the table below (Table 1).\n\nThe adverse reactions are listed by absolute frequency. Frequencies are defined as very common (≥ 1/10), common (≥ 1/100 to &lt; 1/10), uncommon (≥ 1/1 000 to &lt; 1/100), rare (≥ 1/10 000 to &lt; 1/1 000), or very rare (&lt; 1/10 000), and not known (cannot be estimated from the available data).\n\nTable 1: Tabulated list of adverse reactions (MedDRA) from reported placebo-controlled studies and from post-marketing experience\n\n| System organ class                     | Very common                                               | Common                                                                                                                                         | Uncommon             | Rare                                                         | Very Rare   |\n|----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|-------------|\n| Infections and infestations            |                                                           | Vaginal moniliasis, vulvovaginitis, balanitis and other genital infection a Urinary tract infection (including pyelonephritis and urosepsis) a |                      | Necrotising fasciitis of the perineum (Fournier´s gangrene)* |             |\n| Metabolism and nutrition disorders     | Hypoglycaemia (when used with sulphonylurea or insulin) a | Thirst                                                                                                                                         | Ketoacidosis *       |                                                              |             |\n| Gastrointestinal disorders             |                                                           | Constipation                                                                                                                                   |                      |                                                              |             |\n| Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders |                                                           | Pruritus (generalised) Rash                                                                                                                    | Urticaria Angioedema |                                                              |             |\n| Vascular disorders                     | Volume depletion a                                        |                                                                                                                                                |                      |                                                              |             |\n| Renal and                              |                                                           | Increased                                                                                                                                      | Dysuria              |                                                              | Tubulo-     |", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1b2b0da2-e1dc-436a-877d-a80a85c8e548"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:74c7dea0-fc54-43f2-a0b4-e506ed73c260"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:dee50072-99bc-426e-afac-4cceb080f4af"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:54768355-a91e-46b5-a6ad-be187e2e168e"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7fae6c94-5a57-4ba1-89e1-3139c5ffadac", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7fae6c94-5a57-4ba1-89e1-3139c5ffadac", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "| urinary disorders   | urination a              |                                                                                            | interstitial nephritis   |\n|---------------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|\n| Investigations      | Serum lipids increased a | Blood creatinine increased/ Glomerular filtration rate decreased a Haematocrit increased a |                          |\n\na see subsections below for additional information\n\n* see section 4.4", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:77e6a668-b21d-4dc8-8bbf-6ad57538d425"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:0504ce8b-2108-46cc-ab6d-2fb30bf6c9b9", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Description of selected adverse reactions", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "0504ce8b-2108-46cc-ab6d-2fb30bf6c9b9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:a66a82f3-6ad2-413e-9df1-e8dfbd101294", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Body weight", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "a66a82f3-6ad2-413e-9df1-e8dfbd101294", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In a pre-specified pooled analysis of 4 placebo-controlled studies, treatment with empagliflozin resulted in body weight reduction (-0.24 kg for placebo, -2.04 kg for empagliflozin 10 mg and -2.26 kg for empagliflozin 25 mg) at week 24 that was maintained up to week 52 (-0.16 kg for placebo, -1.96 kg for empagliflozin 10 mg and -2.25 kg for empagliflozin 25 mg).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:be4d16e5-34f2-4f77-8e7e-8d7fd5f609ef"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:f66fc56f-c895-4894-ad43-9e2c616f78ba", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM AND CONTENTS", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "f66fc56f-c895-4894-ad43-9e2c616f78ba", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "- 7 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 10 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 14 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 28 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 30 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 60 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 70 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 90 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 100 × 1 film-coated tablets", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:066515df-05f4-4814-9a18-1bd7f91bdf86"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3e28ef44-851e-449b-b32d-dda7ba354384", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "5. METHOD AND ROUTE(S) OF ADMINISTRATION", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "3e28ef44-851e-449b-b32d-dda7ba354384", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Read the package leaflet before use.\n\nOral use", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c6eef1dc-ddfc-4cbf-8419-6df7c9d41ef3"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4683ac0e-319d-4251-983e-d5c27d68670d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "6. SPECIAL WARNING THAT THE MEDICINAL PRODUCT MUST BE STORED OUT OF THE SIGHT AND REACH OF CHILDREN", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4683ac0e-319d-4251-983e-d5c27d68670d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Keep out of the sight and reach of children.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4f8767a2-0f83-451e-a61b-20a9cd68b60c"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:dfa86b49-da3a-48c2-9547-e8836b394e4f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "7. OTHER SPECIAL WARNING(S), IF NECESSARY", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "dfa86b49-da3a-48c2-9547-e8836b394e4f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e1a203ff-ede7-48ea-ba5a-531e9255e43a", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "8. EXPIRY DATE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 42, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e1a203ff-ede7-48ea-ba5a-531e9255e43a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "EXP", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:039cda06-8526-4222-ac17-ec9af4fb16e6"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4e9f0560-9733-4f8b-852e-9baf3585cdd3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "9. SPECIAL STORAGE CONDITIONS", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4e9f0560-9733-4f8b-852e-9baf3585cdd3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "10.\n\nSPECIAL PRECAUTIONS FOR DISPOSAL OF UNUSED MEDICINAL PRODUCTS\n\nOR WASTE MATERIALS DERIVED FROM SUCH MEDICINAL PRODUCTS, IF\n\nAPPROPRIATE", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:406ccd7c-ba6b-4e70-a826-2167e688eef2"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:0de4b1f2-5d2d-4042-8fb7-a030ccf66dda", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "11. NAME AND ADDRESS OF THE MARKETING AUTHORISATION HOLDER", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "0de4b1f2-5d2d-4042-8fb7-a030ccf66dda", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim International GmbH 55216 Ingelheim am Rhein Germany", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6ce2be33-6205-4841-84c9-e26b673c4473"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:01b29649-6dff-4afd-a299-0101ba8c6032", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Blood pressure", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "01b29649-6dff-4afd-a299-0101ba8c6032", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The efficacy and safety of empagliflozin was evaluated in a double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 12 weeks duration in patients with type 2 diabetes and high blood pressure on different antidiabetic and up to 2 antihypertensive therapies. Treatment with empagliflozin once daily resulted in statistically significant improvement in HbA1c, and 24 hour mean systolic and diastolic blood pressure as determined by ambulatory blood pressure monitoring (Table 11). Treatment with empagliflozin provided reductions in seated SBP and DBP.\n\nTable 11: Efficacy results at 12 week in a placebo-controlled study of empagliflozin in patients with", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:77e89a3e-0aa9-465d-b29b-4985d0bfd2d1"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:997dea4c-15b7-4b92-a72d-08d7acb6e732", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "12. MARKETING AUTHORISATION NUMBER(S)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "997dea4c-15b7-4b92-a72d-08d7acb6e732", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "EU/1/14/930/010 7 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/011 10 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/012 14 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/013 28 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/014 30 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/015 60 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/016 70 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/017 90 × 1 tablets\n\nEU/1/14/930/018 100 × 1 tablets", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c178ebc6-6bc3-4739-931d-edf5e1f04674"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:83eeeb46-42ca-4efd-b530-4a967433cacc", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "13. BATCH NUMBER", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "83eeeb46-42ca-4efd-b530-4a967433cacc", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Lot", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5631d8af-166d-4282-8374-0c5e70da23f1"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ecac5b0f-91ea-4e2d-a320-aa929482c2b4", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "14. GENERAL CLASSIFICATION FOR SUPPLY", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "ecac5b0f-91ea-4e2d-a320-aa929482c2b4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3539b541-f892-40f5-b705-6fcf97435f1d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "15. INSTRUCTIONS ON USE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "3539b541-f892-40f5-b705-6fcf97435f1d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ef766b70-16fe-4ec1-a0fd-159470431e58", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "16. INFORMATION IN BRAILLE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "ef766b70-16fe-4ec1-a0fd-159470431e58", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance 10 mg", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:feb95b0c-2c12-4e09-ba3e-3723140106fe"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:f9eb099a-a4ef-4dab-9c50-4429c663dcf6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "17. UNIQUE IDENTIFIER - 2D BARCODE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "f9eb099a-a4ef-4dab-9c50-4429c663dcf6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "2D barcode carrying the unique identifier included.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9fd21917-09d1-4bef-9dc2-911a0b1153cd"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:33d04905-d86a-4892-9446-48a9ce2727d9", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 32, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "33d04905-d86a-4892-9446-48a9ce2727d9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The clinical efficacy and safety of empagliflozin (10 mg with a possible dose-increase to 25 mg) and linagliptin (5 mg) once daily has been studied in children and adolescents from 10 to 17 years of age with type 2 diabetes mellitus in a placebo-controlled study (DINAMO) over 26 weeks, with a safety extension period up to 52 weeks. Background therapies as adjunct to diet and exercise included metformin (51%), a combination of metformin and insulin (40.1%), insulin (3.2%), or none (5.7%).\n\nThe adjusted mean change in HbA1c at week 26 between empagliflozin (N = 52) and placebo (N = 53) of -0.84% was clinically meaningful and statistically significant (95% CI -1.50, -0.19; p = 0.0116). In addition, treatment with empagliflozin versus placebo resulted in a clinically meaningful adjusted mean change in FPG of -35.2 mg/dL (95% CI -58.6, -11.7) [-1.95 mmol/L (-3.25, -0.65)].", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8519dcec-2200-4cac-85ef-abc1806fa153"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7076ad58-2837-4a04-94c0-4aea1af45b39", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Heart failure and chronic kidney disease", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 32, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7076ad58-2837-4a04-94c0-4aea1af45b39", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The European Medicines Agency has waived the obligation to submit the results of studies with Jardiance in all subsets of the paediatric population in heart failure and in the treatment of chronic kidney disease (see section 4.2 for information on paediatric use).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2dba8a8b-2e01-4a51-90b3-a447400441f6"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e5dd357a-e029-47fe-9df1-036cbe90a6e3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "5.2 Pharmacokinetic properties", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 32, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e5dd357a-e029-47fe-9df1-036cbe90a6e3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:35bff488-6193-49e5-9236-a8f0c4f85810", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "18. UNIQUE IDENTIFIER - HUMAN READABLE DATA", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 43, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "35bff488-6193-49e5-9236-a8f0c4f85810", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "PC SN\n\nNN", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:407c6414-77c8-4db5-a550-b0875026c92f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:5edb5648-28e0-49db-9d52-3eee1980467c", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Reporting of side effects", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 54, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "5edb5648-28e0-49db-9d52-3eee1980467c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "If you get any side effects, talk to your doctor, pharmacist or nurse. This includes any possible side effects not listed in this leaflet. You can also report side effects directly via the national reporting system listed in Appendix V. By reporting side effects you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1bccf6ad-ad8a-4794-b611-51af8311baf3"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d8cc1458-ee0a-441e-901d-255bd44cb239", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Latvija", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 57, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d8cc1458-ee0a-441e-901d-255bd44cb239", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim RCV GmbH &amp; Co KG Latvijas filiāle\n\nTel: +371 67 240 011", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f0bd0640-08be-402e-8bb5-25f25d7f7a77"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:f49aaa9f-a235-41d0-a04a-6c166164036b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "This leaflet was last revised in { MM/YYYY } .", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 57, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "f49aaa9f-a235-41d0-a04a-6c166164036b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Detailed information on this medicine is available on the European Medicines Agency web site: https://www.ema.europa.eu.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5eefcda2-bd7a-4626-99ac-363be01f822c"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:838f85ec-c0f0-4676-aec7-17a3ae0762d3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Read all of this leaflet carefully before you start taking this medicine because it contains important information for you.", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "838f85ec-c0f0-4676-aec7-17a3ae0762d3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "- -Keep this leaflet. You may need to read it again.\n- -If you have any further questions, ask your doctor, pharmacist or nurse.\n- -This medicine has been prescribed for you only. Do not pass it on to others. It may harm them, even if their signs of illness are the same as yours.\n- -If you get any side effects, talk to your doctor, pharmacist or nurse. This includes any possible side effects not listed in this leaflet. See section 4.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:038c2086-a3a9-4cb4-9161-1dcad61dbffd"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:259a2982-73e6-4922-b7e3-25c7cdc0df45", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "What is in this leaflet", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "259a2982-73e6-4922-b7e3-25c7cdc0df45", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "1. What Jardiance is and what it is used for\n2. What you need to know before you take Jardiance\n3. How to take Jardiance\n4. Possible side effects\n5. How to store Jardiance\n6. Contents of the pack and other information", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:69d751e6-a543-4592-8fb0-53a40a42c129"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:801c2cb3-8f81-4b5d-8f75-99b66a1ebaa9", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "1. What Jardiance is and what it is used for", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "801c2cb3-8f81-4b5d-8f75-99b66a1ebaa9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2beaba5a-54f8-4e07-82f8-61f70852fe79", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "What Jardiance is", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2beaba5a-54f8-4e07-82f8-61f70852fe79", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance contains the active substance empagliflozin.\n\nJardiance is a member of a group of medicines called sodium glucose co-transporter-2 (SGLT2) inhibitors.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b44529fa-6792-4e2b-aa85-dd239b16ba07"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ba43c7dd-2b90-4f0c-8540-202777228484", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "What Jardiance is used for", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "ba43c7dd-2b90-4f0c-8540-202777228484", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2b1e0419-e56e-4c18-93be-ca7821470263", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 44, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2b1e0419-e56e-4c18-93be-ca7821470263", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "| MINIMUM PARTICULARS TO APPEAR ON BLISTERS OR STRIPS   |\n|-------------------------------------------------------|\n| Blisters (perforated)                                 |\n\n| 1.   | NAME OF THE MEDICINAL PRODUCT   |\n|------|---------------------------------|\n\nJardiance 10 mg tablets empagliflozin\n\n| 2.   | NAME OF THE MARKETING AUTHORISATION HOLDER   |\n|------|----------------------------------------------|\n\nBoehringer Ingelheim\n\n| 3.   | EXPIRY DATE   |\n|------|---------------|\n\nEXP\n\n| 4.   | BATCH NUMBER   |\n|------|----------------|\n\nLot\n\n| 5.   | OTHER   |\n|------|---------|\n\n44", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3bb23899-4acc-4b05-8f1e-3776f2a6b805"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ece1929a-c73b-4ae7-bf42-7c97f9b28cb7", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "PARTICULARS TO APPEAR ON THE OUTER PACKAGING", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "ece1929a-c73b-4ae7-bf42-7c97f9b28cb7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "OUTER CARTON", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c467a889-8d72-4032-8b31-def01f02b860"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:bbc27328-2672-4863-9c7d-127cc97fec4b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "1. NAME OF THE MEDICINAL PRODUCT", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "bbc27328-2672-4863-9c7d-127cc97fec4b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance 25 mg film-coated tablets empagliflozin", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4a1fe6a1-a005-4f87-b6cb-9fa37b051eec"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:5e0cc525-b5cd-43e6-97ee-e9cb1c2a43dd", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "2. STATEMENT OF ACTIVE SUBSTANCE(S)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "5e0cc525-b5cd-43e6-97ee-e9cb1c2a43dd", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains 25 mg of empagliflozin.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e01de776-4fc6-4619-b3da-499b947306ee"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e6786c51-e95e-43d9-b9eb-b467bc7b8cd2", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "3. LIST OF EXCIPIENTS", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e6786c51-e95e-43d9-b9eb-b467bc7b8cd2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Contains lactose, see leaflet for further information.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:37822a66-074d-4e6a-84b7-1b9b67aeea25"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:88c14440-5b32-4630-aa58-599e3ce332a0", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM AND CONTENTS", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "88c14440-5b32-4630-aa58-599e3ce332a0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "- 7 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 10 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 14 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 28 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 30 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 60 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 70 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 90 × 1 film-coated tablets\n- 100 × 1 film-coated tablets", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b9736b45-e00f-4462-ad95-42985e04dfc3"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:befb0c3e-d94a-4e34-b426-f216f1cd3ed1", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "5. METHOD AND ROUTE(S) OF ADMINISTRATION", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "befb0c3e-d94a-4e34-b426-f216f1cd3ed1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Read the package leaflet before use.\n\nOral use", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:924cdbf4-fd05-44fb-a25b-e82242b862d3"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b3ea050a-4f8d-435f-b110-3d17c42a4ad8", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "6. SPECIAL WARNING THAT THE MEDICINAL PRODUCT MUST BE STORED OUT OF THE SIGHT AND REACH OF CHILDREN", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b3ea050a-4f8d-435f-b110-3d17c42a4ad8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Keep out of the sight and reach of children.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:47e8af6b-9a46-421b-89d5-76ba3ab964e1"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:393a3b82-8489-4a79-9a41-d381607b4744", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "7. OTHER SPECIAL WARNING(S), IF NECESSARY", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "393a3b82-8489-4a79-9a41-d381607b4744", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:90391b16-eb61-4c0e-879c-df11749bc69d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "8. EXPIRY DATE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 45, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "90391b16-eb61-4c0e-879c-df11749bc69d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "EXP", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3e05e5ac-97d6-4d4d-9850-4e906ac12516"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ddb548cf-1fa0-46f7-bc38-55621daf65cc", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "9. SPECIAL STORAGE CONDITIONS", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "ddb548cf-1fa0-46f7-bc38-55621daf65cc", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "10. SPECIAL PRECAUTIONS FOR DISPOSAL OF UNUSED MEDICINAL PRODUCTS OR WASTE MATERIALS DERIVED FROM SUCH MEDICINAL PRODUCTS, IF APPROPRIATE", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:12c1eaa5-bd60-417b-b0a6-c9d11da31978"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:458593fd-a438-4cf2-bb8e-cbc3bebf8398", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "11. NAME AND ADDRESS OF THE MARKETING AUTHORISATION HOLDER", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "458593fd-a438-4cf2-bb8e-cbc3bebf8398", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim International GmbH 55216 Ingelheim am Rhein Germany", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:445d7ba8-6f1c-4f76-8787-b093057e7219"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:85616154-431b-4370-9a5c-5ea035dddcd3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "12. MARKETING AUTHORISATION NUMBER(S)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "85616154-431b-4370-9a5c-5ea035dddcd3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "EU/1/14/930/001 7 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/002 10 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/003 14 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/004 28 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/005 30 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/006 60 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/007 70 × 1 tablets EU/1/14/930/008 90 × 1 tablets\n\nEU/1/14/930/009 100 × 1 tablets", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cedd85f0-7d51-45bc-a496-6d09ccf06219"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:f422573b-c6bf-42a9-a9ad-f77302fd021d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "13. BATCH NUMBER", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "f422573b-c6bf-42a9-a9ad-f77302fd021d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Lot", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f868d10f-523b-462d-a490-fb615dbaaa61"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:0d4b9607-4b51-4178-a24a-bcc42b67da47", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "14. GENERAL CLASSIFICATION FOR SUPPLY", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "0d4b9607-4b51-4178-a24a-bcc42b67da47", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:0d10b2a9-f7ef-4de8-bf42-6bf865405014", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "15. INSTRUCTIONS ON USE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "0d10b2a9-f7ef-4de8-bf42-6bf865405014", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:0a2c2cb9-4ae0-466a-baed-4e0c5069af50", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "16. INFORMATION IN BRAILLE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "0a2c2cb9-4ae0-466a-baed-4e0c5069af50", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance 25 mg", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:225ee088-9f62-4214-807f-30de38f08a73"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7a8abc09-7c40-45e0-8ad5-f5972fe08693", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "17. UNIQUE IDENTIFIER - 2D BARCODE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7a8abc09-7c40-45e0-8ad5-f5972fe08693", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "2D barcode carrying the unique identifier included.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:67748e31-883d-447d-8ee5-6214bcc0693a"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:acc6f28f-1d59-421c-92f8-e768575923fd", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "18. UNIQUE IDENTIFIER - HUMAN READABLE DATA", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 46, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "acc6f28f-1d59-421c-92f8-e768575923fd", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "PC SN\n\nNN", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5945c185-db97-4c37-8b02-4badbf5bbaab"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:896838db-bc61-4771-8c23-6d9be8641d3d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Urinary tract infection, seen commonly (may affect up to 1 in 10 people)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 53, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "896838db-bc61-4771-8c23-6d9be8641d3d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The signs of urinary tract infection are:\n\n- burning sensation when passing urine\n- urine that appears cloudy\n- pain in the pelvis, or mid-back pain (when kidneys are infected)\n\nAn urge to pass urine or more frequent urination may be due to the way Jardiance works, but they can also be signs of urinary tract infection. If you note an increase in such symptoms, you should also contact your doctor.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9de9d737-ae29-49d8-8452-a777ee2b9f3f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:fafeb608-3e0c-4e1f-9850-ebd9bad6f2b5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 47, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "fafeb608-3e0c-4e1f-9850-ebd9bad6f2b5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "| MINIMUM PARTICULARS TO APPEAR ON BLISTERS OR STRIPS   |\n|-------------------------------------------------------|\n| Blisters (perforated)                                 |\n\n| 1.   | NAME OF THE MEDICINAL PRODUCT   |\n|------|---------------------------------|\n\nJardiance 25 mg tablets empagliflozin\n\n| 2.   | NAME OF THE MARKETING AUTHORISATION HOLDER   |\n|------|----------------------------------------------|\n\nBoehringer Ingelheim\n\n| 3.   | EXPIRY DATE   |\n|------|---------------|\n\nEXP\n\n| 4.   | BATCH NUMBER   |\n|------|----------------|\n\nLot\n\n| 5.   | OTHER   |\n|------|---------|\n\n47", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8f4d7064-de4f-4f45-8f11-1be0c7d182ec"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:de2b0f85-0b5c-4b61-984e-7f26e2c2a27e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "B. PACKAGE LEAFLET", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 48, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "de2b0f85-0b5c-4b61-984e-7f26e2c2a27e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3ea75281-99cd-4b86-95e9-c60fa4ddff81", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Package leaflet: Information for the patient", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "3ea75281-99cd-4b86-95e9-c60fa4ddff81", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:15d9e924-6587-4919-ab48-cbb09b9bbea8", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Jardiance 10 mg film-coated tablets Jardiance 25 mg film-coated tablets", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 49, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "15d9e924-6587-4919-ab48-cbb09b9bbea8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "empagliflozin", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c04368ce-a2dc-4330-b1bb-c83cee001aae"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:33d4c4e1-c7f5-41af-994f-f01e1ca1e609", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Suomi/Finland", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 57, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "33d4c4e1-c7f5-41af-994f-f01e1ca1e609", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim Finland Ky Puh/Tel: +358 10 3102 800", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ef9468f6-18e3-4540-94d4-18f40af26f16"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ce712b53-95b3-47f9-9976-287cd8cd0e03", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Sverige", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 57, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "ce712b53-95b3-47f9-9976-287cd8cd0e03", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim AB\n\nTel: +46 8 721 21 00", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ac10dca7-1675-4d0a-9185-e112fb25ee93"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:07c6cd0c-8842-459f-b919-2413aafe6359", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Dehydration, seen very commonly (may affect more than 1 in 10 people)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 53, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "07c6cd0c-8842-459f-b919-2413aafe6359", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The signs of dehydration are not specific, but may include:\n\n- unusual thirst\n- lightheadedness or dizziness upon standing\n- fainting or loss of consciousness", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e4cedce2-9017-49ef-9055-4a54433ee98a"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2f6b0a4e-e178-4642-a9ed-fd659f97f3ba", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Hypoglycaemia", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2f6b0a4e-e178-4642-a9ed-fd659f97f3ba", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The frequency of hypoglycaemia depended on the background therapy in the respective studies and was similar for empagliflozin and placebo as monotherapy, add-on to metformin, add-on to pioglitazone with or without metformin, as add-on to linagliptin and metformin, and as adjunct to standard care therapy and for the combination of empagliflozin with metformin in drug-naïve patients compared to those treated with empagliflozin and metformin as individual components. An increased frequency was noted when given as add-on to metformin and a sulphonylurea (empagliflozin 10 mg: 16.1%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 11.5%, placebo: 8.4%), add-on to basal insulin with or without metformin and with or without a sulphonylurea (empagliflozin 10 mg: 19.5%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 28.4%, placebo: 20.6% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg: 36.1%, placebo 35.3% over the 78-week trial), and add-on to MDI insulin with or without metformin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 39.8%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 41.3%, placebo: 37.2% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg: 51.1%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 57.7%, placebo: 58% over the 52-week trial).\n\nIn the EMPEROR heart failure studies, similar frequency of hypoglycaemia was noted when used addon to sulphonylurea or insulin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 6.5%, placebo: 6.7%).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ab9f5e3d-7667-4060-9884-b8ae948f7bc5"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:99b19e85-0e1c-47c0-8ebd-2c4bb47a3332"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:73635b7c-201c-46a8-b5ec-fc01d7db4d2d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Other side effects while taking Jardiance:", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 54, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "73635b7c-201c-46a8-b5ec-fc01d7db4d2d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:3089470f-9d4f-4eee-b7c3-c19414db4b2c", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "ANNEX I", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "3089470f-9d4f-4eee-b7c3-c19414db4b2c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7c8a9094-1048-4d00-a039-940e371e55d5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "SUMMARY OF PRODUCT CHARACTERISTICS", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 1, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7c8a9094-1048-4d00-a039-940e371e55d5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:19f44440-fcc3-4a75-8e22-4b3e40bc492d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "1. NAME OF THE MEDICINAL PRODUCT", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "19f44440-fcc3-4a75-8e22-4b3e40bc492d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance 10 mg film-coated tablets Jardiance 25 mg film-coated tablets", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:fb9fd28a-a780-4b32-a496-ce5b6b7c0151"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:90bd8fae-26e2-4a70-a698-c08c6d35b1c3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "2. QUALITATIVE AND QUANTITATIVE COMPOSITION", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "90bd8fae-26e2-4a70-a698-c08c6d35b1c3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:72043664-d5b7-4ed9-8e8a-39ffb1cf44e7", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Jardiance 10 mg film-coated tablets", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "72043664-d5b7-4ed9-8e8a-39ffb1cf44e7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains 10 mg empagliflozin.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b6c5da61-e7e4-4b4e-878f-3e2bb0a9070b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7be759b0-c4fa-439c-a15e-c495d012756f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Excipients with known effect", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7be759b0-c4fa-439c-a15e-c495d012756f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains lactose monohydrate equivalent to 154.3 mg lactose anhydrous.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:54b22f3e-f9ac-4b0c-b695-83974ae09f56"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6e8e9f19-0b50-42ea-9fd5-15a3af72ac59", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Jardiance 25 mg film-coated tablets", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6e8e9f19-0b50-42ea-9fd5-15a3af72ac59", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains 25 mg empagliflozin.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:79f1e5e1-8bf8-44ca-9224-ad125db0acd4"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:74cea541-8458-48ca-8d92-587141b0c022", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Excipients with known effect", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "74cea541-8458-48ca-8d92-587141b0c022", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains lactose monohydrate equivalent to 107.4 mg lactose anhydrous.\n\nFor the full list of excipients, see section 6.1.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4c7cbaa0-65ef-49d2-a7a8-4401bc3fdefc"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:ccf52c08-9cc3-4ba6-97eb-27dc4abe7bde", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "ccf52c08-9cc3-4ba6-97eb-27dc4abe7bde", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Film-coated tablet (tablet).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:d7d6fe06-c383-478b-b5f4-cca2784cb05e"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7561f639-7882-454b-b411-23c90ede7334", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Jardiance 10 mg film-coated tablets", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7561f639-7882-454b-b411-23c90ede7334", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Round, pale yellow, biconvex, bevel-edged film-coated tablet debossed with 'S10' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim logo on the other (tablet diameter: 9.1 mm).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:efb7f3d5-ac39-4ba2-b3ce-8148499c7a9b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:992b6b63-1c8e-47a7-a308-aee1fa43582d", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Jardiance 25 mg film-coated tablets", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "992b6b63-1c8e-47a7-a308-aee1fa43582d", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Oval, pale yellow, biconvex film-coated tablet debossed with 'S25' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim logo on the other (tablet length: 11.1 mm, tablet width: 5.6 mm).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0be4ecf1-2428-4f6b-9465-a9c8a281f348"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2824ee35-3b1d-4792-964f-a58c8c8bbaa4", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2824ee35-3b1d-4792-964f-a58c8c8bbaa4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b8c312fb-18d3-4b42-9a88-06355658f720", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.1 Therapeutic indications", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b8c312fb-18d3-4b42-9a88-06355658f720", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:37fabc6d-48b2-45a0-9a39-7d25dd312d9f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "37fabc6d-48b2-45a0-9a39-7d25dd312d9f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance is indicated in adults and children aged 10 years and above for the treatment of insufficiently controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise\n\n- -as monotherapy when metformin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance\n- -in addition to other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes\n\nFor study results with respect to combination of therapies, effects on glycaemic control, cardiovascular and renal events, and the populations studied, see sections 4.4, 4.5 and 5.1.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c569da66-fa97-4972-b9c6-a9776deb6003"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:916d3dd8-0293-4e83-a95d-5d42266303f7", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Heart failure", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 2, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "916d3dd8-0293-4e83-a95d-5d42266303f7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance is indicated in adults for the treatment of symptomatic chronic heart failure.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f01f4ec7-a62a-4339-ad04-0b9e17e28cb5"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:edf8c677-dbdf-4d72-a9f0-142c0ed443c5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Chronic kidney disease", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "edf8c677-dbdf-4d72-a9f0-142c0ed443c5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Jardiance is indicated in adults for the treatment of chronic kidney disease.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:82561521-65e1-45e6-8a4f-d8de4f67acea"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:93d8a775-9a92-4470-a919-6a3968e676f1", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.2 Posology and method of administration", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "93d8a775-9a92-4470-a919-6a3968e676f1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:17a62dc7-6880-44b9-bb60-2e75ce412461", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Posology", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "17a62dc7-6880-44b9-bb60-2e75ce412461", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6255a9e3-f098-4b96-9800-27a1d1f3afb3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6255a9e3-f098-4b96-9800-27a1d1f3afb3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The recommended starting dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily for monotherapy and add-on combination therapy with other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes. In patients tolerating empagliflozin 10 mg once daily who have an eGFR ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and need tighter glycaemic control, the dose can be increased to 25 mg once daily. The maximum daily dose is 25 mg (see below and section 4.4).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:419da043-5237-466a-9d3a-d3a7b40c0e07"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2dd90f41-cf84-43aa-83c1-268af0ba8aa9", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Heart failure", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2dd90f41-cf84-43aa-83c1-268af0ba8aa9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The recommended dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:24f49401-d3c7-494b-be3a-61f6c13bcac7"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b9f3eb9a-be8b-4f96-8f20-210ffeeee15a", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Chronic kidney disease", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b9f3eb9a-be8b-4f96-8f20-210ffeeee15a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The recommended dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:64c92c0a-eed1-44ae-932f-a6610959ddcc"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:8cc6c1c4-80dc-49ed-b160-634d92f0d22e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "All indications", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "8cc6c1c4-80dc-49ed-b160-634d92f0d22e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "When empagliflozin is used in combination with a sulphonylurea or with insulin, a lower dose of the sulphonylurea or insulin may be considered to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia (see sections 4.5 and 4.8).\n\nIf a dose is missed, it should be taken as soon as the patient remembers; however, a double dose should not be taken on the same day.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:09805519-5f1e-4f42-b05e-23e264152436"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:93e251f3-c73e-4e5d-a924-a72a680b13db", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Special populations", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "93e251f3-c73e-4e5d-a924-a72a680b13db", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6ff36a3a-d2f6-48b1-812d-240c5ca947ab", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Renal impairment", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6ff36a3a-d2f6-48b1-812d-240c5ca947ab", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Due to limited experience, it is not recommended to initiate treatment with empagliflozin in patients with an eGFR &lt; 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .\n\nIn patients with an eGFR &lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 the daily dose of empagliflozin is 10 mg.\n\nIn patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, the glucose lowering efficacy of empagliflozin is reduced in patients with an eGFR &lt; 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and likely absent in patients with an eGFR &lt; 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . Therefore, if eGFR falls below 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , additional glucose lowering treatment should be considered if needed (see sections 4.4, 4.8, 5.1 and 5.2).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:65e6ce38-33bf-4887-8184-e1d3a60dc02c"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4bec51e7-0d92-43f3-a4a8-8188f3276c3f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Hepatic impairment", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4bec51e7-0d92-43f3-a4a8-8188f3276c3f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "No dose adjustment is required for patients with hepatic impairment. Empagliflozin exposure is increased in patients with severe hepatic impairment. Therapeutic experience in patients with severe hepatic impairment is limited and therefore not recommended for use in this population (see section 5.2).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:55add26d-ef6a-42cd-9d55-e4214ba976af"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:974f594b-d029-4008-9b2c-524455fde10f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Elderly", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "974f594b-d029-4008-9b2c-524455fde10f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "No dose adjustment is recommended based on age. In patients 75 years and older, an increased risk for volume depletion should be taken into account (see sections 4.4 and 4.8).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2b8d61dc-ce25-4204-87fc-4df7cea2338b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b0c0a9ca-1f49-4fb1-ba69-09b754e34493", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Paediatric population", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 3, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b0c0a9ca-1f49-4fb1-ba69-09b754e34493", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The recommended starting dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily. In patients tolerating empagliflozin 10 mg once daily and requiring additional glycaemic control, the dose can be increased to 25 mg once daily (see sections 5.1 and 5.2). No data are available for children with eGFR &lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and children below 10 years of age.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:84552a19-30f2-4233-9dff-d5b3744ce135"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b325c700-365c-4b74-9351-65100b30929a", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b325c700-365c-4b74-9351-65100b30929a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The safety and efficacy of empagliflozin for the treatment of heart failure or for the treatment of chronic kidney disease in children under 18 years of age have not been established. No data are available.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:fc704807-2fbc-44b6-abd2-3f849f9fe01f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:37017a54-58ee-4218-bc2f-8d85988565e8", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Method of administration", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "37017a54-58ee-4218-bc2f-8d85988565e8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The tablets can be taken with or without food, swallowed whole with water.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b153b93e-8521-4516-a546-2f7a966fb62c"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:5655cbfa-9679-42c6-893b-4f48369d1bd5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.3 Contraindications", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "5655cbfa-9679-42c6-893b-4f48369d1bd5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients listed in section 6.1.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e9de16bf-ca1f-461a-8a35-5c3fee9b7fce"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4409b123-117a-48d4-975c-378f436de1ff", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.4 Special warnings and precautions for use", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4409b123-117a-48d4-975c-378f436de1ff", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:dff5d609-8387-412f-adb6-6b2ee91fbe2f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "General", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "dff5d609-8387-412f-adb6-6b2ee91fbe2f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus (see 'Ketoacidosis' in section 4.4).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:724bb5c2-64f5-4c48-b8a1-a102e4eff432"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6b6e7cbf-c89e-484c-b82c-de150615604e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Ketoacidosis", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 4, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6b6e7cbf-c89e-484c-b82c-de150615604e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Cases of ketoacidosis, including life-threatening and fatal cases, have been reported in patients with diabetes mellitus treated with SGLT2 inhibitors, including empagliflozin. In a number of cases, the presentation of the condition was atypical with only moderately increased blood glucose values, below 14 mmol/L (250 mg/dL). It is not known if ketoacidosis is more likely to occur with higher doses of empagliflozin. Although ketoacidosis is less likely to occur in patients without diabetes mellitus, cases have also been reported in these patients.\n\nThe risk of ketoacidosis must be considered in the event of non-specific symptoms such as nausea, vomiting, anorexia, abdominal pain, excessive thirst, difficulty breathing, confusion, unusual fatigue or sleepiness. Patients should be assessed for ketoacidosis immediately if these symptoms occur, regardless of blood glucose level.\n\nIn patients where ketoacidosis is suspected or diagnosed, treatment with empagliflozin should be discontinued immediately.\n\nTreatment should be interrupted in patients who are hospitalised for major surgical procedures or acute serious medical illnesses. Monitoring of ketones is recommended in these patients. Measurement of blood ketone levels is preferred to urine. Treatment with empagliflozin may be restarted when the ketone values are normal and the patient's condition has stabilised.\n\nBefore initiating empagliflozin, factors in the patient history that may predispose to ketoacidosis should be considered.\n\nProlonged ketoacidosis and prolonged glucosuria have been observed with empagliflozin. Ketoacidosis may last longer after discontinuation of empagliflozin than expected from the plasma half-life (see section 5.2). Empagliflozin-independent factors, such as insulin deficiency, might be involved in prolonged periods of ketoacidosis.\n\nPatients who may be at higher risk of ketoacidosis include patients with a low beta-cell function reserve (e.g. type 2 diabetes patients with low C-peptide or latent autoimmune diabetes in adults (LADA) or patients with a history of pancreatitis), patients with conditions that lead to restricted food intake or severe dehydration, patients for whom insulin doses are reduced and patients with increased insulin requirements due to acute medical illness, surgery or alcohol abuse. SGLT2 inhibitors should be used with caution in these patients.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e64015b5-7cbb-47c1-a1ff-01b7c0d0102d"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3db17c21-92fb-4b19-852a-0f58fded81b0"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f20b0465-2f79-4044-bed9-e22153ecfe5e"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:60a8b15c-9c71-4687-9f8c-b515fc74a374", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "60a8b15c-9c71-4687-9f8c-b515fc74a374", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Restarting SGLT2 inhibitor treatment in patients with previous ketoacidosis while on SGLT2 inhibitor treatment is not recommended, unless another clear precipitating factor is identified and resolved.\n\nJardiance should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes. Data from a clinical trial program in patients with type 1 diabetes showed increased ketoacidosis occurrence with common frequency in patients treated with empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg as an adjunct to insulin compared to placebo.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ec769265-ac42-4258-a75e-a09546d34fbe"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:9a7a5961-1e81-4f2f-8886-ceccb3a44061", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Renal impairment", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "9a7a5961-1e81-4f2f-8886-ceccb3a44061", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Due to limited experience, it is not recommended to initiate treatment with empagliflozin in patients with an eGFR &lt; 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .\n\nIn patients with an eGFR &lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 the daily dose of empagliflozin is 10 mg (see section 4.2).\n\nThe glucose lowering efficacy of empagliflozin is dependent on renal function, and is reduced in patients with an eGFR &lt; 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and is likely absent in patients with an eGFR &lt; 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2  (see section 4.2, 5.1 and 5.2).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ea0884bc-6c50-4e0b-8972-b83cefb40e5b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b0a2edfb-2315-4618-b86d-09b5ed86d2c6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Monitoring of renal function", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b0a2edfb-2315-4618-b86d-09b5ed86d2c6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Assessment of renal function is recommended as follows:\n\n- -Prior to empagliflozin initiation and periodically during treatment, i.e. at least yearly (see sections 4.2, 4.8, 5.1 and 5.2).\n- -Prior to initiation of any concomitant medicinal product that may have a negative impact on renal function.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:706eaa4c-937b-42c6-afa5-a13737a69019"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4586acf2-883e-4de4-b333-63abd53adec3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Risk for volume depletion", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4586acf2-883e-4de4-b333-63abd53adec3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Based on the mode of action of SGLT2 inhibitors, osmotic diuresis accompanying glucosuria may lead to a modest decrease in blood pressure (see section 5.1). Therefore, caution should be exercised in patients for whom an empagliflozin-induced drop in blood pressure could pose a risk, such as patients with known cardiovascular disease, patients on anti-hypertensive therapy with a history of hypotension or patients aged 75 years and older.\n\nIn case of conditions that may lead to fluid loss (e.g. gastrointestinal illness), careful monitoring of volume status (e.g. physical examination, blood pressure measurements, laboratory tests including haematocrit) and electrolytes is recommended for patients receiving empagliflozin. Temporary interruption of treatment with empagliflozin should be considered until the fluid loss is corrected.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:210bca7f-6468-43cb-95cd-c413b5806ccb"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:475e338e-bf52-4973-aa24-ff7b4f8be0a6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Elderly", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "475e338e-bf52-4973-aa24-ff7b4f8be0a6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The effect of empagliflozin on urinary glucose excretion is associated with osmotic diuresis, which could affect the hydration status. Patients aged 75 years and older may be at an increased risk of volume depletion. A higher number of these patients treated with empagliflozin had adverse reactions related to volume depletion as compared to placebo (see section 4.8). Therefore, special attention should be given to their volume intake in case of co-administered medicinal products which may lead to volume depletion (e.g. diuretics, ACE inhibitors).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ee0a53e3-2106-4010-aa7a-ac68d63a003c"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:7e20fc68-1213-476f-b61f-bdcd7057e1d2", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Complicated urinary tract infections", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 5, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "7e20fc68-1213-476f-b61f-bdcd7057e1d2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Cases of complicated urinary tract infections including pyelonephritis and urosepsis have been reported in patients treated with empagliflozin (see section 4.8). Temporary interruption of empagliflozin should be considered in patients with complicated urinary tract infections.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1117bd18-288c-4f1e-9dbb-10cb65211614"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d7aa5df9-51be-4cc9-8074-350839411d7e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Necrotising fasciitis of the perineum (Fournier's gangrene)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d7aa5df9-51be-4cc9-8074-350839411d7e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Cases of necrotising fasciitis of the perineum, (also known as Fournier's gangrene), have been reported in female and male patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors, including empagliflozin. This is a rare but serious and potentially life-threatening event that requires urgent surgical intervention and antibiotic treatment.\n\nPatients should be advised to seek medical attention if they experience a combination of symptoms of pain, tenderness, erythema, or swelling in the genital or perineal area, with fever or malaise. Be aware that either uro-genital infection or perineal abscess may precede necrotising fasciitis. If Fournier´s gangrene is suspected, Jardiance should be discontinued and prompt treatment (including antibiotics and surgical debridement) should be instituted.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a239be01-78cb-4ee1-a69e-00bf85412e9d"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e623f3a3-e582-4c07-bdb5-383b763c7849", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.9 Overdose", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e623f3a3-e582-4c07-bdb5-383b763c7849", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:5556d121-5d2f-42f5-b6cb-3847d4b3223a", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Lower limb amputations", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "5556d121-5d2f-42f5-b6cb-3847d4b3223a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "An increase in cases of lower limb amputation (primarily of the toe) has been observed in long-term clinical studies with another SGLT2 inhibitor. It is unknown whether this constitutes a class effect. Like for all diabetic patients it is important to counsel patients on routine preventative foot-care.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a5383fb1-0777-4de0-80e7-d55488aa06b1"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:8e7aa7a7-a2fc-4f07-bc81-4bc7d82f836f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Hepatic injury", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "8e7aa7a7-a2fc-4f07-bc81-4bc7d82f836f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Cases of hepatic injury have been reported with empagliflozin in clinical trials. A causal relationship between empagliflozin and hepatic injury has not been established.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2fa17cee-f4b2-474c-a65d-aaad1e9562d0"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:8d5b8aa6-3e6a-4322-9090-a3afe8d4122a", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Elevated haematocrit", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "8d5b8aa6-3e6a-4322-9090-a3afe8d4122a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Haematocrit increase was observed with empagliflozin treatment (see section 4.8). Patients with pronounced elevations in haematocrit should be monitored and investigated for underlying haematological disease.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:88d74940-6f28-41a1-bd62-6d4265d2fc7d"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:9fbfe13b-d7e9-47c8-b364-22200e5553b5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Chronic kidney disease", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "9fbfe13b-d7e9-47c8-b364-22200e5553b5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Patients with albuminuria may benefit more from treatment with empagliflozin.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5d383eef-d990-47ea-ad53-a18d9aabda16"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e4c9d7e4-676c-4ba6-bd7a-a90f0344acc1", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Infiltrative disease or Takotsubo cardiomyopathy", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e4c9d7e4-676c-4ba6-bd7a-a90f0344acc1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Patients with infiltrative disease or with Takotsubo cardiomyopathy have not been specifically studied. Therefore, efficacy in these patients has not been established.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:79fd6a68-a8fa-4005-ad59-e4b82e14bbca"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:0b339ebd-6013-461d-a133-bd7675c8493b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Urine laboratory assessments", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "0b339ebd-6013-461d-a133-bd7675c8493b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Due to its mechanism of action, patients taking Jardiance will test positive for glucose in their urine.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a1120350-3bb9-4b2a-bc9a-15e0c800b349"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:77d73b63-98f8-4f3b-b9ad-840ab3692dc6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Interference with 1,5-anhydroglucitol (1,5-AG) assay", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "77d73b63-98f8-4f3b-b9ad-840ab3692dc6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Monitoring glycaemic control with 1,5-AG assay is not recommended as measurements of 1,5-AG are unreliable in assessing glycaemic control in patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors. Use of alternative methods to monitor glycaemic control is advised.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cbc00ef9-b6da-4e9a-b83e-8b6201817834"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:74ddfc00-f218-4899-bfc5-81fa0c1e64da", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Lactose", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "74ddfc00-f218-4899-bfc5-81fa0c1e64da", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The tablets contain lactose. Patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medicinal product.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f361aba0-8837-4c34-8557-f711b93faeb6"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d26fc014-0c55-4945-b1cc-c866c2258dc3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Sodium", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 6, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d26fc014-0c55-4945-b1cc-c866c2258dc3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Each tablet contains less than 1 mmol sodium (23 mg), that is to say essentially 'sodium free'.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:07bf460e-91f0-453a-b247-b84cd724b500"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:678b0bd7-8669-4ae5-bf44-a37a85fedf3e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "4.5 Interaction with other medicinal products and other forms of interaction", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "678b0bd7-8669-4ae5-bf44-a37a85fedf3e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:979dfd35-ddd0-460f-a004-36045a8c4e8e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Pharmacodynamic interactions", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "979dfd35-ddd0-460f-a004-36045a8c4e8e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:b9908a1a-c9e1-4cfc-ad05-9bd4f2b282f3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Diuretics", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "b9908a1a-c9e1-4cfc-ad05-9bd4f2b282f3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin may add to the diuretic effect of thiazide and loop diuretics and may increase the risk of dehydration and hypotension (see section 4.4).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:106da502-2fb9-4c91-8a1b-7bfbe5bef5ea"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e0799d46-0074-47d9-b4db-2580f1a1d3ff", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Insulin and insulin secretagogues", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e0799d46-0074-47d9-b4db-2580f1a1d3ff", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Insulin and insulin secretagogues, such as sulphonylureas, may increase the risk of hypoglycaemia. Therefore, a lower dose of insulin or an insulin secretagogue may be required to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia when used in combination with empagliflozin (see sections 4.2 and 4.8).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:acbf3404-2548-4e71-806a-1b73f6a7cef3"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:8dab208a-f8a2-47b5-bb65-db75a1933883", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Pharmacokinetic interactions", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "8dab208a-f8a2-47b5-bb65-db75a1933883", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:f92f4b0d-f96a-4cd5-9830-ecd27c66c021", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Effects of other medicinal products on empagliflozin", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "f92f4b0d-f96a-4cd5-9830-ecd27c66c021", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In vitro data suggest that the primary route of metabolism of empagliflozin in humans is glucuronidation by uridine 5'-diphosphoglucuronosyltransferases UGT1A3, UGT1A8, UGT1A9, and UGT2B7. Empagliflozin is a substrate of the human uptake transporters OAT3, OATP1B1, and OATP1B3, but not OAT1 and OCT2. Empagliflozin is a substrate of P-glycoprotein (P-gp) and breast cancer resistance protein (BCRP).\n\nCo-administration of empagliflozin with probenecid, an inhibitor of UGT enzymes and OAT3, resulted in a 26% increase in peak empagliflozin plasma concentrations (Cmax) and a 53% increase in area under the concentration-time curve (AUC). These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.\n\nThe effect of UGT induction (e.g. induction by rifampicin or phenytoin) on empagliflozin has not been studied. Co-treatment with known inducers of UGT enzymes is not recommended due to a potential risk of decreased efficacy. If an inducer of these UGT enzymes must be co-administered, monitoring of glycaemic control to assess response to Jardiance is appropriate.\n\nAn interaction study with gemfibrozil, an in vitro inhibitor of OAT3 and OATP1B1/1B3 transporters, showed that empagliflozin Cmax increased by 15% and AUC increased by 59% following coadministration. These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.\n\nInhibition of OATP1B1/1B3 transporters by co-administration with rifampicin resulted in a 75% increase in Cmax and a 35% increase in AUC of empagliflozin. These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.\n\nEmpagliflozin exposure was similar with and without co-administration with verapamil, a P-gp inhibitor, indicating that inhibition of P-gp does not have any clinically relevant effect on empagliflozin.\n\nInteraction studies suggest that the pharmacokinetics of empagliflozin were not influenced by coadministration with metformin, glimepiride, pioglitazone, sitagliptin, linagliptin, warfarin, verapamil, ramipril, simvastatin, torasemide and hydrochlorothiazide.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ff427777-0463-4683-9c7e-2a1b0b8fb47c"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4ad325b7-71ff-4416-9ab7-e42f23add2da"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4108c328-e013-4b32-8dd6-9c87d990eeb6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Effects of empagliflozin on other medicinal products", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4108c328-e013-4b32-8dd6-9c87d990eeb6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin may increase renal lithium excretion and the blood lithium levels may be decreased. Serum concentration of lithium should be monitored more frequently after empagliflozin initiation and dose changes. Please refer the patient to the lithium prescribing doctor in order to monitor serum concentration of lithium.\n\nBased on in vitro studies, empagliflozin does not inhibit, inactivate, or induce CYP450 isoforms. Empagliflozin does not inhibit UGT1A1, UGT1A3, UGT1A8, UGT1A9, or UGT2B7. Drug-drug interactions involving the major CYP450 and UGT isoforms with empagliflozin and concomitantly administered substrates of these enzymes are therefore considered unlikely.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8ef5f428-bb1a-4376-bdfd-a2ce8519f6d0"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e8158717-c350-4032-bda0-9a654038afcd", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Common", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 54, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e8158717-c350-4032-bda0-9a654038afcd", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "- genital yeast infection (thrush)\n- passing more urine than usual or needing to pass urine more often\n- itching\n- rash or red skin - this may be itchy and include raised bumps, oozing fluid or blisters\n- thirst\n- blood tests may show an increase in blood fat (cholesterol) levels in your blood\n- constipation", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:36cbd42c-7441-468d-a347-1b517bd565e6"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:a0ddb39b-c2b1-4561-99f1-7dc562743052", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Major hypoglycaemia (events requiring assistance)", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "a0ddb39b-c2b1-4561-99f1-7dc562743052", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "No increase in major hypoglycaemia was observed with empagliflozin compared to placebo as monotherapy, add-on to metformin, add-on to metformin and a sulphonylurea, add-on to pioglitazone with or without metformin, add-on to linagliptin and metformin, as adjunct to standard care therapy and for the combination of empagliflozin with metformin in drug-naïve patients compared to those treated with empagliflozin and metformin as individual components. An increased frequency was noted when given as add-on to basal insulin with or without metformin and with or without a sulphonylurea (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 1.3%, placebo: 0% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg: 0%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 1.3%, placebo 0% over the 78-week trial), and add-on to MDI insulin with or without metformin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0.5%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 0.5%, placebo: 0.5% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg: 1.6%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 0.5%, placebo: 1.6% over the 52-week trial).\n\nIn the EMPEROR heart failure studies, major hypoglycaemia was observed at similar frequencies in patients with diabetes mellitus when treated with empagliflozin and placebo as add-on to sulphonylurea or insulin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 2.2%, placebo: 1.9%).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:96c4477c-37cd-4e29-bc91-2381ebbf1a20"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5323d531-2c7f-44f7-94de-ecd7a90ebbda"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:10a7c9c3-041a-4930-8c48-78dcb2a4d4e5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Vaginal moniliasis, vulvovaginitis, balanitis and other genital infection", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "10a7c9c3-041a-4930-8c48-78dcb2a4d4e5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Vaginal moniliasis, vulvovaginitis, balanitis and other genital infections were reported more frequently in patients treated with empagliflozin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 4.0%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 3.9%) compared to placebo (1.0%). These infections were reported more frequently in females treated with empagliflozin compared to placebo, and the difference in frequency was less pronounced in males. The genital tract infections were mild or moderate in intensity.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0e103c94-df9b-445d-9823-c7d9b650017b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:04735944-4719-46b2-961f-4a9e5e6e4bf2", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "04735944-4719-46b2-961f-4a9e5e6e4bf2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In the EMPEROR heart failure studies, the frequency of these infections was more pronounced in patients with diabetes mellitus (empagliflozin 10 mg: 2.3%; placebo: 0.8%) than in patients without diabetes mellitus (empagliflozin 10 mg: 1.7%; placebo: 0.7%) when treated with empagliflozin compared to placebo.\n\nCases of phimosis/acquired phimosis have been reported concurrent with genital infections and in some cases, circumcision was required.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:6e38e79d-fbec-454a-ad88-f978f4899ce4"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d5de7e51-25cd-47f4-847d-80a99d4d79fb", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Increased urination", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d5de7e51-25cd-47f4-847d-80a99d4d79fb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Increased urination (including the predefined terms pollakiuria, polyuria, and nocturia) was observed at higher frequencies in patients treated with empagliflozin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 3.5%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 3.3%) compared to placebo (1.4%). Increased urination was mostly mild or moderate in intensity. The frequency of reported nocturia was similar for placebo and empagliflozin (&lt; 1%).\n\nIn the EMPEROR heart failure studies, increased urination was observed at similar frequencies in patients treated with empagliflozin and placebo (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0.9%, placebo 0.5%).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:99e57213-def2-496b-8e47-943dc28729a9"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:6ce25d94-8bf5-405d-9cb2-1dde894dd61e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Urinary tract infection", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "6ce25d94-8bf5-405d-9cb2-1dde894dd61e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The overall frequency of urinary tract infection reported as adverse event was similar in patients treated with empagliflozin 25 mg and placebo (7.0% and 7.2%) and higher in empagliflozin 10 mg (8.8%). Similar to placebo, urinary tract infection was reported more frequently for empagliflozin in patients with a history of chronic or recurrent urinary tract infections. The intensity (mild, moderate, severe) of urinary tract infection was similar in patients treated with empagliflozin and placebo. Urinary tract infection was reported more frequently in females treated with empagliflozin compared to placebo; there was no difference in males.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8651d96c-624a-468d-8bbf-9d8f8130ef38"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:12f4b3f5-2014-4e1c-8cec-ce62be529fa7", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Volume depletion", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "12f4b3f5-2014-4e1c-8cec-ce62be529fa7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The overall frequency of volume depletion (including the predefined terms blood pressure (ambulatory) decreased, blood pressure systolic decreased, dehydration, hypotension, hypovolaemia, orthostatic hypotension, and syncope) was similar in patients treated with empagliflozin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0.6%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 0.4%) and placebo (0.3%). The frequency of volume depletion events was increased in patients 75 years and older treated with empagliflozin 10 mg (2.3%) or empagliflozin 25 mg (4.3%) compared to placebo (2.1%).", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:31c1c947-eb54-4dd1-9a68-2d02a844e517"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:11d431cf-486f-4bdb-9a4c-9005159978d5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Blood creatinine increased/Glomerular filtration rate decreased", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "11d431cf-486f-4bdb-9a4c-9005159978d5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The overall frequency of patients with increased blood creatinine and decreased glomerular filtration rate were similar between empagliflozin and placebo (blood creatinine increased: empagliflozin 10 mg 0.6%, empagliflozin 25 mg 0.1%, placebo 0.5%; glomerular filtration rate decreased: empagliflozin 10 mg 0.1%, empagliflozin 25 mg 0%, placebo 0.3%).\n\nInitial increases in creatinine and initial decreases in estimated glomerular filtration rates in patients treated with empagliflozin were generally transient during continuous treatment or reversible after drug discontinuation of treatment.\n\nConsistently, in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME study, patients treated with empagliflozin experienced an initial fall in eGFR (mean: 3 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ). Thereafter, eGFR was maintained during continued treatment. Mean eGFR returned to baseline after treatment discontinuation suggesting acute haemodynamic changes may play a role in these renal function changes. This phenomenon is also observed in the EMPEROR heart failure studies and the EMPA-KIDNEY study.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7c4bb919-a1c1-4c58-9ccc-5064ffaef069"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:0281fd9a-8e55-40c7-8e53-0667bee248d3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Serum lipids increased", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "0281fd9a-8e55-40c7-8e53-0667bee248d3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Mean percent increases from baseline for empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg versus placebo, respectively, were total cholesterol 4.9% and 5.7% versus 3.5%; HDL-cholesterol 3.3% and 3.6% versus 0.4%; LDL-cholesterol 9.5% and 10.0% versus 7.5%; triglycerides 9.2% and 9.9% versus 10.5%.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3b14c2a3-1244-49a4-9208-29ea181794ac"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:96d7c009-ca57-4dd5-9150-c27544ad94b2", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Haematocrit increased", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "96d7c009-ca57-4dd5-9150-c27544ad94b2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Mean changes from baseline in haematocrit were 3.4% and 3.6% for empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg, respectively, compared to 0.1% for placebo. In the EMPA-REG Outcome study, haematocrit values returned towards baseline values after a follow-up period of 30 days after treatment stop.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:df44ee1e-5ee3-4e67-b170-904aa2cc5404"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:592209f6-6bc2-414a-98b7-ec19c04a83ef", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Paediatric population", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "592209f6-6bc2-414a-98b7-ec19c04a83ef", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In the DINAMO trial 157 children aged 10 years and above with type 2 diabetes were treated, in which 52 patients received empagliflozin, 52 linagliptin and 53 placebo (see section 5.1). During the placebo-controlled phase, the most frequent adverse drug reaction was hypoglycaemia with higher overall rates for patients in the empagliflozin pooled group compared with placebo (empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg, pooled: 23.1%, placebo: 9.4%). None of these events was severe or required assistance.\n\nOverall, the safety profile in children was similar to the safety profile in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:831200c5-794d-466a-b743-c511e5e3aa1f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:4b506e4d-9c65-44eb-a962-96d6ca04ac0e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Reporting of suspected adverse reactions", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "4b506e4d-9c65-44eb-a962-96d6ca04ac0e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Reporting suspected adverse reactions after authorisation of the medicinal product is important. It allows continued monitoring of the benefit/risk balance of the medicinal product. Healthcare professionals are asked to report any suspected adverse reactions via the national reporting system listed in Appendix V.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9054e0cc-0e23-44be-8e17-20753e5533f6"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:1e76e7fd-d001-43a5-a0a5-01ecc9f886f4", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Mechanism of action", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 12, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "1e76e7fd-d001-43a5-a0a5-01ecc9f886f4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin is a reversible, highly potent (IC50 of 1.3 nmol) and selective competitive inhibitor of sodium-glucose co-transporter 2 (SGLT2). Empagliflozin does not inhibit other glucose transporters important for glucose transport into peripheral tissues and is 5 000 times more selective for SGLT2 versus SGLT1, the major transporter responsible for glucose absorption in the gut. SGLT2 is highly expressed in the kidney, whereas expression in other tissues is absent or very low. It is responsible, as the predominant transporter, for the reabsorption of glucose from the glomerular filtrate back into the circulation. In patients with type 2 diabetes and hyperglycaemia a higher amount of glucose is filtered and reabsorbed.\n\nEmpagliflozin improves glycaemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes by reducing renal glucose reabsorption. The amount of glucose removed by the kidney through this glucuretic mechanism is dependent on blood glucose concentration and GFR. Inhibition of SGLT2 in patients with type 2 diabetes and hyperglycaemia leads to excess glucose excretion in the urine. In addition, initiation of empagliflozin increases excretion of sodium resulting in osmotic diuresis and reduced intravascular volume.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e660463f-50de-40a8-a90c-9159e1d4c432"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8ea12248-1fb2-49bc-857a-fd261dd97d27"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:deecb14f-6525-4bb3-819d-fd6e87487433", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "deecb14f-6525-4bb3-819d-fd6e87487433", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In patients with type 2 diabetes, urinary glucose excretion increased immediately following the first dose of empagliflozin and is continuous over the 24 hour dosing interval. Increased urinary glucose excretion was maintained at the end of the 4-week treatment period, averaging approximately 78 g/day. Increased urinary glucose excretion resulted in an immediate reduction in plasma glucose levels in patients with type 2 diabetes.\n\nEmpagliflozin improves both fasting and post-prandial plasma glucose levels. The mechanism of action of empagliflozin is independent of beta cell function and insulin pathway and this contributes to a low risk of hypoglycaemia. Improvement of surrogate markers of beta cell function including Homeostasis Model Assessment-β (HOMA-β) was noted. In addition, urinary glucose excretion triggers calorie loss, associated with body fat loss and body weight reduction. The glucosuria observed with empagliflozin is accompanied by diuresis which may contribute to sustained and moderate reduction of blood pressure.\n\nEmpagliflozin also reduces sodium reabsorption and increases the delivery of sodium to the distal tubule. This may influence several physiological functions including, but not restricted to: increasing tubuloglomerular feedback and reducing intraglomerular pressure, lowering both pre- and afterload of the heart, downregulating of sympathetic activity and reducing left ventricular wall stress as evidenced by lower NT-proBNP values which may have beneficial effects on cardiac remodeling, filling pressures and diastolic function as well as preserving kidney structure and function. Other effects such as an increase in haematocrit, a reduction in body weight and blood pressure may further contribute to the beneficial cardiac and renal effects.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:92cd0e09-ec19-4416-abda-84d7f533a6c0"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c07d0ae4-bb57-4eed-a56d-390dba02ba58"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:d624b43c-483f-4835-982f-ebfc6b4bcfc2", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Clinical efficacy and safety", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "d624b43c-483f-4835-982f-ebfc6b4bcfc2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:2a5be72d-81f0-4e49-b100-65202149e3a2", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "2a5be72d-81f0-4e49-b100-65202149e3a2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Both improvement of glycaemic control and reduction of cardiovascular morbidity and mortality are an integral part of the treatment of type 2 diabetes.\n\nGlycaemic efficacy and cardiovascular outcomes have been assessed in a total of 14 663 patients with type 2 diabetes who were treated in 12 double-blind, placebo- and active-controlled clinical studies, of which 9 295 received empagliflozin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 4 165 patients; empagliflozin 25 mg: 5 130 patients). Five studies had treatment durations of 24 weeks; extensions of those and other studies had patients exposed to empagliflozin for up to 102 weeks.\n\nTreatment with empagliflozin as monotherapy and in combination with metformin, pioglitazone, a sulphonylurea, DPP-4 inhibitors, and insulin lead to clinically relevant improvements in HbA1c, fasting plasma glucose (FPG), body weight, and systolic and diastolic blood pressure. Administration of empagliflozin 25 mg resulted in a higher proportion of patients achieving HbA1c goal of less than 7% and fewer patients needing glycaemic rescue compared to empagliflozin 10 mg and placebo. Higher baseline HbA1c was associated with a greater reduction in HbA1c. In addition, empagliflozin as adjunct to standard care therapy reduced cardiovascular mortality in patients with type 2 diabetes and established cardiovascular disease.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9d645e92-f4ed-48fa-823d-40ca72466e51"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9d7cfc7b-6f7d-4f59-a9ca-b63261e6b146"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:75c96592-f767-4df2-9e70-b76cf412ebf1", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Monotherapy", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 13, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "75c96592-f767-4df2-9e70-b76cf412ebf1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "The efficacy and safety of empagliflozin as monotherapy was evaluated in a double-blind, placebo- and active-controlled study of 24 weeks duration in treatment-naïve patients. Treatment with empagliflozin resulted in a statistically significant (p &lt; 0.0001) reduction in HbA1c compared to placebo (Table 2) and a clinically meaningful decrease in FPG.\n\nIn a pre-specified analysis of patients (N = 201) with a baseline HbA1c ≥ 8.5%, treatment resulted in a reduction in HbA1c from baseline of -1.44% for empagliflozin 10 mg, -1.43% for empagliflozin 25 mg, -1.04% for sitagliptin, and an increase of 0.01% for placebo.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:35d99392-af0b-453d-8451-10bccc990d0d"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:fbac01df-4a29-4b24-9891-f9197379ea6e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "fbac01df-4a29-4b24-9891-f9197379ea6e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "In the double-blind placebo-controlled extension of this study, reductions of HbA1c, body weight and blood pressure were sustained up to Week 76.\n\nTable 2: Efficacy results of a 24 week placebo-controlled study of empagliflozin as monotherapy a\n\n|                                                              |   Placebo | Jardiance             | Jardiance             | Sitagliptin            |\n|--------------------------------------------------------------|-----------|-----------------------|-----------------------|------------------------|\n|                                                              |           | 10 mg                 | 25 mg                 | 100 mg                 |\n| N                                                            |       228 | 224                   | 224                   | 223                    |\n| HbA1c (%)                                                    |           |                       |                       |                        |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              |      7.91 | 7.87                  | 7.86                  | 7.85                   |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       |      0.08 | -0.66                 | -0.78                 | -0.66                  |\n| Difference from placebo 1 (97.5% CI)                         |           | -0.74* (-0.90, -0.57) | -0.85* (-1.01, -0.69) | -0.73 (-0.88, -0.59) 3 |\n| N                                                            |       208 | 204                   | 202                   | 200                    |\n| Patients (%) achieving HbA1c < 7% with baseline HbA1c ≥ 7% 2 |      12.0 | 35.3                  | 43.6                  | 37.5                   |\n| N                                                            |       228 | 224                   | 224                   | 223                    |\n| Body Weight (kg)                                             |           |                       |                       |                        |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              |     78.23 | 78.35                 | 77.80                 | 79.31                  |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       |     -0.33 | -2.26                 | -2.48                 | 0.18                   |\n| Difference from placebo 1 (97.5% CI)                         |           | -1.93* (-2.48, -1.38) | -2.15* (-2.70, -1.60) | 0.52 (-0.04, 1.00) 3   |\n| N                                                            |       228 | 224                   | 224                   | 223                    |\n| SBP (mmHg) 4                                                 |           |                       |                       |                        |\n| Baseline (mean)                                              |     130.4 | 133.0                 | 129.9                 | 132.5                  |\n| Change from baseline 1                                       |      -0.3 | -2.9                  | -3.7                  | 0.5                    |\n| Difference from placebo 1 (97.5% CI)                         |           | -2.6* (-5.2, -0.0)    | -3.4* (-6.0, -0.9)    | 0.8 (-1.4, 3.1) 3      |\n\na Full analysis set (FAS) using last observation carried forward (LOCF) prior to glycaemic rescue therapy\n\n1 Mean adjusted for baseline value\n\n2 Not evaluated for statistical significance as a result of the sequential confirmatory testing procedure 3 95% CI\n\n4 LOCF, values after antihypertensive rescue censored\n\n* p-value &lt; 0.0001", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e71b5ced-0c1d-4140-882f-4dc48e90429e"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0bffa2c3-f19f-453b-a0e5-8aa082e97819"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a7e1855b-d31d-4106-9f16-8fe27062fe03"}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:01cef9ac-8e6d-47d1-a1f8-e988fab31377"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:691c0d49-486d-4575-8859-432aa3d2c8b7", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Combination therapy", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "691c0d49-486d-4575-8859-432aa3d2c8b7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:5e98039a-f382-497c-9aae-2db86ec89dc1", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Empagliflozin as add-on to metformin, sulphonylurea, pioglitazone", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "5e98039a-f382-497c-9aae-2db86ec89dc1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Empagliflozin as add-on to metformin, metformin and a sulphonylurea, or pioglitazone with or without metformin resulted in statistically significant (p &lt; 0.0001) reductions in HbA1c and body weight compared to placebo (Table 3). In addition it resulted in a clinically meaningful reduction in FPG, systolic and diastolic blood pressure compared to placebo.\n\nIn the double-blind placebo-controlled extension of these studies, reduction of HbA1c, body weight and blood pressure were sustained up to Week 76.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:dfa68f73-4f43-4aec-be65-5d93cc634e95"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:jardiance:section:e300cce3-3c80-4879-b4e9-84a0ed4ef53b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "product_information", "section_id": "e300cce3-3c80-4879-b4e9-84a0ed4ef53b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf", "source_document_id": "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40", "text": "Table 3: Efficacy results of 24 week placebo-controlled studies a\n\n|                                                              | Add-on to metformin therapy                     | Add-on to metformin therapy            